UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Shield still allows bullet penetration when strafing...', post_text = 'Just finished off a series of Aztec, Cobble, and Militia with the latest 1/31/03 update and confirmed that the shield still is letting bullets penetrate when strafing. I tested standing still, crouching, crouch moving in all directions, walking and running in all directions, and jumping in all directions, with shield both deployed in front and undeployed to the side. In all cases the shield only blocked bullets when standing still, crouching, jumping, or walking/running/crouch walking/jumping forward and backward. But side strafing (running/walking/crouch walking), side jumping, and diagonal (2 arrow keys) strafeing & jumping let bullets through. Basically any movement that requires the left or right arrow to strafe allowed bullet penetration. The same effect occurs against knife slashes and stabs. They are blocked except when in a strafe movement. Another bug is that with shield both deployed and undeployed, a player can not jump forward-left, left or rear-left when walking or crouching, only when running.\n\n__________________ "Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader' WHERE post_id = 18113 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'If you notice, when running left or right (strafing) various body parts tend to move outside of the shield\'s protection. That may be what\'s up. Many a time have I seen people\'s legs pop out of the shield when strafing and killed them because of it.' WHERE post_id = 18116 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Yeah I am aware of that effect except I intetnionally altered standing still and strafing when someone was shooting right at my shield, and the times when the strafe arrows were pressed was when the bullets were penetrating. Also when walking or crouching while strafeing and facing the enemy, the arms are not exposed as much as when running outright. I\'m positive there were no arm/leg hits occurring to the side of the shield, as the people shooting at me were aiming center mass. The biggest indication was the times I was crouching with shield deployed and facing the enemy directly. The movement speed is practically non existent when crouching with a deployed shield. When I tapped the left and right arrows the bullets were clearly penetrating, and when the arrow keys were released the shield blocked the bullets. There was no movement to expose arms or legs in those cases.\n\n__________________ "Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader' WHERE post_id = 18119 AND is_historical = 1;
