UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I have noticed that since the last update that the shield is much harder to kill. I think you guys need to look at how the shield carriers are getting hit. I have been watching the movements of shield carriers and have noticed that body parts are exposed as they crawl and the body hitbox must extend out past the shield where the ass sticks out. It doesn\'t take much strafe movement to the side to get a shot on a piece of exposed body. It doesn\'t look like much but try shooting the ass with a scout and you\'ll see its not hard to hit. In close range a fast strafe spray will get a piece of that exposed hitbox. The freeze effect of getting hit further ensures that you will strafe around the shields faster than the shield carrier can turn towards you. He really is only safe when crouching still, but forward rushes combined with a jump and firing down from above will kill them quick. It appears that the shield takes quite a bit of skill to use properly. It is only really effective when used with another player with a rifle. Its great for drawing fire so the guy with the rifle has the first shot in most instances. I have forced my self not to shoot the shield first and go for the guy with the rifle. But if the shield carrier is smart he will then open up and has a great chance to kill me with a pistol. The shield is very effective as it is currently implemented, but it does require alot of skill. It is important to realize this and know the the level of protection the shield actually provides. It is most vulnerable from side angle attacks of about 40 degrees from either side. It doesn\'t take much strafing to get into that position and get that first shot which stuns. Like I said above this only compounds the problem for the shield carrier because it stuns them allowing the opponent to strafe further with each shot exposing more each time. Its a additive effect once they are hit. I have not witnessed any headshots through the shield since the last update while the carrier is crouching. I think this latest patch has found a great balance and users must realize when they are exposed and understand that to carry a sheild alone takes great skill. It is best to team up with a guy with a rifle. Thats is the most effective strategy, not only does it allow your team the first shot (from the rifle or you depending on who the opponent goes for first) but it also prevenst the enemy from being able to strafe and to a shallow agle that leasves you exposed. Go with a rifle teamate and when you see an enemy duck and hold still. You won\'t get alot of kills but your team will and you won\'t take much damage either. Your only real oppurtunity for kills with the shield is when the enemy fires at the rifle backup first. Then it is your turn to open up and blast them. If the enemy shifts targets to you the the shield still offers limited protection and hopefully the opponent is injured enough that a few landed shots takes him out. The shield is very balanced when you understand how to use it and how you get killed with it. There is almost no side protection. Use the buddy system and your team will benifit from your shield. I did not even go into how it effects enemy movement through choke points which is a whole other bonus. Quick example is the bridge on Aztec. This choke point is a whole new animal now with CT shields. Same with the double doors if the T\'s don\'t rush through before they set up and draw fire so the snipers have the first shots. The last bonus for your team from using hte shield is greater ammo consumtion by the other team. I am always on my last clip at the end of the round and I am having to pickup guns as I go while playing Aztec or Dust2 because of the amount of players and choke points. The shields require more ammo to pin down. Sorry but your not a tank with the sheild if you\'re alone and crouching still.' WHERE post_id = 18685 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I agree with some of the operational abilities of the shield noted above, however in my tests it was definately not bullets hitting an exposed hitbox. The bullets were penetrating the shield itself, and headshots were occurring through the shield frequently during those tests. The shield certainly is not a tank, in that it\'s a 2-d slab that only protects the front of the user and is only effective directly facing the enemy, however it should not suffer from penetration bugs while strafing the way it currently does.\n\n__________________ "Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader' WHERE post_id = 18698 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'The strafe thing is true. Another problem I have with the shield is when you are in a vent of under some stairs with a shield and the shield sticks out and lets people know you are there.' WHERE post_id = 18727 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'What do you want? A tiny piece of shield that no one will ever be able to see, yet will stop anything that is shot at you, no matter which way you are moving. I have a feeling that if the game introduced "invisible, non-penetrable body armor, you guys would forego buying guns at all, and just "BE SAFE". Cmon now, lets get real, obviously the shield cant stop every bullet while you are MOVING, if it did, everyone would have a shield. So stop thinking that the shield is supposed to be the best thing since sliced bread, and learn to use it properly. And in my opinion, properly does not include working perfectly while moving, running and jumping. -Agent' WHERE post_id = 18754 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'If the shield is meant to block bullets, and a bullet hits the shield while the user is moving sideways, the bullet should not penetrate, because it hit the shield. There\'s no problem if the bullet hits exposed parts of the player behind the shield, but if it is supposed to be impenetrable it should be so all of the time. As to the clipping issue in vents, that specifically occurs mostly on assault, and will just have to be dealt with, unless the shield is made "solid" like a player model rather than intangible to the map like the weapons are(they stick into and through walls, doors and crates). Of course if the shield was made solid to the rest of the map environment, then you wouldn\'t even be able to enter the vent in the first place.\n\n__________________ "Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader' WHERE post_id = 18777 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Hey, I got some weird thing: What if u r a terrorist holding only a dual berreta (nevemind the spelling). Will you be able to pick up the shield. If yes, will u be only be able to use one berreta??\n\n__________________ ">.< ">.< ">.<' WHERE post_id = 18895 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'The shield can\'t be used with Dual Berettas at all. No nifty single Beretta modification for shield. So the shield works with knife (no stab), USP (no silencer), Glock (no burst), Deagle, P228, 5-7 and grenades. When a Terrorist takes out the bomb the shield just disappears completely. Must be some big pockets or other voluminous spaces that the shield is put into, probably the same place snipers put thier AWP\'s when not in use... [] []\n\n__________________ "Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader' WHERE post_id = 18963 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Steam 2/14 Release', post_text = 'We\'re released a new version of our products on the Steam beta. Servers will need to be restarted to come back online. If you launch your game you will automatically update. Changes are as follows: All Games: - Fixed netgraph. Dedicated Server: - Complete reworking of the user interface. Counter-Strike - Fixed streetlamp in Inferno - Fixed floating staircases in Inferno - Fixed bullet penetration problem with railings in Inferno - Fixed bug where you could throw the bomb to a place where it could not be picked up in Aztec - Fixed spawn kill probelm in Aztec - Swapped door orientation back at CT spawn - Fixed silent plant bug at A in Airstrip - Added sign crate to B in Airstrip - Fixed bug where players would get stuck behind a tree near bridge from the T spawn in Airstrip - Added in ability to buy items by name to allow for scripting. Item names are: Pistols ------- "glock" "usp" "p228" "deagle" "elites" "fn57" "ak47" Shotguns -------- "m3" "xm1014" SMG --- "mac10" "tmp" "mp5" "ump45" "p90" Rifles ------ "galil" "scout" "sg552" "awp" "g3sg1" "famas" "m4a1" "aug" "sg550" Machine Gun ----------- "m249" Ammo ---- "primammo" "secammo" Equipment --------- "defuser" "vest""shield" "vesthelm" "flash" "hegren"' WHERE post_id = 20634 AND is_historical = 1;
