UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Steam 2/21 Release', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Erik Johnson If anyone runs into a crash in Steam, please check your Steam install directory for .mdmp files and e-mail them to me at erik@valvesoftware.com (mailto:erik@valvesoftware.com). Odd, I\'m not finding any of these .mdmp files even though Steam crashed twice for me today. One wasn\'t exactly a crash but I was unable to see my desktop or any new windows and thus was unable to end the program in any way other than restarting the computer. The other was more tame and only crashed Steam itself - I was able to just use good ol\' CTRL-ALT-DEL and end the application windows of Steam. I\'m on Windows XP with the service pack and critical updates and whatnot. My friend on Windows Me, however, has an absolutely miserable time trying to get Steam to run stable on his computer. It crashes so badly and frequently that he has to sometimes restart his computer 3 times in a row just to get back into a server successfully. He recently had to reformat his computer, so it\'s nice and minty fresh and everything else of a non-Steam variety runs well, so it\'s obviously an issue directly with Steam. I\'ll ask him later if he has any of these .mdmp files you mentioned.' WHERE post_id = 22449 AND is_historical = 1;
