UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Peter Rye If Valve can update your CS or half life program anytime thru Steam. What would stop a hacker disguised as Valve employee (or plain hacker plugging into Steam) to write subroutines in the half life program update where it can be asked to read your entire hard disk, or activate your web cam to see into your room? We can ask antivirus to detect trojan, but in Steam where any file can be integrated right inside Half Life anytime, what would stop writing program subroutines to read hard disk,etc.? Peter dude your paranoid. but your right. there is a certain ammount of trust associated with steam. i bet the number of people at valve that have the ability to do updates is very limited. for that exact reason.' WHERE post_id = 34296 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Peter Rye If Valve can update your CS or half life program anytime thru Steam. What would stop a hacker disguised as Valve employee (or plain hacker plugging into Steam) to write subroutines in the half life program update where it can be asked to read your entire hard disk, or activate your web cam to see into your room? We can ask antivirus to detect trojan, but in Steam where any file can be integrated right inside Half Life anytime, what would stop writing program subroutines to read hard disk,etc.? Peter WTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!! have u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is cs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. plus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe] just get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry' WHERE post_id = 34309 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'look if u get a firewall sure it will stop programs to acess the internet and prevent people from reading files but the firewall says if it is ok for that program to use the internet What peter is saying that a hacker goes THROUGH steam and if u let steam acess the internet it is only "STEAM" that is affected and the so called "hacker" uses its skill and programs through steam. And it can look at ur files. so the firewall is use less but it is good to have one on your pc although i think it is impossible for that to happen buddy unless a group of terrorists took over valve and forced a program to be uploaded to ur pc updating steam causing them to acess ur pc easily although that would never happen Who would want to take over Valve? I can see y someone would threaten them by blowing them up because they keep delaying the date of CS 1.6, CZ, or CS 1.7, but not take over hahahahahahahhaha []' WHERE post_id = 34314 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Neo Vortex WTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!! have u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is cs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. plus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe] just get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry dude all a firewall does is block unrequested internet traffic. simply put, the way a firewall works is as follows. you open/run a program that access the net. the firewall sees this, looks to its list of filters/rules. if it finds one that matches then it allows traffic in both directions. so for someone to \'hack\' the steam system they would have to do it from inside. that being said. nothing is 100% secure. i garentee you that if serious hacker/cracker, not these little script kiddes that download sh*t off the net and click the \'go\' button, want to get inside your box there is no firewall/router/proxy server/nat server that will stop him/her. everything has a vunerability. everything.' WHERE post_id = 34316 AND is_historical = 1;
