UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Raging_Wulf Bump, and I think Microsoft might consider taking over Valve. They might! I\'m sure they want HL and CS on thei X-Box! GOD! We\'ll have new 56k players! lol (only if Valve implements a multi-player feature)' WHERE post_id = 44603 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Re: Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by oDin dude all a firewall does is block unrequested internet traffic. simply put, the way a firewall works is as follows. you open/run a program that access the net. the firewall sees this, looks to its list of filters/rules. if it finds one that matches then it allows traffic in both directions. so for someone to \'hack\' the steam system they would have to do it from inside. that being said. nothing is 100% secure. i garentee you that if serious hacker/cracker, not these little script kiddes that download sh*t off the net and click the \'go\' button, want to get inside your box there is no firewall/router/proxy server/nat server that will stop him/her. everything has a vunerability. everything. Firewalls have multiple functionalities (i have a linux one myself: Astaro). But the main function of a firewall is to block ports. But it is mainly in one direction: incomming. Because there is no use of blocking outgoing ports, except if you are a parent and don\'t want your children to use certain programs on the net, or you want to make people use a logged proxy, so you block port 80 and open another one. So again, the only way people would be able to hack your computer via Valve (even though they wouldn\'t b/c it is much easier with emails and other ways), they would have to modify Steam so it runs their programs everytime someone starts Steam, and then could hack Valve\'s servers to make an update... But if haxors were to hack Valve, they would erase the data because they hate Steam... [] Frankly, if you guys are that paranoid, you could also start on Windows\' breaches... You could switch to linux if you want. But remember: Choose between easy utilization, or security. Consider nothing being between those two.' WHERE post_id = 44604 AND is_historical = 1;
