UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Gabe Newell confirms.....', post_text = 'NOTE: I didn\'t send this email, somebody from the halflife2.net forums did. -----Original Message----- From: Mr.Radar [mailto:mr_radar@charter.net] Sent: Friday, July 25, 2003 7:29 PM To: gaben@valvesoftware.com (mailto:gaben@valvesoftware.com) Subject: 4th Video... Just in case you aren\'t paying attention to any of the fan forums(or even your own Steam forum) things aren\'t going too well. We\'ve been waiting for this 4th video to unlock for 3 and a half hours now. Now I can understand about the whole thing with waiting until steam got encryption but I mean jeez! We\'ve been waiting for this video for a WEEK! Can\'t you at least do whatever you need to unlock it on time?!?! If you\'ve waiting for site like FilePlanet to upload the file then I don\'t care if non-steam users won\'t be getting it for a while but NOT unlocking it when you say you will(ok, on the second set release date/time) is only going to get people(like me) angry and won\'t be helping your reputation. Even though I will still buy HL2(if I don\'t read a bad review of it, and I WILL be reading reviews) I am majorly dissapointed. Could you at least inform people of when things go wrong and what action is being taken to correct whatever is wrong? This(news and info) seems to be a major problem for Valve software. How can you claim to be the most community oriented game developer if you can\'t even tell your fans that there are problems and you are working to correct them and that there will be delays. Gabes responce quote:Well, Erik and his wife had a baby last night, and we\'re operating a little slowly around here in his absence.' WHERE post_id = 63358 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Erik might have been absent, sure.. but is he seriously the ONLY person running Steam? Not quite a comforting thought, actually. Anyways, congrats to Erik for his lil\' Alyx or lil\' Gordon []' WHERE post_id = 63359 AND is_historical = 1;
