UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Do your bink videos run like crap in a bucket???', post_text = 'Do you want to change that? well now you can! with this quick and easy method! I\'m going to explain what the problem is and how to fix it! it\'s the blitting that messes up, it makes low-ended machines lag the movies terribly, to fix this go to binks website and download the RAD Tools, install and startup RAD Tools. Then select the bink video and click advanced play, then under blitting style switch it from the default to: DIRECTDRAW UYVY off-screen. u\'ll have a perfect framerate! this won\'t be permanent unless u click make EXE and use that one to play the video instead of the steam one in the movie folder. B4 you say, "I don\'t care, i\'m a computerz genuizez and that won\'tz fixz it. I PWN JOO!!!!!!" just read these testimonies! Poster - Memory Gap: yep this worked, thanks a bunch hunter. also the sound was synched properly too. Poster - mr_badger: Thanks Hunter. Now the videos look the way they should. Perhaps making this a sticky guide for ppl will help them to experiance the videos as they were meant. Poster - Kilko: Btw, thehunter1320, it looks much better now!!!! Soooo smoooth!!!!! I thought they just put it bad together before, but now it\'s all good! THX ALOT thehunter1320!!!! Poster - trepid_jon: Yeah, thanks for that info. They play all smooth now. Very cool. Everything\'s lined up right now. The crowbar swing actually looks right. Man, I\'m glad I read that post in this thread. the web site where you can get RAD Tools is www.radgametools.com (http://www.radgametools.com) Happy watching! P.S.: if this helped you achieve a better frame-rate please bump this topic.' WHERE post_id = 67934 AND is_historical = 1;
