UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Problems with the new Steam after running the beta?  Solution within!', post_text = 'The new Linux Steam client has a couple problems that can crop up on a lot of Linux-based computers. It took me and a few others a while to track down the problem, but here are the problems, and their corresponding solutions: Broken Pipe error After downloading the hldsupdatetool.bin file, and executing it, it may abort something like this:code:Enter \'yes\' to accept this agreement, \'no\' to decline: yes sh: line 1: uncompress: command not found Broken pipe [hlds@funball hlds_l]$ If it does, the error actually is telling you ecactly what the problem is- you lack the \'uncompress\' tool, which is rather common, but some Linux distros (more notable some Red Hat versions) lack. You can get the RPM you need here (http://rpmfind.net/linux/rpm2html/search.php?query=uncompress). Once you have it, su up to root, go to where the file is, and run this command:code:rpm -i ncompress-4.2.4-33.i386.rpm Assuming you get no error messages, you should now be able to log out as root, log back in with your HLDS user, and successfully run the .bin file. It\'ll extract one file, \'steam\'. The \'Connection Reset\' Problem At first, this one was a bear to nail down, but it seems that we\'ve got it. You\'ll know you ahve this problem when, when you try to run steam to update a server, or to create an account, this happens: code:[hlds@funball hlds_l-steam]$ ./steam -update tfc . myusername mypasswd Checking bootstrapper version ... Getting version 0 of Steam HLDS Update Tool Connection Reset If this happens, all you need to do is run this command... code:rm -rf ~/.steam/...and you should be all set. Run that command, and start from the \'create an account\' step in the Readme file. I hope this helps!' WHERE post_id = 88496 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Problems with the new Steam after running the beta?  Solution within!', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Ghoti The \'Connection Reset\' Problem At first, this one was a bear to nail down, but it seems that we\'ve got it. You\'ll know you ahve this problem when, when you try to run steam to update a server, or to create an account, this happens: code:[hlds@funball hlds_l-steam]$ ./steam -update tfc . myusername mypasswd Checking bootstrapper version ... Getting version 0 of Steam HLDS Update Tool Connection Reset If this happens, all you need to do is run this command... code:rm -rf ~/.steam/...and you should be all set. Run that command, and start from the \'create an account\' step in the Readme file. I hope this helps! Ghoti thank you very much I would have never realized that command would fix it. If you don\'t mind me asking I am learning linux and would like to know what caused this error and why the rm -rf ~./steam/ fix it. Thanks Again\n\n__________________ Whats cooler then being cool \'ICE COLD!!!\'' WHERE post_id = 88583 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'m happy to! The Steam beta kept the user identification information (your Steam usernamd and password) in a special directory (.steam) in your account\'s home directory. When the new version came out, Valve didn\'t tell us that it wan\'t \'beta-aware\', and when you ran the new Steam, it looked in ~/.steam/ for the Steam account information, which, since the Steam user database was reset, is no longer valid. This is what causes the \'Connection Reset\' problem- it\'s more of a \'Bad Password\' problem, just badly labeled, or an overgeneralized error message. ~ is Unix-ese for \'home directory\', and since the Steam data was kept in a directory \'.steam\' in your home, its path is \'~/.steam/\'. As another side note, files and directories with names that start with a \'.\' are hidden- they won\'t show up unless you ise the \'a\' switch on the ls command, like this:code:ls -a' WHERE post_id = 88592 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'thanks man\n\n__________________ Whats cooler then being cool \'ICE COLD!!!\'' WHERE post_id = 88613 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Glad to help!' WHERE post_id = 88875 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Heres the story, people: An FAQ about Steam', post_text = 'The Official Steam Client was released, along with the final of CS 1.6, and currently Valve is finalizong the Steam Content Network servers in anticipation of the relase of Half-Life 2. This thread is for Steam users that are having difficulty with the program. If you continue to spam this thread, I will delete it, as I have no need to use the answers posted here. This means no more all caps posts, no more spammimg, no more useless crap. GOT IT? The following is a FAQ for Steam. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 1] Will my cd key still work? Yes, it will. Steam will prompt for it during installation. 2] Is WON offline? No, it will stay up for about 2 weeks, and then the WON servers will be shut down permanently. 3] Can I hold a LAN game? Yes, you can, but, and this is quite a but, every system has to be online and connected. The likelyhood this will change is great, however. 4] Will my MOD work under steam? It should, but chances are that if it isnt a mainstream mod i.e. NS or DoD, then you should wait before installing it untill the next patch is released. Full MOD support is included with Steam, however, so wait before spamming the forums with complaints. 5] I was in the beta for steam.....it will update itself, right? No, a new steam client was released and the beta program will not work anymore. You must delete the original beta install and run the new installer. 6] Can I still play CS 1.5? Again, yes, for two weeks untill WON goes offline. 7] When will CS 1.6 become final? The Counter-Strike version 1.6 final has been released. 8] Is there spyware in Steam? No, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Any other questions have more than likely had threads dedicated to them, and all one has to do is search for them. If there are any more questions you think I may have missed, feel free to add them with the answers. ~retribution' WHERE post_id = 88984 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Also, here is some general info. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- - The old Steam beta accounts have all been deleted. you will have to create a new account. - It is strongly recommended that if you had the beta client installed, that you uninstall and delete all of it before installing the official steam client. It is necessary for the official Steam client to work. - You will be able to install custom models for CS 1.6 under steam. - The Official FAQs are up and running once more, if having chronic problems you should head over there. - The Half-Life 2 movies have been pulled temporarily due to the extreme network usage the content servers have been experiencing. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- more will be posted as it comes up.' WHERE post_id = 89046 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for writing this. Here\'s a link to the official FAQ (/faq.htm), for other questions. Towards the end are questions & answers regarding mods and custom content.' WHERE post_id = 89074 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I have some questions (yes I have visited the FAQ page) Question 1: Are the Steam content provider servers and Steam ID autherisation servers on seperate machines with seperate networks? Reason I am asking is that if the authersation and content providers are on the same network it is possible that whenever a popular update/patch or a new game (HL 2) becomes available the servers will be overloaded and autherisation will be unavailable. Question 2: The FAQ wasn\'t too clear on this issue. If I understand this correctly a Steam enabled game will allow single player usage untill the player enables Steam for that game (for multiplayer or patching/updates ) thereafter even single player gameing will require a internet connection, is this true ? Question 3) If the answer to Question 2 is yes, isn\'t it a bit much to expect players to connect to the internet even if they merely want to play single player ? I mean not all of Valves supporters have the luxury of a always available or on broadband connection. Question 4) Will the updates and patches for Steam enabled games be available for manual download and deploy, and will it be possible to store these updates on media for later retrieval ? Question 4 relates to the bandwidth availability issue, if its possible to manually download, store and deploy patches/updates then those with a decent connection can download them and upload to a local server for those with dial-up. I commend Valve for thier attempts to provide a service whereby supporters can get the latest patchs/update and games, whereby a system that assists in keeping gaming cheat free and providing ease of use in finding game servers and friends, however I must add a note of caution that not all of Valves supporters have broadband options and internet connectivity can be problematical. I have faith that Valve will consider the plight of those supporters and provide other means to work around these issues.' WHERE post_id = 89148 AND is_historical = 1;
