UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'a continuation of the FAQ..........', post_text = 'quote:Question 1: Are the Steam content provider servers and Steam ID autherisation servers on seperate machines with seperate networks? Question 2: The FAQ wasn\'t too clear on this issue. If I understand this correctly a Steam enabled game will allow single player usage untill the player enables Steam for that game (for multiplayer or patching/updates ) thereafter even single player gameing will require a internet connection, is this true ? Question 3) If the answer to Question 2 is yes, isn\'t it a bit much to expect players to connect to the internet even if they merely want to play single player ? I mean not all of Valves supporters have the luxury of a always available or on broadband connection. Question 4) Will the updates and patches for Steam enabled games be available for manual download and deploy, and will it be possible to store these updates on media for later retrieval ? Question 4 relates to the bandwidth availability issue, if its possible to manually download, store and deploy patches/updates then those with a decent connection can download them and upload to a local server for those with dial-up. In regards to your questions: ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 1] No, they are the same, and yes, the risk is real. however, the certain upcoming addtition of bandwith will ease this congestion. 2] Yes, you understand correctly. Take HL2 for example. Say that you buy the box and install the game, nut not through Steam. You will be able to play the single player offline. However, you also will not be able to dl any patches that may be released. Once you connect to Steam, all patches will dl automatically, but you will be required to stay online in order to play HL2 from then on. 3] You are absoluty right, and Valve is putting serious consideration into changing this requirement. Expect news in this concern in the next week or so. 4] At this point, it looks like manual download will not be enabled, although it may be possible to cache the data and store it on disk, i.e. such as was done for CS 1.6b recently. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- quote:say i downloaded all of the halflife game through steam, the whole lot all the levels sounds etc so that it does not require an internet connection. do i have to be online to play the single player, even if i have all the files for it? oh yeah and how do i find my steam id out? As of the moment, yes, you will be required to have a net connection while online, the reason being an allowance for automatic updates, as well as anti-piracy. Although this may not seem satifactory for 56k users and LAN event hosts, it is most likely that this will change. And to find your Steam ID, when connected to a server, type "status" in the consol.' WHERE post_id = 90177 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Number three takes care of itself. That decision is incredibly idiotic, and if its not done my HL days are over (BF 1942 was becoming more fun, anyway). "8] Is there spyware in Steam? No, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors." Then what the hell else is steam using all this processing power for? Are you seriously going to argue that the proggy requires a 1 gig processor simply do "stream content" (something it does poorly, btw)...' WHERE post_id = 90822 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '"4] At this point, it looks like manual download will not be enabled, although it may be possible to cache the data and store it on disk, i.e. such as was done for CS 1.6b recently." If this is true then the only people with "hard" access to patches (ie, not through steam) will be those who pirate them. Why inconvienence real supporters like this? And if the steam developers think they can keep these patches away from the warez kiddies by streaming them then their vastly underestimating the dedication people have to receiving free software.' WHERE post_id = 90830 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Propagandhi Number three takes care of itself. That decision is incredibly idiotic, and if its not done my HL days are over (BF 1942 was becoming more fun, anyway). "8] Is there spyware in Steam? No, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors." Then what the hell else is steam using all this processing power for? Are you seriously going to argue that the proggy requires a 1 gig processor simply do "stream content" (something it does poorly, btw)... i run steam on a 555mhz 128mb ram 6 year old hp. trust me, the requirements are not accurate, merely recommendations at best. as for number 3, valve is reconsidering its decision.' WHERE post_id = 90847 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'FAQ: Why are you forcing everyone to use the bug laden software that is Steam? A: Because we are moving to the pay-to-play model and this must be done. Trust us, it will be better for us in the long run. FAQ: Steam contains many \'features\' that users say they don\'t need or even want, why put them in? A: Well, we needed some guise to shove this thing down your throat. See? It\'s a "good thing"! Think of it as \'Vaseline\' if you get my drift. I will never pay for a game that requires Steam.' WHERE post_id = 91039 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: a continuation of the FAQ..........', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by retribution 2] Yes, you understand correctly. Take HL2 for example. Say that you buy the box and install the game, nut not through Steam. You will be able to play the single player offline. However, you also will not be able to dl any patches that may be released. Once you connect to Steam, all patches will dl automatically, but you will be required to stay online in order to play HL2 from then on.And if this doesn\'t change, it will be no HL2 for me. I\'ve commented elsewhere (http://boards.straightdope.com/sdmb/showthread.php?s=&threadid=211017) about my strong negative feelings about this. However, I\'ll repeat some of the objections: 1) If my net connection is down, I am more likely to play SP. Requiring online authentication means that when my net connection is down, my retail game is down as well. 2) If Steam is down (unlikely, right?) that means I can\'t play SP or MP. My shiny new box is just so much garbage. 3) If something happens to Valve in the future, there is no guarantee I\'ll be able to use the software I purchased. 4) There is nothing to prevent Valve discontinuing support for HL2 sometime in the future, thus preventing me from playing ever again. All this presumes that I buy the retail box and play online or get patches and then play more SP--of course, that follows my gaming patterns with every game I have (with the exception of Homeworld, which I never played online.) It\'s even more aggrivating that the reason for this policy is most likely to deter unlicensed copying of the game. Of course, it won\'t deter that, but it will be a thorn in the side of legitimate players. I don\'t like being treated like a thief first, customer second. If this is still the case when HL2 ships, I won\'t be buying it. I\'ll spend my money and time on Halo instead (at least they\'ve gone gold, and aren\'t deceiving their customer base about a release date).' WHERE post_id = 91059 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Amen to that! I\'m a university student and have a 10mb/s line, but if/when I go home during summer (1-3 months) I don\'t want to have to use my parents dial-up connection every time I want to play an offline game, right? I guess and hope that Vavle gets their act together and makes sure you don\'t need internet access just to play at a LAN or in places where there\'s no internet access, otherwise their good reputation from half-life will go to waste...' WHERE post_id = 91232 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Official Steam Bug-List #1', post_text = 'Hey guys, sorry forums been down. Feel free to post all bugs that you have encountered in the current version of Steam. We are also accepting any suggestions that you may have to improve Steam. Bugs -Banned for cheating when your really not cheating. -Mp5 muzzle on m4a1 gun. -Shield sometimes not showing in buy menu. Suggestions -Chatroom support in Steam. -Changing Steam skins w/o restarting Steam. -More Games added to Friends. Update You can also post bugs you are encountering in-game.' WHERE post_id = 89099 AND is_historical = 1;
