UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'duck button will still not close spectator GUI. it will activate it, but not close it. i use shift for duck, if that helps. MOTD\'s - scroll bars do not work. and at 640, you can only see the first few lines. well the bars work, but when you scroll down the message doesnt move. this one may be hard to explain properly, but ill try. i normally launch Steam to the "server" menu. if i then launch CS from the "games" menu, when i click on "servers" i get a blank list saying no servers pass my filter requirements or whatever. my favorites show up, when i click "spectate", what i presume to be HLTV servers show up, but when i select "internet" it will not refresh servers. if i then quit CS, i can refresh the server list all day long with no problems. Steam still runs in background after you "Exit Steam" from system tray. so the only way to launch Steam again is to ctrl+alt+del, end the process, and start Steam again. im sure im forgetting some...post em later' WHERE post_id = 89123 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well i know they already got some of this but what the heck. Bugs: After joining a server with a nonofficial map, it crashed. And when i restarted it said there was an error in my cache, and i should flush it. The inprogram delete cache and, the flush cache option in the dialog did not work. Reinstall was the only workaround. It was a rare bug so it\'s probably not gonna get spotted again. Also the grey Steam skin has some of the green skin, ingame. Suggestions: Regions and closed servers: I don\'t know if this is in already. Make content servers by region. And maybe even disable access to it to people out of that region, to lure more people into hosting. Error correcting cachefiles: If your cache fails, make a validate data system, where it checks every file against MD5 hashes and then patches them with proper data. Less serverchecks: Well some of the options, delete local cache and monitor and so on. Shouldn\'t need to require a servercheck. Servercheck and download icon: Instead of the current working icon, make a servercheck icon, so people know when it\'s authenticating, and when it\'s working. And instead of the current working icon also include a downloading icon, so people knows when it\'s downloading. Edit: Better status: Also in conjunction with the above suggestion, dialog status boxes should be made if it has connection trouble and whatever. Shares: Already in the works, but a shared license and local steam content server client. P2P - Bittorrent: Bittorrent based P2P system. http://bitconjurer.org/BitTorrent/ (http://bitconjurer.org/BitTorrent/) Should also be allowed for ingame content(maps, mods and so on) via Friends. Massive database: Steam that serves a big database of maps, mods and whatever. Which are downloaded through external sites, p2p or in some cases content servers. Better HTML browser: With the suggestion above we will need a better working in-steam browser.' WHERE post_id = 89126 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Steam Client + Fix properties page(includes Calculate Cache Status) hanging if content is not downloaded fully + Disable memory dumps + Fix GUI hangs, almost everywhere + Logout doesn\'t exits Steam + No lingering process after exit + Fix monitor to show kilobytes(kB) instead of kilobits(kb) + Use maximum bandwidth to download, not download only when the connection is idle + Fix GUI hangs on server connects (Sometimes you cannot even click Cancel) + Fix reset of "Automatic updates" + Add previews for skin chooser + News is opened in Steam, no window popups + Screenshots for un-installed games (Aka Preview) + Better progress bar (With percentage complete) + Ability to cancel update (Steam main client updates) + Enable pause / resume for downloads + Enable multi-source(aka content server) downloading + Menu to select which content server to use, amount of bandwidth available, country + Limit file size of logs and errorlogs + Disable logging and errorlogs + History(Servers played on, frags.deaths.statistics) + Detailed logging of bandwidth usage, average DL speed + Fix inaccurate measurement of bandwidth + Fix inconstant downloads, downloads blink in and blink out in Bandwidth Monitor Friends Client + Fix games reappearing multiple times + Add smiles + Add groupings + "X" people online + Send msgs to inform other users why they should add him/her (Current system does not enable others to know who and why one should add someone to his/her friends list) View Server Info + Show server CVARs + Show MOTD + Show anti-cheat options Server Browser + Country filter for server window + Server side filtering and pinging before sending results + Saves serverlist so no refresh is needed (Refresh takes damn long) + Enable third-party server browser support, eg. ASE (Provide documentation on how to add support) + Tree list with filters, like ASE + Customised filter options + Scripting language to find servers with certain CVARs on Required + GCache explorer + Map browser + Skins & Models explorer + Fast logins + Create safe mode + Force downloading of content + Compression support in transfers, eg maps, textures + MP3 player support + Better MOD icons support + Choosing minimum Steam Cache size, ability to increase for updates (No point leaving space for reserved updates) + Start in offline mode + Lite mode(No fancy GUI functions, no Friends list, just games only) + Change of email address + Provide manual downloadable patches and updates (Like the Steam+CS1.6 installer) Start Menu + Start in safe mode + Manual / Readme + Delete all login details (Useful for LAN shops) + Uninstall Steam In game + Media player + Clock & date with timezones + Minimise buttom + User friendly voting functions(Like RTCW:ET) Steam Links + Add server to favorites + Add contact to Friends automatically onclicked Eg of Steam link: steam://|friend?friend@domain.com| Note: This list will be updated. Contains bugs+requests quote:Its not a bug, its a feature' WHERE post_id = 89152 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Master_America Selecting gateways (US East/West, etc) doesn\'t seem to display all the servers actually available. Altogether, the summation of all the gateways\' servers would be about 300 servers, when altogether (with World selected) there are 4500+. This could be because Steam doesn\'t know which country each server is in, but I\'m not sure. The location of the server is an operator-set cvar. Valve, in their server documentation, recommends initally setting this to "World"; thus, said servers are only going to show up under world. (Do the US East/West servers show up on the World list?) Anyways, at some point in the future the World setting, at least server-side, will disappear so the region-based stuff should be correct then.' WHERE post_id = 89161 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'quick suggestion', post_text = 'At the moment, the only way to install new items (Greyed out) is to double click on it. Probably be easier if you had an install menu option when you right-click on it.' WHERE post_id = 89166 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'DoD key doesn\'t work', post_text = 'OK, my girlfriend is hooked on CS now ever since she started playing it after watching me play it all the time. Steam beta was coming to an end, Valve states that any half-life based product CD key will unlock all the content once final Steam comes out. OK, sounds like a deal and a half, I guess I\'ll go hunt down a Half-Life product so that she can continue playing with me once Steam final is out. Only thing I can find is DoD, but, hey, they said any Half-Life based product. So that should be fine, sure hope so, nobody\'s got anything but DoD on the shelves. Well, Steam final is out, and I install it on my machine, plug in my Half-Life key as I\'m adding CS to my \'games.\' Good to go. Install Steam final on her machine, try adding CS, plug in the key, and INVALID. Lovely. Maybe I typed it wrong, try again. Nope. Try again, nope. Try again with CAPS LOCK in case it\'s that dumb. Nope. Invalid. OK, try adding DoD. WTF, that works. And nothing else will let me add it with that key. OK, so now I just wasted good money on DoD retail that will never get played, ever? Or is this a problem that will be fixed shortly?' WHERE post_id = 89178 AND is_historical = 1;
