UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by randomthoughts Ok...heres my situation: I go to fileshack download the steamengine for CS then go to open it.... It locks up... I delete it through DOS(cause viewing the folder in windows with it in it locks it up) So I say...ok I\'ll try it upstairs and bring it down here I download through a dif mirror just in case it was a case of bad-file-itus..... Mirror: half-life2files.com I bring it downstairs and plug the damn CD and voila......it freezes...so I say screw this and come here for help.... *end story* now HELP ME! MY COMP INFO: OS: WIN ME Processor: P4 Harddrive left: 14 gigabytes RAM: 128mb RDRAM I know its not an error with any part of my hardrive....all clusters have been checked and are good........ HELP ME! if the install is locking up without any errors then i would suggest disabling/shutting down all background apps (antivirus, utils, etc) and trying to install again. also you might as well try dl\'ing the ricochet version of the steam install like i suggested just to see if that will help.' WHERE post_id = 107146 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Changing Fonts in CS1.6 + STEAM', post_text = '******* Check at the end of this post for new Tutorial ******** ******* Check the Second Post to get the Fonts + Updated Optimal TrackerScheme File!******** Check the screenshot to see how you can probably change the fonts and sizes to the maximum in CS 1.6 It\'s really easy. You can use -ANY- font that you have in your fonts foler (usually c:\\windows\\fonts) and I\'ve tested it with a lot of resolution, it works great. First, you\'ll need to use the GRAY skin in Steam. So load it in your steam and close steam totally. Now go to x:\\steam\\skins\\gray\\resource Open the TrackerScheme.res file with Notepad There will be a lot of text with comments (comments = preceeding with //) So you\'ll get your way around it. Go down to //////////////////////// FONTS ///////////////////////////// (you can change all the other colors like menu color and stuff like that if you want and are capable) Now you\'ll see a bunch of configs like "Default" { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "12" "weight" "0" } } "DefaultUnderline" { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "12" "weight" "0" "underline" "1" } } "DefaultSmall" { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "12" "weight" "0" } } "DefaultVerySmall" { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "12" "weight" "0" } } "MenuLarge" and so on. I tried out many font sizes and configurations and here\'s what\'s the best: Set all the fonts that are originally ranging from 8 to 14 to 12 Set all the fonts that are originally ranging over 14 to 14. So a font size 8 would become 12, and 18 would become 14. This has the nicest and cleanest impact on your steam console, the CS console and everything else. It might seem a bit smaller in the consoles but who cares, you can still see very clearly. **The screenshot is an example of one of my tries where fonts under 14 were set as 10 and fonts over 10 were set as 12. A bit too small, but it looks really nicer** The only fonts that rest unchanged are the fonts in the Game Scores. (while pressing TAB) Also, If you wonder what font I used, it\'s Square 721 BT. It really fits Counter-Strike (and it\'s easily findable) Enjoy! Update: If you don\'t want to use the gray skin (I just use it to keep the original font sizes) you can always use the x:\\steam\\resource\\Trackerscheme.res which will edit the fonts for the default steam skin. *** New Font Changing Tutorial *** So I\'ve made a few researches on the different font categories in the TrackerScheme.res configs... Here\'s what I have for you guys. First, Let\'s open the Tracker file in the gray skin folder: X:\\Steam\\Skins\\Gray\\Resource\\TrackerScheme.res You will see a bunch of text and configs you can change (I\'ll talk about those later on) Scroll down until you see something like /////////FONTS///////// I\'ve added NEW comments to the configs so read them! NOTE: The font i primarly use is SQUARE 721 BT //////////////////////// FONTS ///////////////////////////// // // describes all the fonts Fonts { // fonts are used in order that they are listed // fonts listed later in the order will only be used if they fulfill a range not already filled // if a font fails to load then the subsequent fonts will replace "Default" // This is the default font used in all Steam consoles/windows { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "antialias" "1" } } "DefaultUnderline" // Same thing as above, but underlined { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "underline" "1" "antialias" "1" } } "DefaultSmall" // Default font formatting... (Just Ignore this if you don\'t want to change steam, but only CS1.6) { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "antialias" "1" } } "DefaultVerySmall" // Yet again ignore this if you don\'t wanna change STEAM { "1" { "name" "Tahoma" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "antialias" "1" } } "MenuLarge" // Same as above { "1" { "name" "Verdana" "tall" "16" "weight" "1000" "antialias" "1" } "2" { "name" "Arial" "tall" "16" "weight" "800" "antialias" "1" } } // this is the symbol font "Marlett" // This determines what font will be used in the minimize/maximize/close buttons in STEAM { "1" { "name" "Marlett" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "symbol" "1" } } "EngineFont" // You guessed it, This is the font that is used in all Steam Games (That\'s where we start editing for CS1.6 fonts) { "1" // 1= 640*480 and LOWER resolutions. I already edited the variables so you can alter them in your file. These are the best values I\'ve tried. { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "12" "weight" "0" "yres" "480 599" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "2" // Change this section if you are playing in 800*600 mode (again, the following variables have been changing for better ones) { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "13" "weight" "0" "yres" "600 767" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "3" // 1024*786 Fonts { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "14" "weight" "0" "yres" "768 1023" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "4" // 1280*1024 (most popular) Fonts { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "18" "weight" "0" "yres" "1024 1199" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "5" // Anything over 1600*1200 Fonts goes here. { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "20" "weight" "0" "yres" "1200 6000" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "6" // My screen can\'t handle over 1600, but I think these are for the Higher Resolutions like 1900*X . The following numbers *should* be looking good on your resolution. { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "22" "weight" "600" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } "7" // Same thing as above but probably for 2200*X + Resolutions. { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "24" "weight" "800" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } } "CreditsFont" // This doesn\'t seem to appear anywhere in the CS Engine. { "1" { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "16" "weight" "600" "antialias" "1" } "2" // Same as above { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "16" "weight" "600" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } } "Legacy_CreditsFont" // Added to accomodate 3rd party server plugins, etc. This version should not scale. This is where you fix your fontsizes if things like AMX or Adminmod show HUGE fonts. The following fontsizes are optimal. { "1" { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "16" "weight" "700" "antialias" "1" "yres" "1 10000" } "2" { "name" "Square 721 BT" "tall" "16" "weight" "600" "dropshadow" "1" "antialias" "1" } } } // ******************************* Now Let\'s see how we can modify other Steam Appearance Values! Right above the ////////FONTS/////////// Line, there should be an interesting section looking like this (I added comments again) InGameDesktop // InGameDesktop is the screen with the 2 CS dudes and the menus on each sides + the Steam Windows { "MenuColor"// The Normal Menu Text Color "200 200 200 255" "ArmedMenuColor"// This is like a onmouseover color. The color that the menu text takes when the user puts his mouse over it (like highlighting) "255 255 255 255" "DepressedMenuColor"// Same thing as above but this is the color that appears after the user has clicked on a menu text "192 186 80 255" "WidescreenBarColor" // This is a fun thing to play with, If you have widescreen enabled, you can change the color of the big black stripes here with RGB colors, the Last number is the visibility so set it to 255 if you put any color except black "0 0 0 0" "MenuItemVisibilityRate" "0.03" // time it takes for one menu item to appear No need to alter anything after this. if you do, all your menus will be weird. hehe "MenuItemHeight" "28" "GameMenuInset" "32" } *************** There is still a LOT we can change but that\'s what I\'m giving you so far! Happy editin! ******* Check the Second Post to get the Fonts + Updated Optimal TrackerScheme File!********\n\n[]Attachment: cs_assault0005.jpg (attachment.php?s=7dd387096c4c6493e71f414dd726e321&postid=90074) This has been downloaded 4052 time(s).' WHERE post_id = 90074 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Update: For resolutions 1280+ use the following: Fonts originally under 14 = 14 Fonts originally over 14 = 16 With Fonts like Terbuchet MS, Arial, Verdana. ** Square 721 BT Download here ** (VERY GOOD FONT FOR CS!!! (IMO)) *** Download the updated TrackerScheme.res File here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&postid=93023#post93023)' WHERE post_id = 90476 AND is_historical = 1;
