UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'HERE IS THE SOLUTION to the invaild steam ticket problem!!!!', post_text = 'I know the solution to your problem..!!!! If you move your dedicaded server to the computer connected directly to the Internet. That should do the trick. Then you should be able to connect whith your SteamClient from the computer in the network to the computer with the dedicaded server witch is directly connected to the Internet. EX.1 This should work... it did for me Computer 1 with the dedicated Server connected directly to the Internet. IP 192.168.0.1(LAN) and IP 213.113.28.42(Internet) Computer 2 with the SteamClient IP:192.168.0.2(LAN) Computer X with another SteamClient IP:192.168.0.X(LAN) and so on Computer 1 is sharing Internet to the LAN. This setup makes everybody able to connect even me :-) ---------------------------- That is what I did and it should work for you to. I have tried it before and it worked. But now I don\'t have it like i descibed above because I have my SuperComputer(2.8Ghz,512Ram,128MbATI Connected directly to the Internet and my dedicaded server in the Lan on a Basic Computer(1.1Ghz) And I dont want to change my setup like in examle 1 Because i want it to work like this: ---------------------- EX.2 Computer 1 with the SteamClient connected directly to the Internet. IP 192.168.0.1(LAN) and IP 213.113.28.42(Internet) Computer 2 with the Dedicated server IP:192.168.0.2(LAN) Computer X with another SteamClient (this client probably have no problem) IP:192.168.0.X(LAN) and so on Computer 1 is sharing Internet to the LAN. Everybody else is able to connect to my server trough the internet, while I get the annoying message Invalid Steam.... -------------------------- I have tried several portmapping solutions with EX.2 but nu luck... So I still have a problem. And if someone know any other solution to make it work with EX.2 I would really apreciate it. BTW I have: winXP where I have my SteamClient (internet sharing) I have: winxp on the dedicaded server (DOS installed) I have tried to forward ports: UDP 1200 UDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive TCP 27030 to 27039 to both the server and the client, but im not really shure what all the ports are used for. Maybe I did it wrong to. And also: 5273 TCP is for validating Steam client IDs, and 27012 UDP is for security modules (CS-only right now). I think somehow the ports are being blocked somhow, but i don\'t know how to solve it. ----------------------------- On 1.5 dedicaded server you just forwarded port like this: UDP 27010: Outgoing connectivity to this port on remote destinations. Used for advertising a server on the master lists for server browsers. UDP 27011: Communicating with the BanList Server from YOUR Server Was formerly 27013 - much in/out traffic too UDP 27015: Incoming connectivity to this port (or whatever port the server had been changed to, if not the default). Used for all client/server game traffic (including voice), server info requests, etc. -------------------------------- So for now if you want to connect to your own dedicated Server you should place it on the computer connected directly to the Intenet. (EX.1) It doesn\'t work to have the server inside a network and connect to it from the computer connected directly to the Internet.(EX.2) I really hope that someone know how to fix the EX.2 problem. Maybe som advanced portmapping. I dont have a ROUTER!! I use servises on my connection. (settings|networkconnections|my shared internetconnection|Advanced|settings|services|add service) to portmapp. Thank\'s in advance and good luck to you who wanna try EX.1 !!! lantz69 aka [Hlm]Valve' WHERE post_id = 95935 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'What fixed it for me was simply by joining my Internet server via LAN, instead of throught the external IP via Favorites...' WHERE post_id = 97617 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by tadmaz What fixed it for me was simply by joining my Internet server via LAN, instead of throught the external IP via Favorites... Well, that works for you maybe, because you have your dedicated server connected directly to the Internet. Correct me if im wrong about that. To CLERIFY some things: 1. This aint that invalid steam ticket id, that all you have to do is to log out and then back in. 2. This is\'nt the one, that you connect into your lan server either. I am saying that this one is to STEAM dedicated server host-ers that cannot connect into their own servers. Probably bacause they have it setup Like the EX.2 like I desribed in my BIG Post. BTW thanks for your reply tadmaz !!! Hope someone has an answer like these ex below: If you configure your ports like this bla bla bla then you solve your problem. OR It\'s just not possible right now because............ We really need a definite answer, so we can sleep well at night ;-) Game on lantz69 aka [Hlm]Valve' WHERE post_id = 97860 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for clearing things up a bit Lantz, but it doesnt really solve the problem - it\'s sort of a tweak to get around the fact that there is something strange with Steam. I used the same setup with my old 1.5 server, and it worked just fine. My server is connected to the internet via my other computer, as in example 2. I don\'t want to reconfigure my network, or buy a router just for this. I don\'t want to be dependent on my server machine to get on the internet, it\'s a crappier computer, and I dont want to have it turned on constantly - just when i use it as server. Since i am using xp shared internet connection I need the computer that\'s connected directly to the internet to be ON for the other computer to get out on the internet, and I simply dont want that to be my old machine, sitting there humming when it doesnt need to. There must be a solution to this. Is any Valve staff actually reading these forums? It would be nice to get some feedback to our problems. Like - "we are working on it, just wait.." or "Nope, we won\'t fix that - go buy a router, or go play The Sims"' WHERE post_id = 100831 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'we have the same problem Inkyape', post_text = 'Inkyape!!! Thanks for the response Your desciption of the problem is the same as mine as I wrote in my first post. From my first post: I have my SuperComputer(2.8Ghz,512Ram,128MbATI Connected directly to the Internet and my dedicaded server in the Lan on a Basic Computer(1.1Ghz) And I dont want to change my setup like in examle 1 -------- So maybe you see now that I totaly agree with you. I also don\'t want to have my dedicated server on all the time making all that noice. I also used the same setup with my old 1.5 server, and it worked just fine. So why should\'t Steam do the same I wonder. But I know for a fact that EX.1 works just fine. I hope Steam fixes the problem soon so we can connect our dedicated server. Or maybe post all the portsettings and and what they do. for exampl port xxxx is for validating steam user ID. That\'s all for me..\n\n__________________ Game on!! Don\'t give up. Regards [Hlm]Valve' WHERE post_id = 102050 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'There\'s something else causing the problem. If it\'s a port sharing problem it has to do with something not sharing ports or finding new ones. I\'m trying to run the client/server on the same machine and I get the invalid ticket error every time I try to log into my server. Seeing as how my computer is connected directly to the internet there shouldn\'t be any problems with this. The server was set to use port 27016 so it wouldn\'t conflict with the client just like I\'ve done in 1.5 before. If I remember correctly I was even able to log into someone else\'s server while leaving my server running and it ran just fine. I can\'t double check now because I have another error I\'m trying to figure out how to get past. Everything ran fine(except for not being able to play on my server) for a day or two but now I get some error about the local steam service not running if I just start up steam and attempt to play CS. I can\'t play any game using steam atm.' WHERE post_id = 103703 AND is_historical = 1;
