UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Router and TCP/IP Help', post_text = 'Hey guys alot of you have been asking about this so i pulled this from the FAQ if you\'re trying to use a router or connect to steam, these are the tcp/ip settings you\'ll need. Remember these are pulled from the faq so here goes! (When it says lan party that means using a router for anything so keep that in mind) How can I have a LAN party or similar event using Steam? Any Steam game, when played on a LAN or otherwise, requires that each individual client be able to authenticate via the Internet. At a LAN party, this means that Internet access must be available to every machine on which Steam games are being played. If desireable, the network administrator of such an event can limit internet access to only the TCP/IP ports which Steam needs. These are: UDP 1200 UDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive TCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive At large events, it will be necessary for each attendee to let their games fully update before attending to avoid taxing the shared internet connection with too much content delivery. I\'ve got Steam installed - why can\'t I connect? If you get an error message saying that Steam cannot connect properly, please check your ports. Steam requires that your firewall have the following ports open: UDP 1200 UDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive TCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive For information about how to control your networking device to open those ports, check the documentation that came with your device or the manufacturer\'s web site.' WHERE post_id = 96456 AND is_historical = 1;
