UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'ing Rules', post_text = 'Since the recent onslaught of spam here are some rules to follow. 1) Any thread flaming another person or organization gets closed on spot. 2) Any Swearing in the topic gets closed on spot. 3) No "bumping" of threads because you can. There\'s is enough spam already 4) No one is going to sympathize with the "Steam/VAVLe sucks". This happened in _every past release_. The exact same thing happens. People complain, and then they get over it. Steam isn\'t going away, so complaints/flames aren\'t going to help your cause. 5) Please use common sense. If you wouldn\'t say it to you parents in common conversation, it\'s not appropriate here. Ritchey~\n\n__________________ #Steam on GamesNET http://forums.counter-strike.net http://csnation.counter-strike.net http://server.counter-strike.net' WHERE post_id = 96590 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'If anyone posts a thread with a non-constructive rant, expect it to be deleted. We\'ve given a lot of leeway in this respect lately, because we understand the large amount of frustration due to the rocky release. Noone is more frustrated by it than us. But in order to maintain some semblance of order and usability here, posts are going to be monitored a little more strictly. If you want your criticism to be heard, post it in a constructive manner. Contrary to what some people believe, we do take feedback from here into account, and well-thought-out and constructive feedback is seen by the entire Steam team, whether it\'s negative or positive. (Also note, posting threads complaining about people who complain won\'t fix the problem. [] That just creates more animosity.) update: It shouldn\'t need to be said, but here it is anyway: Please do not post: - leaked emails, in part or in whole - images from leaked HL2 builds - links to any leaked content' WHERE post_id = 97410 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Listen Up People!!! Server Issues!!!', post_text = 'Okay people listen up, I\'ve been running around this tech board for the past 45 minutes coming accross the same postings over and over again. I\'m puttting this post up because this should address most of your connection and account issues: Account verification First off yes, the verification server is down. I don\'t know for how long it is down it happens like this randomly. The servers right now are very overloaded in case you all haven\'t noticed they just released a new steam (The 700 mb one with all the cache files) and it is fnarking with their bandwith. So what does this mean for you guys? It means: you cannot login if you\'re not already You cannot change passwords You cannot set up new accounts Most of the steam is unplayable Also be adivsed that creating multiple accounts from the same installations can result in your cd key being blocked and having to go through steam technical support which is like waiting for Duke Nukem forever to come out...meaning its gonna take a while.... Games This is another souce of strife so here goes The general consensus I\'m getting is that most of the people (inclduing me) have had numerous problems with the 500k steam installer, the one that converts all of your old installations to the steam cache. So what should you do? AVOID THIS DAMN INSTALLER! THIS HAS BEEN POSTED ON STEAM\'S NEWS AND OTHER CS WEBSITES! Use any of the installers with the cache files preloaded and you should be able to avoid alot of headaches. I repeat, they have released a steam installer with 700 mb of cache files which covers all the games: hl, cs, OpFor, tfc, dod, ricochet, and dedicated server. Any other hl mod you\'ll have to convert at your own risk. there is no general reliablity anywhere for any of the other games right now beyond those which i have mentioned. WON There also seems to be a major confusion regarding won out there. Like it has been mentioned in steam news, WON will not be shut down until steam is fully operating AND operating smoothly. That means your old installations will still work if you can find servers for them. Valve is not going to monkeyshaft us anymore than they have to so just so you know. The general timetable for the WON shutdown has not been established but from what I\'ve been hearing it should be within a month. Technical issues I\'ve already posted a lot of stuff regarding tech stuff in previous posts, heres the links for First: TCP/IP issues, and teh Second: For sound and Graphics Issues /forums/...&threadid=14229 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=14229) Graphics and Sound Issues: /forums/...&threadid=12366 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=12366) Okay guys? Just take this one day at a time. Yes Valve and Steam have messed up CS and whatnot but it will be ironed out just give em some time and they will get it fixed ok? Happy CS\'ing!' WHERE post_id = 96703 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for the post. Hopefully this will reduce the numerous topics being posted about login/registration issues regarding the current problem.' WHERE post_id = 96742 AND is_historical = 1;
