UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I helped someone on another forum earlier today that had a very similiar problem. His error finally was tracked back to a port forwarding issue. Granted, his problem was not identical to yours but it might be worth the time to look into you Internet connection a little closer. What exactly are you running?\n\n__________________ Do you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some. "Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM Stupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is. Add some chlorine to the gene pool... -Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-' WHERE post_id = 121157 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well i did some more searching and found this... Home > Error Messages > "NET_SendPacket ERROR: WSAEINTR" This error may be caused by the following things: 1.) Bad Winsock dll 2.) Bad TCP/IP stack 3.) Conflicting Ports 4.) Firewall 5.) VIA KT133A motherboard chipset w/o proper 4-in-1 patch 6.) Windows 2k w/o service pack 2 7.) Punkbuster conflict 8.) Wrong vCache settings Also, this MS Knowledge Base Article may solve this issue. Possible solutions: 1. Bad Winsock dll: Contact Microsoft Technical Support for step-by-step instructions on how to reinstall Winsock for your operating system. 2. Bad TCP/IP stack: Remove all TCP/IP instances from Network Properties. Go to Control Panel >> Add/Remove Programs >> Windows Setup and remove all of the Communications components. Restart then repeat the same procedure, but instead check the box and install the components. Next readd the TCP/IP protocol in your network properties. 3. Conflicting Ports: Try adding this to the end of your command line: +clientport 27055 4. Firewall: Disable your firewall. If you run BlackICE setup an allow set for ports 27005 thru 27030. If you have Windows XP disable the internal firewall, or if you use ICS disable that. 5. VIA KT133A motherboard chipset w/o proper 4-in-1 patch: Visit www.via.com (http://www.via.com) and get the latest 4-in-1 patch. 6. Windows 2k w/o service pack 2 Read the following Microsoft Knowledge Base article here. 7. Punkbuster conflict: Disable the PunkBuster client on your machine and try non-PunkBuster servers. 8. Wrong vCache settings To fix this problem you need to go to the system.ini file and check the [vcache]. If there is nothing there, add these lines under the word [vcache]: MinFileCache=**** MaxFileCache=**** It should look like this. [vcache] MinFileCache=**** MaxFileCache=**** Replace **** with one of the following values: If you have from 16-32 MB of RAM: MinFileCache=2048 MaxFileCache=2048 If you have from 32-96 MB of RAM: MinFileCache=4096 MaxFileCache=4096 If you have 128 MB of RAM or more: MinFileCache=8192 MaxFileCache=8192 Another way would be setting the maximum amount of RAM HL/CS is allowed to use. Right click on your CS shortcut and select "Properties". Right now the Target line should read something like this: CS retail version: C:\\Sierra\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.exe -console CS mod version: C:\\Sierra\\Half-Life\\hl.exe -game cstrike -console Change it to this: CS retail version: C:\\Sierra\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.exe -console -heapsize ***** CS mod version: C:\\Sierra\\Half-Life\\hl.exe -game cstrike -console -heapsize ***** Replace ***** with 75% of your total memory in KB, ex. you have 128 MB RAM then heapsize should be 98304. 1 MB = 1024 KB. If a steam representative would please read this and reply that would be just neat!' WHERE post_id = 121221 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well, I doubt you\'ll get a Valve rep answering this post but my bet is on #4 (or a related issue). Specifically, do you have a router? It might also help to include your exact system specs including motherboard and Internet connection/related hardware.\n\n__________________ Do you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some. "Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM Stupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is. Add some chlorine to the gene pool... -Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-' WHERE post_id = 121267 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I had the same problem when I used to play on a dial-up. The problem only occured in WinXP for whatever reason. I read somewhere that it has something to do with noise in the line. I know, it\'s a pretty strange theory. Anyway, I had to switch back to Win2k to fix the problem. If your on a dialup, try yelling into your phone while connected; and then go back to your computer to see if you get the error. Good luck.' WHERE post_id = 121283 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I tried running CS 1.6 without my firewall and without my antivirus running to see if that was the problem, and I still got the same net_sendpacketerror:WSAEINTR I have checked just about every forum, with just about no fixes. I tried the uninstall QoS Scheduler, and that didn\'t work. I\'m not on 56k, and I\'m not using a router. This problem has only just recently happened to me (within the last 3 days) And this error only seems to come up when im doing good in CS. I\'m a little wary of trying what I listed earlier because I uninstalled the QoS scheduler in order to fix this problem, and it didnt, so I basiclly uninstalled QoS scheduler for nothing, and I dont want to mess up anything more especially with some of the stuff that I listed. Could someone with some real expertise please help.' WHERE post_id = 121386 AND is_historical = 1;
