UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'You forgot the most important thing about Steam though. . .', post_text = 'It\'s the devil incarnate (in software of course) because we all know how Gabe Newell is actually a huge demon-incarnate. However, being the more subtle, conniving, and cunning 2nd-hand-to-Satan, he decreed all of his naive lackeys at Steam to create the devil incarnate (in software of course) so it can SWALLOW YOUR SOUL!!!!! Now you all know the *****REAL***** reason it\'s called Steam. We all know that it\'s too hot in a demon\'s abode for water to exist in liquid form, but they still need to drink water like us. So in a metaphoric way, Steam is turning all of us into a more digestible format for Gabe\'s insatiable appetite for young, naive souls. I, for one, welcome my new demon master Gabe. *ALL HAIL GREAT MASTER GABE!*' WHERE post_id = 123221 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Three things EVERYONE should know about Steam.', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by UndeadScottsman Dispite this being old news, I keep seeing these coming up repeatedly and felt the need to reiterate that they are false or have been changed. 1. You will NOT need to be online to use Singleplayer or LAN Despite the multiple erroneous listings in the FAQ, Valve has stated that eventually they will have it so you do NOT need to be online to use singleplayer or lan. WILL SOMEBODY PLEASE EXPLAIN THIS THEN???? /faq.htm#technical2 (/faq.htm#technical2) Do I have to be connected to the Internet when I play Steam games? The short answer is yes. All Steam-enabled games require you to be connected to the Internet in order to play. Note: some Steam-enabled single-player games (such as Half-Life 2) purchased at a retail store will allow offline play until the user decides to play online or enable other Steam functionality. From that point on, an Internet connection will be required. top ...and... /faq.htm#technical8 (/faq.htm#technical8) How can I have a LAN party or similar event using Steam? Any Steam game, when played on a LAN or otherwise, requires that each individual client be able to authenticate via the Internet. At a LAN party, this means that Internet access must be available to every machine on which Steam games are being played. If desireable, the network administrator of such an event can limit internet access to only the TCP/IP ports which Steam needs. These are: UDP 1200 UDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive TCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive At large events, it will be necessary for each attendee to let their games fully update before attending to avoid taxing the shared internet connection with too much content delivery. (those are the FAQ entries in question) If they are wrong, WHY HAVEN\'T THEY BEEN CHANGED? Huh???' WHERE post_id = 123288 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Note his use of the word "eventually", as in "not right now, but in a few weeks". This means that you cannot plan on LAN without a net connection "right now", but you will "eventually" be able to. Erik and others at Valve has repeatedly stated this, and I really wish people would read the FAQ AND news more carefully []' WHERE post_id = 123304 AND is_historical = 1;
