UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'First off - I know you asked us to post specs if we are having issues, but I thought I would post mine as well in case it helps. I\'m not having issues. It\'s important to know the difference (For anyone who may post to this thread) between network lag, causing choppiness and video/CPU lag causing FPS to drop. So be sure to report the actual FPS, and not just that it\'s just choppy. (To see the FPS, pull up the console in game and type net_graph 3. To turn it off, type net_graph 0 in console) My specs: CPU Intel Celeron 1.8Ghz RAM 512MB PC2100 DDR RAM VIDEO CARD MSI GeForce 4 TI4200 64MB WINDOWS VERSION Windows XP Home - Updated with latest downloads from windowsupdate DIRECT X 9.0 VIDEO DRIVERS Not sure of the version offhand. Downloaded the latest one 2 days ago from NVIDIA VIDEO METHOD OpenGL GAME RESOLUTION Desktop at 1024*768, game looks like it is running in 800*600 ever since steam started - haven\'t tried increasing GAME COLOR DEPTH Whatever steam set it to, unchanged since updating to steam V-SYNC Whatever is default ADDITIONAL FEATURES None INTERNET CONNECTION High speed DSL (130k/s downstream and 13k/s upstream max) MOTHER BOARD ASUS P4B533-VM (I\'m using the on board sound) FPS Constant 60FPS, even in smoke (I have not made the change that allows it to go above 60FPS) Firebreak P.S. My game does get choppy from time to time, but when this happens I notice my ping has jumped up. My FPS is still high and everything is smooth except other players jump around the screen like they are teleporting. (Common symptom of network lag) I have noticed that pings seem to be a bit higher since 1.6, but nothing too major.' WHERE post_id = 132053 AND is_historical = 1;
