UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'will Valve publically address security concerns from hl2 code leak?', post_text = 'With the recent hl2 code leak, I\'m concerned about HL2 and what steps valve will take to ensure proper security of the gaming experience and of everyone\'s future purchase. In particular, I\'m hoping that Valve will make a public statement that will satisfy the community that proper measures have been taken. What I\'m most concerned about: - That the cd-key is never transmitted to a privately run game server in a form that can be reversed to get the original cd-key--what I\'m thinking about here is, now that the code is out, it would be simple for someone to break their algorithm and get the key. What would be better is either to transmit part of the key that can be verified without the rest, or to transmit a hash. If the full key is ever sent directly to the game server, cheat and hacker groups will just open key-collector servers so they can gather thousands of cd-key\'s and then proceed to cheat and do other things with impunity. - That Steam hasn\'t been compromised by this leak, and thus will be able to authenticate hl2 clients to ensure that people are not using customized cheat versions, and also that the steam system hasn\'t had enough code exposed to enable a hacker to hijack it to install malware on thousands of peoples\' PC\'s. - That the servers which handle billing for Steam are not directly connected to the Valve dev. network in a way in which "trusted" PC\'s that could potentially be compromised in the future can access them with lower security restrictions. I really don\'t want to buy myg0t and friends a brand new video card with my credit card info. If you\'re concerned about issues like this, and want Valve to address these issues publically or at least give us some reasonable assurance, please add your comments.' WHERE post_id = 153562 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well put, I also think Valve need to be open about the situation. If there are things that are compromised beyond repair, don\'t be quiet about hoping the hackers won\'t figure it out... Just let the community know and we\'d be happy to wait for the game while you recode.\n\n__________________ *Help! the paranoids are stalkling me!*' WHERE post_id = 153567 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Just some rumors: Now get this, several team members from Valve broke the lockdown and have made a few comments (no identification, they wished to remain anonymous, but they are confirmed to be legit Valve employees). Most distressing is this... they said that Valve is looking at a minimum of SIX lawsuits, possibily more depending on the total damage. And that there have also been talk WITHIN Valve of scrapping the entire game. They also claimed that an estimated 1.32GB of data was transferred off Valve\'s computers, which matches the 1.32GB beta reported to be stolen. The latest development is this... starting yesterday several simple, custom-made maps were released that allowed people to walk around in a small room using the HL2 engine. Today, the people have dug up and activated the MULTIPLAYER code... and IT WORKS. The latest rumour is this... the full beta will be released on the internet at midnight tonight, but there has been no confirmation of this. According to a number of inside-sources, things may get a lot worst, and the worst-case scenario is the cancellation of Half-Life 2 (a probability) and the shutting down of Valve (less likely but still possible at this point due to the lawsuits). So yeah i would also want to hear what valve has to say, instead of all of these probably fake rumors.' WHERE post_id = 153571 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: will Valve publically address security concerns from hl2 code leak?', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Barbarian With the recent hl2 code leak, I\'m concerned about HL2 and what steps valve will take to ensure proper security of the gaming experience and of everyone\'s future purchase. In particular, I\'m hoping that Valve will make a public statement that will satisfy the community that proper measures have been taken. What I\'m most concerned about : - That the cd-key is never transmitted to a privately run game server in a form that can be reversed to get the original cd-key--what I\'m thinking about here is, now that the code is out, it would be simple for someone to break their algorithm and get the key. What would be better is either to transmit part of the key that can be verified without the rest, or to transmit a hash. If the full key is ever sent directly to the game server, cheat and hacker groups will just open key-collector servers so they can gather thousands of cd-key\'s and then proceed to cheat and do other things with impunity. - That Steam hasn\'t been compromised by this leak, and thus will be able to authenticate hl2 clients to ensure that people are not using customized cheat versions, and also that the steam system hasn\'t had enough code exposed to enable a hacker to hijack it to install malware on thousands of peoples\' PC\'s. - That the servers which handle billing for Steam are not directly connected to the Valve dev. network in a way in which "trusted" PC\'s that could potentially be compromised in the future can access them with lower security restrictions. I really don\'t want to buy myg0t and friends a brand new video card with my credit card info. If you\'re concerned about issues like this, and want Valve to address these issues publically or at least give us some reasonable assurance, please add your comments. Key is transmitted as a hash. Next point its called VAC source was included Last one I can\'t comment on I ain\'t at valve.' WHERE post_id = 153575 AND is_historical = 1;
