UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Most commonly reported bugs Even if a bug has a fix, it is STILL a reported bug, and VALVe will hopefully eventually remove it from the program. But just use the fix for now. Cannot find any servers, despite not having any filter settings. Fix: /forums/show...;threadid=24394 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=24394) \'Unbind all\' symptoms when dead (keyboard and mouse buttons don\'t work). Cause: Having the spectator menu open when you \'spawn\' on the next round. Fix: Either close the spectator menu before you spawn, or type \'spec_menu 0\' in console if it occurs. Typing \'+duck\' and then \'-duck\' also works, but is slower. Left handed models on return from alt tab. Fix: Type cl_righthand 1 in console. Mouse cursor visible on return from alt tab. Fix: Open and close the in-game GUI (escape, or console). Cannot see the speech tab for people using in-game voice com. This usually occurs when holding the scoreboard open. Fix: None known. FPS issues, lag and netsync issues, interp and various other tweaks. Fix: None known. Players submerged in ground or running in sky. Cause: None known. It\'s noticed that it appears to be at either the highest elevation possible, or the lowest elevation possible, on the map, and only seems to happen on certain maps (I\'ve seen it on dust/dust2, but not elsewhere so much.) Note also that the player doesn\'t see this for himself, and the hitboxes will still work, it\'s just the model goes flying or sinking. Apparently, only YOU see this: they themselves, or anyone else do not see the same person doing this at the same time, except by coincidence(?). This even works when you spectate that person from first person perspective, the viewpoint is too high or too low. Fix: None known. However, should the player in question change elevation from what he\'s currently on (go up/down a ramp, or jump), it\'s been known to fix itself. Note: If someone can find a way to repeat this bug, and the steps taken to cause it, I\'m sure it would be most helpful to VALVe. Game Not Available and/or No Children Registered. Cause: Clicking Cancel on the \'Preparing to play Counter-Strike...\' window. (Or end-tasking the program at this point.) Fix: Shut down the computer, making sure the shut down is successful. The power should be off at this point (a restart or reboot does not work). Then turn the computer back on, try again, and this time, just be patient. (If the three periods are moving, the program has NOT locked up.) Please, if your bug is in this list (which I will keep updated as per the posts in this thread), PLEASE do not post it again. I will also post fixes as well, if somebody mentions them in this thread. If you are posting an uncommon bug, or a bug with an error message attached, then PLEASE post your SYSTEM SPECS as well. Operating System Processor, MHz, RAM Bandwidth Graphics Card, and amount of video RAM Graphics display type (Software, OGL, D3d), Resolution, and 32 bit or 16 bit' WHERE post_id = 155943 AND is_historical = 1;
