UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Comrade Cruz Yes, it has it\'s own cdkey, but it is the same format as hl and cs, so there is no way to tell if it is a blueshift key or not. If they were nice about it, they could do it like this: Supply one CD key, and get the Platinum Pack, supply a second one, and get Blue Shift. This would be really nice to loyal customers who bought Half-Life and CS retail (either out of stupidity or kindness) and have 2 keys as a result, get a bonus Blue Shift. I\'m already stoked that I have the Platinum Pack thanks to Steam, I only ever bought Half-Life: Game of the Year edition, and now they have essentially thrown me Opposing Force for free. I\'m going to wait until Blue Shift is avaliable on Steam, and then, depending on what\'s easiest, I\'ll get it. (wether it be retail or through Steam) I know the story is really short, I just want the High-Definition Pack.' WHERE post_id = 168096 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', post_text = 'I have been dealing with Steam for awhile now, & have a major concern about their Log In system that seems to be bound to your CS key. At first, it was a little annoying, but then I heard it could be used to set all your personal controls simply by creating your own login name may have made it worth it. BUT: Then I notice it asks for you CD key. This is where the problem comes in. If you for example let your friend make an account with steam, & pull out you CD key when it asks you, you in effect are giving your buddy your CD for free. So now, when your friend goes home to play counterstrike & gets all logged in as he normally would, he is now playing on YOUR CD Key. Meaning you would not be able to play until he is finished & logs out. Still: Don\'t forget that steam set it up to auto load at windows startup as well as auto log you in, so your friend may actually have your CD key used up for quite some time. I did go back and look for info of steam telling us of this issue, but so NO info warning us when creating accounts. Thanks for the bonus Steam []' WHERE post_id = 174850 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'OK, this one is easy: - don\'t give people your CD key - if you do, ask them not to create a Steam account with it. - if they do, ask them to hand that account over to you (change the password to something boring, then you log in and change it to your own). It will have the "wrong" email address as the account name, but that doesn\'t really matter.' WHERE post_id = 174862 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', post_text = 'I hear you, but that�s kind of weak. Why should you be afraid of entering your OWN CD Key on your OWN Computer? Steam has no warning letting you know that the Key goes with the login name. Something, ANYTHING to let us know what the account will carry with it. I have played CS from the very first beta, and never have we had this issue. We have had to enter in our CD key with every beta & non-beta so far. I thought it was natural when I let a friend play CS v1.6 on my computer before I did. Then I created me an account and played. Never did I realize what had just happened. It\'s not like I gave my Key to someone else on purpose. It\'s my computer. I didn\'t see the problem. Still: Steam took no time to let us know what it was doing with the key or accounts. Thanks for the bonus Steam!' WHERE post_id = 174881 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Sorry, I didn\'t realized he\'d created the account on your computer. Did you create your account first? if so, then you\'ll "own" that cd-key, and eventually his subscription will get canceled.' WHERE post_id = 174890 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'If you already had an account on your computer then went to your friends house there is no reason for cd key. After install you just log in instead of creating an account. If he already had steam you could just log in too.' WHERE post_id = 174897 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', post_text = 'I thought I covered that... I let him play first. Thats why it seemed so normal to enter in my CD key on my computer when it asked for it. Steam took no measures to let us know of the changes they made to our game. I repeat, Steam said NOTHING about it. To make things worse, I have 20 Half-Life CD\'s for my home Lan set-up. Now I have NO idea what CD Keys I let out by mistake, vs what ones I caught before letting friends create their own account. Your new login system has put me in a real bad situation.' WHERE post_id = 174899 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'American Zombie Reply', post_text = '{ If you already had an account on your computer then went to your friends house there is no reason for CD key. After install you just log in instead of creating an account. If he already had steam you could just log in too. } Well I�m glad someone is happy with Steam. In my area, you would be rare. That is not how it worked on my computers. Plus: How long does it take to log out of your steam so someone else can login on your computer? Yikes.... Then you ad "game not available msg" after logging in. You find yourself repeating the same thing again... Usually ending up reinstalling before your done.' WHERE post_id = 174912 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Lol, everything i hear gets worse', post_text = 'Yeah theres a point thats probably more worrying. About 500,000 folk using KEY GENERATORS, thats gonna be crazy. If i cant get playing cause some ****wits using my number i\'ll be ****ing at STEAM\'S door with my CD box to attack the development team. I hate this software so much, wont even install in my comp after 4 downloads at about 1.72GB (3* 340 MB + 700 MB) and when u goto the SUPPORT PAGE you find ****e like "IS STEAM REALLY FREE?" and "WILL I STILL BE ABLE TO BUY VALVE GAMES IN-STORE?" ****ing no real help to anyone. Only people keeping this software afloat are the folk in the forums helping each other figure out this pish. Hopefully they\'ll fix this KEY issue but i wont hold my breathe, better off with monkeys on roller blades designing the software. Azraels_Fury........' WHERE post_id = 175149 AND is_historical = 1;
