UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by jet jaguar Maybe Valve shouldn\'t have moved Steam from beta status so quickly. Not that it would stop the whining but still... I\'m not familiar with the time usually taken to take a program out of beta stages. But Steam was in fact in beta for at least 8 months... But yes a lot of the programming has gotten tweak in the wrong direction quite often... Btw something like this (sort of) happened in the beta stages. They released a patch for steam client, hours later a new one popped up, and it was because it had \'raped\' itself in the process. But nothing as major as deleting files....' WHERE post_id = 180807 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Go back to WON? Id love to*, but they want to take it away from us and replace it with this ridiculous Steam thing. Why cant they leave well enough alone? Sure, I dont mind CS updates, update us to 1.6, and so on, but leave Steam out of it. Won seemed like a much more efficent system than steam, requiring much fewer resources to operate. Steam is just so bloated and expensive with having to support those content servers. Its mind boggling that a sane person would want to make Steam. Are we paying for it? No. Good. But what kind of argument is that anyway? How bout this, with about the same footing as that argument I could say Steam should be paying us for all the agravation and time lost due to its many shortcomings, most especially server ops. We should have big checks coming our way. * Actually I have gone back to WON. I closed my CS 1.6 server and only run 1.5 servers now. I wish it would stay.' WHERE post_id = 180844 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Ludwig van Go back to WON? Id love to*, but they want to take it away from us and replace it with this ridiculous Steam thing. Why cant they leave well enough alone? Sure, I dont mind CS updates, update us to 1.6, and so on, but leave Steam out of it. Won seemed like a much more efficent system than steam, requiring much fewer resources to operate. Steam is just so bloated and expensive with having to support those content servers. Its mind boggling that a sane person would want to make Steam. Are we paying for it? No. Good. But what kind of argument is that anyway? How bout this, with about the same footing as that argument I could say Steam should be paying us for all the agravation and time lost due to its many shortcomings, most especially server ops. We should have big checks coming our way. * Actually I have gone back to WON. I closed my CS 1.6 server and only run 1.5 servers now. I wish it would stay. When WON is removed, steam will be as efficient (or more) than WON was. That\'s the entire goal. Duh.' WHERE post_id = 180878 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = '::INFO:: New Update Patch ::INFO::', post_text = 'Ok for all of you out there... If you installed the patch, remove steam, as it will screw up CS when you put the reverse patch on. Then reinstall steam and get the updates, this will save you HOURS of downloading. Now you can stop complaining [] Then it will only take about 10 minutes to download... also, check out the status, most servers are bogged down atm. /status.html (/status.html) Its not that bad, really... quit flaming.' WHERE post_id = 180742 AND is_historical = 1;
