UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'no news updates? well not on the DoD site, but if you look around you can find some info http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php...amp;news_id=245 (http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php?page=common/news.php&news_action=showitem&news_id=245) http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php...amp;news_id=254 (http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php?page=common/news.php&news_action=showitem&news_id=254) I think it\'s coming out after the huge CZ load is over on Steam.-\n\n__________________ FLeK0 www.Counter-Strike.hu' WHERE post_id = 185313 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'What\'s wrong with 1.0 anyway? Retail DoD is an above average WW2 shooter at best. When 1.1 comes out we will hear the usual "this release killed DoD" like with every new version. Mark my words. Learn to be patient and respect the devs.' WHERE post_id = 185319 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Interacting with the community is a rather time consuming (and ever so often an ungrateful) job. I\'m very happy that they rather keep working on improving their products and stomping bugs than making a daily Q&A session with the fans. I\'m not saying that I don\'t understand the frustration this situation causes in some of us, I\'m just saying that I\'m trying to understand Valve\'s point of view as well. I am very sure that they are working their asses off to get things done as soon as possible and that they are as unhappy about setbacks and delays as much as we are (if not even moreso).' WHERE post_id = 185320 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I think half the problem is that the DOD team themselves don\'t even know when it\'s coming out. Every time Steam seems to stabilise, a new patch comes out that de-stabilises it. Steams a great concept, just needs a bit more beta testing to get it right. I\'ve decided to just go play other games for the time being, and come back when Steam is stable and 1.1 has been released. I\'m only an occasional gamer anyway, so I can live with it. quote:Originally posted by Kiff Guys, don\'t take his bait. I made the mistake of doing it. Ignore him. I bit over on the DOD forums a while ago as well. The guys just a confrontational muppet with nothing better to do than be abusive to anyone and everyone about anything. Perhaps he should take his own advice and get out a bit more. Oops, bit again [] Thank god for the ignore feature on these forums, only time I see his posts is if someone quotes him []' WHERE post_id = 185340 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Funka J What\'s wrong with 1.0 anyway? Retail DoD is an above average WW2 shooter at best. When 1.1 comes out we will hear the usual "this release killed DoD" like with every new version. Mark my words. Learn to be patient and respect the devs. There are loads of major bugs in 1.0 that should have to been fixed ages ago. The most annoying to me is the hitbox problems. I guess you can\'t have played Dod much if you haven\'t seen the many bugs in the game. As for being patient I\'m willing to be patient if I knew why I was waiting. As far as I can understand from the dod website 1.1 has been finished months, and therefore there is no reason to delay it any longer. All Valve have to do is give the Dod community a statement regarding the status of 1.1 and when its going to be released, and then the majority of ppl complaing about where 1.1 is, would sit and patiently wait for it. Its a simple thing that would take them less than 5 seconds, and keep many ppl happy. At least then I wouldn\'t feel Valve are just ignoring Dod' WHERE post_id = 185348 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Fleko, if U notice the latest news U linked is from 10.10. it\'s 2 weeks since "very soon" Waldo statement. He was supposed to have a meeting after that statement with Valve t omake them release the patch at once. No info from him since then. lack of info in front of "very soon" release of the patch is confusing. Since 1.0 changed the way dod was before (in a good direction if U ask me) the game occured unbalanced. Kar is overpowered, garand to weak and MGs lost any functionality, since walls became to difficult to penetrate. Add the screwed up hitboxes and U will find out why the patch is needed so bad. For several months for now.' WHERE post_id = 185349 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Day of Defeat 1.1 - A plea to Valve', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Kiff We were informed by development team members back in August that the patch was finished but needed testing from Activision. A mid September release date looked promising. It was not to be. The problem is, with the recent stolen source issue activision has been locked out for testing[]' WHERE post_id = 185353 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Re: Day of Defeat 1.1 - A plea to Valve', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Intrepid00 The problem is, with the recent stolen source issue activision has been locked out for testing[] Yep [] Unfortunately this was part of the reason it was delayed. But since the hacker attack Steam updates to CS and TFC have been released. So clearly Valve are confident that the network is secure.' WHERE post_id = 185369 AND is_historical = 1;
