UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No ppl will accept something thats true. most ppl have u on ignore cos ur an annoying little bugger. quote:OOh dear they won\'t release 1.1!!!!!!!!! VALVE SCREWED UP!!!! DISGRACE!!!! CALL THE POLICE!!!!!! Theres an example of u not exactly acting as mature as u reckon u r.\n\n__________________ Piro: when did Tsubasa get a cable modem? Largo: Sometime this morning. You should proberly tell him about it PH33R MegaTokyo. It ownz j0o f00lz' WHERE post_id = 185425 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No maturity necessary for a thread which slags off the Valve team for not releasing DoD before breakfast. Oh and why is it that I have to prove to you that if a person isn\'t acting mature 24 hours a day, they are immature? I honestly don\'t give a flying flippidy-flop what anonymous posters think of me, much less ones such as yourself.' WHERE post_id = 185453 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here\'s what I\'m confident on as of yesterday: 1) Base 1.1 testing is done and final code work implemented. 2) 1.1 will be a small release...dll\'s and some player models. 3) Reworked maps will come later. 4) There\'s at least one new map (dod_switch) but I\'m not sure if it\'s in the 1.1 release itself...it might be part of the post-release map-release period stated in 3 above. 5) Release is imminent except for the following unknowns: A) If the aborted Steam release is required B) If a new HL.exe is required. If either of those two are required then all bets are off A big caution: Although DoD 1.1 changes things I caution you not to think this is as radical a change as we\'ve had in the past...a lot of the changes (other than the VGUI) are invisible for the most part and do not surface until you\'ve played for a while. You\'ll eventually notice the player models "move" a bit differently now that 9-way animation has been implemented and you\'ll obviously see more deaths in the game now w/the hitbox, MG, wall penetration, and Kar movement-accuracy changes. I look at a lot of these changes to be more tweeks than bug-fixes. The majority of the actual "bug-fixes" will come when the re-worked maps are released. And I have not heard of any great fps increase other than the fix to the rain...I do not know what Valve-proper is working on w/respect to figuring out why the mask-technology models (grass, tanks, etc) cause fps drops. Since the plan of a few days ago (could have changed since then for all I know) was not to include any maps yet I think a lot of folks will say "What\'s the big deal?" when it\'s released...the hard-core DoD guys will notice things but newer players might not notice that much beyond the interface and the MG cook-off sequence. This is truly a evolutionary release...not revolutionary.' WHERE post_id = 185478 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'m with you, Kiff.\n\n__________________ Proud Member of The [Idioteam] DoD squad. Feel free to embrace the Brown Side of DoD, Join [Idioteam]' WHERE post_id = 185483 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'If Steam asks for your CD-KEY again', post_text = 'The Steam system has begun filtering through accounts that used duplicate cd-keys to subscribe to the games. When it finds a duplicate, it unsubscribes but does not delete that account. Only the first account which used a given cd-key will remain subscribed. If you are using one of the duplicate accounts, you\'ll see the games get moved to Available Games in the Games window, and Steam will ask you for your cd-key again if you try to play one. If you created multiple Steam accounts using the same key, then you\'ll need to use the first one. repeat: the first account to use a given cd-key will REMAIN subscribed and can be used to play the games. The system will not automatically delete any accounts.' WHERE post_id = 186055 AND is_historical = 1;
