UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = ':( almost good idea!!', post_text = 'Man i got so excited when i read this post.... Makes so much sense that that would fix the problem. I Copied my atioglxx.dll (9800 pro) and pasted it into my drvmap folder, change the text file.... and even changed the 3dfx files name and backed everything up of course. Joined Cs and same bs. 70 fps when im looking at people. i can stare out the wall and max fps, but wtf does this do for me. Anyways... curious cause i read the other posts i check that 3dfx.dll and sure enough it was back in my folder along with the original i changed its name. Someone was using their head when they came up wit this solution... but it is code somewhere that steam is going to load that 3dfx.dll... ALSO it didnt change the ati driver text from the .txt file i edited... strange. Also I know people say shut off ati_npatch, and ati_subdiv.... which i have and does nothing for me... but can anyone tell me what these 2 commands do???????? I miss playing CS like i used to.... feels so choppy now. Makes me wanna play my smooth ass playing HALO or Max Payne2. You would think cs is the new game with the high tech graphics. This is SUCH a big issue for cs players I so shocked VALVE hasnt addressed the problem, let alone FIX IT. I know they were robbed but a customers loyalty is only as good as the service. We arent gonna keep being [atient and supportive of you guy if you dont give us answers... or a response, yes we know its there... we will try to fix it. OR SOMETHING. Back to the subject... this fix would be sweet if we could figure out how to implement it without it changing.......... update us!!' WHERE post_id = 190970 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'ati_npatch "0" and ati_subdiv "0" disables TRUFORM(tm) on ATI based video cards. TRUFORM is ATI\'s method of adding more polygons to an object for more realism. D< O >A, as for your fps problem on your Radeon 9800 Pro, you can try disabling V-SYNC in your Display Properties > Settings > Advanced > 3D Tab > Open GL > Use custom settings > Click on Custom. (This is only for ATI Catalyst 3.9 drivers) On the near bottom of the window you\'ll see "Wait for Vertical Sync", move the slider all the way to the left until it says Always Off. Next load up Counter-Strike 1.6, go into console (~ key) and type down: fps_max "101" developer "1" fps_max "101" raises your FPS, and developer "1" uncaps the 100FPS barrier in Counter-Strike.' WHERE post_id = 190982 AND is_historical = 1;
