UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'OK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file. Just in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out.' WHERE post_id = 192107 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by bigj22 OK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file. Just in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out. I did edit the txt file. I told it to load the fax admin driver. Still ran fine. No errors. And yes I\'m running OpenGL.' WHERE post_id = 192114 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by bigj22 OK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file. Just in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out. The point it is would only make a difference if (a) you were stupid enough to select 3DFX mini-driver in the first place and (b) you didn\'t know how to go back to the default driver from the drop-down list or via the registry. I think the current fps problem is purely due to the increasing complexity of these games and the number of times functions such as glVertex3f are wrapped both in the game engine and in the driver DLL. Older games like Half-Life call OpenGL functions for every single vertex they want to render (Half-Life even partially-transforms all the vertices itself with no acceleration) which causes massive CPU dependence and is a lot slower than using vertex buffers or display lists like newer games use.' WHERE post_id = 192118 AND is_historical = 1;
