UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Heh, sorry dude, buts that an lousy and unusable solution. Cant force all the clients to change their settings, that would\'nt work. The problem is within the server, and should therefore be solved within the servers settings etc. So... where is the moderators and steam staff in this forum ?! :/' WHERE post_id = 213487 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox Heh, sorry dude, buts that an lousy and unusable solution. Cant force all the clients to change their settings, that would\'nt work. The problem is within the server, and should therefore be solved within the servers settings etc. So... where is the moderators and steam staff in this forum ?! :/ How exactly is that a lousy and unusable solution? Did you even try it? How the hell do you expect a moderator to waiste his time helping you if you won\'t listen to common sense suggestions? Its simple. In your console, type \'cl_timeout\' and see what number it gives you, then increase the number. And there are thousands of reasons why you might need to set this high. 90% of those reasons have to deal with either your comp or your ISP, neither of which any server running CS is responsible for. Try a suggestion before you shoot it down next time... /EDIT: BTW, no global set of configuration settings for any game is ever going to work for every computer and every player. Every single person who has ever played CS has changed some client side setting...even if it is just their player nickname.\n\n__________________ The Hit List - Revised: *e-bitchslaps steamuser *e-bitchslaps matpatnik *e-bitchslaps trimp *e-bitchslaps Politics *e-bitchslaps Sapiens *e-bitchslaps ErrorClone Proud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.' WHERE post_id = 213491 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'It seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8! The problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures. And the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/ And, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings.' WHERE post_id = 213496 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox It seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8! The problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures. And the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/ And, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings. Every client? You sure? You asked every single Steam user? If all the player on your servers are suffering from this, then I would think you would want to try every possible solution. And the fact that it works with under 10 players only suggests I am right. And if I\'m not right then so be it. But I am telling you how I solved my problem. And this has helped others solve the same problem. Bottom line, don\'t post about a problem if you don\'t want help. And if you do want help, don\'t be so quick to jump on someone\'s back. Even if their suggestion doesn\'t work, it might lead you to the solution.\n\n__________________ The Hit List - Revised: *e-bitchslaps steamuser *e-bitchslaps matpatnik *e-bitchslaps trimp *e-bitchslaps Politics *e-bitchslaps Sapiens *e-bitchslaps ErrorClone Proud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.' WHERE post_id = 213505 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox It seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8! The problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures. And the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/ And, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings. Very, very wrong. The reason you have to do it in 1.6 is because in 1.6 it has defaulted to a lower value than you may have needed in 1.5. cl_timeout works in the following way; the value you give it is the maximum amount of time that CS (client-side) will wait inbetween map changes for new information (about the map, other players, etc). If your cl_timeout value is LOWER THAN YOUR AVERAGE LATENCY to that server, you will be d/ced because CS will stop waiting. So up it to a ping spike value (say 175-200). This applies when you already have the map next in the server rotation. When you do NOT have the map; it can take 2-3x as long to get new information (I don\'t know why, but it is so). So if you\'re going to play on servers that have map rotations that you don\'t have... Take your ping and double/triple it and that should be your cl_timeout rate.\n\n__________________ SYSTEM SPECS __________________ OS: MS Windows XP Pro SP1 HDs: 120 GB (NTFS) & 40 GB (FAT32) CPU: Intel Pentium 4 @ 2.53 GHz GPU: GeForce4 Ti 4600 128 MB (45.23 Drivers) PRAM: 1 GB DDRAM VMEM: 3.4 GB Connection: Comcast Cable (600/80 Kbps) Settings: -OpenGL w/VSync, AA, AF and TS Off -1280x1024 resolution -32-bit color Proud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol. 66.208.104.166:27015 - KDB pub 69.56.171.228:27015 - S_c_T pub 208.184.33.208:27015 - team.cH pub' WHERE post_id = 213525 AND is_historical = 1;
