UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I cant understand why Anti Aliasing and anisotropic filtering doesnt work with the original ATI Catalyst but with the regeneration modified drivers it works fine. On the other side - the Counterstrike background picture is a set of some bitmaps. When i m setting the video mode to D3D i can see the border lines from every bitmap, but under openGL the border lines are not visible. Using the regeneration drivers make the border lines visible in openGL mode but AA and AF works fine. Also the textures are a little bit more coarse-grained as with the original drivers from ATI. Interesting is that AA and AF works in D3D with the ATI drivers but set them to 6xAA and 16xAF forces the fps to drop down to 60 or more. With the regeneration driver and the same AA and AF settings under opengl the fps drops not so often down and not so far down. Any explanation ?!' WHERE post_id = 509055 AND is_historical = 1;
