UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Bug Finding Help', post_text = 'There are a couple of bugs that we\'re having a bit of trouble tracking down. It would be extremely helpful if someone in the community could help out. The bugs are: - Players starting the map either stuck in the floor or floating above ground. - Slow demo recording performance. - Crash on demo playback, possibly related to +showscores. If you\'d like to help, record a demo that exhibits one or all of these behaviors and mail it to me at erik@valvesoftware.com (mailto:erik@valvesoftware.com). Thanks. Erik' WHERE post_id = 261926 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Hello Erik, Not sure if this will help you or not, but MiSmith7 has found a temporary solution that seems to help. It involves a demo fix written by Martino@valvesoftware.com (mailto:Martino@valvesoftware.com) that was dated a little over a year ago. This was a fix for 1.5 demos that updated the GameEditor.dll and GameUI.dll in the valve\\cl_dlls folder, and the core.dll in the Counter Strike folder. It was a "viewdemo" fix, or something like that. The thread on how to watch demos without them crashing can be found here. (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=40705) So far, following these steps at least allows us to watch demos without crashing, and also displays the scoreboard correctly. (since the introduction of 1.6 they\'ve been blank, so this should be a step in the right direction, at least) I\'ll test and see if demos work launched straight from console, but I think they still crash unless you start a listenserver on the map the demo was recorded on. But I figured maybe you could revisit these .dll\'s and figure out a way to combine them into 1.6 and maybe find the solution you\'re looking for.' WHERE post_id = 262086 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Also, as for the players floating in the air... someone in the bug list thread suggested this is caused by custom decals being downloaded to the client. This makes perfect sense because generally the only time it happens is during the pistol round on a map change (when most decals are downloaded, obviously). And I would bet money the random times it happens during a round is when a new player has just connected, and his decal is being uploaded. So far, the only testing of this theory I can provide is I have had cl_allowdownload "0" cl_download_ingame "0" cl_allowupload "0" set for about a week now, and haven\'t had it happen at all. So that\'s at least one area to look into for a fix.' WHERE post_id = 262112 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Ok, scratch that first post. On a whim I decided to delete the DemoEditor.dll and GameUI.dll, and replaced the core.dll with the default one. These have nothing to do with the fix. Simply starting a listenserver on the map the demo was recorded on is what allows the scoreboard to display properly and doesn\'t crash the demo, either. So those .dll\'s had nothing to do with the demos working right. -edit- also tried launching demo straight from console via splash screen...and it crashed on first scoreboard viewing. starting a listenserver on the map the demo was made on is the key to them not crashing. so i hope that helps figure out why...' WHERE post_id = 262158 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'radar not always on even when drawradar "1" in console d3d not working and look at my specs i use opengl fine but i like d3d to!' WHERE post_id = 262324 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'dude, read the friggin\' topic and the first post. this isn\'t a bug list thread. it\'s a thread for people to help narrow down the 3 bugs that are listed. not to post new ones...or rather...very old ones. use the bug report thread.' WHERE post_id = 262607 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Indeed, turns out the viewdemo fix has nothing to do with the problem. The demos crashing is directly related to the +showscores command. There are currently 2 methods of fixing this, hex-edit out all the +showscores and replace them with -showscores, or this: 1) Load up CS from the \'Games\' window of STEAM. 2) Click on "New Server" (listen server) and load up the map the demo you are trying to view was recorded on. 3) Wait for the server to load, then go into spectator mode. 4) Bring up the console, and view the demo using the "viewdemo" command. Not only does this prevent the crash - it actually shows what the scores were.' WHERE post_id = 262755 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Erik, your mail server is not being nice!', post_text = 'Erik, I just emailed you three times, trying to send you a link to a demo. Your mail server wont accept attachments. Your email keeps bouncing back undeliverable, even without the demo. PM me and I\'ll give you my contact information, or anything else I can help with! And the link to this demo is http://216.240.145.190/~viper/ocs12.zip (http://216.240.145.190/~viper/ocs12.zip) The beginning of the demo shows a player on the back deck of the militia house, when in fact, he is under the stairway, not on the deck. As I toggled between players and back to him, he was under the stairs where he should have been. The beginning of the next round shows the +scoreboard crash as soon as I enter the tunnel from CT spawn. Thanks' WHERE post_id = 262792 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Erik Johnson, I have reported about the floating/sinking player model issue many times before. I am almost certain it is because of this: Whenever I see a player(s) shoot up in the air or sink in the ground, I check my console. There will be a message that says: "Requesting pldecal.wad file from the server" Every time this message appears in the console, floating/sinking player models appear. EVERY TIME. I have verified this throughly and many others on the same server, other servers, my friends and people on these forums have verified it before. This doesn\'t just happen on pistol rounds/map starts. It happens anytime the server requests a pldecal.wad file. The server requesting pldecal.wads from players is the cause of this issue. I hope this helps.' WHERE post_id = 263951 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '^^ At first I was skeptical of that, but I validated it the other night.' WHERE post_id = 265554 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Yes, I am so certain that the server requesting pldecal.wad\'s is the cause of this issue, that is why I didn\'t provide any screenshots or demos (which I can easily do). If anybody thinks I am incorrect or if you are skeptical, see for yourself. Next time you see your teammate shoot up into the sky, bring down your console. I am 100% sure there will be a message saying "Requesting pldecal.wad from server".' WHERE post_id = 266975 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here is a little additional information. Last night during a 2x3 match in HLDM everything was fine until the match ended and we changed maps. During the first minute or so, one client out of the five of us saw one other player floating in midair. The player was moving around, then suddenly fell down and was normal again. During this time, the HLTV proxy was recording the entire thing, but when I went back and viewed the recording, there was nothing wrong and all players were on the ground running around like normal. This tells me that the player position data the server was sending out was good all the time, and the problem is a client related one only. The only client that saw the problem was also the client that was closest to the server, actually on a LAN so there was no internet connection issues at all. The rest of us were on Internet.' WHERE post_id = 267697 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Erik... any news? This thread is getting buried! Bump!!!! If you need any more demo samples, please let us know!' WHERE post_id = 278028 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'just wondering if it\'s possible to separate the pldecal wad request into it\'s own cvar. so instead of turning off allowing all downloads we could simply turn off decal downloading. like cl_decaldownload "0" or something. i know a large percentage of people could care less about seeing others decals, but would still be able to get maps and sounds, etc from the server. this would at least eliminate this bug.' WHERE post_id = 278153 AND is_historical = 1;
