UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'pretty bad bug', post_text = 'I\'ve been getting a pretty bad bug when running tfc. i don\'t have enough of cs or the other mods downloaded to run them yet, so i\'m not sure if it will be present in them (i\'m expecting it to affect all mods, since it\'s video card related). The problem has something to do with AGP support for my video card. Before i disabled AGP using dxdiag, at the moment when tfc would start using my video card, hl.exe would get a page fault error, and either freeze my display on the menu (if tfc was started by shortcut), or simply dump me back into my desktop (if it was started through the connect option in steam). When i got it to dump me back into my desktop, since the in-game video settings were set to a lower resolution, it changed my desktop video settings to that resolution. I then tried to reset the resolution, and my rundll32.exe crashed (so i was screwed). Now that i have disabled AGP, i can get into a tfc game ONLY by using the connect option in steam. If i try to open up the game from a shortcut, it has the same error as before, where hl.exe crashes in the background, and i\'m left with a frozen display until i reboot. Hopefully, since this is a major bug, valve will try to find a fix for this as soon as possible. for FULL details, including my system specs, see my main thread in the Support forum: /forums/...?threadid=42164 (/forums/showthread.php?threadid=42164) note: since my last post there, i have re-installed the new video card driver, and tfc still behaves the same as i have described with AGP disabled. Steam is updated to the most recent version. I still have not tried to see what happens in d3d mode, (which i will do shortly).. all my testing has been done in openGL. Hehe.. i say "testing" because it feels like i\'m a beta tester [] EDIT: Ok, now that the playable part of CS downloaded, i tried loading it up from the steam connect option and the freeze happened right when steam said "Validating game resources". This happened with AGP still disabled. Unless that is the point at which CS begins using the video card, it\'s strange that it happens then, instead of right before you would normally see the server message. NOW I\'M CONFUSED: TFC isn\'t acting like it did before. First it crashed when i had AGP enabled, whenever i re-enabled it, it always crashed.. and i mean ALWAYS. Anyways, my display was all messed up the other day, so i turned AGP on again. Later in the day, i attempted to play tfc, and it worked... with AGP on! What is going on here.. something is messed up about this. Also, i\'ve experienced a brand new problem (besides the connection lost on map change) After being kicked by tfc because of a connection problem, hl.exe crashed (it seems to love doing that) and then steam crashed, giving me this: Program D:\\PROGRAM FILES\\STEAM\\STEAM.EXE File: \\p4clients\\rel_beta\\Projects\\Common\\Misc\\Win32Stru cturedExceptions.cpp Line: 261 pStructuredExceptionPointers->ExceptionRecord->NumberParameters==2 (Press Retry to debug the application - JIT debugging must be enabled) When i click on Retry, it says: Runtime Error! Program: D:\\PROGRAM FILES\\STEAM\\STEAM.EXE This application has requested the Runtime to terminate it in an unusual way. Please contact the application\'s support team for more information. So here i am... trying to contact the support team [] How many bugs will i stumble into? Wanna start taking bets? [] rofl!' WHERE post_id = 268141 AND is_historical = 1;
