UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Let me just say....w00t!! I\'ve been experiancing all the problems that you guys have. Delete steam.exe and all that junk. Well I think I found a way to fix. When I tried updating, it would keep giving me error messages after 26%. So I went into my steam directory and found that Steam had made two new files. SteamTMP and Steam_new Or something on the lines of that. What I did, was delete the old steam.exe and the steamtmp, and renamed the stean_new to steam_new01. Thus the steamnew file being the only .exe in the folder. Oh the steamnew file\'s size is 1.03mb I think, and the older one was 956kb or something close to that. After that, I tried updating with only the steam_new01 in the folder....I only got a cannot connect to network... -_- so that this morning I went into the folder, and got the idea to do the same thing I did last night, but after deleting all the other .exe files, I renamed the new .exe that was 1.03 mb, to steam.exe (same name as old one) It started to update. *i held my breath* and then once it got to 26%....it stopped, dissapeared, and then came back up again, but only to be at 29%...at that point I was overjoyed. I don\'t know why the steam.exe files are all getting screwed up, but this seems to work. I hope this has helped you guys, please post telling me what you get.' WHERE post_id = 275156 AND is_historical = 1;
