UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'The Monitor', post_text = 'OK, I asked this when the steam forums first started up, "What is the monitor for?, and if it is only a monitor for network usage, isn\'t it just going to use unneeeded bandwidth usage. "Does it cause any us to store any extra junk on our pcs?. I dont really need to know the network usage to tell me if I want to play, do I?. Yes, your right, I don\'t have a clue what it is for and would appreciate if someone could explain the need for the monitor. Thanks' WHERE post_id = 276990 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'The monitor portion of the Steam interface only functions when content is being downloaded to your client, and at that only content associated with Steam or the MOD you play that is an update. When it is displaying information, it doesn\'t take any additional resources, only displays what is going on, and nothing additional (for the monitor that is) is stored on your computer. The display of the Monitor certainly does not take any bandwidth away from your gameplay itself, although the content or update being sent to you certainly does use incoming bandwith mostly and a very small amount of outgoing bandwidth. The graph you see just displays when and how much information is being sent to your computer as well as what MOD the content is for. The limit rate and button are there so you can eventually control how fast you want to get content. On dsl or cablemodem you would probably not want to limit it at all, on dial-up modem you might want to set it to a smaller value while you are playing only. The "need" for this monitor is so you know Steam and/or MODs are being updated in the background, otherwise how would you know?\n\n__________________ Would you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?' WHERE post_id = 277388 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Quicksilver', post_text = 'Thanks for the info, i appreciate it.' WHERE post_id = 277513 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'If you get a crash after restarting/relogging into Steam!!!', post_text = 'If after the latest update, you get an error looking something like this... steam.exe (main exception): Win32 StructuredException at 0163048B: Attempt to write to virtual address 2439276314 without appropriate access rights. STEAM.EXE - APPLICATION ERROR The instruction at "0x1000ecd" referenced memory at "0x016470c0." The memory could not be "read." [edited by Greg; see note below] This is a known issue with the Steam developers, and I am sure they will be working on a fix to push out soon. In the mean time, an apology for this error :^(' WHERE post_id = 278375 AND is_historical = 1;
