UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'m with you guys all the way. I\'ve been helping out in #steam ever since this thing started out. People have NO idea what\'s going on with Steam software and we have NO idea how to fix any of these problems. I mean, a dedicated support department isn\'t necessary, but if you\'re going to let your "fan base" support your software, why don\'t you COMMUNICATE WITH THEM? I think you have serious issues with this rendition of customer support and, honestly, if this company is going to keep half of it\'s customers, communication and support of your customers is needed. You have an official #steam channel on gamesnet and your developers stopped showing up after 2 weeks. I stopped supporting people there about a month and a half ago just because of that. We\'re not going to support you if you\'re not going to support us. It seems to be a one-way street at this point. I honestly don\'t know about another company that does things like that. I mean, sure, sierra did your support in the past and we\'re fully aware of that, but now that you\'re making your own software products and throwing sierra out of the loop on cs 1.6, you need to make up for your lack of a support department. The way to do that is NOT to let your fanbase try to support itself. People are starting to wish WAN will stay online.\n\n__________________ JBDubbs has spoken. The CS Revolution has begun: http://www.csrev.com' WHERE post_id = 284574 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'I Agree', post_text = 'I Agree... Not Only Are We Not Getting Support In #Steam... But Even Some Of The Support We Get Does NOT Support Us... I\'ve Been Down From CS Since The New Update... Now It Cannot Connect To Steam... I\'ve Tried Every Possible Solution And Nothing Works... I\'d Like To Say Good Game Steam, I Loved Ya, Now I Could Care Less... STRIKE!!!!!!!!' WHERE post_id = 284598 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I really think this is tragic. I\'ve worked actual tech support jobs, and i found a greater reward than being paid, or recognized at my job, was being appreciated by the individual i helped, not the person i was working for. Even though i am not part of steamskinners they have made me an op in their channel because i am almost always availible and able to help people with skinning steam. I get no perks from steam skinners, though they could easily make me an admin on their site, etc. I don\'t do it to get recognized though, i do it because i enjoy helping people, and possibly because i have too much free time on my hands. But it feels rewarding to me just to help people. I\'m sorry that you all don\'t find helping people enough reward in itself, but maybe you could attempt to offer to more people the chance to help so that there are more helpers availible. With chanserv on gamesnet, if you add some one as just an op, it\'s not like they\'re going to break anything in the channel. I come from EFNet, where hostility towards adding people as ops is well needed, but on gamesnet theres no need for this. Maybe there\'s other wacky people like me who actually do like to help, why not let them try being an op in #steam and allowing them to help others with their problems? the couple weeks that i was an op in #steam i tried to help as many people as i was able to. mostly what i ended up doing if i wasn\'t already familiar with the problem was searching and directing them to threads on these forums of the issues they were having, most of the time i was able to solve the peoples\' problems, if not i directed them to try to seek help on the forums for their particular problem, because possibly it was a bug that was not yet addressed, and should be known about by the software makers. Any bug/fix that there is, is usually addressed already in the forum some where. All the time i see people from valve posting on these forum, with possible fixes to known bugs. That is why this is the Steam Support / Help section. That i know of, they have not asked you to set up a support channel for them on IRC.\n\n__________________ i like stuff.' WHERE post_id = 284647 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Your Mistaken', post_text = 'Sorry bro, You totally misunderstood... We Want Steam to join with us to help the cause... Sometimes we don\'t know the answers, and when we ask steam they could give a s**t less! ThAt\'s why I\'m on strike... I\'m not doing it to be recognized... Read More, Smoke Crack Less, kthx bai' WHERE post_id = 284651 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'kthx bro, i\'m not a bro myself, i happen to be a girl. The times i\'ve had "major" problems with steam, or just a simple question that i couldn\'t resolve on the forums, i emailed valve and got a responce within the same day. I\'m sorry you\'ve not experianced that. From what the first post i read: "Due to the lack of adequete information(on bugs and fixes) and/or recognition from the good people at VALVE" What i said doesn\'t seem completely out of line as you suggest.\n\n__________________ i like stuff.' WHERE post_id = 284664 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'aww... poor babies. Cry to your mommies. Give the channel up to people who are willing to help, you attention wanting elitest teens are a joke.' WHERE post_id = 284669 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'There never has been any official designation of the #steam channel as an official place to get help. Also there\'s never been any attempt (on either side) to set up official communications. So how about if all of you who are ops in there let me know, and I will attempt to set up some kind of system for you. Either a set of PMs with info, emails, something. This isn\'t something anyone\'s at fault for I think - just that nobody ever asked anyone to set anything up - on either side. It\'s important to note that the #steam channel is not nor ever will be any kind of official channel. It exists, it\'s got some great potential to help, but it\'s not any kind of official support channel. For Valve to try and manage it could be a big headache. Trust me, as owner of #dod for a while, I know all about the ops squabbles, arguments over who\'s voiced and who\'s not, etc. that happen. It\'s a wild wild place that has it\'s ups, but also downs as well.' WHERE post_id = 284680 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by [cDD]Slash aww... poor babies. Cry to your mommies. Give the channel up to people who are willing to help, you attention wanting elitest teens are a joke. Dude do you not get the **** we are saying!? We are saying we need HELP from VALVe because right now we can\'t do **** because we don\'t know anything! its like setting up a computer with out the parts @Waldo: I tried to contact Taylor Sherman and all I got back was "That is not planned to happen". But if you could do that that would be great, thanks\n\n__________________ H4xDaPlanet Member of (unofficial) #Steam Support team. <3 to VALVe Quote from Xah: "Yeah seriously! since when do bullets kill? it\'s ridiculous. If I took a bullet in the head I\'d probably be whining too "Hey that\'s not fair, you killed me!". I mean cmon! Isn\'t CS about realism? I don\'t understand why guns kill people in this game? we should shoot flower petals and throw candy wrappers instead of grenades. .."' WHERE post_id = 284685 AND is_historical = 1;
