UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'This is much bigger than two updates (both of which are actually pretty big as far as clans go), this is us(the gaming community) noticing something wrong, writing a highly informative post about it (thanks shaguar), and valve saying "hey, you have a point".' WHERE post_id = 297355 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'New Gametypes', post_text = 'I hope this happens. It would be a first for Valve in quite some time. What about bringing in some new gameplay styles or scenarios? How about having a Terrorist VIP (Mob Boss or Drug Lord) that the CT\'s have to take out? This would be the easiest to implement and it would counter as_oilrig. What about the Terrorists having to steal some data from multiple locations (2 objectives)? You would have to break your teams into 2 teams with coordinated attacks and defense. You could even do this with the CT\'s and have hostages at 2 locations. Just like having 2 bomb points. What ever happened to the vehicles or at least the moving items? cs_alpin has a gondola, which is pretty fun. Add some more maps with elevators that can be stopped or broken. Bring some excitement back into the game!' WHERE post_id = 297364 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Roger That :P' WHERE post_id = 297368 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'at the risk of going offtopic to reply to SxRxRnR: I agree that this is a first in some time (ignoring the slight change in 1.6beta of reverting to showing DEAD on scoreboard while alive), this is much more like the days of \'the scoped m4 is unfair\', \'p90 is too powerful\', and all of the map complaints. terrorist assasination maps would have to be well made, I\'d rather see es_ brought back. RTCW style stealing two documents would be really interesting to see, as it would be a huge political shift (probably one valve wouldn\'t want to risk making). Think it through for a bit, why would \'Terrorists\' want to steal documents? Maybe its because these are documents proving government action against their country that the govt tried to coverup, thus the debate of Terrorist vs Freedom Fighter begins. And vehicels were removed because they were too buggy in HL1. You duck, you die. You jump, you die. You look at a jeep the wrong way, you die.' WHERE post_id = 297374 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'The Future of Anti-Hack Technology', post_text = 'Writing anti-hack technology & programs that detect foreign objects on a machine is actually a lot like anti-virus, difference being anti-virus companies have a lot more experience at it. I\'d like to see an anti-virus company take interest in this problem. I believe an anti-virus company (jointly or not) could probly produce the most effective anti-hack software/detection ever seen. An anti-virus company could do this jointly with another (gaming) company, produce their own software/standard (like pb) or even integrate definitions into current/public AV software Not only could the anti-hack/anti-virus-like software be built into the gaming client but the definitions could also be passed over to the actual normal/public anti-virus software and/or easily could \'lock\'/remove files/modifications from the user, which it already does anyways when \'viruses\' are detected. (or even auto report to the associated gaming company that a hack has been detected) If you had to uninstall your anti virus completely, previous to putting a hack on your system or using it at all, to get your hack to function, a lot of ppl would think twice. Push come to shove having anti-virus programs auto report a hack could eliminate the possibility of uninstalling the anti-virus to get the hack to function. What if you could only scan your system for viruses if you had the hack completely removed from your system first. Keep in mind every piece of software leaves something behind even after being \'removed\'. Current AV software can already detect viruses that have been previously removed. What if it actually came down to not being able to use any anti-virus software at all if you\'ve ever had a hack on your system. This in combo with an AV company working on some kind of AV/AH integration/detection on the actual gaming client could slow this problem way down. Another issue to bring up is the fact that a lot of Anti-Virus companies already detect \'hacking programs/exploits\' that aren\'t viruses at all, if it was globally/widely accepted that online gaming hacks are considered to be on the same level of threat, then their definitions could be passed around such globally between AV companies. Even on this (lower) level the file(s) would be locked from the user if the AV was running/installed. Whatever anti-virus company makes the move first will surely be bringing in the profits. Lets face it, when it comes to detecting un-wanted software anti-virus companies have been doing it for quite a while, its time to stop trying to make everything from scratch, and team up with people who\'ve been doing this for a very long time. If an anti-virus company got involved in any fashion regardless of how (joint or not) i believe would make quite a difference.' WHERE post_id = 298436 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'lol, actually, a lot of the people who made punkbuster used to work for macafee and symantic. But your idea is very interesting. But AV company\'s would want to charge for there software. It\'ll cost Valve lots for them incorperate it. Valve themselfs can do a very good job of stop lots of hack but the problem is, VAC is never updated. If punkbuster was supported in CS and used instead of VAC, it would be a lot hacker-free. I think punkbuster is one of the best anti-hack programs ever.' WHERE post_id = 298484 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Certainly it would cost money, however i think people (including me) would be willing to pay a cpl extra dollars. Both sides could actually make money off the deal. Picture a nice big AV company stamp on the box the game comes in with something like "anti hack, powered by <x> (anti virus company)" it\'d look & sound good & it\'d work! + the AV company of choice would be able to distro a great free demo of their products with the game.' WHERE post_id = 298491 AND is_historical = 1;
