UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'You don\'t want to be looking for hacks that have already been removed, because then people who have legitimate uses for them (league admins that want to check demos against known hacks, clan leaders that want to test certain cheats so that they know what to look for when recruiting people, that sort of thing) won\'t be able to install them, use them with VAC off, delete them, and continue playing.' WHERE post_id = 298962 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Blaze947 your retarded man And you are pointlessly insulting. Furthermore your inability to spell a simple word like "you\'re" is revealing. Either you are not old enough to have attended school yet or you weren\'t paying attention when you did. I suggest that you take your posting to mummy or teacher to have it checked before you submit it. Otherwise you should try acting your age. BGL: An interesting idea but the exploits are generally particular to each game. To make a product like that commercially viable it would probably need to support more than one game/engine. This would make it considerably more difficult to program and support. It might be viewed as analogous to a single anti-virus program that works on many different operating systems? Of course there are AV programs that support more than one version of Windows, but tens or even hundreds of them might be a little too ambitious. [] Finally, I am not sure that the similarity between the expertises you describe is actually relevant. Writing anti-hack programs requires knowledge of the game and the way it works. Anti-virus technologies focus primarily on the operating system so I am not sure the skills would necessarily be appropriate. Having said that. I would not completely rule your ideas out. It is good to see someone trying to come up with constructive suggestions, instead of fatuous abuse.' WHERE post_id = 298994 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'America\'s Army and RTCW:ET are much less popular than HL/CS. The HL engine is quite simply a bigger target for hackers than AA and RTCW:ET. It\'s like why Windows gets hacked more than Linux. Sure, it might be inherently less secure, but there\'s also a hell of a lot more Windows machines out there than Linux boxes, so it\'s much more worthwhile to find Windows exploits.' WHERE post_id = 299090 AND is_historical = 1;
