UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CES Las Vegas 2004 - Valve\'s reputation hit hard in front of ALL', post_text = 'Microsoft, Apple, ATI, Sennheiser, and another several thousand computer, tech, manufacturing companies across the globe appeared at the annual CES show which showcases each year the new upcoming technologies that will appear for consumers. Keynote speakers Bill Gates, Steve Jobs, among other notable figures speaking there. Guess what? CES was sponsoring the newest International Gaming Tournament in the United States in Las Vegas. CyberXGaming! As you all will soon hear teams from South America, Europe, Asia and across the country arrived to compete in a variety of games. From Quake3, to CoD, to CS, to WC3. As a result of the recent problems with Steam and Valve being unable to get a simple lan only CS up and running. CyberXgaming is the first International Tournament on American soil to cancel outright and send thousands of gamers back to their countries early. Fortunately for all these teams and competitors and their sponsors ( Intel, Ati, AMD, nVidia, Compusa, and others ). Cyberxgaming will be covering all their costs and reimbursing them for airfare, hotel fees, food and other travel expenses. This amounts to a minimum of already 1-200,000 dollars just in reimbursements. Already it is rumored that Valve will be facing a huge lawsuit as a result. - Valve yall should have prepared in advance for this. As I said before Valve should have been keeping in touch with the gaming community and the sponsors and the companies. Too bad.' WHERE post_id = 309381 AND is_historical = 1;
