UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Vac Banned my HLTV?  Why??', post_text = 'I run about 4 CS 1.6 HLDS\'s on a major gaming provider\'s network. I also have FOUR HLTV processes that login to each respective server and record demos 24/7. This is so we can later review a suspected hackers demo if necessary. Today, we noticed our HLTV "bot" was not on one of the servers. When I checked the server console, I saw this on EACH HLTV process: quote: ******************************************** Your connection to this secure server has been rejected. Because of past cheating violations, you have been banned from playing on all secure servers until 2008-12-20 23:44:39. Repeat violators may be permanently banned from all secure servers. For more information, visit: http://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html (http://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html) ******************************************** Now, how can a HLTV possibly be VAC banned?!?!?! What must I do to get it back online? I swear, the server has NOT been tampered with in anyway. What gives? Does an HLTV instance use a steamid? And is it based soley on the "update" user name? Thanks VERY much, Dave PS, Despite all the negative comments about "steam", I like the update "delivery" system and where things have headed. Kudos to developers. Only problem I have had is that the linux binary is a CPU hog and does not support multiple processors AND the update that was issued on a holiday (Thanksgiving). Everything else has been gravy :P' WHERE post_id = 313014 AND is_historical = 1;
