UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'A lot of suggestions (long read, but good read)', post_text = 'ive been testing this since day 1. so i thought i would leave my feedback: 1. Games are defined per account, wouldnt it better to define it per creditcard number? Or make a lost password including your credit card number. To more secure it if he looses his password. 2. The small games you have on your friends list, make a little how-to for every game, and bots. 3. Make us decide if we want steam to start up at windows start. 4. Make the current system better for customizer. have a online database filled with mods, maps, plugins and other they can browse. Like instead of only have Half-Life and Counter-Strike on the list, you would make steam 2.0 compitable with nonpublic mods, where you could just select it from a list and it would begin downloading, the same with the maps, the plugins and etc. It would be like you just press the thing you want, and then its installed, that would help out a lot of users using plugins. In properties of the game you would also set the properties of your downloaded plugins, and downloaded maps would already have the bot layout for the bots so you can start up with bots. 5. Bittorrent based system. To take off load of servers when we\'re talking patches and games, a user can choose 3 download methods(if he has payed for the game of course) Seeder: He will get in queue, but he will have to send it out to others for a given time where the option will be locked, closing the app, restarting the computer should not help, the content should then just be locked till his time is over with seeding. Normal user: He uploads while he downloads, nothing special in that, he can set his upload and download rates to make sure it fits his connection. Though lower uploads(if there still is a need) = lower downloads. Leecher: He gets to be the last in the queue, but he doesnt have to upload anything. Perfect for a normal day where noone is downloading anyways. 6. Maybe more of an idea for retail, make free demos available, which you also can choose from the list, like at the release of HL2, you could get a limited version of HL2 that maybe wont play other than 1/4 of the first chapter. 7. Make unsubscribe buttons, and account management, preferably something capable of calculating what you use on it, and what you have used on it. You could call it some kind of cc status online? 8. Maybe a option to make it download every free update or game available when it comes out. 9. Another cool thing could be if you could setup your games from outside steam, if you i.e set the resolution to high, or makes other changes that make it crash, a sorta better safe mode. 10. maybe some beta games on steam? Other: 11. It could be cool if you had deals with hardware vendors allover the world to maybe give you discounts if you bought through steam. Edit: 12. SDK for Steam, so you could make plugins, skins, and games for it(those on the friends list). It would have to be signed by Valve first of course. 13. Chatrooms on friends. New Edit: 14. Some kind of offline ticket, its generated based on your hardware: Harddisk drive, graphics card, soundcard and cpu. It would then make a kind of startup disc for steam so you can use it offline and over lan.' WHERE post_id = 49694 AND is_historical = 1;
