UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'For me, this problem has ocurred only when using my keyboard. What happens is, my mouse freezes and I keep moving after I release the key. Worse on heavy maps, like de_aztec. I mostly play CS but the problem is even worse in NS. DO NOT tell me to update my keyboard and/or mouse drivers as I\'ve had the problem on both my computers with wildly differrent specs and I\'ve switched between several differrent keyboards and mice. (no cordless crap)\n\n__________________ Specs: Windows XP Pro. English SP1 Motherboard: MSI K7N2 Delta CPU: AMD Athlon XP3000+ Memory:2x DDR 512MB PC3200 Video: ATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128MB /w Catalyst 4.2 drivers - "High Performance" settings Sound: Integrated nvidia nForce2 ---- input ---- Mouse: Intellimouse Explorer 3.0 (usb) Keyboard: Logitech internet navigator SE (usb /w PS/2 adapter) ---- Steam: CS 1.6 ---- 800x600 - 16bit official CPL-GUI.' WHERE post_id = 438400 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I used to have this problem. My system specs are in my signature. To add to what phluid said: Please post when the problem began, what steps you have taken to try and resolve the problem, what programs you have set to run on startup, and what system services you have active. Please also try the following steps: 1. Ensure that your problem is actually an independent control lag problem, not one brought on by a ping of 5000. That is, you have keyboard or mouse lag even when you only have 10-40 ping. 2. Ensure your PC is free of viruses, adware, and spyware. 3. Try the DirectSound "emulation only" workaround: go to Start->Run->dxdiag->DirectSound->drag the slider at "sound acceleration" to the far left. 4. Right-click Counter-Strike in the Games menu, go to Properties, and add -noforcemparms -noforcemaccel -noforcemspeed under launch options. 5. Uninstall any third-party mouse and keyboard drivers (ones that did not come with Windows itself.) 6. Roll back your sound card\'s drivers if possible. 7. Open Task Manager and end any extraneous processes (programs not needed for your PC or Counter-Strike to operate.) 8. Use BlackViper\'s Services 411 (http://www.blackviper.com/ (http://www.blackviper.com/)) to tweak your system services if you are using Windows 2000 or XP. 9. Try setting the theme to "Windows Classic" (if running Windows XP) and uninstalling any third-party theming programs (WindowBlinds, etc.)\n\n__________________ Neoflame CS-Relevant System Specs: P4 1.8 gHz 512MB PC2100 DDRRAM ATI Radeon 9600 Pro OC\'d to 480/320 1024x768 85Hz FSAA=2x AF=4x ATI Catalyst 4.3 Crappy Avance AC\'97 Soundcard Windows XP Home Edition SP1/Mandrake Linux 10.0 Community 256/1024Kbps Cable If pro is the opposite of con, what is the opposite of progress?' WHERE post_id = 438403 AND is_historical = 1;
