UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Bugs and Such', post_text = 'Another point that was mentioned but not really discussed is that the game worked better before their last major update (March 10?), So why not just undo the last update until they have these bugs worked out? I also agree that someone from Steam at least acknowledging the problem and letting us know they are working on it would be a common courtesey. ---This lack of intrest on Steam\'s part makes me think that, indeed, they have no plans to fix this problem.--- (sad) Also - Saying that it isn\'t really that big of a deal is kinda avoiding the issue, yeah compared to alot of other problems in the world this is not a big deal, but for the people that have an hour or two of free time here and there to play dod, having to reboot the game every 20 minutes or so is a pain in the ****[]' WHERE post_id = 479238 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'What $30.00 is worth!! Read Now!!', post_text = 'Okay Valve seriously screwed up on this one, this is worse than the Blue Shift release since that actually had a single player game that was half-way entertaining. They are charging $30.00 for CZ, they won\'t let you use the new Ritual models, they updated some maps, and included Bot support, wow POD bot is free. They have had 3 years to make this game and well they put out a pack that is worth maybe 10 bucks for the "new" contnent. On retrospect lets look at what some other game companies are releasing for $39.00 now a days? Well DICE recently released Battlefield Vietnam. A completely new game with new vehicles, upgraded graphics engine, awesome soundtrack, killer huge maps, changed variations in play styles and tactics. That seems like a worthy $39.99 these days. Okay since that may be a sole exception lets try another one. Hmm what else just got released, oh yeah Epic Games Unreal Tournament 2004. Well if you have read any reviews they say this is "the" game to have. What did they offer to players? An upgraded graphics engine that is gorgeous, new game play modes "onslaught is a blast!", new models, they brought the assault mode back, over 100 maps (Yes 119 total), and the fastest shooter in the world. Okay lets take Valve, they charge $30.00 for it over Steam and $39.99 in stores. Okay I have faith in Valve, they won\'t screw the community. For my $30.00 I get bots (that don\'t work all that well and cannot jump or climb ladders), I get some redone maps (only 3-4 are new), no upgraded graphics engine same old **** models, no new game modes, no new sounds. I used to believe that Valve was concerned about their community, at one point they were, but that time was long ago and now all if about money and making a profit. They really screwed us on this release in hoping the CS name would sell another product. This is not the first time they screwed people, what they charged people for CS 1.5 and DoD although it was a free download. Epic and DICE seem to have gotten the idea that they need to listen to their community, Valve has forgotten us, it is a very say day indeed.' WHERE post_id = 461407 AND is_historical = 1;
