UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Thanks', post_text = 'This is a great list, Lunchtimemama. It\'s rare to see bugs written up so professionally. Some of these were already on our to-do list, but many of them weren\'t. I\'ll reply to this thread again to address your bugs individually.' WHERE post_id = 504158 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: A long list of small UI bugs and inconsistencies', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Lunchtimemama - (Bug) There is a scroll glitch for certain property-editing windows that do not have enough fields to require a scroll bar. For these windows, activating either scroll arrow will cause a one-time scroll �jump.� Examples of such windows include the �Create Server\' window > �Game\' tab for the games TFC, DMC, DoD, and Ricochet. Also, the �Options\' window > �Multiplayer\' tab > �Advanced�\' button for TFC, DMC, DoD, Opposing Force, Ricochet, and the �Options\' window > �Advanced\' tab for Half-Life. Definitely worth fixing. Alfred and I will look into it. quote: - (Bug) There is a scrolling bug in \'Update news\' windows; the scrollbar goes beyond the bottom of the text\'s scroll. - (Bug) There is a conflict between (what I presume to be) the Internet Explorer scroll bars and the Steam UI scroll bars for the CZ �More Info\' window. There are other scroll bar problems for server welcome screens that include html elements. Either the IE issues need to be remedied, or another solution should be considered for html rendering. Alfred thinks these two bugs are my problem, and I think they\'re his. So the bugs persists while we feud. quote: - (Bug) In the board game Go\'s UI, the horizontal axis is labeled with the letters of the alphabet. The letter "I" is conspicuously absent. This could be by design (to avoid confusion with the number 1) but the horizontal bars at the top and bottom of a capital I distinguish it from a 1 as much as the loop at the bottom of the J or the foot of the L. This one is by design. At any rate, I don\'t think it\'s going to make it high enough on the priority list. quote: - (Minor Issue) In the Half Life game > �Create Server\' menu item > \'Game\' tab, the 4th field from the top has the label "Valid teams, leave blank f..." and there is no way of resizing the window to allow all of the text to display. I hate when that happens. I\'ll look into it. quote:- (Minor Issue) The text color for an offline friend is light pale green (hex - #758666). When you select one of those names, it is highlighted in orange-ish yellow and the text color changes to white (so that you can still read the name against the yellow highlight). Clicking on a blank area of the Friends window will then cause the text to change back to it\'s light pale green, but the orangey-yellow highlight remains, rendering the name impossible to read. The same is true for the Games window with unactivated games (whose text is also #758666). Either the yellow highlight should disappear too or the text should remain white (I think the latter would be preferable.). This one\'s my personal pet peeve. We\'ll fix it. quote: - (Minor Issue) If you right click on Counter-Strike (not Condition Zero) under �Available Games,� the context option is �Purchase.� Since you are not yet able to �Purchase� the original CS through Steam yet, the option should be the same as all of the other classic games: �Install.� Hey, you\'re right. We must have broken that just recently. This one\'s pretty high priority. Thanks. quote: - (Inconsistency) Text selection is not consistent in windows that display html files (�Update news\' windows, for example). Ordinary click-and-dragging will not select text, but Ctrl-clicking, Shift-clicking, and click-drag-release-click-ing will select text. I think the intended behavior is to prevent text selection all together (since the most common method of selection has been disabled). It\'s not intended that HTML text selection be disabled, but it\'s not easy in our HTML control to enable it. I\'ll see what we can do, but don\'t hold your breath on this one. quote: - (Inconsistency) For the �Games\' and �Friends\' windows, clicking on a listed item will highlight that item, then clicking in a blank portion of the window will keep the item highlighted. However, right-clicking on a listed item will highlight that item, and then clicking in a blank portion of the window will un-highlight the item. I don\'t know if we\'ll fix that one. But I do want to fix the fact that you can\'t right-click on two things consecutively. As in, right click on one list item (context menu appears), then right click on another (context menu doesn\'t appear). That bugs me. quote: - (Inconsistency) When in offline mode, the title of the Friends window is "Friends - Offline" (note the capital O in \'Offline\') but the Monitor and Games windows both have titles that spell \'offline\' with a lowercase o ("Monitor - offline" and "Games - offline"). I would think that a capital O would fit with the convention used for window titles. Yeah. quote:- (Inconsistency) The "Steam - working" window that appears when Steam is performing certain operations (sending verification e-mails for instance) spells "working" with a lowercase \'w\' in the window\'s title. This breaks the window-title convention that is observed throughout the rest of the application. Uh huh. quote: - (Inconsistency) The process for re-setting an account password includes a window that requests the verification code and answer to the secrete question. If the fields are left blank and the user clicks �Next,\' nothing happens. It would be more consistent with the program\'s UI if there appeared an alert telling the user that all fields must be completed before continuing. So true. We\'ll fix it up. quote: - (Enhancement) In the "Update news" windows, you should be able to expand/collapse the previous updates information as you can when viewing the page in IE. If only that were possible. I won\'t go into why it\'s not. I\'ll be changing the format of the update histories to fix this a different way. Just haven\'t gotten around to it, yet. quote: - (Enhancement) If you change your language and select "Cancel" from the \'Restart Required\' dialog, then change your language back to the language you are currently using, the \'Restart Required\' dialog comes up again. There is no need for the dialog since a restart is not required to keep your language the same. Well, true, but this one will probably go unfixed. quote: - (Enhancement) Now that Steam has offline capabilities, the "Update news" html files should be stored on the user\'s computer so that they can see the update info if they are offline. Interesting idea, but we probably won\'t use that solution. Seriously, thanks for writing these up.' WHERE post_id = 504202 AND is_historical = 1;
