UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Sloppy work, just very sloppy', post_text = 'Ok, after reading all the comments ppl have on CZ, I must say I agree with them. And I did pay the $30 for CZ. But that\'s not my main grudge here. Something else bothers me even more. Fatal error: R_Drawspritemodel: couldn\'t get sprite frame for sprites/richo1.spr http://www.csrealism.com/files/error.jpg (http://www.csrealism.com/files/error.jpg) The deleted scenes section of CZ is constantly crashing. I get this all the time, completely random. Since I know a little about modding in HL, this means either a corrupted file or some part of the program is calling a frame in the sprite that does not exist. (see pic) In other words, Valve, this is sloppy. This should have been picked up at testing. You DO test don\'t you? Such bugs are fixed in less then 2 mins! A few months ago while I was developing my own models for CS I emailed Valve if some bugs were going to be fixed. They replied: "yes, we\'ll fix that". * Crouch aim pistol anim on the player models, the left hand is flapped back...(ref_aim_onehanded5.smd) * The m4 muzzle flash is in the middle of the weapon (attachments people!) * With right handed models, the shells eject from the left on the M3 shotgun, the scout and the awp. In other words, they eject out of nothing... * I asked them if we could influence the direction of the shells...now my shells eject from the right (in most cases), but still fly over to the right...while I have right ejection ports... None of them were fixed. Nothing. Nada. Dipkus. These bugs EVEN I can fix in 2 hours if I had acces to the code. You know WHAT is weird? They did take the time to fix the model enforcement on the ump45 and sg550! Then why not spent 5 mins more? Please people! Yes yes yes I know CZ and CS are on low-prio for you guys. I know you put much of your efforts in HL2 and steam (which you DO pay attention too by constant fixes, bravo), but then don\'t publish new software for $30 without paying any attention to it. I\'m wondering if you guys are lacking resources. Logically, you haven\'t published in 5 years and did a lot of development. That\'s a hellof a bill to pay. Look, I may moan alot. But hey, I\'m not asking too much for $30 am I? And I don\'t even mind the old models.... * software NOT crashing (CZ Deleted scenes) * Bugs so small even the smurfs could fix them So my main grudge is the total attitude of Valve towards CS and its community. I thought that with CZ comming out Valve would (for a final time), pay attention to the CS community, and give this popular mod a final boost to carry us all to HL2. I\'m idealistic,m I know. Apparently I was wrong.\n\n__________________ Devlin CS|RU Developer' WHERE post_id = 470153 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Sloppy work, just very sloppy', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Devlin A few months ago while I was developing my own models for CS I emailed Valve if some bugs were going to be fixed. They replied: "yes, we\'ll fix that". * Crouch aim pistol anim on the player models, the left hand is flapped back...(ref_aim_onehanded5.smd) * The m4 muzzle flash is in the middle of the weapon (attachments people!) * With right handed models, the shells eject from the left on the M3 shotgun, the scout and the awp. In other words, they eject out of nothing... * I asked them if we could influence the direction of the shells...now my shells eject from the right (in most cases), but still fly over to the right...while I have right ejection ports... None of them were fixed. Nothing. Nada. Dipkus. That sounds like VALVe to me so I don\'t know why ur even amazed :P\n\n__________________ www.Anime-XG.com I am 65% addicted to Counter-Strike' WHERE post_id = 470371 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'The deleted scenes weren\'t completed, that\'s why there\'s bugs in it. I started playing it last night, and it is laughable how bad it is. I don\'t like the gun models any better than the default CS models and the new gun sounds just plain SUCK. I do like the player models though, they look pretty cool from what I\'ve seen so far. Aside from aesthetics though, the gameplay is truly pathetic, and its easy to see why Valve switched developers away from Ritual after seeing their work. I think part of the reason Valve made the deleted scenes available to us in the first place, was just to show WHY it took so long for the game to come out, and why they weren\'t happy with the work that was being done at Ritual. Its truly like playing a barely mediocre 1997 singleplayer game, so I guess that\'s why they were "deleted" in the first place.' WHERE post_id = 470423 AND is_historical = 1;
