UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here\'s somthing for you: what you saw as "advertised" was really "previously advertised". Let me explain for those who don\' know. Origionally VALVe outsourced the development of Condition Zero to a software develop company called Ritualistic Entertainment. That game had new weapons, models, maps - and a single-player mission campaign accross the world, and is now known as the deleted scenes. What happened to that about 2/3 of the way through the development process was that VALVe rejected what Ritual was developing for unknown reasons and transfered the project to Turtle Rock Studios. What Turtle Rock produced is what we now know as Condition Zero: bots, some new maps and textures, and a Tony Hawk-esque single-player game. Now the confusion is 2-fold; one, that many retailers (and the publisher SIERRA) continued to advertise the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game, which was no longer being developed. Two, that the game was boxed in a Ritual boxed which was designed to point out the features of the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game. Honestly, I understand the frustration - but if you\'d read the latest CS Nation review you\'d have known all that. You cannot blame VALVe for your inability to keep up with current data reguarding their projects - you can however blame SIERRA, and your local retailer. What you can blame VALVe for is switching developers. That was most likely an upper management decision, and they\'ll have to live with that for a while - for as we all know, the deleted scenes kick ass. As for the models, 1 of 3 things is occuring. One, VALVe does not have sufficient permission or rights to use the Ritual material (new skins, models, maps, etc) on the Turtle Rock game. If this is the case, the possibility remains that they will be released as an update. Two, Turtle Rock refused to incorporate Ritual\'s work in their game - wanting to keep the game true to their namesake. VALVe may be bound by their decision to do so. If this is the case, it still lends to the idea that the Ritual material may be released officially. The last possibility is the VALVe is holding them out of sheer spite, that they think that because its in the Deleted Scenes that they do not need to include it in the actual game. I hope this has explained many of the questions being asked in this thread. As a reminder I am not an employee of VALVe and do not speak on their behalf - I consider myself and informed observer.' WHERE post_id = 472002 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'As i understand, and please p-wolf, correct me if I am wrong, the retail box has the ritual logo on, thus is an error. However I went into my local retailer (EBGAMES), and looked at the stragtegy guide which has the turtle rock logo on it (not ritual), in this stragtegy guide it has the training from deleted scenes, the new weapons, new maps, but with the rest of the guide is all based on how the "official release" is. So to summerize, the stragey guide covers a mix between rituals and turtle rock, but wit the turtle rock logo on it. I suggest you go look in your retailer for it and then post a reply. As a reminder, I like valve.' WHERE post_id = 472071 AND is_historical = 1;
