UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Warning - completely un-informed opinion', post_text = 'Gentlemen: As a non-CS / CS:CZ player I make the following observations: 1. Fine thread you have started here. Nice to see that there are CS players with more than the ability to twitch and shoot. 2. cerebrix: I have yet to see any responsible statement from any Steam - Valve employee of any degree of authority or knowledge on this web site, in any forum or in any thread. With all due respect to the other Steam - Valve employees who have posted, I am talking about SENIOR Steam - Valve employees or decision makers. 3. P-Wolf: [ this is where the un-informed opinion comes in... I know nothing of CS / CS:CZ other than it exists ... I\'m a DoDer and would be playing, but for the latest round of Steam bugs ] P-Wolf said: Now the confusion is 2-fold; one, that many retailers (and the publisher SIERRA) continued to advertise the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game, which was no longer being developed. Two, that the game was boxed in a Ritual boxed which was designed to point out the features of the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game. Zot says: What? You have *got* to be kidding me? That must be on the very edge, if not over the line, of false advertizing. I\'m sure these things are checked by lawyers for Valve - Sierra - Ritualistic, but if not illegal that is right at the top of the list of mis-leading practices. P-Wolf said: if you\'d read the latest CS Nation review you\'d have known all that. You cannot blame VALVe for your inability to keep up with current data reguarding their projects - you can however blame SIERRA, and your local retailer. Zot says: Huh? All due respect P-Wolf, getting solid regular information out of Valve is anything BUT easy and certainly finding anything realiable about Valve projects on the internet is like looking for a needle in a hay stack. There is ten times as much ....er...make that 1 million times more bs and speculation about Steam - Valve and their projects than any solid information provided by those who could/should be providing that information. Blame Sierra? Ya, ok. I\'ll go along with that. Blame your local retailer? For what? Selling product? Not warning you that you may not like what you are buying? Not ripping the packaging off and wrapping it in plain brown paper? I don\'t see the retailers role in this deception. Likely the retailers are even more in the dark than buyers of pc games when it comes to these issues. Zot final comment: It is nice to see a well presented thread. It is also pathetic to see that Steam - Valve et al have abandon the floor, so to speak, and left it for their customers and "the community" to try and figure out what Steam - Valve might say to explain these types of issues, if it were not for the fact that Steam-Valve et al have the hear-no-evil, see-no-evil, speak-no-evil policy of dealing with customers, complaints and the community in general. Regards, Zot' WHERE post_id = 472198 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'d hardly consider my opinion uninformed. I\'ve played CS for 4 years, and beaten this game already - and yet I SOMEHOW managed to keep up with the developer change unlike apparently: you. What I said is what happened. As for the release information - did you try CZ\'s official site?' WHERE post_id = 472204 AND is_historical = 1;
