UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I use gentoo for my x86-64\'s and the performance is horrible compared to fedora. hondaman www.hardgaming.com (http://www.hardgaming.com)' WHERE post_id = 491537 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'m assuming you\'ve compiled the sources properly for the AMD64 arch. I\'ve always have had equal or better preformance with Gentoo compared to other distros. In the end it really just comes down to the distro you prefer the most, personally I\'d try a couple. Especially if you are trying to learn here too. If you aren\'t trying to learn and just want to get a server up, I would not recommend Gentoo because of it\'s more involved setup. If you just want to get a system up and running Fedora (basically RedHat\'s development distro) wouldn\'t be a bad choice. http://www.distrowatch.com (http://www.distrowatch.com) http://www.gentoo.org (http://www.gentoo.org) http://www.debian.org (http://www.debian.org) http://fedora.redhat.com (http://fedora.redhat.com)' WHERE post_id = 492259 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'SuSE. Because people in the industry dont have an entire day to compile Gentoo! []' WHERE post_id = 493179 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well, that completely depends on the industry. If you are doing webhosting, *BSD would be the way to go. [] BSD based servers consistently come up with the longest uptime and lowest failed requests of any OS. Besides if you really want you can get precompiled Gentoo optimized for most architectures. I haven\'t used SuSe in quite some time, but I\'m interested in the changes Novell will bring to them. I think the addition of suse to the discussion just leaves Mandrake and Slackware out for the major distros. http://www.distrowatch.com (http://www.distrowatch.com) http://www.gentoo.org (http://www.gentoo.org) http://www.debian.org (http://www.debian.org) http://fedora.redhat.com (http://fedora.redhat.com) http://www.suse.com (http://www.suse.com)' WHERE post_id = 493325 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Master Ruthless SuSE. Because people in the industry dont have an entire day to compile Gentoo! [] Did you ever hear about stage tarballs? Or do you really want X running on your gameserver to waste a few more resources ...' WHERE post_id = 495263 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'after somer reading (thanks for the links Scorpian_Sting) i think im ganna give slackware a try... any comments on my decision (such as, reasons not to)?' WHERE post_id = 497454 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Hi does the cpu usage really drops with debian or slackware? i use suse 9.0 and for 16 slot cs 1.6 in need 20-50% of a XP2500+ !! its a little to much :-(' WHERE post_id = 497541 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Slackware is the oldest continually developed distro out there. I know several people who really like it though I\'ve never actually used it. It may be a bit more complex than something like SuSe or Fedora, but probably is a good choice. CPU usage will be dependent on the plugins running on the server, people on the server, map of the server etc. It will also depend on the other services running on the machine and can also be affected by different compiling optimizations. If you are running a i686 compiled software (assuming that is right for your cpu) and have already eliminated unneeded services you are unlikely to find much of a difference between distros. Though each one does have a slightly different kernel which may give you a percentage point of difference here and there.' WHERE post_id = 497927 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by LaMersSs Did you ever hear about stage tarballs? Or do you really want X running on your gameserver to waste a few more resources ... Hum It is not that hard to install any distro minus X... Gentoo isn\'t the only distro you can strip X from. Also have you ever heard of init3???' WHERE post_id = 498770 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'whats this "X" that is referred to many times in this thread?' WHERE post_id = 499318 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by white_rabbit whats this "X" that is referred to many times in this thread? I hope your joking but just in case your not heres an explaination... It is the MS Windows like GUI interface that make Linux or UNIX look kinda like Windows instead od DOS. People feel including myself that to run X on a server drains resources that can be put to better use. Kinda like DOS doesn\'t use up near as much in the way of memory and processor power as Windows does.' WHERE post_id = 499444 AND is_historical = 1;
