UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'what did the server owner do in the cal configs that are diff from the others? i would look there and ask what settings are different. mostly it would be settings that effect clientside connect speed or bandwidth caps maybe?\n\n__________________ my pc stuff: amd 2500 barton gigabyte mobo 7n400l 1024 mb ddr400 (pc3200) ram dual channel Plantronics dsp 500 headset with built in soundcard and speech recognition. ati 9500 128 mb maxtor 80 gb with xp 2nd drive 30 gb maxtor dsl 768/256 - creative 7410 external modem TFC nutaholic...oh my gawd.. dont touch that! thats my flag! [dont flame all the noObs...you werent born playing half life!!!] playin da TFC since demos had 4 mirvs! I lub de demo spammo! Member of [TNT] THE NAMELESSTEAM Copper Div. Champs 3-15-04 YaY !' WHERE post_id = 498211 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'thank you for the help guys! but i just found out my prob like 2 hours ago, i got into a scrim, and my ping didn\'t jump over 60. now... i\'m a CS n00b and i probably should have known that, but i was talking to somebody in #team3d on mIRC and they were talking about values, so i got into the conversation, and told them i only play online, what are the perfect values? they told me this, and i suggest you guys do this too.... in your console, type the following..(without <> ) <rate> - if this is at 1, which mine was, that\'s EXACTLY why you\'re having probs.. change this by typing rate 25000 (most server will cap it at 9999, but some servers now allow 25000) in addition to this very important value, there are 2 others that have to do with how much information your internet allows CS to send info to and from the server which you\'re playing on (so i\'m told).. <cl_cmdrate 101> <cl_updaterate 101> well, i hope this works for you guys, and thank you for the help [] adios!\n\n__________________ LoNDoNbo! pwns!!!' WHERE post_id = 513430 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Strange Lag Spikes (DoD)', post_text = 'Hello fellow Steamers, I think I may be experiencing a problem similar to this thread: /forums/show...ghlight=bizarre (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=64421&highlight=bizarre) When playing Day of Defeat, every minute or so my game freezes/stutters/stalls for a few seconds - you know that old lag symptom: when all the players around you seem to freeze in their tracks, and then 1 to 3 seconds later they\'re half-way across the hall, indicating that they\'ve actually been moving while you\'ve been stuck. Has anyone else been experiencing this lately? I recently switched my motherboard and cpu (upgraded) and performed a standard hard drive format, and reinstall of Windows XP. Everything runs beautifully, except this strange succession of freezes/lags in Day of Defeat. These symptoms occur on all servers, and usually aren\'t accompanied by an increase in Ping. My ping usually hovers between 30 and 60. My specs are as follows: Pentium 4 3.0c 1gb DDR 3200 RAM Nvidia Geforce FX 5600 Asus PC4800-E Deluxe Mobo I guess the first thing i\'m trying to determine is whether this is a Steam issue or something wrong with my PC. If there are any other threads I may have missed, I\'d appreciate a link to them.' WHERE post_id = 498792 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Mine does this on CS, have reinstalled video drivers, reinstalled steam. Doesn\'t help. Started this after the last update. Although mine does it about every 20-30 sec. Any fixes out there yet? Please let us know=)' WHERE post_id = 498924 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'m glad to hear that i\'m not the only one experiencing this difficulty. It\'s really detrimental to gameplay. A little more info: i\'ve been monitoring my own lag spikes, and they seem to occur more often than just every minute, especially during large amounts of in-game activity, i.e. explosions, bullets firing etc. I\'ve noticed that complaints about this lag-spike issue have been coming from all quarters of the Steam world: CS, DoD, NS et al. Could it be the recent update that caused this? Perhaps the implementation of offline mode? Here\'s another thread which is kinda similar... they seem to be experiencing the same \'lag spikes\' as we are. /forums/show...;threadid=72499 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=72499) The gist of it is that Norton Anti-Virus may be hampering online play by running in the background. You may want to experiment with different settings. I\'m using Norton Anti-Virus 2004, that\'s about it, and don\'t see too many settings to tweak, but its worth a shot. I hope more people post here with suggestions or comments. Thanks, Koala' WHERE post_id = 499155 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'At least you can play a game. Steam reports that all of my games require an update and I cannot launch any game. The last time I launched Cstrike, it told me that the game would be available for play in like 115 minutes. By the way, I noticed that I have been getting Steam updates in dribs and drabs... every 20-30 seconds. This may account for your laggy situation. Take a look at your monitor and see if you have been getting these annoying updates in small pieces.' WHERE post_id = 499162 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Also of note, I\'m sitting on a 768k DSL and Steam is only updating every 20-30 seconds for about 3 or 4 seconds at a rate of 41kb. Anyone else seeing this?' WHERE post_id = 499178 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Actually, every update is at 41.5kb.' WHERE post_id = 499179 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'yea, i didnt get to play steam for about 4 mothes from teh prior update..............the people at steam arnt good at updating (on offense) but they keep to test more, and yes ive had that problem...................just gotta sit it out till they fix it' WHERE post_id = 499231 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for those thoughts. I\'m sorry to hear that you can\'t even play Steam games right now. I\'m sure a lot of people are in the same boat right now, and I can definitely sympathize: I too have had to perform endless reboots of my pc, uninstalls of steam, reinstall\'s of steam, and have spent a great deal of time combing the forum for help. Hang in there! I checked my monitor. I doesn\'t look like anything is updating at the moment. Good suggestion though, it may definitly help some others. Everyone having this problem should at least check to see if Steam if trying to download stuff while they\'re playing. Ok, now: per my last post above, I tried to tweak my Norton Anti-Virus settings to see if that cleared up the lag-spikes I am experiencing. It didn\'t make any differance. The other two threads I linked above make referance to Norton settings that I don\'t have and "refreshing" activities that I don\'t think my Norton Anti-Virus \'04 performs. In either case, it didn\'t seem to help much. I don\'t think its an issue with my hardware, although I haven\'t ruled it completly out yet. My younger brother often plays DoD online with me. He is on the same network as I am, but using a much less powerful computer (AMD 750mz Duron. 512 mb SD-Ram. Elsa Gladiac Geforce 3; [too bad about that company by the way]) and isnt\' having any trouble at all with lag spikes. I\'m actually jealous. :-) He did tell me however, that there are times when from his point of view i\'ll appear to freeze in the middle of whatever i\'m doing during the game. This helped to confirm that i\'m definitely experiencing a lag-related issue when in-game. The next thing i\'m going to try is some LAN activity with Sturm-Bots to see if I experience any lag spikes on a local game. Any other thoughts or comments are appreciated!' WHERE post_id = 499505 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here\'s another thread that appears to be talking about the same problem, a "stuttering" and "choking" resembling lag spikes. /forums/show...;threadid=56353 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=56353) Here\'s a quote from one of the last posts in that thread: "Lately (after the April 2nd update, supposedly only modifying Steam and not CS) I\'ve been stuttering like Zaren has been. I\'ll be in a game and all of a sudden everything will stop... a few seconds later, everybody pops up wherever they moved to while I was stuttering, and I usually wind up dead on the ground. It\'s a bit harder to keep up with my team if I have to stop moving every 5 seconds to wait for my game to start again." There is some talk about Spyware eating up resources. I\'ll run a test with ad-aware on my pc and check it out.' WHERE post_id = 499511 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I have also the same problem !!! here my thread /forums/show...;threadid=72662 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=72662) It must be something with the relation of my hardware and Steam .... or the code of steam perhaps !! I couldnt guess anything ..... but my problem is more that my ping gets into high value 500 + und so i am lagging around ! MY Fps are still good 50++ I have also a very good PC ..... and i have ATI RADEON 9700 graphics card .... so it cannot be a problem with graphic company ... i guessed that ! We must wait to for Steam to fix this probelm ..... i payed for Fastpath and i hope this will help me ! I also getting into lag when much activity is on my inet connection ...... much shots,bulletts or in great rooms like in Aztec ! I also shut down my virus detection software ... always the same ! Dont know anything ... its reallly really strange ! greetz Space' WHERE post_id = 499799 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Another question ! By net_graph 3 you can see In and Out kb by your connection ! How i can make this value higher so my client receive more kb/s !! I think this is perhaps the prob ..... always when i must get more than 100 k/s my ping gets higher and higher .... this would also include the prob why i lag in great rooms and in big fights only !! With what things i can affect this value?=???? greetz Space' WHERE post_id = 499818 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'hey guys, i\'ve been having this problem for months on end now.. /forums/...ghlight=bizarre (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=64421&highlight=bizarre)' WHERE post_id = 499951 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for posting those threads guys. Of course, I wish none of us had these problems, but its nice to know that i\'m not the only Steam user with these issues. Spacejunkie - could you explain a bit more about net_graph? I seem to remember something about this in the old days of Half-Life and Ping tweaking when most people still had 56k modems. You might be on to something. I\'ve noticed that I tend to get more "stuttering" during moments of intense activity - people running around, shooting rifles, throwing grenades etc. Meesh - thanks for chiming in. when it comes to your network config, you really seem to know your stuff! I\'m glad to see that disabling Norton Anti-Virus auto-protect has helped solve the issue for some people. Do you have any idea what other posters mean when they refer to Norton\'s "90 sec refresh?". I\'ve been rummaging around my Norton 2004 Anti-Virus and haven\'t seen any option relating to a consistent refresh. Also - you\'ve been experiencing this for months?? Yikes. So this didn\'t become noticeable with the last steam update? How have you dealt with this over time? Have you received any assistance from official Steam/Valve staff? I do appreciate these forums, I think they\'re an invaluable resource, but sometimes it feels like we are participating in a very large, unwieldy beta-test. :-) A little bit more from my own testing as well: BOTS Thank god for Sturmbot. I played some LAN matches on my PC with bots and didn\'t experience any "lag spikes". I went ahead and increased the load by adding some custom sounds, models, skins and sprites. Even with 16 bots running around causing havoc on Anzio I didn\'t get the same freezing or stalling. So local area network play isn\'t being affected. ONLINE Strange. When I experience a lag spike, i\'ll usually hit TAB quickly to see if my ping rises in conjunction. Sometimes it does, sometimes it doesn\'t. At certain times it will jump a 100+ more than it should be, like from 30 to 400. Other times it\'ll merely jump between 40 and 50, seemingly normal ping variation whilst online. Occasionally too, other players will start "disappearing and reappearing" in and out of sight while running.' WHERE post_id = 500156 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'New Info : I have tried to play online at my freinds inet connection !!! I also have the same lag spikes ... but he doesnt have any problems !! SO IT CANNOT BE THE INET CONNECTION ... i guessed so ! Its something with my computer ... but what`??? i have turned off all Anti Vir or firewalls ...... i think that i have no trojans or such things on PC !!! What causes this hard lag ???? .... anyone have some ideas ??? I dont know .... really ........ any other inet games or any other games without steam run very well on my comp ! The campain of cz also works fine .... its must be something with the steam program or code or any inet program at behind ... or the relation to this programs !!!!! Any mod can answer some solution or make of course a command that they recognisted this problem ???!!! Its really bad to play cs so ..... of course you can play only a few maps .... at the others the lag is really too high to play !!!! I have spend 30 Euro and so i want a game that i can play ... not that **** !' WHERE post_id = 500309 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Are you experiencing any dramatic and sudden increases in your ping rate when this happens? I have been observing my online sessions more closely, and more and more frequently there does appear to be a large increase in ping whenever I get temporarily frozen or stuttered. Also, I\'ve noticed more and more threads talking about ping and lag issues lately. More people may be experiencing the same problems.' WHERE post_id = 501722 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'For experienced 56k users in need of help', post_text = '56k Tweaks For All OS\'s -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- I\'ve seen a number of people asking for some 56k tweaks lately and thought this might help out. For 98 & ME: 1. First and most important make sure you have the latest drivers for your modem, from the manufacturer. 2. Open modem properties in Control Panel and under advanced port settings slide both all the way to the right. 3. Set maximum port speed to 115,2000. 4. Open Internet Options in IE and under temp internet files - settings select - Automatically. 5. Under extra settings (where init strings go) put in s11=55 to make your modem dial faster or s10=60 if you have frequent disconnects. 6. Make sure you have a good "clean" phone line, the #1 reason 56K modems don\'t connect at a good transfer rate is static on your phone line, and remember your throughput is more important than what your connection says it is connected at. If you are connected between 44,000 - 50,000 that is as good as it gets (you are limited to 53,333 by the FCC) 7. Download TCPOptimizer and put in the following settings: Under the "settings" tab select "dial up" and "custom settings", in "network adapter selection" choose "dial up adapter". Then use the following settings: MaxMTU - 1500 TCP Receive Window - 8760 MTU Discovery - Yes Black Hole Detect - No Selective ACKs - Yes Max Dup ACKs - 2 Time to Live (TTL) - 128 TCP 1323 Options - uncheck both boxes "Other settings" tab: Max Connections per Server - 4 Max Connections per 1.0 Server - 8 Then select "Apply changes" and reboot to take effect. 8. Open your registry (start - run - type regedit) and change the following registry entries: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\Class\\Net\\000X (where X is a number between 1 and 9)there is a value named SLOWNET, change it from 01 to 00. HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\VxD\\COMBUFF it has a value called Start, change its value from 00 to 01. HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\VxD\\VCACHE, it has a value named Start, change it from 00 to 01. 9. Open your sys.ini file (start - run -sysedit - ME type system.ini) close the boxes until you are at the one with the title C:\\WINDOWS\\SYSTEM.INI, under [386enh] add the line ComXXIrqXXbuffer=4096, XX=Com port your modem is on and Irq assigned to your modem, it should look like Com03Irq07buffer=4096. Then select file - save and reboot to take effect. For 2K & XP: For 2K & XP users I suggest using Cablenut to tweak your settings due to the fact it installs the AFD parameters and allows you to tweak them. These values utilize memory for buffers that help speed up and stabilize your connection and latency. The following ae my suggestions for settings to use in Cablenut: DefaultReceiveWindow = 8192 DefaultSendWindow = 4096 DisableAddressSharing = 1 InitialLargeBufferCount = 10 InitialMediumBufferCount = 24 InitialSmallBufferCount = 32 LargeBufferSize = 4096 MaxFastTransmit = 6400 MediumBufferSize = 1504 PriorityBoost = 0 SmallBufferSize = 128 TransmitWorker = 32 FastSendDatagramThreshold = 1024 EnableFastRouteLookup = 1 EnablePMTUDiscovery = 1 IgnorePushBitOnReceives = 0 GlobalMaxTcpWindowSize = 8760 MaxFreeTcbs = 2000 MaxHashTableSize = 4096 MaxNormLookupMemory = 5000000 SackOpts = 1 SynAttackProtect = 1 Tcp1323Opts = 0 TcpLogLevel = 1 MaxDupAcks = 2 TcpMaxHalfOpen = 100 TcpMaxHalfOpenRetried = 80 TcpRecvSegmentSize = 1460 TcpSendSegmentSize = 1460 TcpTimedWaitDelay = 30 TcpUseRFC1122UrgentPointer = 0 TcpWindowSize = 8760 MaxConnectionsPer1_0Server = 8 MaxConnectionsPerServer = 4 DefaultTTL = 128 DisableUserTOSSetting = 0 TcpMaxDataRetransmissions = 6 DefaultTOSValue = 92 Also add the following entry to your registry: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\AFD\\Parameters Add the parameter BufferMultiplier and give it a value of 400 hexidecimal which will make it 1024. 1. First and most important make sure you have the latest drivers for your modem, not Microsoft\'s, but the one\'s from the manufacturer. 2. Open modem properties in Control Panel and under advanced port settings slide both all the way to the right. 3. Set maximum port speed to 115,2000. 4. Under extra settings (where init strings go) put in s11=55. 5. Make sure you have a good "clean" phone line, the #1 reason 56K modems don\'t connect at a good transfer rate is static on your phone line, and remember your throughput is more important than what your connection says it is connected at. If you are connected between 44,000 - 50,000 that is as good as it gets (you are limited to 53,333 by the FCC) 6. Download TCPOptimizer and put in the following settings: Under the "settings" tab select "dial up" and "custom settings", in "network adapter selection" choose "dial up adapter". Then use the following settings: MaxMTU - 1500 TCP Receive Window - 8760 MTU Discovery - Yes Black Hole Detect - No Selective ACKs - Yes Max Dup ACKs - 2 Time to Live (TTL) - 128 TCP 1323 Options - uncheck both boxes "Other settings" tab: Max Connections per Server - 4 Max Connections per 1.0 Server - 8 Then select "Apply changes" and reboot to take effect. Leave all other boxes blank, select save to registry and reboot. 7. Open Internet Options (IE)and under temp internet files - settings select - Every visit to page. 8. Open your Network Connections from the Control Panel � right click on your Cable connection and select properties, if you have the �QoS Packet Scheduler� installed highlight it and select uninstall. 9. Open up regedit, navigate to HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE/Software/Microsoft/Windows/Current Version/Explorer/RemoteComputer/NameSpace, find the key named {D6277990-4C6A-11CF-8D87-00AA0060F5BF}. Right click on it and delete it. Also add the following entry: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Contro l\\PriorityControl (if PriorityControl is not there, make the value) - on the right hand side right click and select new DWORD value, name it IrqXPriority (X = Irq assigned to your modem), then right click it and select modify and give it a decimal value of 1. For ALL OS\'s: The most important thing to remember about dial up is that the maximum you can download ANYTHING under absolute perfect conditions is 6.7kb/s, so don\'t be frustrated with your speed, remember it is only 56K (actually 53333). To understand a little better, most dial up connections have a connect speed of somewhere in the mid 40K range, which is very good, so say you connect at 48000, to find your maximum throughput divide that by 8 which gives you 6kb/s, which actually very good for dial up. The tweaks I have provided will help you maximize that throughput as best possible, don\'t expect super speeds by tweaking your dial up, be happy if you are getting 6kb/s. FOR FASTER WEB PAGE LOADING: This tweak will help web pages load faster, it has no real effect on download speeds, just helps your pc look up websites faster thereby speeding up how fast the page loads and making websurfing more enjoyable. Navigate to this registry entry and change the following settings: For XP & 2K HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\Tcpip\\ServiceProv ider For 98, 98SE & ME HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic es\\VxD\\MSTCP\\Service Provider On the right for ALL OS\'s change these entries: (ALL values are HEXIDECIMAL) Class - 1 DnsPriority - 1 HostsPriority - 1 LocalPriority - 1 NetbtPriority - 1 Write down the current values PRIOR to changing them in case it doesn\'t work so you can revert back. To change the value right mouse click on the value and select modify and enter the values above once you have done all of them reboot to take effect and see how fast your pages load. P.S. If you have a dial up connection I HIGHLY recommend using a download manager, it will help maximize your download speed, resume downloads if you are disconnected and you can even schedule downloads for the middle of the night (it will automatically dial up and download the desired file and hang up when done) when you aren\'t using your pc. credit: http://forums.speedguide.net/showthread.php?t=68127 (http://forums.speedguide.net/showthread.php?t=68127) you can get the programs mentioned [cablenut, tcpoptimizer] @ www.speedguide.net (http://www.speedguide.net) or type the names into www.google.com (http://www.google.com) first link is correct one' WHERE post_id = 500930 AND is_historical = 1;
