UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Why not just un-ban everyone from this week?', post_text = 'I will not subject you all to the full bulk of my wrath, if you want to read my entire rant.... /forums/...;threadid=75784 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=75784) there you go. In terms of numbers, I went through the forums (before they started removing people for complaining that is) and counted all of the people that I felt were probably legitimately banned due to a bug, myself being one of them. I did not count the numerous "my lil Bro DL\'d h4x" complaints, but only people (from April 1st and on) that were banned and had no idea why. I counted a total of 218 different users..... wow. 218 that actually have accounts to post on these boards (I made one as a result.) 218 that were actually home, or had enough time to post... Im guessing that the actual number is into the thousands. Why would it be so hard to simply unban everyone banned since April 1st? Sure, a few hackers would get off, but they would either get caught again, or be scared enough by there temporary banning that they would quit cheating. I just dont see why we have to go through the wait (and the insult) of the "Im sorry for being a dirty cheater" form. I paid for this game. I want to play it. Im sorry if that is unreasonable. Straighten your crap out Valve, you arent making any friends with the customers. David Thompson' WHERE post_id = 516697 AND is_historical = 1;
