UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'What to Do About SpyWare & Virus Problems!', post_text = 'For any of you with Spyware, Virus or Trojan infections here are solutions and help! First, you can try and fix it yourself. Here is a collection of mostly free tools to de-infest your computer: First Line of Defense Tools: Microsoft Update for all Operating Systems (http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/en/default.asp) Spybot Search & Destroy (http://www.security.kolla.de/) Lavasoft Adaware (http://www.lavasoftusa.com/) Bazooka Spyware Scanner (http://www.kephyr.com/spywarescanner/index.html) McAfee AVERT Stinger (http://vil.nai.com/vil/stinger) NOTE: If you are having problems updating your O/S you may also have problems Installing/updating Steam! If you are unable to update your Windows, go here and troubleshoot your update problem (which might fix Steam as well): http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/troubleshoot/ (http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/troubleshoot/) As an additional step to check your systems, Microsoft has provided a "Baseline Security Analyzer" that will check for many security-risk related problems. Special Diagnostic and Repair Tools used only with Instruction from qUiCkSiLvEr and Computer Cops HijackThis and CWShredder (http://www.spywareinfo.com/~merijn/downloads.html) HijackThis Tutorial for Inquiring Minds (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/SteamyThings/HijackThis_Tutorial.htm) WARNING: USE HIJACKTHIS ONLY IF YOU ARE INSTRUCTED TO DO SO Information about Spyware and Virus and Trojans: Computer Safety Online (http://www.cjwd.demon.co.uk/compsafetyonline.html) SARC Symantec Security Response (http://www.sarc.com/) Doug Muth\'s Anti-Virus Resources (http://www.claws-and-paws.com/virus/) Christian Wagner\'s Excellent Spyware/AdWare/Malware FAQ and Removal Guide (http://www.io.com/~cwagner/spyware.html) DSL Reports Spyware and Adware F.A.Q. (http://www.dslreports.com/faq/spyware) What is Spyware (http://www.spychecker.com/spyware.html) Gibson Research OptOut! Internet Connection Misuse & Abuse (http://grc.com/optout.htm) Gibson Research Shields Up! (http://grc.com/default.htm) CounterExploitation! [cexx.org] (http://cexx.org) Adware, Badware & Spyware Profiles (http://www.accs-net.com/smallfish/advw.htm) Reputable Online Virus and Trojan Scanners: Panda ActiveScan (http://www.pandasoftware.com/activescan/com/activescan_principal.htm) Trend Micro Housecall (http://housecall.trendmicro.com/housecall/start_corp.asp) Full Virus and Trojan Scanner packages some are free all have trial downloads: Norton/Symantec (http://www.symantec.com/nav/nav_9xnt/) Trend PC-Cillin (http://www.trendmicro.com/en/products/desktop/pc-cillin/evaluate/overview.htm) Panda Anti-Virus (http://www.pandasoftware.com/com/nprod2002/platinum_home.asp) AVG Anti-Vrius from Grisoft (http://www.grisoft.com/) Kapersky Labs Anti-Virus (http://www.kaspersky.com/trials.html) McAfee Security ViruScan (http://download.mcafee.com/us/eval/evaluate2.asp?cid=9445) Norman Virus Control (http://www.norman.com/Download/Trial_versions/en-us) F-Secure Internet Security 2004 (http://www.f-secure.com/download-purchase/list.shtml) Vexira Antivirus for Windows (http://www.centralcommand.com/downloads.html) and here is a list of more free spyware removal tools: Spyware/Adware removal tools: PestPatrol! (http://www.pestpatrol.com/) <-- will detect and clean many resistant problems but $$ Webroot Spysweeper (http://www.webroot.com/php/tryme.php?bjpc=64000&vcode=DT02) Trojan Remover (http://www.simplysup.com) KL-Detector (http://dewasoft.com/privacy/kldetector.htm) X-Cleaner Free (http://www.xblock.com/download-freeware.shtml) Spyware Blaster (http://www.javacoolsoftware.com/spywareblaster.html) <-- doesn\'t scan or clean spyware but it blocks it Spyware Guard (http://www.wilderssecurity.net/spywareguard.html) <-- scans, removes and blocks spyware SpySites Plus (http://camtech2000.net/Pages/SpySites_Program.html) TrojanHunter (http://www.misec.net/) BHODemon (http://www.