UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Allowing Steam: Response from Dunkle requested', post_text = 'At the last E3 Mike Dunkle told me that cafe\'s that did not buy into the program could still have the Steam client downloaded as well as all the modules so that individual could use their own Steam accounts at the cafes. Now it is my understanding that Valve has changed their stance on this matter. Valve has now been quoted as saying, "you would be required to erase the copy of the Valve products after that user logged off the system". This makes little sense to me as those products are un-useable without the password, and forcing someone to re-download all of the software each time is a bit rediculous. It would be like saying that a CyberCafe couldn\'t keep Everquest installed even though the gamer would need to have purchased the game and be paying Sony every month to play it. Without the account info, the game is useless. It was my understanding that a person\'s Steam account was portable but could only be played from one PC at a time. Why does it matter if the person plays their own game at home or in a cybercafe? You would punish the user because perhaps their home computer or connection is not so hot or because they want to play face to face with their buddies? Or is it that not enough of these cafe licenses are being sold in the states and you are now deciding to change the rules? I hate to end in such a strong worded manner, but it has to be said. Mike, we need an answer on this. Are people allowed to use their accounts wherever they want? Do you expect them to download the client each time they go to a cafe? Are you trying to punish the cafe or the gamer who owns the account?' WHERE post_id = 532416 AND is_historical = 1;
