UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'There is a lot going on behind the scenes here Raul. On a recent conference call with iGames, Valve (Mike Dunkle) said that having Steam available for people who have their own accounts was OK. He then turned around and e-mailed an iGames member center saying the exact opposite. What we need now is a public clarification. This forum is where centers, iGames members or not, go for answers. So it is here that Mr. Dunkle should clarify. Especially since many are reporting that Valve is not responding to licensing requests. We all know he reads these boards, and this is not an unusual request. We simply cannot have different rules depending on who Mike is talking to. Perhaps there was a mis-communication. Perhaps within that month Valve changed their mind and didn\'t tell anybody. We won\'t know until Mike chimes in.' WHERE post_id = 598844 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I don\'t believe there is any miscommunication, its just the case that "Steam" choose not to answer because its not in their best interests to. To Whit, the older copies of HL Generations for Cyber cafes are "LEGAL" and are ok to be used with Steam. However, once you buy a copy from Vivendi universal publishing, the licence key has now been deleted by Steam, although according to the paperwork, we are entitled to use it. I have been speaking to so many people now, its beyond a joke, both my Solicitors and the legal Dept. of vivendi Universal publishing both say my licences are Valid, even Mr Dunkle admitted they were, (if they were not, I can assure you he would have sued me faster than you can say Steam). However, only Steam can issue new licences, hence the reason they are so quiet, So quiet in fact that after some 20 plus emails from me in 6 weeks, over a years worth of chasing by my local Cyber supplier and ten months of chasing by Vivendi universal Publishing, NO ONE HAS HAD A REPLY. The question..? are the licences Valid..? If so what is the new Key? If not, what am I being charged yearly for? This question has gone unanswered for so long its ridiculous, I am personally waiting for a reply to this question, and I have a feeling hell will freeze over before it is answered, the only thing I have no doubt on is that I SHALL be receiving yet another email from M dunkle stating using CS in a shop is illegal unless licences are for cibers, again I will provide all he asks for, and again once he has his proof, he will ignore me and hope I go away, like you. Well , I am waiting for a reply, I keep emailing weekly, and phoning 3 to 5 times a week, and always no reply, ALWAYS. But, soon the yearly charge for my CS licences will arrive, which is kinda funny, I have 37 legal licences, and only 12 work.. yet I am charged for 37, yet Steam refuse to acknowledge I have a claim, yet I am paying for the game, and accoriding to the paperwork supplied by Vivendi I am entitiled to use this software in a Cyber Shop. but the licence was issued by Sierra, but Steam refuse to honour that contract, choosing to ignore it. Well, let me put it this way, the clock is ticking, when the next bill arrives for my 37 copies, if I still have no reply, then my reply will be, to permanently remove Steam from my shop. I have just completely lost all faith in Steam, in Mike Dunkle and in their Customer Support, all I get is "Nothing", all I ever get as a reply is "Nothing" and all Steam seem to think of their clients both and and new is "Nothing". Steam.. so well named, a company so bloated in its own self worth, it is just full of hot air, vaporware to be blunt. Mr. Dunkle, if you are reading this.. please answer the question.. Are the Sierra issued licences for Cybers valid..? If not why are we being charged yearly for them..? and if they are valid.. why have you disabled the Vivendi Universal Publishing CD keys for Cybers and not re-issued new ones? Steam as a company have renaged on the licences as granted by Sierra, and simply hoping we will go away will have far more repercussions than you can imagine, for we will go, and not return. As Always, waiting for a reply. Signed on behalf of 1000\'s of Cibers Everywhere.' WHERE post_id = 599371 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'guys... we are talking business here! they are on business... but what any company around the world knows is to make their earning being fair. As I am in Brazil, my monthly fee is cheaper, but, dont thing it will be expensive, it will! my price per hour, in us$ is 1 dollar per hour... if the charge, in your case, was cheaper no one, as far as I see, would conplain. Everyone here knows about being legal and apreciate others work, but come on... 10 per month is almost a robery! as I said in other topic, I tried to move away from cs as soon as I notice that I was going to have another thing to pay monthly. did not work... people move away from my lan house (as cyber cafés as known here) they went to other cafés just to play CS... imagine 1 US per station per month! mine has 30 pcs... how many 30 pcs cybers around the world? 1000? 1000*30= 30000 per month 10000? 300000 per month 100k? 3.000.000 per month! only on the cyber café program! in any case, they can pay a few servers to validade accounts... site, support, and so on! i am not being greedy, i dont mind paying somtheing that I feel that is fair! i have pleasure to pay to someones work that makes mine easier! enough complaining guys! company policies! sooner or later another game will come! ever saw battlefield II? cool game! try some DC (Desert combat)! lol!\n\n__________________ Sorry.. CS is business... BF is fun!' WHERE post_id = 603614 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'This thread technically is not a debate as to wether or not the Steam program is a good deal. This thread is to allow Mike Dunkle to say wether or not Steam can be installed at centers that are not on the program so that people who have their own Steam accounts can use them there.' WHERE post_id = 603756 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by RevH This thread is to allow Mike Dunkle to say wether or not Steam can be installed at centers that are not on the program so that people who have their own Steam accounts can use them there. I just don\'t see Valve telling centers they can go ahead and install the software without paying for the priveledge. In March 2004, they claimed (on their cybercafe page) that they had 800-1000 centers (/forums/...;threadid=71458 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=71458)) signed up and paying $10 per month per machine with a minimum of 10 machines. They are making a minimum of $100 a month from 800 centers. That adds up to a million dollars a year in revenue from those game centers alone. Now, imagine if they told centers they could install the game for free for customers who already have accounts. What idiot game center owner would continue to pay the $100 a month. All the owner would have to do is tell their customers that they can play Counter Strike at their centers, but they have to buy their own personal accounts now before they can play. Unfortunately, I (along with most people) wouldn\'t run out and purchase an account just so we could play CS at the center we frequent. We would just play the games that do not require that we have our own accounts. On the other hand, if customers can play CS at the 800-1000 centers that are paying the cybercafe fees, think of how many of those customers do not have their own accounts, but decide to run out and buy a copy so they can play at home. I know I have run out and bought several games for home after I have played it at the center I go to. If only 4 or 5 customers a month at each of the 800-1000 centers buys a copy for home, that\'s about 50,000 game copies sold because of the influence of game centers. Valve needs to figure out how to get 10,000 or 100,000 game centers to go with their cybercafe program. Hey Valve, imagine if you had 100,000 centers paying $100 a month. Over $100 Million! What if you made it $20 per month per machine...that would be $200 Million. Yeah, that\'s the way to go....just be patient. With 800-1000 centers today and more joining everyday, it won\'t take that long to get to that 100,000 game center mark.' WHERE post_id = 606425 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Crucifingers In March 2004, they claimed (on their cybercafe page) that they had 800-1000 centers (/forums/...;threadid=71458 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=71458)) signed up and paying $10 per month per machine with a minimum of 10 machines. They are making a minimum of $100 a month from 800 centers. That adds up to a million dollars a year in revenue from those game centers alone. Just to clarify... 10 machines @ $10 a machine @ 800 centers is $960,000.00 But thats close to a Million. The fact of the matter is they are bringing in somewhere between: $960,000.00 to $1,200,000.00 a year off of thier current cyber client base and thats only if each location has 10 mcahines. I\'ve only been to two and they both had 50 plus machines. 800 locations with 50 machines = $4,800,000.00 Thats over 4 million a year. Cha-Ching!' WHERE post_id = 608310 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I am not attempting to debate how much money Valve can rake in by forcing centers to give them money or how sucky the game is or how Valve could make more money from people who run home and buy the game after playing at a center. While all those topics are valid, they have been discussed in other threads. This thread is really for one purpose, for Mike Dunkle to publicly say once and for all what Valve\'s stance is on making Steam available in a center to people who already have accounts. Mike has stated in person and on the phone that the Steam client can be installed so that people can use their own accounts. Recently he e-mailed a center the exact opposite response. I just want to know from Mike what Valve\'s current stance is.' WHERE post_id = 609420 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Dont mean to hijack your thread, but I think one Issue that is just blazing a light here, is that Mike Dunkle / Steam, just are NOT responding. That is pretty much the case in point, see the thread date, any one of us got a response yet? I know I haven\'t. I think the thread topic confused matters with the "response from Dunkle" requested, we are all beyond exasperation at waiting for a response. What gets me though is how the heck can Steam go to E3 and wax lyrical about their super this and superb that.. when they cant even manage to reply to a thread on their own forums, which is without doubt both clear as water, not full of profanities and asking some very straightforward and understandable questions. Next time I am asked for my views on Steam, I\'ll point the reporters to this website, and in particular to this thread, and use this as a perfect example of Steam customer care. Now I mention this, I am kicking myself as I had a newspaper guy here the other day, hmm, ill see if I can find his card, see if he is interested in the dark side of support.' WHERE post_id = 612404 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by RevH I am not attempting to debate how much money Valve can rake in by forcing centers to give them money or how sucky the game is or how Valve could make more money from people who run home and buy the game after playing at a center. While all those topics are valid, they have been discussed in other threads. This thread is really for one purpose, for Mike Dunkle to publicly say once and for all what Valve\'s stance is on making Steam available in a center to people who already have accounts. Mike has stated in person and on the phone that the Steam client can be installed so that people can use their own accounts. Recently he e-mailed a center the exact opposite response. I just want to know from Mike what Valve\'s current stance is. Understood... my point being with that kind of income they could invest in some quality support/customer service... Still no reply from MD?' WHERE post_id = 624124 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'NO. [] like I said, hell wil freeze over first.' WHERE post_id = 627078 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'MIKE! (I imagined myself yelling it like Kirk did for Khan in Wrath of Khan...man, am I a nerd)' WHERE post_id = 628903 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Khaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaan!!!! \'er, I mean Mike. old nerd here' WHERE post_id = 633301 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Give it up guys, he won\'t answer. If he wanted to then an answer would\'ve been posted by now . . .\n\n__________________ It seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.' WHERE post_id = 633320 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I gave up long ago on getting a quality reply on any level from valve on any subject... I quit kidding myself 3 months into steam. Not to mention the pre-steam years. Why do I keep posting. To further the proof that valve has no excuse.. They are getting a bad rap by their own hand.. not because people just want to Bi*ch, or have it in for them. There are a multitude of post requesting official assistance on any number of levels, they request this help in a polite manor. They are blatantly ignored... and there is NO EXCUSE! VALVE/STEAM you are alienating your customer/market share. The leather interior and silk underwear doesn\'t grow on trees.. Can you say disruption of revenue flow! MD or someone official... answer the question. You folks(sales/support) are loosing respect here.' WHERE post_id = 633442 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well Mr. Dunkle, you are back posting on the forums and still no response, yet sadly I don\'t seem to be going away. I don\'t see why this one is so difficult to answer. You\'ve answered this question many times in the past. I am guessing now that the e-mail the CyberCafe received was pure intimidation. A desperate move from a company that made a lot of promises about this program and kept very little, and now is growing concerned why more cafe\'s aren\'t immediately jumping on the band wagon. My guess is that you know that it is OK to allow people to use their own accounts in a center, and you know you don\'t have much legal ground to stand on concerning this issue. With no response from Mr. Dunkle, this is all I have to assume. I will not ask for an answer here again.' WHERE post_id = 659418 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Reply', post_text = 'In general, users can use their Steam accounts for personal use (non-commercial) at multiple locations (e.g. logging in at a cybercafé they may occasionally use or using it on their work computer and home computer). In short, the portability of a user\'s Steam account does not mean that commercial establishments like cybercafés can exploit our games without a license whether it be a tournament or pay for play. If indeed a user installs Steam on a cybercafé computer to access their account, you could allow an activity like this, but you would be required to erase the copy of the Valve products after that user logged off the system (through a program like DeepFreeze or the like) just like any other software that is installed by a customer that you do not have a license for. Mike\n\n__________________ Business Development and Cafe Operations' WHERE post_id = 662282 AND is_historical = 1;
