UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '3) Can you re-create it? may be this screen showing server side data (http://home.arcor.de/matrixstorm/files/cstrike/msmod0001.jpg) can help you. It shows data from a custom metamod plugin (i posted this one on the hlcoders list a while ago). As you can read in the text there is an headhitbox on the server but the client sees s.th. different. You can test this very simply for your self, just code an smal metamod plugin, that does an traceline from the players aim and shows the hitgroup etc.. In fact this bug occurs very often but in the most cases the difference is only like on the pic. This bug seems to be related to the following player movement: turning around (rotation) (when you\'re moving your mouse too look around). Also when starting on maps like aim_map players are sometimes not updated Please don\'t apologize about the doted lines, this was another feature of the plugin that has nothing to do with the traceline one. The height is not draw correctly, but the other coordinates are correct. If i can help with some thing else let me know (i.e. a demo with plugin running). 1) how often have you seen it? using the plugin you can see this bug in every round. without plugin you would only recoginize the difference 2 times a week (when there are huge ones, player facing the wall, fraggin you). this may be not the case on non DSL connections, because on modem this bug may often feel like lag or latency! 2) When did you see it first? sry, don\'t know but must have been before 2004-03-12 (YMD) However, I have not seen this bug again yet on the new 05.03.04 and 04.28.04 updates! 4) Were you runnning custom skins? no, never! 5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod? CS' WHERE post_id = 590194 AND is_historical = 1;
