UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'AWP Uproar, Suggestions to Fix this Problem', post_text = 'This is taken from the GotFrag Community News, where there are several other threads condemning the updated AWP. www.gotfrag.com (http://www.gotfrag.com) quote:Well, I was going to post on the steam forums about my compliants towards the new AWP situation. Now, before I started reading the steam forums I wasn\'t really to concerned, but I see alot of people posting with explainations like this... "The AWP was bugged, you shouldn\'t have been able to quickswitch a fire like you could, it was good to fix it." Now I can understand taking out the ability to "quickswitch" between your deagle/awp as fast as it was...but added like a 2 second delay before you can even fire?...thats absolutely ridiculous. Another common post was.. "This was needed so that the leet players wouldn\'t take advantage of the other players." Wow...how about finding a server, or starting a server that doesn\'t allow awp if ANYONE is going to say something this stupid. Also, is it fair that there is a 2 second delay on the AWP, but if you switch between ANY OTHER GUN there is no delay what so ever...so running around with a pistol with any other gun, then you run into someone switch to your gun, you now have a 2 second headstart on shooting someone if they have an awp, instead of any other gun... Its the dumbest update I\'ve seen in a very long time. Most updates I\'ve been able to handle, and this one I\'d handle to, I just decided never to awp anymore, its pointless, its almost a negative effect now, you miss that first shot and you are a sitting duck. After reading the Valve forums, and reading some very very newbish post, I got fed up and decided to make a post here. I tried registering for the forums on Steam to make my post but it didn\'t seem to work....go figure "its steam"... Anyway...how does Valve/Steam/nub users find it fair, that you now hae a 2 second delay on the AWP shot when switching between pistol/gun, but you don\'t have that delay on any other gun, even funnier NONE of the other sniper type guns with zoom ability... Steam, I actually liked what CS was....until this updated, it wasn\'t as bad as everyone said...this update just made those 47 year olds that still play CS, with there own server, statsme, and every wav file imaginable on their server, very very happy people, cause those are the type of people that love when steam comes out with the shield, and now...this AWP 2 second delay. As you can see, the competetive community is seething from this update. Sure, it may make the newbies happy, along with the recreational gamers, but there is a way to make both parties happy, the non-competetive and the competetive gamers! Here is another letter on the GotFrag? Community News www.gotfrag.com (http://www.gotfrag.com) quote:Dear Steam, Are you tired of having so many people complain about the changes you make to Counter-Strike? One of the reasons Counter-Strike is as popular as it is today. Is because it\'s different from other games in the aspect that skill has to be developed to be very good. Which is the reason some of us have been around for years, we\'re constantly trying to develop new techniques to become better. Lately though, it seems that the time taken to develop this skill is being nulled out by the fact that the game is becomming much more friendly to the newer players. I have a suggestion for you. To alleviate some of the whining every time there\'s an update. Consider having two different Game Modes. I\'m sure implementation of this wouldn\'t take much time or effort. Because obviously you can change large things in one simple patch. One of the modes I\'m suggesting would be for the professional audience. Those who compete online and on LAN for money as well as reputation. Changes to this mode of the game can be specifically directed to the professional audience. After proper investigation has been completed, changes can be made to this mode. This can help to alleviate some of the whining that is generally accompanied with each update. The second mode could be the "Normal Gameplay Mode" whos main audience would be those who take Counter-Strike less seriously. The gamers that tend to only play Counter-Strike once or twice a week just for fun. It seems that the changes that have been implemented in the most recent updates of Counter-Strike, have been specifically for the non-professional audience. Which is understandable, because the bulk of the community aren\'t avid Counter-Strikers like myself. To sum it all up, have two different CS modes. One for the pro\'s the other for the newbies... this way you can appeal to ALL of your Counter-Strike audience, and peace will be restored to the CS community once again! Sincerely, meridian | plat #meridian If you visit www.gotfrag.com, (http://www.gotfrag.com,) you will see there is an uproar over this latest update. These are just a few sample letters, and I have no doubt you will see more letters from very profound gamers, such as shaGuar with his money article.' WHERE post_id = 554976 AND is_historical = 1;
