UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Bunnyjumping was a herritage from the quake engine. It was not an exploit, since: Half-life was not based 100% on the Quake 1 engine. The Quake 1 engine is the only Quake engine to date that had bunnyjumping that wasn\'t intended. In Quake 2, rocketjumping and strafejumping (bunny if you so please) was a know feature and Part of the game. Counter Strike was based on a game where bunnyjumping WASN\'T an exploit. Removeing it from the game was a Design decition! Get you facts right next time...' WHERE post_id = 584903 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by krokko You cannot state that my argument isn\'t valid. If you wish to do so, prove it to me. It seems to me you\'re avoiding my points. What I wanted was someone to prove me wrong on all my points and no just the moronic "you\'re wrong" Tell me then: If it were an exploit, why was only one weapon fixed? Makes no sense to me And if it were an exploit, why wasn\'t it changed until a whorde of noobs who couldn\'t cope with the skill in it started whining on 50 pages in these forums? Please TELL ME THAT Wow, you\'re dense. 3-4 people just proved your argument invalid through comparing it to absurdity. Reread the page. The noscope exploit only applies to very slow ROF weapons with no zoomed crosshair. Only the AWP and Scout fall under that category. And you\'ve got it backward; it wasn\'t until after the change that noobs who couldn\'t cope with the real skill involved in using the AWP started whining. It was an exploit, because it took advantage of something that was not intended to be possible in the game. So was bunnyhopping.' WHERE post_id = 584904 AND is_historical = 1;
