UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CZ Mission Packs List', post_text = 'This is the old CZ Mission Packs List thread, please go here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=119505) for the new one [] (mark 3) Also, the list is now hosted online at www.sandwiregames.com (http://www.sandwiregames.com) - this is where this Mission Packs project will eventually be managed. Here\'s a list of all the CZ mission packs I\'ve found so far, in rough order of release. If you know of any I\'ve missed, or have new ones, reply and I\'ll edit them into my first post in order to keep things orderly... Name: The Counter-Strike: Condition Zero Mission Pack Author: Turtle Rock Studios Website: http://www.turtlerockstudios.com/ (http://www.turtlerockstudios.com/), http://www.counter-strike.net/ (http://www.counter-strike.net/), http://cs-conditionzero.com/ (http://cs-conditionzero.com/) and / (/) In-Game Name: CONDITION ZERO Directory Name: TurtleRockCounterTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Release Info/Changelog: Updated every time CZ is patched - go here (/platform/update_history/Condition%20Zero.html) for details. Description: This is the official pack - it comes with CZ. As such, it includes the 18 official maps that came out when CZ was released - but none of the official ones which have appeared since. My main issue with this pack is that it appears twice in the pack list... Bugs/Glitches: - Appears twice in the list - The web link is wrong (does not need the /CZ/ extension, and there are more appropriate sites as well) - There is no in-game link to czmissiondoc.rtf Name: Havok\'s Terrorist Mission Pack Author: Havok Website: http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/ (http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/) (nothing about the pack though) In-Game Name: Havoks T Missions Directory Name: havokTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/Havokstpack.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 05/01/04. Installation: When installing, use the readme, but don\'t follow what it says about the "CareerGame****" files (**** being the difficulty level) - rename the "CareerGame****" files to just say "****", and then put them in the MissionPacks\\havokTerrorist area with the other files. Also you may want to delete the save file that comes with this pack. Description: The first ever pack. Everything is the same as in Turtle Rock\'s campaign, but you are a terrorist. Things start to get tricky when you have to get a kill with a CT gun, but it gets impossible when you have to rescue a hostage... Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name) - No pack description in the pack selection menu (it just says #Career_MissionPackt instead) - The website link has not been changed - Missions on easy difficulty involving rescuing hostages are impossible - Missions on easy difficulty involving using CT weapons are hard/impossible - Certain files are named wrong, and must be renamed (see above) Name: The Terrorist Mission Pack Author: Anders Konradsen Website: http://www.kenand666.tk/ (http://www.kenand666.tk/) (nothing about the pack though) In-Game Name: Terrorist Missions v0.2 Directory Name: Terrorist (BigDaddyK changed this to KonradsenTerrorist when he installed, you can if you like too) Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_dust2_cz, ds_italy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_torn_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_airstrip_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_stadium_cz and as_tundra Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/terrorist.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 0.2, released on 05/06/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v0.0 - Changed the original pack to a T pack v0.1 - Minor bugs fixed - Added a new overview.tga v0.2 - New story line - New map order - Eddit bug fixed (mispelled name, should be Eddie) - Minor bugs fixedInstallation: Unzip all of this to your czero directory - apart from the Terrorist folder, which you should put in your czero\\MissionPacks directory (like it says in the readme) Description: This is what the Havok\' pack should have been like. The new missions mean you don\'t get \'rescue the hostage\' missions, but \'plant the bomb\' missions instead - much better than Havok\'s pack. This is the first pack to use a map that are not the 18 in Turtle Rock\'s campaign - as_tundra Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The National Insecurity Mission Pack Author: D-Link Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: National Insecurity Tour of Duty Directory Name: NationalInsecurityMissionPack Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_dust2_cz, ds_italy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_torn_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_airstrip_cz, cs_downed_cz and de_piranesi_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://mysite.verizon.net/res1g4li/NationalInsecurityMissionPack.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second version, updated 05/04/04. You can still get the first version here (http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/NIMissionpack.zip). Installation: Put everything in your NationalInsecurityMissionPack folder, then put that in your MissionPacks folder Description: Basically a CT pack with new missions, but the same maps as in the Turtle Rock campaign. Bugs/Glitches: - The website link has not been changed - The pack description refers to the maps in their old order, not their new one Name: -=[Sj]=-\'s Original CS Mission Pack Author: -=[Sj]=- Ice Killer Website: http://www.clansj.com/ (http://www.clansj.com/) In-Game Name: ORIGINAL CS MISSION PACK V03 Directory Name: OriginalCS Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust, de_dust2, cs_office, de_prodigy, de_italy, de_inferno, cs_militia, cs_havana, de_cbble, de_aztec, de_torn, de_airstrip, de_train, de_vertigo, de_survivor, de_nuke, cs_seige and cs_747 Download Link:You can get the full install here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/MissionPackv03.zip), or you can get the v0.2-v0.3 patch here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/quickfixv03.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 0.3, released 05/21/04 and last revised 05/22/04. You can still get version 0.2 here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/MissionPackv02.zip) and version 0.1 here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/MissionPackv01.zip) if you want, just for reference purposes. The goals were changed and improved between the three releases, and a custom bot skin was added between the second and third releases. Installation: Inside this zip is an exe - just point it towards your Condition Zero directory when installing and it does the work for you [] Description: Instead of the CZ maps, this pack uses 18 of the original CS maps, hence the pack\'s name. It is also the first pack to use custom bot models. This is well worth getting. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description)' WHERE post_id = 587046 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: "The Balancing Guide" Terrorist Mission Pack Author: BigDaddyK Website: There isn\'t one Directory Name: It doesn\'t have one, but I put it in BalancedTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrrorist Download Link: You can get it here (http://mysite.verizon.net/res1g4li/t-balance.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 1.1, relesed on 05/07/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Readme created - CareerBotProfile.DB was editted to smooth over T teammate imbalances - The T \'Characters\' list was amended (the Eddie/Eddit name mispelling bug again)Installation: Everything is in place for you to unzip it to MissionPacks\\Nameofyourchoicehere Description: This is not a pack, and cannot be played. It\'s actually some better balanced terrorist bots, created for any other pack-creator to use if they wish. BigDaddyK sugests you put the files here into another pack\'s directory, and see how it affects gameplay. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The Worst Case Scenario Mission Pack Author: Blue Dog Anchorite Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: WORST CASE SCENARIO Directory Name: WorstCaseScenario Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_downed_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_nuke, cs_siege, de_cbble_cz, de_piranesi_cz, cs_estate, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, cs_backalley, de_vertigo, cs_assualt, de_train, de_fastline_cz, de_office_cz, cs_747 and as_oilrig Download Link: Welcome to Geocitiesville [] You need two files for this - this one (http://www.**************/tolgeros/WorstCaseScenario.zip) and this one (http://www.**************/tolgeros/WCSwidemaps.zip). You need to copy the 2 links, paste them into your browser and replace the stars with geocities .com (minus the space)... Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 05/05/04. Installation: Like downloading this pack, installing it is not as easy as it should be. Place the vga files, the db file and thumbnail.tga (all from WorstCaseScenario.zip) into czero\\MissionPacks\\WorstCaseScenario\\ Put the other files in WorstCaseScenario.zip into czero\\gfx\\thumbnails\\maps\\ Finally, put all the files in WCSwidemaps.zip into czero\\gfx\\thumbnails\\maps_wide\\ Description: This pack uses a mixture of the original CS maps and the new CZ maps. It is not a bad pack. Bugs/Glitches: - Installation is difficult (two parts when there could be one, geocities) - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Shadow Operations Mission Pack Author: D-Link Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: Shadow Operations Directory Name: ShadowOps Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_drugbust, de_train, cs_nightstrike, cs_747, as_oilrig, cs_estate, cs_assualt, de_iraqi, cs_siege, cs_backalley, de_vertigo, de_nuked, de_suntower, de_mill, as_palace, de_ruins, de_scud and de_museum Download Link: You can get it here (ftp://public:content@65.39.204.184/COURTESY/GAME_RELATED/CZERO/MISSION_PACKS/D_MONKEY/shadowops.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 06/05/04. Installation: Extract it all to your czero directory - except for the ShadowOps folder, which should be moved into your MissionPacks folder - and the botpacklist.db file, which needs to then be put into the ShadowOps folder. Description: This was D-Link\'s second pack and the first mission pack to feature wholly custom CS maps, but as a result is much much bigger than the ones which came before it. It is still worth getting though. Bugs/Glitches: - The website link has not been changed - Some of the maps included in the download are just renamed versions of CS maps - so don\'t need to be included at all Name: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg]\'s Mission Pack Author: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg] Website: http://www.mkg-clan.tk/ (http://www.mkg-clan.tk/) In-Game Name: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg] maps mission pack Directory Name: Kidd-Eggmissions Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_militia_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_office_cz, cs_mortal, cs_rats5, de_dock, de_rats6 and de_schoolke Download Link: You can get it here (http://home.filternet.nl/~j.van.baalen/files/KEmissions.zip). Release Info/Changelog: Released on 05/08/04, this is the first and only version. Installation: Everything is already in the right directory, so unzip it straight. Description: This pack uses a mixture of 5 custom CS missions and the CZ missions. A good pack. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Operation Black Sun Mission Pack Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/) In-Game Name: Black Sun Directory Name: BlackSun Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust2_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_tides_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_cbble_cz, cs_militia_cz, cs_italy_cz and as_oilrig Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/downloads/blacksun1-4.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the fifth release, released on 05/20/04. You can still download v1.0 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/downloads/blacksun1-0.zip), v1.1 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/downloads/blacksun1-1.zip), v1.2 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/downloads/blacksun1-2.zip) and v1.3 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/blacksun1-3.zip) though, just for reference purposes. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Simplified install - Some unneeded files removed - Added botprofile.db v1.2 - Added custom names for teammates - Updated bot weapon preferences v1.3 - Completely custom bot file created for CTs and Ts - bot settings updated - NOTE: This version is a beta version - easy, normal, hard and expert modes are all the same for now v1.4 - Renamed from \'Black Sun 2\' to \'Black Sun\' - Readded different missions for different difficulty settings (should now be more challenging) - Changed the number of missions needed to win back to default (3)Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory Description: This pack doesn\'t contain any custom maps, but it is very balanced and well worth getting. The Version 2.0 is in the works at the moment. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The S.I.J. Clan\'s Terrorist Mission Pack Author: The S.I.J. (Japanese) Clan Website: http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/ (http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/) (it\'s in Japanese) In-Game Name: T\'s Mission Directory Name: sij_t_mission Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/tool/sij_t_mission.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 1.3, released on 05/09/04. Version 1.0 was the initital conversion to terrorists, 1.1 changed the goals slightly, 1.2 changed/removed missions requiring the use of CT-only weapons and 1.3 removed missions involving hostage rescue. Installation: Just put it straight into your Condition Zero directory [] Description: While this doesn\'t have any new maps, some missions have changed. The map order is the same though. It is similair to the Terrorist Mission Pack, in fact. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name and description) - The website link is invalid' WHERE post_id = 620325 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: Tony-Strike: Condition Hawk - Blue Version Author: Rip3001 Website: http://www.*******.com/rip3001/tsblue/ (http://www.*******.com/rip3001/tsblue/) (replace the stars with geocities .com (minus the space)) In-Game Name: Tony-Strike: Condition Hawk - Blue Version Directory Name: Tony-Strike Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_vegas, aim_map_usp, cs_old_office, cs_mansion, cs_rio, de_dust2_cz, de_nuke, cs_pacman, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, awp_city, de_rotterdam, cs_downed_cz, aim_dust2003, de_skud_2k1, de_morningstar_csc, fy_snow and de_vertigo Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.kormagraphics.com/tonystrike_missionpack.zip). Also, you need to get the 1.2 patch here (http://www.angelfire.com/hero/ripstuff/tsbv_patch1-2.zip) (for the patch, you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third release, released on 06/16/04. You can still get 1.1 here (http://www.angelfire.lycos.com/hero/ripstuff/tonystrike_patch_1-1.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). Also, you can get Rip3001\'s custom navs here (http://www.angelfire.com/hero/ripstuff/rip3001_nav_files_vol01.zip) if you want (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). A Red Version is coming soon, as is another secret Tony-Strike project... Installation: Just put it in your e-mail directory. Description: This pack features 12 non-standard maps and five new skins, making it the biggest yet. It is also the hardest yet, by far. Bugs/Glitches: - The website is on Geocities (the link shows up as stars in the Steam Users Forums) - Gramatical errors (pack description) - Some users have reported the game crashing on cs_rio and other levels. This is due to incomplete nav files for the bots. If you experience this bug, carry out the following steps: 1. Load the map up in either TOD or multiplayer with bots and then open your console. 2. Type bot_stop 1 then bot_nav_edit 1 then bot_nav_analize If, having done the above, the map still crashes, report it here in this thread. Thanks to Rip3001 for the fix [] Name: The Crimson Ice Mission Pack Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/) In-Game Name: Crimson Ice Directory Name: CrimsonIce Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust2_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_tides_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_cbble_cz, cs_militia_cz, cs_italy_cz and de_vostok_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/downloads/crimsonice1-2.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third release, released on 06/04/04. You can still download v1.0 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/downloads/crimsonice1-0.zip) and v1.1 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/downloads/crimsonice1-1.zip) though, just for reference purposes. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Changed so that you get teammates earlier (3rd map instead of 4th) v1.2 - Removed as_oilrig - Added de_vostok and de_sienna - Increased reaction time for all bots (makes everything slightly easier)Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory Description: Was the first to make use of Sienna and Vostok, and features new missions as well. A fairly solid CT pack, designed to be the opposite of Black Sun. This one\'s very difficult... Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The Terrorist Missions Mission Pack Author: Napos Website: http://napos.axred.net/terroristmissions.html (http://napos.axred.net/terroristmissions.html) In-Game Name: Terrorist Missions Directory Name: MissionsTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://napos.axred.net/TerroristMissions.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second release, released on 05/31/04. You can still get the beta release here (http://napos.axred.net/TerroristMissionsBeta1.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your email directory. Description: Much like the other Terrorist missions pack, only IMO slightly worse. The author has removed the goals which are impssible for terrorists, but not added new ones (e.g. Plant the bomb...) Bugs/Glitches: - The pack name used is already taken by another pack - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Counter-Strike: Evolutions Mission Pack Author: Crotch Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: CS Evolutions 1.1: Counter-Terrorist and CS Evolutions 1.1 - Terrorist Directory Name: CS Evolutions - Counter-Terrorist and CS Evolutions - Terrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Both Map List/Order: cs_assualt_beta1, de_dust_beta4, cs_mansion_beta1, de_inferno_old, cs_desert_beta1, de_vegas_beta7, cs_office_beta7, de_nuke_beta5, cs_747_beta6, de_train_beta5, cs_siege_beta7-1, de_prodigy_beta5, cs_estate_beta7, de_cbble_beta7, cs_militia_beta3, de_aztec_beta7, de_aztec_1-3 and de_aztec_1-6 Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.endlessrayne.com/~crotch/CS_Evolutions_1-0.zip). You also need to get the 1.1a patch from here (http://www.endlessrayne.com/~crotch/CS_Evolutions_1-0_to_1-1a.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third release, released on 07/14/2004. Installation: Extract it to your Condition Zero directory. You may want to be aware though - it is set to give you a custom background/startup music. If you do not want these, delete the \'music\' and \'resources\' sub-folders. Description: This is a very big pack, with a lot of custom maps. It has various versions of the same maps (e.g. aztec from 1.3 and aztec from 1.6). I recommend you get it, if only to see how the maps have changed over time. It is also the first pack to have both a Terrorist and a Counter-Terrorist section. There is a planned patch to iron out some of the bugs. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name) - Gramatical errors (pack description) - Click here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&postid=662696#post662696) for several bugs - In the terrorist\'s part of the pack in easy, you cannot select de_cbble_beta7 in the list, and its\' thumnail shows up as that of cs_siege_beta7-1 - Several people are reporting bugs with this pack, meaning once installed none of the TODs will work - it appears to be due to grammatical errors in the coding Name: The Operation X: Code Omega Mission Pack Author: -=[Sj]=-Ice Killer Website: http://www.clansj.com/ (http://www.clansj.com/) In-Game Name: OPERATION X: CODE OMEGA v1 Directory Name: OperationX-CODE-OMEGA Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_shogun_final, de_avalley, de_priory, de_aztec2 (unofficial verson), cs_pine, cs_tibet, cs_pipeline, de_indust, de_legato, de_cstle, cs_ciudad, de_tartarico, de_karnak, de_luxor, de_citadel, de_vine, de_plaka and de_celtic Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.liveice.com/download/OXCO.zip). There are also now three small patches - you only need the third one from here (http://www.liveice.com/download/fixv3.zip), which fix some bugs and also lower the difficulty settings. Release Info/Changelog: This is the fourth release, released on 06/20/2004. Here is a changelog:quote:v0.0 - Release v0.1 - Lowered the bots\' start from 6 to 4 - Lowered the bots\' agression - Fixed misspelling on the Overview.vdf file - Tweaked the bot profile a bit v0.2 - Fixed an issue with a bot not buying a \'Galil\' or \'IDF\' on the first level on Easy v0.3 - Fixed bots not buying the MAC 10 - Added as_tundra.wad, which was missing from the installer beforeInstallation: Inside the zips are installers. Just point them towards your Condition Zero directory [] Description: This is a very big pack - it weighs in at a hefty 324MB unzipped! It contains custom maps and is the first to feature fully custom skins - every bot has a unique skin! Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description)' WHERE post_id = 620330 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: The Black Sun 2: Reign Of Terror Mission Pack Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/) In-Game Name: Black Sun 2: Reign of Terror (CT) and Black Sun 2: Reign of Terror (T) Directory Name: BlackSun2 and BlackSun2CT Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Both Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_builder_yard, de_canal_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_italy_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_torn_cz, de_tides_cz, de_vostok_cz, cs_creetor_cz and de_plaka Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/blacksun2_v1-1.zip), and then put the 1.2 patch on top here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/blacksun2_v1-1-1-2patch.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third version, released on 06/19/2004. You can still get 1.0 here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/blacksun2_v1-0.zip) and the 1.1 patch here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/BlackSun2/BlackSun2_v1-0-1-1patch.zip) if you want, for reference. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Removed some unnecessary .tga files (pointed out by BigDaddyK) - Fixed the directory of the team-selection screen thumbnails (they will now display the new models) v1.2 - Fixes an error on de_canal_cz map that disallowed it to run.Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory. You can view the readme online here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/readme_v1-2.html). Description: This is one of the best and most solid packs out there. You can now only select ten bots, meaning that you get to know the bots better. The pack uses a selection of standard and well-picked custom maps, meaning it\'s great fun to play. The pack is also regularly patched, which is good. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The Counter-Strike: Condition Zero (REMIX) Mission Pack Author: peterchen620 Website: http://peterchen620.proboards15.com/index.cgi (http://peterchen620.proboards15.com/index.cgi) In-Game Name: Counter-strike: Conditon Zero (REMIX) Directory Name: czremix Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, de_corruption_cz, de_vostok_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, cs_office_cz, de_tides_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_truth_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_fastline_cz and cs_torn_cz. Download Link: You can get it here (http://peterchen620.orcon.net.nz/czmissionpack/czremix_1.0.zip), with the 1.1 patch here (http://peterchen620.orcon.net.nz/czmissionpack/czremix_1.0-1.1.zip). You must go \'Save target as...\' to get them, otherwise it comes up as being corrupt or invalid (that is what I found anyway). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second version, released on 07/18/2004. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation - Removed cs_militia_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_chateau_cz - Added de_truth_cz, de_corruption_cz, de_vostok_cz, de_sienna_cz - Decreased the reaction time and increased the skill of the enemy bots on Expert Mode. - Increased the reaction time and decreased the skill of the enemy bots on Easy Mode. - Deleted and re-added newer tasks - Added New CZ Model GFX (Thanks to SteelV []) v1.1 - Removed all Spetsnaz Models (In the Bot Selection) - Removed all Militia Models for Terriosts - Improved tasks to be alot more LESS fustrating and easier to complete - Fixed an issue with de_corruption_cz, preventing it from running - Changed Normal.vdf to change the required number of kills on one goal from 45 to 25 - Fixed the EddiT typo - Removed Weasel as there were too many terrorist bots (9 to 8)Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero directory. Description: This pack has a geniusly simple idea. Since release, several new maps have come out officially on top of the original 18. All peterchen620 has done (apart from changing objectives, difficulties etc) is swapped the old for the new. Not only does this mean that some of these maps are in a pack for the first time and that all the maps are of high quality, but it also means that the installer is incredibly small, while the pack is still very different from the offical one. This makes the name very appropriate, as the pack seems like a continuation of the offical one. Taking a leaf out of Tony-Strike\'s book, this pack is very hard though, so beware... Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name) - Gramatical errors (pack description) That\'s 18 mission packs so far [] (including the official one) Below are any tools designed specifically to aid the creation of such map packs (well, OK, there is only one such tool at the moment): Name: The RND Mission Pack Creator Author: Ross and Andromeda Website: http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/ (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/) Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version, released on 05/16/04. Download Link: You can get the installer here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/setup.exe) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). You computer needs to be able to read Delphi in order to use it, however, so if it doesn\'t work immediately, get this (http://www.infojet.cz/download/files/qtintf.exe) and extract it to your C:\\WINDOWS\\system\\ folder [] Installation: Install the application to your Condition Zero directory. You can also get some sample thumbnails (the pictures which appear by the map names when selecting a map to play) for some maps. Get some awp_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/AWP_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") , some as_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/AS_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") , some cs_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/CS_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") and some de_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/DE_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). Put these dlls in your czero directory. Then, when you run the application, you can go to \'Library Images\', select the directory as your Condition Zero directory, and extract each of the thumbnails to the correct place, ready for your map pack. Description: Personally I wouldn\'t bother with this. Some of the thumbnails are handy to have, but due to the poor english of the creators this is in fact harder to use than czmissiondoc.rtf (the text file Cliffe made on how to create map packs). Get it for the thumbnails, but don\'t use it for the actual coding... Bugs/Glitches: - Grammatical errors make this almost unusable - Could be more straightforward to use - Is not actually needed ([]) That\'s one pack creator []' WHERE post_id = 620336 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Also, here are any Deleted Scenes maps currently availlable: Name: Swamps Of Zambia Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_swamp (cz_swamp1, cz_swamp2 and cz_swamp3) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, released on 05/01/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_swamp.zip). You can also get the source for it if you want, here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_swamp_ent_src.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_swamp1 in the console. Description: An excellent map, made by one of Ritual\'s mappers, so it is very profesionally done - indistinguishable from the official maps. The map sees you first trying to stop terrorists blowing up a railway line, and then you must rescue hostgaes they have captured. My only complaint is that to get to it you have to use the console, and it isn\'t on the World Map - but there is nothing the author can do about this. Bugs/Glitches: - Some terrorists are sometimes inivisble at one point near the end of the mission Name: Bloody Rubble Author: abalone Website: http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/ (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/) Map List/Order: rubble (rubble, rubble1, rubble2, rubble3, rubble4 and rubble5) Release Info/Changelog: This is the second release, released on 05/19/04. Download Link: You can get it here (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/rubble.zip). Installation: Put the maps folder in your czeror folder, then put the graphs folder in your czeror\\maps folder. This is where it ends for people who bought CZ in a shop - but if you bought it over Steam, you must then also download this (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/steamwads.zip) and extract it to your czeror directory. Description: This is not as professionally done as Swamp - there are no custom sound files, or event sequences. The map feels like it has less atmosphere as well. It is also harder to install for people who bought CZ over Steam. Furthermore, it is much harder to play - in places almost insanely hard. I got to this one bit where I found myself with 10 hp, no bullets and facing 2 guys with LAWs. Despite the difficulty, however, it was fun to play through, and well worth getting. Bugs/Glitches: - Harder to install for people who bought CZ over Steam (see above) - At one point I got onto a roof I shouldn\'t have, and could see over the edge of the map Name: Terrorist Retaliation Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_retaliation (cz_retaliation2 and cz_retaliation) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, and it was released on 07/12/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_retaliation.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_retaliation in the console. Description: Again from Kiltron, this map is the first to be played from the Terrorist perspective, breaking new grounds. Set in Scotland, you play a member or the Real IRA trying to rescue a botched mission, whilst fighting the SAS. Like Swamp, this mission features a strong atmosphere, and is as professionally done as the official maps. Well worth a play [] Bugs/Glitches: - Sometimes, the hostages call you \'commander\'. This seems a bit inappropriate. - There is one room inside where it rains. This may be intentional ceiling dripping, but does not seem like it to me. - Sometimes the enemies forget they are Counter-Terrorists now and think they are Terrorists, so start shooting each other. Kiltron knows about this, but does not know how to fix it. - At some points you must press a button to move a crate, which will move back after a certain period of time. On the second of these occasions, pressing the button again does not re-move the crate. Also, it is possible to get stuck on top of this crate. Name: Runaway Trains Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_trainrun (cz_trainrun2 and cz_trianrun) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, and it was released on 07/30/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_trainrun.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_trainrun in the console. Description: Kiltron\'s third release, this map reminds me of a bit in Poke646 and a Sven Co-op custom map - you\'re on two parallel moving trains, and you must move down them both, informing your collegues of hostage locations, defusing warheads (:P) and eventually stopping the trains. This was a pretty tough map - I blew all my health and ammo at the start, and more wasn\'t very readily forecoming. At one point you must take down a helicopter, and I felt that some people might not have enough ammo to do that at that stage of the level, which I thought was harsh. The time limit of 15 minutes isn\'t too tight, but you do have to be aware of it - time limits haven\'t been used much before, and here it adds a feeling of panic whilst playing the map. The foggy atmosphere fitted perfectly, and despite being under 15 minutes (:P) I feel that this is one of the better maps by far. Bugs/Glitches: None That\'s four DS maps [] Coming Soon: - v0.4 of the Original CS Mission Pack (might not be happening now) - Crimson Ice 2 - Tony-Strike: Red Version - New secret Tony-Strike project - Pancak3\'s aim mission pack - willover\'s mission pack (might not be happening now) - Operation: Lone Wolf (peterchen) - New Shadow Ops pack (might not be happening now) - Mooshi\'s rats mission pack - It Ain\'t Easy Bein A T/CT, by 1nev1table - The Loner Mission Pack (peterchen) - CS Evolutions 1.4 (done, waiting for me to update the thread) - Extended Duty, by BigDaddyK (done, waiting for me to update the thread) - chessclubreject\'s Skrivan Mission Pack - chessclubreject\'s Training Mission Pack - DS map: Death From Above, made by Kiltron - you can get a video of it here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/dfa_sneakpeak01.zip) - DS map: Urban Ruins, by abalone - you can see the website here (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/urban.htm) - DS map: Frost Mission, by Snake18 - CZ DS .fgd, as created by Kiltron :P Have I missed a released pack/DS map? Maybe you are creating a pack/know of a pack in creation that is not on the above list. Or maybe you have found a bug which is not on the list (I\'m looking at BigDaddyK here - he\'s good at finding bugs). If so, please reply and tell me all about it, so I can edit it in... Continued in my next post...' WHERE post_id = 620339 AND is_historical = 1;
