UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Maxey Even if we all had a super uber computers that run all games at 5000 FPS with all settings at insane, we are still limited to the refresh rate of our screens. If you have a PC that runs HL2 at steady 100 FPS at 1024 x 768, but a screen that only supports 75 Hz at that resolution, then you\'re screwed, because 35 FPS get wasted. cl_showfps 1 with developer 1 on and fps_max set to 2000 shows that I have around 200-300fps in CS and I only have a monitor with a refresh rate of 75. The correct thing to say would be "You wouldn\'t see the difference between 100 and 75 unless you turned v-sync off, when then it probably wouldn\'t matter because above 60 you really can\'t tell the difference"\n\n__________________ Chieftec Server Chassis w/ side window, Silver Abit NF7-S *Nvidia and Abit split up..:(* AMD Athlon XP 2500+ Overclocked to 3200+ (about 2.2Ghz) 512MB of PC3200 DDR RAM ATi Radeon 9600XT 120GB 7200rpm 8mb cache Maxtor HDD' WHERE post_id = 642331 AND is_historical = 1;
