UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'IMPORTANT: For Those With Input Lag Problems  **Fixed Update**', post_text = 'I was having problem with my CS and CZ with some strange mouse -key board lag... The user phluid started a post about it... /forums/...;threadid=65356 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=65356) I was about to trash my cs and somone had said that all they did to fix the problem was .. --- This setup is for Windows XP --- Hit CTRL-ALT-DELET keys go to Processes Tab . You will see a long list of programs that are running.. Look for Steam.exe Right click on it and go to SET PRIORITY .... Set it to LOW and your game will work great, back too my 4:1 ratio like the old days!! Just want to say thanks to phluid and all the people that replayed to his post as I joined here just to say THANK!!!!!!! Too bad steam customers are doing all the work!' WHERE post_id = 642286 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'WOW!! Thanks for starting a new thread and posting the fix. I had read about this fix previously in the forums, but it seemed to have random cases of it working so I ignored it, but it works great for me. Now I won\'t have to turn DirectSound on and off. Thanks.' WHERE post_id = 642728 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Strange fix. Low priority? Input devices typically are running on real-time I do believe, sooo... [] Oh well. A fix is a fix!' WHERE post_id = 642742 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Indeed it works!!!! ATTN: There really needs to be an option to set this, judging from the previous threads there are many many people with this problem and having to ctrl-alt-del to change the priority of of hl.exe is a pain in the [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color]!!!' WHERE post_id = 645713 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Ok, well here\'s what I\'ve found as a problem with this solution. When I set the priority of Steam.exe to low, I find that I will get occassional lags while I\'m playing which is not due to lags(pretty sure about this b/c it\'s periodic but consistent). This isn\'t that big of a problem b/c when it lags, if I\'m moving my mouse during the lag, when the lag is over, the mouse ends up where I expect it, so I have not that big of a problem with this, it\'s just like online lag. Another problem I\'m having is that if I alt+tab out of steam, one of the best features about steam, then go back to CS, the sound gets REALLY bad. As in it\'s barely audible, the sound quality is down, and there\'s crackles alll the time. I didn\'t have that much of a problem with the DXDiag fix, so I think I will go back to that for now. Although that is a bit more tedious, it\'s not much more than the priority fix since you have to set the priority each time you reboot and there was no problems at all with gameplay. I really hope Valve gets off their asses and figure out what the hell the problem is. I mean, I understand the game is over 5 yrs old and they got more pressing matters at hand *cough*Half Life 2*cough* but whatever development team that has been working on Steam up until now has decided to implement Steam when the old version was working fine(despite all the hacking) and "fix" it. Well, it wasn\'t broke, and now it is, so please fix it Valve. Does Valve even moderate these forums? I still say we need to all get together and plan a time to have a crapload of people submit problem tickets of this exact problem and see if we can emit a response. I suggested this before but there didnt\' seem to be much interest. Pleasem PM me if you are interested.' WHERE post_id = 645748 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'hmmm thats strange... no matter whats runing input should be getting the higest priority. maybe its somehting wrong with windows xp. also since theres a new thread i would also post a warning of a powertoy that can cause some sorta input lag. its installer is taskswitch.exe and what it does is replace your task menu (alt-tab) with one that has screneshots of the tasks. it also seems to cause input problems and lag. to fix it uninstall the task menu modifier and reboot.' WHERE post_id = 645761 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I mentioned this fix to some of my team so we went and tested it and they were pleasently surprised. some were apprehensive or sceptical, but they did notice a change on a lower ping server. guess we will be doing this each time we start steam, yes it goes back to default normal priority when you close steam out. I close steam as a normal thing to allow my other stuff to work like email surfing etc. I ran a test and left it open to see how my normal tasks would operate tho. I did notice that on low settings steam didnt stop web pages from loading as before.' WHERE post_id = 646644 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'so: 1. This is NOT a Steam problem it has been around since cs 1.5 so is a Valve problem (i always hated the HL engine, the Unreal engine was a lot better then and even now ...1998) 2. Is more related to DirectX, because in OpenGL this input lag doesn\'t happen, or at least no1 says this is related to opengl. So first change to OpenGL this can solve ur problem if it doens\'t affect your fps. How to fix it ? 1st. Temporal Fix: go to the Hardware Manager / Mouse / Properties / Advance Settings (I hope u understand i have and spanish version of WinXP), then change the 1st and 3rd options to its highest (sample and buffer �?, the second option is the wheel mouse detection), in my case they are 200 and 300 respectively. Maybe even if this doesn\'t fix your problem u may want to leave these settings to its highest, because u can improve the resolution/precision of your mouse. 2nd. Workaround: lower the priority of steam.exe to Below Normal, and u can also set the priority of explorer.exe to High (Task Manager / Processes Tab). Do it every time before you play. 3rd. Workaround: run Dxdiag (Win+R) and in the Sound Tab disable Hardward Acceleration (remember to restart your pc). If this works then start moving the slider to the right to the best setting, cause u can mess the sound in the game if u disable the HA). 4th. Workaround: Unistall Alt+Tab Powertoy or end the Taskswitch.exe process before playing on Steam. 5th. Workaround: Disable your Antivirus before playing on Steam. Note: sometimes one of these options can help u with the input lag, if not try them all! or 6th. Stop playing on Steam and try UT2004, Far Cry, CoD, or whatever u like [] REAL FIX: Its up to Steam to really solve this problem, why? because it seems that only the valve games are affected by this input lag and if u have read the systems specs of the others users THIS IS NOT A HARDWARE PROBLEM At least it would be nice if they post a new about that this is really an issue and that they are working on that, WE ARE YOUR CUSTOMERS, WE PUT THOSE FKING DOLLARS ON YOUR POCKETS!...or maybe they can\'t handle this problem and they are afraid of saying that valve/steam suk note: i still think that cs and dod (haven\'t played ns) are excellent games, the problem was that the modders just chose a bad engine for those games. sorry for my incipient english' WHERE post_id = 646769 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I really dont think you actually have any idea what we are talking about Loki. If you experienced this lag you would know that it is not some constant thing, and nearly everyone who is subject to it are adament that the problem is only recent. And the fix is not to lower steam.exe\'s priority but that of hl.exe, to demonstrate this people experiencing the problem of intermittent mouse/keyboard lockups where the mouse wont respond and the keyboard will become stuck for between 0.5 and 2 seconds raise your hl.exe\'s priority to High and you will see that the problem increases drastically, lowering the priority stops it occuring. The other fix for this is too lower Direct Sounds acceleration in dxdiag, this reduces the mouse/keyboard lockups but adds a short delay on all sounds. It is not the sort of mouse delay experienced under direct x, it is a non-constant and sometimes infrequent one caused under opengl which is not reproduceable (u cant simply point at a specific place for it to occur, the occurances are more or less random).' WHERE post_id = 649249 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by minus_human I really dont think you actually have any idea what we are talking about Loki. If you experienced this lag you would know that it is not some constant thing, and nearly everyone who is subject to it are adament that the problem is only recent. "Recent"??? well you are wrong, i don\'t know since when u r playing valve\'s games but for me it\'s been years. and if I said that is not only from a personal experience, friends of mine did have this problem years before too. you can read the original thread where a lot of users confirm this on that time the only solution for my friends and I was to switch to OpenGL. In OpenGL mode none of us got an input lag anymore; "but" as u can read on my previous post I didn\'t said that this only can happen on DirectX I just said that this seems to be "more related to DirectX" .. can u notice the difference? On the other side: quote:Originally posted by minus_human And the fix is not to lower steam.exe\'s priority but that of hl.exe, to demonstrate this people experiencing the problem of intermittent mouse/keyboard lockups where the mouse wont respond and the keyboard will become stuck for between 0.5 and 2 seconds raise your hl.exe\'s priority to High and you will see that the problem increases drastically, lowering the priority stops it occuring. The other fix for this is too lower Direct Sounds acceleration in dxdiag, this reduces the mouse/keyboard lockups but adds a short delay on all sounds. If you read again I said "Workaround" and a workaround IS NOT A FIX...why would I want to disable my Sound Hardware acceleration???!!! ... when everything works better (except steam) with it? AND, lines below...(well now, up) I said: Note: sometimes one of these options can help u with the input lag, if not try them all those workarounds "can" help you but I didn\'t tell anybody that any of them are a REAL SOLUTION!. The only thing I agree with you is that this seem to be random, but I notice that when you strafe and move the mouse a lot (and at the same time) its more probably that you will get an input lag, even if there is no other player in your field of view. Come on minus_human, I\'m only trying to resume the original thread, because when [OG]Menacer open this new one, he left some useful info that other users wrote. we are here to help each other not to fight against us without even read what someone\'s post' WHERE post_id = 650369 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Disagree its related to open gl, wtf would any1 want to paly in direct x is beyond me anyway, even tho i know ppl do.' WHERE post_id = 652309 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by .[oni].Loki "Recent"??? well you are wrong, i don\'t know since when u r playing valve\'s games but for me it\'s been years ... In OpenGL mode none of us got an input lag anymore; "but" as u can read on my previous post I didn\'t said that this only can happen on DirectX I just said that this seems to be "more related to DirectX" .. can u notice the difference? Ok i\'m still just not sure exactly what you are talking about. For a long time now anyone i know using direct 3d (way before steam) has been subject to a delay between moving the mouse and it moving on screen. What we are talking about here is something entirely different which *only* occurs within opengl. The direct 3d lag is old school and unimportant as its as simple as changing to opengl to fix. The lag people have been experiencing in the recent past occurs within opengl and is not really a *lag* as the name implies but rather *lockups* which occur with mouse movement and keyboard movement (movement become stuck strafing) periodically. It is more detremental in counterstrike and day of defeat because of the need for precise aiming but it occurs much more frequently in natural selection. Just so we have this clear, the *input lag* we have been refering to is not that experienced under direct 3d, it is different, much different infact and i would hope that valve even as a quick fix would implement a command line trigger to lower hl.exe\'s priority because this is rediculous and rendering the game unenjoyable for many.' WHERE post_id = 652397 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks Guys piority thing did the trick' WHERE post_id = 663709 AND is_historical = 1;
