UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CS:CZ 1.2 Released --->', post_text = 'The official 1.2 update for CS:CZ has been released, and all other Steam games have been updated. Steam will update itself automatically when you restart. Here is a list of the changes: COUNTER-STRIKE: CONDITION ZERO ADDITIONS: Added new hostage models and animations Added new hostage behaviors and dialogue Added SPETSNAZ and Militia player models Added crosshair customization (color, size, opacity) Added player location system Added exponential fog in OpenGL Added in-game vgui progress bar for nav mesh analysis Added de_sienna_cz Added de_vostok_cz COUNTER-STRIKE: CONDITION ZERO CHANGES: Upgraded de_inferno_cz Upgraded deagle view texture Updated cs_italy_cz with 32 spawns Upgraded weapon UI images Tweaked glock and USP sounds Tweaked snow walking sound Corpses fade out with cl_corpse_stay Grenades are dropped on death Improved player turning right hitbox behavior Improved shield behavior Improved brass ejection behavior Bots can use silencer on m4a1 Improved bot_auto_vacate behavior with spectators Career tasks are reset on mp_restartround Improved tutor behavior hud_draw 0 doesn\'t remove blackout Scope blackout drawn in software mode Flashlight sound no longer masks weapon firing sounds Improved text behavior in top-right corner of observer mode Round timer doesn\'t re-appear until the round restarts when the bomb is defused or explodes Improved player model hands ALL STEAM GAMES: Added refresh login dialogue for invalid login sessions (Invalid UserID ticket message) History area in game console no longer gets key focus' WHERE post_id = 647850 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I love you' WHERE post_id = 647853 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'More information on the new hostages: ------- Movement and Navigation Hostages can now crouch, use ladders, and break windows as well as walk, run, and jump, allowing them to go just about anywhere a player can. Rescue from Far Away The �use� range of Hostages has been greatly increased, allowing CT�s to rescue Hostages from across the room. If the Hostage is waving at you, you can �use� him! Emotions Hostages can be quite emotional. They will fidget if bored, watch other players moving near them, and show fear and terror when gunfire erupts. Escaping If the Hostages find themselves alone and unguarded after about one minute into the round, they will sneak off and attempt to escape on their own. Hostages will not try to escape if they have seen a Terrorist recently, or a Terrorist is anywhere in the nearby area (visible to them or not). Waving to CTs Un-rescued Hostages will wave at far away CTs they happen to see, unless that Hostage also sees a Terrorist at the same time. If a nearby Terrorist is looking at a Hostage, the Hostage will not wave to a CT. If a Hostage sees a CT and simultaneously sees nearby Terrorists who are not looking at him, he will shake his head "no" to the CT to warn him. Warning CT�s about Terrorists When a Hostage is rescued by a CT and there are Terrorists in the area, the Hostage will warn the CT of their presence. Fear and Fleeing Hostages can become afraid and even terrified. A terrified Hostage will sometimes flee to a nearby hiding spot. Hostages are afraid of gunfire, people being killed, and loud noises such as breaking windows. They become terrified if they witness someone die, or are shot. A Hostage will usually not flee if there is a Terrorist in the vicinity. Hostages and "Home" Spots The location of a Hostage at the beginning of a round is considered to be its "home" spot. Hostages tend to stay in their home spots, and Terrorists can return Hostages to their home spots if they are caught while escaping or fleeing. A Hostage will only leave its home spot if it is rescued by a CT, is injured, sees another Hostage die, or is left alone long enough to try to escape. Returning Hostages to their "Home" Spots Terrorists can return escaping or fleeing Hostages to their home spots by moving close to them while pointing their weapon towards them. This intimidates the Hostage, who will turn around and walk back to his home spot � even if it is all the way across the map. Hostages that are returning home will stop if they spot a CT, however. Technical Notes: Nav Files The new Hostage behaviors use data from the CS Bot .nav files. If a map does not have an associated .nav file, the Hostages will revert to their legacy behavior system. Models The new hostage system uses models HostageA.mdl, HostageB.mdl, HostageC.mdl, and HostageD.mdl. These models are assigned via code, and override whatever hostage models were placed in the actual map.' WHERE post_id = 647854 AND is_historical = 1;
