UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'This is the reason. I also get the same error now and did some searching. When i get the error i do a netstat which gives me this. steam13.steampowered.com:27038 This is the steam content server which its trying to download this new update? or whatever, it needs to contact this server. This can be supported by the errorlog - Error:CJoinGameDialog::OnSteamError() : launch game failed, with steam error: SteamProcessCall(WaitForAppReadyToLaunch)(0xab0014 ,0x160fc04,0x160fd0c) failed with error 1: Failed to get valid content ticket Which means that it connot connect to a content server. However when you ping this server. Pinging steam13.steampowered.com [207.173.177.130] with 32 bytes of data: Request timed out. Request timed out. Request timed out. Request timed out. Ping statistics for 207.173.177.130: Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 0, Lost = 4 (100% loss), So why dosent it try to contact another content server? Who knows.....Valve coded it...thats probably your answer. My conlusion is that, whoever didnt update their cs from when his server WAS working, is now screwed because the server has gone down or somthing arather. It would be great if this was in the FAQ or somthing, because their are no explainations for it (other then the hl.exe already running, which isnt the case here) The other solution to this was to log off and on to change content servers, however this dosent work as i get the same content server every time. Btw the only game that does launch is Codename Gordan Maybe if valve spent their time fixing their bad coding and software instead of creating sh*t like Codename Gordan, we wouldnt have this problem. Please Valve, fix it for crying out loud.' WHERE post_id = 651717 AND is_historical = 1;
