UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Leagues do have that choice to revert back to 1.3. It has been released for Steam. They at any time can put that in as standard and you can all go back to when the game needed "skill." If I\'m not mistaken, I didn\'t really read through the whole thing as it was just boring league team talk but they didn\'t really specify what decreased the skill gap except for that small mention of fixing bunny hopping. From what I read, people took their tactics from league demos so the teams got screwed on that. So all that was left was individual fighting. There\'s nothing there for Valve to read on what needs fixing. Quote something out if I missed it.' WHERE post_id = 668268 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I\'ve played CS for several years, and I never heard of CAL or whatever until I joined this forum... This game wasn\'t made for the pro\'s it was made for players...that someone turned it into a matchevent also, is okay and all, but that is not why the game exist.... Actually you would have to blame the "pros" and "leet" players for the game being fixed... If it wasn\'t for all those leet players who used bunyyjumping, bunnyjumping would not need to be fixed and the lame delay that happens when you land after jumping would not exist today. If "leet" players had not abused the quickswitch and AWM, there would not have been made a fix for it.. etc etc....from my personal experience, I would say that if anything, leet players ruined the game...not Valve.... But that\'s just me...' WHERE post_id = 668620 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Last Soul Reape I\'ve played CS for several years, and I never heard of CAL or whatever until I joined this forum... This game wasn\'t made for the pro\'s it was made for players...that someone turned it into a matchevent also, is okay and all, but that is not why the game exist.... Actually you would have to blame the "pros" and "leet" players for the game being fixed... If it wasn\'t for all those leet players who used bunyyjumping, bunnyjumping would not need to be fixed and the lame delay that happens when you land after jumping would not exist today. If "leet" players had not abused the quickswitch and AWM, there would not have been made a fix for it.. etc etc....from my personal experience, I would say that if anything, leet players ruined the game...not Valve.... But that\'s just me... WOW is all I can say, you are very ignorant for this reason: it\'s not an exploit, or cheating or abuse IF THE GAME ALLOWS IT, it is called being smart, and using everything you can do (without downloading hacks) to your advantage. WOW' WHERE post_id = 668659 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'wow you must live under a rock lol. It\'s not the pros who have ruined the game. Look at some of the stuff that is taking place before thin summers CPL. Players are getting signed for $40,000 a year. Esports is becoming a viable career and a possibility for some. Players are getting annoyed because the game is becoming slower and slower. I don\'t have a problem with the recent fixes, and I think the pro gamers are dealing with it as well. Your so called "leet" players didnt ruin the game. Cause if I\'m not mistaken I\'ve yet to see a "leet" player run around with a shield.' WHERE post_id = 668668 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '"As I said before basically CS is going to be interesting now since the skill gap is reduced and yet that is arguably the most important factor followed by teamplay issues. The future isn\'t super organised teamplay from hours of practice combined with meticulously thought out tactics, instead it\'s roster changing until you have the best 5 skill players available to you, working with them to establish some sembelence of teamplay and then applying some of the myriad of tactics available for you to download. Rinse and repeat until CS is dead. Not only did competitive CS devolve but there is nowhere for it to evolve to. Thanks once again Valve software for the software equivalent of inbreeding the CS family tree until future generations lacked thumbs and higher brain functions." "The skill gap is shrinking with every update" And that is what MANY of us have been claiming for a long time. April 28th update was just another of these de-evoloving updates. in the article they point out that the skill gap has been shrinking since the jump to 1.4. yet another point i have stuck by since its release. nice one valve..' WHERE post_id = 668686 AND is_historical = 1;
