UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Server getting bad spikes after Update', post_text = 'Okay so I have three servers (2 CS and 1 CZ) running on my box. I updated all the servers last night once the udpate came out. Since then only one of the servers is experiencing issues where it will play fine for a while then all of a sudden everyone will freeze for about 5-10 seconds then it will go back to being okay but a minute or so later it will do that again. I have disabled all the plugins (like metamod and amxx) but the issue still happens. Funny thing is how the other two servers will fun just fine. I even tried coping the entire directory structure from one of the working servers to the non working one but that didn\'t fix anything. Anyone else seeing issues like this? (Server specs Dual Xeon 2.6ghz, 2 gigs PC2700, SATA 10000RPM Hard drive, T3 connections)' WHERE post_id = 679637 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'That just doesn\'t make sense to me :\\ How are you making sure the other 2 server instances are spike free when the other one spikes? Also, can you tell me the memory usage for each one, and the amount it uses upon starting up, i.e. 60MB. Disabled plugins, meaning using mp.dll for gamedll file? Really from what you say, the only thing different would either be the server ip\'s, or the port it is running on. Which one is piking, one of the cs or the cz? If it is CZ...........then it is CZ. I think atleast, lots of said about CZ servers and people getting booted out of nowhere. Not sure if this happens with CS though, haven\'t played that game since cz came out []' WHERE post_id = 680003 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'How am I checking....well I got people on each of the servers and they aren\'t spiking when I am spiking on the other. Yes using mp.dll for the server when I disabled everything (but that didn\'t help so I went back to metamod) Memory usage depends on how many people on in there but typical is about 60 like you said maybe a lil more Each server runs on a different port Trouble server is on 27015 the other two are one 27016 and 27017. Its a CS 1.6 server that is having issues. Didn\'t start till the recent update.' WHERE post_id = 680029 AND is_historical = 1;
