UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I would say while testing this to ensure mp.dll is being used on all servers. There have been reports of memory leaks directly with metamod, and who knows what the new versions of metamod can do now. Also, are you using the same server.cfg settings, excluding the obvious different things i.e. name, rcon pw, etc...Basically, the settings relating to the maxrate, updaterate, etc...they are they same on all 3 server instances? This situation is very hard to troubleshoot since it is on the same box with same bandwidth connection. Instead of copying another folder of a non-spiking server, try making a new folder, updating directly with hldsupdatetool, and make new configs, change port, and start up and see. I\'ve had some strange problems before and that was the only way to fix them - copying another server\'s folder, redoing configs, etc, didn\'t work for some things. Also, can you have a pingplotter running in the background while servers are up, from www.pingplotter.com (http://www.pingplotter.com) ? Get that, run it for a long time, a day straight or something, have a few running and pingplotting to different locations. See what yields.' WHERE post_id = 681390 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Same problems here, running a complete plugin free windows dedicated. Thank god I had a backup of the DLL\'s (from before the last update) Valve, now it\'s your turn, i guess' WHERE post_id = 681431 AND is_historical = 1;
