UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Sweet cliffe, thanks! quote:And you can buy Half-Life and co. over Steam with credit card now! No need to go to a shop! That said, the cost seems to be $34.95, which seems a tad steep, really. Does seem a bit steep: at least compared to what the HL pack goes for in my area, seems like there\'s no discount for the fact that you don\'t get a box or materials. I would have thought that selling it online would be a lot cheaper than creating/shipping retail boxes. But maybe: 1) since the price has to be global, it has to be averaged out from all the sale locations (i.e. can\'t be cheaper in North Dakota than it is in New York the way it is in stores) 2) Vivendi owns a cut of every sale of games it was liscenced to distribute, so Valve can\'t cut prices because it has to pay Vivendi as if it was using them to sell a retail box 3) the cost for download bandwidth is roughly the same for contracting out the production of retail boxes, so there isn\'t really any money saved 4) Don\'t want cheaters to be able to buy up tons and tons of accounts. 5) I\'m no business guy, so what do I know?' WHERE post_id = 683852 AND is_historical = 1;
