UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thank you Cliff for responding. I seem to be the only one complaining about the shield crashing server problem. I enabled the shield over the weekend on my two pubs and I believe they crashed no less then 10 times each before I disabled them again. As always there does not seem to be pattern, it just happens. Thanks again Cliff, for at least acknowledging there are problems. If anyone at Valve wants to see it happen, let me know as it doesn\'t take long for the server to crash after shields are enabled.' WHERE post_id = 697699 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'File links for fixing server spiking.', post_text = 'Well, yet again it appears valve has outsourced it\'s coding to a bunch of kindergarden children. Is there a fix (From Valve) for the cpu spikes that have occured after the last update or do we all just have to piss off as usual and wait weeks for you guys to come up with a fix. It really makes gaming suck. Thanks again for making me abhor administrating hlds based servers. Props to the community for picking up the slack and offering a temporary solution. Using the old mp.dll This link courtesy of XGS-Barry http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll (http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll) A link from us here at Dick http://files.dickathon.com/mp.dll (http://files.dickathon.com/mp.dll)' WHERE post_id = 690350 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'temp fix', post_text = 'Here is my post to the other email thats just like this one. " Well I read thru everyones post and I must say that there is no certain reason why the servers are spiking. We have everything from 8 player privates to 32 player publics out of all four locations and there is no set reason why the problems are being caused. Its not a actual CPU problems itself as I noticed when it does do the random lockup the cpu spikes some but on our Dual Opterons the cpu was not going over 20% cpu usage with the spike but the players in the server we feeling the lockup. I updated all our servers and just used the old mp.dll for now to fix the problem. Make sure to use the mp.dll that is 1.25mb in size and the only problem you should see is the countdown clock will not showup. Its a burden yes but its better then the lockups every 10 seconds or so. I would have to say 90% of my servers were having problems and the others were not. Some were on the same box so out of expierence I know this is defiantly not a overloaded problems which some were trying to suggest. I have been running servers since 1999 and this is just one of these updates. Lets just hope that they come out with a fix soon to remove this problem. Download the 1.25mb mp.dll below. http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll (http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll) "' WHERE post_id = 690359 AND is_historical = 1;
