UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I get this error also.. it says: [ The instruction at "0x0ed35969" referenced memory at "0x0efc5800". The memory could not be "read". Click on OK to terminate the program ] I can\'t play CS for more than a few minutes at a time... I notice that the error ocurrs most frequently when things are actually happening in CS such as guns being shot, lots of people joining servers... lo3 restarts/CAL.cfg being activated. I know it\'s not a problem with my computer because i just built it and i had the same problem on my last computer which was a compaq. I am needed on my team, and this error happens when we scrim all of the time. I tell my team NOT to start me because It\'s useless. There is no reason for me to play if whenever something happens "The instruction at blah blah" comes up. Someone needs to address this, it seems to be a major problem effecting mostly the CS community. I am currently running: AMD Athlon 2600+ 2.08 Ghz 512 mb PC2700 Ram (It\'s not bad ram so dont even try to tell me) ATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128 mb ASUS a7n8x-x Mobo Maxtor 60 gig 8mb Its not a problem with my system, its a problem with steam, it needs to be fixed...' WHERE post_id = 690203 AND is_historical = 1;
