UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by StealthMode Hmmm, this is not why servers are lagging. Think about it, if the mp.dll were causing the lag, then ANY metamod server wouldn\'t lag. There is a deeper issue at work here. I\'m not familiar with CS so much, but all Metamod does is allow multiple DLLs to be loaded - the core game DLL still must be launched through it. Check your Metamod configs and you will see that it is there.' WHERE post_id = 709057 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Plugins.ini (for metamod) lists the dlls metamod calls upon/loads. Nowhere in that file does it say mp.dll. Thats the only "config" metamod uses other then its own native .dll And when you install metamod, you have to rem (remark) out (//) the stock dll in order to add the line to run the metamod.dll. So I think that I was correct in saying metamod doesn\'t use the mp.dll. This is easily proven, by DELETING the mp.dll and starting a server running the gamedll /addons/metamod/dll/metamod.dll in the liblist.gam file. If metamod needed mp.dll it would have crashed the server when it tried to load without it. 8)\n\n__________________ Representin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere... -=LoT=- StealthMode Legion of Terror http://legion.nuclearfallout.net http://www.teamlot.net VALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there! STOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!! WHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!' WHERE post_id = 709069 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '...so then where exactly does it get the game code from? I\'m sorry, I\'m really unclear on how CS works (I\'m a TFC guy). Metamod can\'t simply recreate CS on its own... I don\'t have the HLDS version of CS installed so I can\'t check.' WHERE post_id = 709074 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Good question. Honestly I think it gets all its code from the gcf file. OR in the case of servers, from the servers cache file. Metamod is just an alternate dll to use instead of the mp.dll. I will test this since I started it. 8) EDIT: Ok I tested it. Looks like I am mistaken and metamod DOES call to the mp.dll (or the server still wants it loaded outside of metamod). I removed the mp.dll and tried to start the server, it crashed saying it could not find mp.dll (even with mp.dll remmed out of the liblist.gam file, and metamod.dll listed as the dll for the mod). /EDIT\n\n__________________ Representin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere... -=LoT=- StealthMode Legion of Terror http://legion.nuclearfallout.net http://www.teamlot.net VALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there! STOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!! WHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!' WHERE post_id = 709346 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Actually, your all wrong. Metamod is a WRAPPER to the mp.dll...all it does is intercept and pass calls to the .dll So basically...metamod.dll is just a second dll attached TO mp.dll mp.dll is still being used. Metamod does this for all mods...thats why sometimes "special support" has to be added because not everyone calls their dll mp.dll If you used +localinfo game_dll [path to a new dll]...then it would actually use whatever new DLL you listed. Thats how you get things like non-mm bots working.\n\n__________________ www.TKWired.com' WHERE post_id = 709564 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Steam Hot Fix', post_text = 'Message: 4 Date: Wed, 23 Jun 2004 17:04:39 -0700 From: "Alfred Reynolds" <alfred@valvesoftware.com> To: <hlds@list.valvesoftware.com>, <hlds_linux@list.valvesoftware.com>, <hlds_announce@list.valvesoftware.com> Subject: [hlds] CS lag fix Reply-To: hlds@list.valvesoftware.com (mailto:hlds@list.valvesoftware.com) We have identified the cause of the lag and have created a fix for it. Updated game dlls will be released via Steam next week. In the meantime we have a hotfix available, the updated game dlls can be downloaded from: /drop/06...ke_gamedlls.zip (/drop/06232004_cstrike_gamedlls.zip) Unzip this file into the cstrike/dlls directory. The md5 sums of the updated game dlls are: 10f2dcdbacc50e9fe198fa05b85e5ca8 mp.dll 1c4d3d4d073be72829e8d81dce59a4c7 cs_amd64.so 6a57b0d1817cfc659059694e6e281d33 cs_i386.so - Alfred --__--__--' WHERE post_id = 707887 AND is_historical = 1;
