UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'no, this is freebsd. what i meant by that was i made steam download everything for a czero server, then i tar\'d up that entire directory and cp\'d it to my other customers home dir\'s to update their servers since steam wont update their servers correctly. in other words, im having to completely reinstall all of their servers from scratch with the latest downloaded files via steam instead of just running ./steam -command update. since it looks for a "InstallRecord.blob" file that doesn\'t exist, or use to exist at one point before steam deleted it itself and then complains it isn\'t there. (i tested it, i placed a completely perfect insteallrecord.blob file from a czero server that i hadn\'t touched yet into the directory of a czero server that refused to update via steam cause the InstallRecord.blob file wasn\'t there, ran ./steam -command update and steam deleted it and then complained that it couldn\'t find InstallRecord.blob)\n\n__________________ How Valve got control of CS: Gooseman and Cliffe were hard at work coding when the door burst open and in came several MIB. Once the area was secured, in walked Gabe in a pimp outfit (from pimphats.com). He took took one look at them and said omfg i pwn joo, joo h4lf l1f3 nubcake h4xors. With that, he walked out and the MIBS bag and tagged them and took them back to Valve HQ. -phr0z3n' WHERE post_id = 719277 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'hlds101.tk UP!!', post_text = 'I\'m happy to report that my website is now online, as usual. The cause for which my website was innaccessible was due to a... *caugh*firewall*caugh* problem. I had upgraded to Apache 2 without reassigning firewall policies. Finnaly, I would like to thank my fans for alerting me that my site was offline, and if it ever happens again, I would like to get emails stating that at paulius (at) hlds101 (dot) tk. ___________ So here are the links again: Short link: www.hlds101.tk (http://www.hlds101.tk) Direct link: http://hlds101.servegame.com/hlds101/ (http://hlds101.servegame.com/hlds101/)' WHERE post_id = 717477 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Linux is the operating system of choice for HLDS As much as I\'d love to say that this is true... in my HUMBLE (don\'t flame me []) opinion... the extra CPU effeciency in win32 makes it the "choice" OS for HLDS.' WHERE post_id = 717732 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by BMJ As much as I\'d love to say that this is true... in my HUMBLE (don\'t flame me []) opinion... the extra CPU effeciency in win32 makes it the "choice" OS for HLDS. I\'ve heard of that before... It\'s hard to believe but don\'t worry! I\'ll soon establish my HLDS testing lab and will release benchmark graphs comparing both.' WHERE post_id = 717739 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Counter-Server already did that some time ago (although I can\'t find it anymore), so you go ahead and do that. [] Valve never anticipated Half-Life would be as massively played as it is when they developed it... and HLDS was originally not very sophisticated... the client/server coding is almost the same, really...it was a Windows game, and so HLDS was a Windows program. The Linux port came later, and it was not nearly as efficient as the Windows version at first... it has gotten a LOT better over time... but when it gets down to heavy CPU usage... the Windows version of HLDS is going to be more efficient. The gap isn\'t as large anymore... but it is still there.' WHERE post_id = 717759 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by BMJ Counter-Server already did that some time ago (although I can\'t find it anymore), so you go ahead and do that. [] Valve never anticipated Half-Life would be as massively played as it is when they developed it... and HLDS was originally not very sophisticated, it was essentially a special client... the client/server coding is almost the same, really... and it was a Windows game, and so HLDS was also a Windows program. The Linux port came later, and it was not nearly as efficient as the Windows version at first... it has gotten a LOT better over time... but when it gets down to heavy CPU usage... the Windows version of HLDS is going to be more CPU efficient. The gap isn\'t as large anymore... but it is still there. Interesting... But technically, maybe Linux would still have advantage because it\'s core doenst take as much space as Windows and it runs console so it doesn\'t waste too many CPU cycles... Also, after browsing my 8 computers, I think I\'ll take my 450mhz one, shove a 5200rpm drive in it and do some testing... That was, performance difference will be VERY clear. Finnaly, have you heard about this article: http://www.osnews.com/story.php?news_id=7324 (http://www.osnews.com/story.php?news_id=7324) interesting and I agree. That\'s why I support the project Minix from scratch... Hint: HLDS port on there?' WHERE post_id = 717767 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'If you have money to spend and want to host multiple instances of HLDS... buy some Windows Server licenses... If you\'re cheap... use Linux. []' WHERE post_id = 717768 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by paulius Interesting... But technically, maybe Linux would still have advantage because it\'s core doenst take as much space as Windows and it runs console so it doesn\'t waste too many CPU cycles... Also, after browsing my 8 computers, I think I\'ll take my 450mhz one, shove a 5200rpm drive in it and do some testing... That was, performance difference will be VERY clear. Dude, you\'d have to use a better CPU than that. And go right ahead... anybody who has hosted both Linux and Windows HLDS will tell you the Windows versions use less CPU. And surely if you run proper tests, you\'ll see that too.' WHERE post_id = 717771 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'We\'ll see... 450mhz is so that we could FEEL the dirrerence... not is nanoseconds but in real human time. I\'m personnaly for Linux because it\'s free and opensource... Would be weird if closed would rule open...' WHERE post_id = 717775 AND is_historical = 1;
