UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: CS:Source beta ...only one map', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Kadayipolokov A2597 got an email response from Gabe Newell regarding the forthcoming CS:source beta and posted it at www.halflife2.net (http://www.halflife2.net) forums:- http://www.halflife2.net/forums/sho...4214#post574214 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?p=574214#post574214) It looks like there will only be the one map, and that map will most likely be De_Dust. It\'s a beta so for testing purposes one map makes sense...but De_Dust.... Thanks for the link, at least it answered one question for me... quote:CS:Source is in great shape, and I don\'t see it impacting the RC date. It is the plan to include it in the regular and collectors edition boxes. I\'ve heard the rumours about CS:Source but it was unclear if I would have to shell out more money e.g. if CS:Source was only included with the collector\'s edition. Well now that that\'s addressed, does anyone have any idea what the difference is between the versions? Will the collector\'s edition include DoD or something else? Or is it going to be something useless like a T-shirt and poster?' WHERE post_id = 783047 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'wtf are you talking about? do you know what "Beta"s even are?', post_text = 'I think that you guys are forgetting what a "beta test" is really about. They\'re not released so that the players get to have fun. They\'re released so that the players can help find bugs, and the payoff for them is free gametime. While a lot of you will just get the game, and just play it, there is a majority of the people out there that will take the beta the way they should. They will look around for bugs, and expirement: IE: What happens when I throw this nade in this map problem area. What visual defects do I get on XXX video card. The reason they would only release one map? Again, this is a beta test, not a free "play b4 u pay" thing. And, you saw what happened with CS:CZ, so don\'t you think you\'ll expect to see someone trying to package up CS:S and trying to give it out to their friends with some bypass? Most likly. So, 1 map, because that\'s all you need to be in the enviroment of the game. 1 map because it\'s just a beta to see how it works on everyones computer. Because VALVe doesn\'t have a replica of all our computers at their building. Havn\'t you guys ever beta\'d before? They\'re will be problems, we WILL find them, That\'s why we beta, to fix, not to play(well, also to play, but the other thing more). But you guys that are crying are just gonna say "WTF!! WHY DOES IT CRASH? I\'M NOT GONNA SWEAR!!", When you should be saying, "When I do this \'xxx\' while standing at \'xxx\' I get \'errors/visual defects/unexplained major lag/crash\', and this is how you replicate the error so you can text/fix it yourself \'xxx\' "' WHERE post_id = 783063 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Re: CS:Source beta ...only one map', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by gregrout Thanks for the link, at least it answered one question for me... I\'ve heard the rumours about CS:Source but it was unclear if I would have to shell out more money e.g. if CS:Source was only included with the collector\'s edition. Well now that that\'s addressed, does anyone have any idea what the difference is between the versions? Will the collector\'s edition include DoD or something else? Or is it going to be something useless like a T-shirt and poster? Gabe Newell said that even he is totally not sure of what all they\'re will be, but that he does know that their will be a few little things packaged in, and as far as the game, their will be some sort of extra content to play. Maybe extra levels, maybe extra who knows.' WHERE post_id = 783069 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'stop external voice programs from working', post_text = 'The main problem as I see it with the game is people being able to utilise external programs which go against the game principles. For example once you have died you can\'t talk to your team mates that are still in the game. Programs like Teamspeak , Roga Wilko etc. make everyones lives a misery in my opinion. Need to find some way to prevent the programs from working whilst CS/CZ is operative.' WHERE post_id = 783202 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thats not for everyone...And it\'s probly just certain settings you have on your soundcard that do so. I\'ve been able to run teamspeak, ventrilo, and CS at the same time(don\'t ask why). But, it has happend to where i lose voice in one program or the other. You may want to go look for some fixes or read up on the vidcard you have and settings that may do that.' WHERE post_id = 783235 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'yeah. Why stop there? You know, when my friends come over and we play CS, I think it\'s really unfair that we can talk to each other after one of us have died. Valve should make people wear an electronic muzzle. What about lan parties? Yep, unfair to talk to each other. Maybe Valve should remove the lan option. Wouldn\'t want anyone talking to each other after they died, would we?' WHERE post_id = 783251 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'oops lol...i just skimmed through it and read it wrong...my bad.' WHERE post_id = 783281 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Xaleth yeah. Why stop there? You know, when my friends come over and we play CS, I think it\'s really unfair that we can talk to each other after one of us have died. Valve should make people wear an electronic muzzle. What about lan parties? Yep, unfair to talk to each other. Maybe Valve should remove the lan option. Wouldn\'t want anyone talking to each other after they died, would we? I recently went to ECL about a week ago, and my friend\'s clan were using ventrillo. The catch was that ECL had a server setting that made the screen turn black when they die. So they wouldn\'t be able to view the game anymore. I think that works well to stop \'voice(lan) hacking\'.' WHERE post_id = 783412 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by an80sbboy I recently went to ECL about a week ago, and my friend\'s clan were using ventrillo. The catch was that ECL had a server setting that made the screen turn black when they die. So they wouldn\'t be able to view the game anymore. I think that works well to stop \'voice(lan) hacking\'. Thats a setting called mp_fadetoblack but its not the greatest option to use in a pub server. I think the first poster has a valid point. CAL and other leagues started allowing the use of 3rd party chat programs like ventrilo and teamspeak to be used in matches for the soul reason that they could not control it. The thing about a match is that once u die, your screen goes black so you really can\'t see anyway but you can still communicate your position and who killed you. And also, your voice comm is not recorded in the demo\'s that you have to record while playing matches. The thing is that now most people are going into pubs using the same chat programs and after they die, they lead they friends are clan mates around telling them where each member of the other team is at. Its actually easier than if you were lanning with someone cause you never have to take your eyes off of the screen. Its starting to get abused and everyone can laugh now but when someone else does it to you over and over, you won\'t laugh any more.' WHERE post_id = 783579 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'you can still use the friends network...there is still a phone...different messengers...Your not going to stop it, if a server deosn\'t want to allow it they\'ll put forcecam on. There isn\'t a lot you can do about it so its not going to happen' WHERE post_id = 783582 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by MrHamolka you can still use the friends network...there is still a phone...different messengers...Your not going to stop it, if a server deosn\'t want to allow it they\'ll put forcecam on. There isn\'t a lot you can do about it so its not going to happen I said he had a valid point, not that valve was going to do anything about it. Also, since you mentioned them. You have to drop console to get to the friends network and message someone on your friends list You have to alt tab out of game to use various other messengers How many people actually sit on the phone and tell each other where the other team is? That leaves them playing with one hand or a crocked neck. If there was a plugin for any of the admin controls that are out there that would allow admins to be void of the forcecam, I would have that option enabled. But you are right, I doubt Valve would have control over such programs so in that light, they will probably never move to do anything about it.' WHERE post_id = 783601 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by MrHamolka ...there is still a phone... OMG would ppl really go that far to raise their score 1 point, to go from rank 3 to 1. quote:Originally posted by i||ega|-op Thats a setting called mp_fadetoblack but its not the greatest option to use in a pub server. This is probably the best way to prevent this chat cheating. But even if they do report to their other teammates on their last position, the enemy that killed them is more than likely to move to a new location, or find a hiding spot for more kills.' WHERE post_id = 783653 AND is_historical = 1;
