UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Vigil for HL2\'s ongoing product development...', post_text = 'While this thread is in direct response to the announcement of the leaked version of CS: Source, it is not designed to provide any information to the persons responsible for the incident. I\'ll make this as simple as I can, because this has gone on long enough. 6 years ago when Valve Software first released Half-Life, they came under a lot of scrutiny when the sourcecode for that game was hacked by someone who wanted to undermine their company. I can\'t exactly remember whether anyone was caught, but it did cause a serious blow to gaming as a whole. Then, after five years of development put into its sequal, the company was again attacked last year, when HL2\'s sourcecode and videos from E3 2003 were hacked straight from their own servers. This also followed with several anonymous postings on the Net from the supposed hacker about how Valve had been lying to us about the status of the Source Engine. Proceedings followed with several arrests worldwide of people in possesion of hacking materials that were needed to breach Valve-security. Finally today, HL2Central reported a leaked copy of CS: Source on a warez site, further spreading rumours about Valve\'s disloyalty. I don\'t know who is doing any of this, but if this is the same person who started this little drama, let me say this... maybe you\'re doing this to prove how good a hacker you are, maybe you\'re being paid for it from a competitor, I don\'t know, and frankly I don\'t really care. If this is an attempt to make a name for yourself in the community, at best you are only making the rest of us wait longer for Half-Life 2 because they have to keep changing the encryptions on their servers. I call for all at Valve Software and in the community to rise up with me and rid ourselves of this continuing threat, whose desire is only to get their kicks from hacking games developers because they have nothign better to do with their time... like get a job.' WHERE post_id = 797759 AND is_historical = 1;
