UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Faulty Bans ?', post_text = 'I\'m hoping I\'m not the only case, but here it goes :x The point of this so you don\'t get edgey is that I was banned from a server, with no indication why, and no admin banned me, strictly server. I have never hacked in my entire life, nor use any scripts or modified any skins for CS. It\'s the basic install with my own custom modifications (crosshair, sensitivity, nofrocem stuff, video/audio, et cetera). Here\'s what happened: I joined a server, was playing de_prodigy, stays on that for 10 or so minutes, then changes to some aim map no one likes on a pub >.< I do bad, but I stick it out, shooting up with some friends, not really trying as much as I am talking. Then the map changes again to de_inferno. Somehow, I do really well (that or the opposing team just really sucked, but it sounds better the other way :x), and I am able to kill 5 people in the first 30 seconds of the first round with all headshots, and as I\'m running to go kill another, I get a message that says that I\'m on the banned list. Is there some type of detection that anti-cheat programs use that might have caused it to think my randomness could have been the sign of hacking ? I can still connect to VAC servers, but I can\'t connect to this particular server. Any ideas on why I\'d get banned from a server ? O_o Atre. PS I suck at cs :x and new nvidia driver is out, go go reforce !' WHERE post_id = 798393 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'An admin mayb thought it was suspicious.' WHERE post_id = 798401 AND is_historical = 1;
