UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Video Evidence: Quickswitching was not an exploit', post_text = 'Now that the awp delay has been in the game for a while and the arguing has diminished a bit, i\'d like to show actual proof that quickswitching was not an exploit. http://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi (http://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi) Created by Drax (previously of zEx). zEx was one of the top American clans in case you didnt know. I\'m not complaining or trying to get CS back to the good ol days, i\'m just stating some simple facts here people. Jeff Cliffe says this was a "quickswitch exploit". Draw your own conclusions. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- edit #1: there is another video made by sacko http://home.online.no/~ovassend/awp.avi (http://home.online.no/~ovassend/awp.avi) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- edit #2: Also, if you wish to discuss the use of Quickshots, at least know what they are first. Here are 3 demos of it, all by different top players. This is more evidence that i wish to show of why the delay was added, i think everyone should watch at least one of these demos. Ksharp: http://www.team3d.net/index.php?s=demos&id=115 (http://www.team3d.net/index.php?s=demos&id=115) * this demo is in 1.6 before the awp delay was implemented. You also have to register(it\'s free) on Team3D\'s website to d/l this. Deathmatch server, alot of nice awp and deagle action. Pag.Xero: http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/546/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/546/) *this is a 1.3 demo(you can run it in 1.5, it will work) and probably the best example of what i\'m talking about. This d/l also requires a free registration. He goes 38-0 in a pub before they kick him. Drax (he created the first video): http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/3763/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/3763/) *this is a 1.5 demo, really nice shots in this one, it\'s in a pub and they all think he\'s cheating. My quick guide to playing demos. Just d/l, extract into your /cstrike folder. For 1.5 this would be Sierra/Counter-Strike/cstrike. For steam it\'s /Steam/Steamapps/your-email/Counter-Strike/cstrike Then start up CS, go into console type playdemo "nameofdemo" -WITHOUT the quotes. Or you can d/l SKplayer or Geekplay.' WHERE post_id = 834972 AND is_historical = 1;
