UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by kekekeke2101 Just because a clan did it doesn\'t make it right. It was still an exploit, as it wasn\'t something that was meant to be done. You were supposed to have to wait for the animations (that\'s why they\'re there). I could really go either way and wouldn\'t mind it being back, but it was an exploit. That explanation is a copp out. Just think about it, why of all things in counter-strike to change would be to make people watch the bolt animation? It sounds trivial until you see it in action. We all know why it was "fixed". I\'d rather valve just admit it than use that as an excuse.' WHERE post_id = 835029 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by garfong People used the quickswitch primarily to get out of the zoom mode, skipping animations only gave them an advantage if they actually wanted to use their pistol instead of switch back to awp. The video actually shows you it\'s slower to quickswitch then to just wait. Your partly correct. You can STILL swtich back to your pistol and fire just as fast with or without the delay. Which leaves only one type of thing affected: Quickshots. And who were the only people able to use quickshots to it\'s full effectiveness? You see what im getting at?' WHERE post_id = 835040 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by n3vin That explanation is a copp out. Just think about it, why of all things in counter-strike to change would be to make people watch the bolt animation? It sounds trivial until you see it in action. We all know why it was "fixed". I\'d rather valve just admit it than use that as an excuse. It\'s not for the animation itself, the animation is so that you see how long of a delay you have until you can use it - you aren\'t supposed to skip the delay, so you aren\'t supposed to skip the animation. They were put there so you could see when you were actually allowed to use the gun rather than watch the \'pretty effects.\' It was put there to show the delay. VALVE wanted the delay, so they fixed the exploit. quote:Originally posted by n3vin Your partly correct. You can STILL swtich back to your pistol and fire just as fast with or without the delay. Which leaves only one type of thing affected: Quickshots. And they didn\'t want these \'quickshots\' there, so they put in a delay. I\'d really hope that they at least add the animation delay to the pistols, too, as it makes little sense not to.' WHERE post_id = 835042 AND is_historical = 1;
