UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Host_Error: UserMsg: Not Present on Client 232', post_text = '**EDIT: I was just informed that the error code 52 (as well as 232) was also reported to some clients. I and many clients who conect to my server experience this error on a regular basis. Server: Athlon XP 2200+ 512MB RAM 80GB hdd up to date all around Gentoo Linux, kernel 2.6.7 w/pax/grsec patches MetaMod 1.17.1 AMXModX 0.16 Some simple scripts like AWP-Punish, some extra basic unrelated admin tools installed (ie, to allow amx_alltalk <0 | 1> to be a command), etc. I had WC3 2.5.0 installed, but unloaded it to see if it fixed the errors -- the errors still happen. I basically tried that with all of the AMXX plugins, but the errors happen, regardless. I\'ve searched for this error on this forum, AMXX\'s forums, googled for it, and searched on other forums, with no luck. I found an abundance of similiar errors, but all with completely different error codes (19 instead of 232, for example). Anyone know the problem? THanks.' WHERE post_id = 838783 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'I\'ll take a shot at explaining ;)', post_text = 'Well I\'ll take a quick guess that you have a Linksys router? And I\'ll also guess you\'ve updated it with the new firmware? If that is the case your stuck in the same place as alot of people. It seems that something in the new firmware conflicts with steam and allows only a few seconds of gameplay (I\'ve managed to gain 30 seconds.) The only solution is if you can find the old firmware here: ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub (ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub) I unfortunately have the Linksys BEFSR81 v3 - It seems apparent they haven\'t placed the old firmware on their site/ftp like they have for every other bloody router :/ that really doesn\'t help. I hope Valve or Linksys come up with a solution in the very near future as I am missing Half-life. [] Hope this has helped you in anyway possible even if it\'s just stating why it is happening.' WHERE post_id = 839746 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'ADD - Also search in this directory: ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub/befsr41/ (ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub/befsr41/)' WHERE post_id = 839747 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Actually, personally, there are no routers between me and my server. My HLDS server also acts as a router for my windows box. My switch is Linksys, but it\'s a switch only, no router. My router was provided by my ISP -- I don\'t know the make and model of it, they claim they build it themselves. The SSL cert for the router was issued by Linksys, however, and all available information from the router and the router\'s cert seems to imply a WRT54G model router (which is a wireless router), so my guess is that it\'s got the innerparts of a WRT54G, but built up with other parts than the standards. Regardless... I have no control over its current firmware version, and even if I did, it can\'t possibly be the problem -- the packets from my windows box to the server box never see the Linksys router. And yet it happens to me, as well as my clients (my clients most likely do use Linksys routers -- two that I talk with regularly do for sure, not sure about the rest.) Any ideas on why I might be disconnected? Checking my firewall logs shows that nothing related to hlds and my windows box was blocked...' WHERE post_id = 839825 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Hmmm ok I just thought I\'d put that information incase it was any help and because its a common problem at the moment.' WHERE post_id = 840050 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'It seems like a lot of users (mainly linksys routers) are having this problem. And from everything I can gather, it started happening after the last Steam update. I am bumping this in hopes of getting it acknowledged by someone that can look into a possible solution to the problem. The router I use is a Linksys, and it is currently working 100% fine with every app I use: Internet browsing (IE, Mozilla Firefox) Quake 3 Wolfenstein Enemy Territory Unreal Tournament 2004 Diablo II Usenet applications Peer to peer applications network samba sharing You name it! Even Half Life/CS/TFC/DOD before the move-over to Steam. This is a real problem. I don\'t think the router is at fault because everything else I do works with it. I\'ve read one thread in this forum where someone said it works as long as you downgrade your router\'s firmware to a version from 2002. That is unacceptable, because the current firmware fixes many security flaws within the router, and has not caused problems with any other app I use. I am going to really press this issue, because I am anticipating Half LIfe 2, and it would be a shame to not be able to play online. I\'m not trying to be inflammitory at all. If anyone from Valve reads this, I thank you for your time. My main intent is to get a response from somone to see if it\'s something Valve is aware of, and working on, and if they have contacted Linksys about a possible fix.' WHERE post_id = 840850 AND is_historical = 1;
