UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Could not connect to steam network, or your inet connection is down error - fix', post_text = 'Loads of people have got this error (including me). Here\'s how I fixed it. 1. Remove the file called ClientRegistry.blob from your steam folder. 2. Run steam again and let it update. 3. Create a new account with a valid e-mail addy (dont use the same one you used before). 4. You should be able to progress to the next screen after this account is created. From looking around the forums, it seems that some accounts have got messed up when steam was installing the first time around, or if people tried to inherit an account from the beta releases. By creating a brand new account, it seems to scrub the corrupted one and everything works fine from then on. This fix worked fine for me, (after pulling my hair out for 5 days). If this is indeed whats causing so much hassel for folks, then I think the Valve support team need to seriously pay attention to the posts on these forums, cos such a simple fix should have been posted by them ages ago. Just to make it easier for people to get this fix, please post a reply if this worked for your steam installation, that way it will keep getting bumped up to the top of the lists and will be seen by people quicker. - in fact rate it so it can be seen quicker, this must be the single most infuriating problem folks are having - so help them to see the answer. _________________________________________________' WHERE post_id = 116411 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '/bump' WHERE post_id = 116742 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Sooo... All we have to do is get a new CDKEY, ok!' WHERE post_id = 116756 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Ok, I\'ll try to clarify what Tor is hinting at. There are issues associated with creating accounts on different e-mail addresses because the cd key is locked to the e-mail address of the account. This means that 2 different accounts with different e-mail addresses would run the risk of steam banning the cd number since it would assume the same cd key was being used by 2 different pc\'s. However. This fix is for those of us who installed the Steam Client and got the error message \'Can\'t connect to the Steam Network, etc ,etc,\' every time they tried to use Steam. The fix works because the original account is recognised by the authorising servers, but they do not seem to validate it. This appears to be caused by attempting to use an old account from the beta versions, or possibly by interrupting the installation of the latest steam versions. In any case, the account info is wrong and it has to be fixed (otherwise you dont get past the error message) By creating a new account IN THIS SITUATION ONLY the problem is solved and the new account is recognised as the only valid account. The old account is no longer recognised. I hope this clears up this issue. (and I hope Valve get round to fixing the problem once and for all in the next client upgrade).' WHERE post_id = 116835 AND is_historical = 1;
