UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CS Pro Mode', post_text = 'This post is directed to the STEAM/VALVe staff if you happen to be browsing this forum =). I\'ve played cs for over 4 years, and I think the game is great.. I\'ve stuck with it through the recent changes that caused you guys all that grief; awp delay, crosshair fiasco, etc. I\'ve played CS:S at LAN last night, and I mean - the graphics are awesome. The concept of the game is great, but the gameplay is really lacking some of the barebone essentials of counter-strike. I mean, there IS a big competitive community out there who love this game and make money off this game. The CPL/CAL etc are all organizations that rely on this game to keep their respected economys flowing without problems. I\'m suggesting, merely suggesting the following: VALVe working together with "higher-up\'s" in the competitive cs community devloping a cs "pro" mode. This "pro" mode would be used at CPL/CAL and any other LAN event that plans on hosting a CS type tournament. I can assure VALVe just from my experience that a CS pro mode would not be tearing up the community, it\'d be making it larger. Theres tons of people who\'ve quit cs due to the massive ammounts of changes and would love to come back to try out a new mode that was designed by gamers. I understand you will question the credibility of the competitive scene but as you can see the CPL (www.thecpl.com (http://www.thecpl.com)) and CAL (www.caleague.com (http://www.caleague.com)) Both have over 10,000 registered players for just CS alone. I\'ve been a gamer ever since I could remember, whether it be sega, n64 or super nintendo.. and what "hooked" me deep into CS was the fact that it was a unique game, slightly fast paced but not too fast; slightly real but not too real. It was a balanced game, a game that I become hooked on. Most games are either too fast and boring, or too real and boring. Counter-Strike was always a real but not game that kept you wanting more time and time again. In closing I ask VALVe/Steam to consider the points in the above and please see if anything could be done, It would not be a waste of time/money to fund this project because you\'d be helping your communtiy.. the communtiy that made the game what it is now, I think our input means something; So please, do the right thing.' WHERE post_id = 919846 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'AGREED', post_text = 'Completely agree with you... VALVe whether or not you realize it, competitive cs players have kept this game alive. Making it popular with their friends, keeping server companies up and running, advertising for the game... without this cs WILL die. I love the new graphics engine but the pro mode is much needed in order to keep this great game we love alive. Tommy "poNzi" McDonough #globalmenace #ponzi' WHERE post_id = 919894 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'i think if there were a pro-mode, everyone would play only that, its like the maps, some are different and nice but we all play de_maps.' WHERE post_id = 919909 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I Agree.. This would be a good move for halve and it would promote a stronger community. I\'ve personally introduced about 4 people to Valve games and im sure this is thew way most people are brought into the game. Anything that could build on this community should be seriously considered' WHERE post_id = 920036 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'i agree, i\'ve played cs for almost 5 years now (3 years competitive) there are some things that need to change back to how they were... first thing being the awp delay, it was something that kept the game fast-paced and exciting, and with the introduction of the new smoke grenades in cs, and especially in cs: source, where the smoke grenades are great, there are good ways to counter the awp. second is boosting needs to be possible in cs: source as well, was a lot of fun and created some good options for tactics. rest was pretty good far as i could tell [] but cs: source pro mode would be a great idea especially if it\'s supported by valve itself, the big leagues and tournaments (lans) and the top of the competitive gaming community.' WHERE post_id = 920134 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'i agree, definitely. i\'m certain valve isn\'t so blind that they don\'t realize that professional leagues/tournaments help keep counter-strike alive. i understand that people who play in "pubs" for fun make up a large part of the counter-strike community, i find that many of those players move on to the new games as soon as they come, leaving counter-strike behind. of course, cs:source will help keep that alive, but for how long? i myself thought about taking up doom 3 and leaving counter-strike behind, due to some of the patches that i myself did not like. valve has made an excellent game, and i commend them for that. however, valve\'s newest ideas do not suit the professional scene. i hear boosting does not work with the new engine on cs:source. (i haven\'t been able to go out and play it myself, correct me if i\'m wrong). boosting and stacking was a HUGE part of professional counter strike. i\'m sure there\'s a way to get around the physics engine, even though i believe it would be a lot of work. i enjoyed the accuracy in 1.3 - though i have gotten over that guns have more recoil - boosting does not seem to be something that can easily be forgotten. and valve, you have made errors before. example - the riot shield. it was an excellent idea on paper, but in the end, it was just too glitchy and slowed down gameplay even more. i commend you for admitting the problems with the riot shield and taking it out of counter-strike source. we just need you to do this with some of the other problems. i agree that if valve would take some time to ask the professional counter-strike community about what needs to be done and actually listen to the ideas of someone who actually plays the game for a living, we would all be better off. take shaGuar for example, he wrote an essay about how the money system should be changed, and valve listened. excellent. now we need to do that for other parts of counter-strike too. ask for our advice, we\'re more than willing to give it. counter-strike IS going downhill, most of the serious counter-strike players will tell you that. valve, all you\'re doing is hurting yourself by not taking input from us. so please, just take our advice. counter-strike cannot live forever the way its going. i love the game and i want it to stay alive, and even if you don\'t make a "pro mode" i would suggest making some modification to the good game of counter-strike, to make it wonderful once again.' WHERE post_id = 920235 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I just want to throw in that I also support this idea. Making your game toward casual players doesn\'t keep the game alive. Casual players move from game to game like crazy, it\'s the smaller core of competitive gamers who stick with a game that keep a steady influx of people to play a game. A pro mode would be an acceptable compromise. Boosting is just vital to Counter-Strike teamplay.' WHERE post_id = 920294 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I agree with this poster 100%. The game cannot live long with the way that the patches are gearing towards : being more "newbie" friendly. Sure, people will buy it, and they will get headshots when they first play the game. Great. But once you play it for 3 days, 3 months, 3 years, you SHOULD be better than people who have just installed the game. And why not? You\'ve invested the time to learn the tricks, the patterns, master the recoil, learn which guns are good and which aren\'t. This is a GOOD thing, and makes people strive to learn these tricks -- therefore investing more time in the game. And when you DO master it, you feel proud. When I first mastered bunnyhopping in 1.6, it felt good, I could do what most players couldn\'t. Then I learned strafe jumping to places where I thought were impossible, (ie the nuke jumps, I can do both) and that gives you something to brag about, which in turn makes the game fun. However, its not at the point where its too unrealistic, all the guns, the recoil, they\'re all realistic, which makes it fun. If I may, I\'d like to bring another game into example. America\'s Army. A game striving for realism. I tried this game for a few days, and what did I say when I first played it? This is too realistic. I dont want to be playing a game where I could be doing something to help keep me alive, but the game won\'t let me. If I wanted to run with stamina, stop as soon as I fall off a ledge, and be blind even though a flashbang lands behind me, I\'d have stayed with that game. But I didn\'t, and I stayed with my favorite game, Counter-Strike. We\'re asking you (the competetive community) in a civilized, organized plea, we\'re almost begging you to help keep this game alive. If you look at the timespan of most games and their activity, you see they may last for a year, 2 years, until a new one takes their place. Counter-Strike, based on an engine built in the mid \'90\'s, has OUTLASTED all the other new games. And why? Because it is fun. However with these new changes, it looks as if you\'re gearing to take the fun out of the game and give someone a dose of the military. Please VALVe, we\'re asking you, keep this game fun, and keep it alive.' WHERE post_id = 920335 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Would pro-mode, be more unrealistic? If I get this right; Pro-mode would allow stacking, no awp delay, and I guess the one shot one kill awp should stay. Counter-Strike was originaly designed for realistic, life like, gameplay. In real life, no 308 rifle would tear through full kevlar and armor at 200 yards. The awp does. The awp also kills you in it hits you in the left arm, once. Stacking is a map exploit. It alwasy has been. Keeping a map exploit for the sake of nothing more than league play is unbeliveable. In reality, jumping and shooting would be so inacurate that nobody should be able to register a three shot burst. In reality, it takes a delay for your eye to focus from normal vision to scoped, is is almost imposible to pan fast while looking through a scope. I vote to advance the original intent of reality game-play in Counter-Strike. If league players want a less real mod, then play 1.5, or another custom mod, the engine is open-source. I also don\'t agree with the idea that non league players are irrevelavant, and that pub players are not a valued part of the financial makeup to Valve. Let\'s advance the game, not have it dragged down by people who are stuck in their ways. Improvise, Adapt, Overcome. If the league players are truly leet, then they should have no problem adapting.' WHERE post_id = 920356 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'That\'s not the point. These newer changes are taking away our "leetness" as you call it, making us at the same skill level as people who just install it. Is that good? No. How do you know that stacking is a map exploit? Even if it was, what\'s wrong with it, anyone can do it. And out of curiosity, how do you know what Counter-Strike was originally designed for? This is a question, not something to put you down. I\'d like to know. Basically what you\'re saying is "Advance the game, make it boring! Lets go!".' WHERE post_id = 920389 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Nobody wants to buy a game where everyone kicks their [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] when they log on. All, fultime Player-killer, RGP\'s are this way. Log on to any of them, and the second someone level 100 sees you, you are dead. No new players, just old players who clock more hours than a normal guy and make the game less enjoyable for the new player. This is why people don\'t like cheaters. Skill or no skill, people don\'t like to log onto a server and just get their [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] handed to them for 30 minuets. People usualy don\'t ptake the tame to learn a game that they have no fun playing. This does not create new players, it cause them to leave and play something else. As a business model, you need the new players. Catering to the exploit players, is not smart. Most people who play computer games, don\'t clock 4 hours a day. Most people don\'t have that much time. Most people want a fun game, not a super competitave "I owned you" slugfest. There is nothing worse than a new player getting killed by an AWP/degal scripter who shoots through all the bad wall model because they shot every inch of the map in their previous 1000 hours of play. CAL and CPL, along with the stats and rank admin mods killed CS. There are already too many people playing for personal rank and forgetting about team play, defuse and hostage rescue. This is what Counter-Strike is. Not, a I\'m better then you are, I owned you, harrasment forum. The game is set up to allow custom games. Just make a custom game and play it in CPL.' WHERE post_id = 920491 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Exactly, we want FUN. Not something that takes no skill to play? If no one wanted to see their [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] handed to them for 30 minutes straight, then why are there people playing? People are doing it now, and it\'s the most popular multiplayer game out there. People want to be that person handing other people their [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color], so they invest the time to get better. If you don\'t have the time, then why should the people who do be punished? It\'s a game, not a army simulator.' WHERE post_id = 920512 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'This is the problem then. You see it is a punishment. The engine is-open source. If you want to create a community within the engine, then go ahead, with a custom game. Don\'t mold the game to the people who play 4 hours a day. Mold your own mod to the 4 hour a day players. Reality and History show that this game is played so much because the learning curve is not that steep. People can pick up the box and get some kills on their first day. If you get upset when a "noob" ownes you, then you need to stop and think that this is a computer game where everyone needs to be able to have the same ability on round one.' WHERE post_id = 920551 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'It is very clear that you have not been paying attention in the community. There was a 1.3 and a 1.5 game ported back, but we need VALVe to either support them or at least put VAC on them because of the cheaters that were rampant throughout. That\'s what we\'re asking for, for a different game, you get your realism, we get our fun.' WHERE post_id = 920636 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Noob4Life: Are you that ignorant? You have no idea how the game works for us old players, you\'re so dumb. why do you care if VALVe makes a pro-mode? Are they forcing you to play it? I don\'t think so! If you don\'t have something intelligent to say don\'t post on this thread. You\'re posting garbage, you don\'t know anything about the game at all. You\'re a typical newb who likes to make this game easier, and easier. Realism? Where have you been! The game was never created for realism, it was always a game in the middle. Real but not to real to the point that it became boring and not fun. Honestly, you\'re clueless. Just don\'t post. How was the game made with realism in mind? You could run while shooting, bunny hop, midair accuracy. Tell me when you can go stand on your neighbors head and boost into a window. The game had its special perks (boosting, jumping, etc) that made it fun! Now it\'s just like every other game that dies after 3-4 months of hype. CS was the game of all games, key word- was. Unless VALVe helps the "pro" community, we\'re stuck at a gridlock that nobody wants to be stuck at.' WHERE post_id = 920790 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CZ Mission Packs List - Mark 3!', post_text = 'This is the new new CZ Mission Packs List thread, replacing the old ones (which can still be found here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=84247) and here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=88092) for reference purposes). Also, the list is now hosted online at www.sandwiregames.com (http://www.sandwiregames.com) - this is where this Mission Packs project will eventually be managed. Here\'s a list of all the CZ mission packs I\'ve found so far, in rough order of release. If you know of any I\'ve missed, or have new ones, reply and I\'ll edit them into my first post in order to keep things orderly... This thread was started on 05-06-2004 at 05:46 PM. Name: The Counter-Strike: Condition Zero Mission Pack Author: Turtle Rock Studios Website: http://www.turtlerockstudios.com/ (http://www.turtlerockstudios.com/), http://www.counter-strike.net/ (http://www.counter-strike.net/), http://cs-conditionzero.com/ (http://cs-conditionzero.com/) and / (/) In-Game Name: CONDITION ZERO Directory Name: TurtleRockCounterTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Release Info/Changelog: Updated every time CZ is patched - go here (/platform/update_history/Condition%20Zero.html) for details. Description: This is the official pack - it comes with CZ. As such, it includes the 18 official maps that came out when CZ was released - but none of the official ones which have appeared since. My main issue with this pack is that it appears twice in the pack list... Bugs/Glitches: - Appears twice in the list - The web link is wrong (does not need the /CZ/ extension, and there are more appropriate sites as well) - There is no in-game link to czmissiondoc.rtf Name: Havok\'s Terrorist Mission Pack N Author: Havok Website: http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/ (http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/) (nothing about the pack though) In-Game Name: Havoks T Missions Directory Name: havokTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.3chavok.netfirms.com/Havokstpack.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 05/01/04. Installation: When installing, use the readme, but don\'t follow what it says about the "CareerGame****" files (**** being the difficulty level) - rename the "CareerGame****" files to just say "****", and then put them in the MissionPacks\\havokTerrorist area with the other files. Also you may want to delete the save file that comes with this pack. Description: The first ever pack. Everything is the same as in Turtle Rock\'s campaign, but you are a terrorist. Things start to get tricky when you have to get a kill with a CT gun, but it gets impossible when you have to rescue a hostage... Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name) - No pack description in the pack selection menu (it just says #Career_MissionPackt instead) - The website link has not been changed - Missions on easy difficulty involving rescuing hostages are impossible - Missions on easy difficulty involving using CT weapons are hard/impossible - Certain files are named wrong, and must be renamed (see above) Name: The Terrorist Mission Pack Y E terrrorist-v-0-2.zip Author: Anders Konradsen Website: http://www.kenand666.tk/ (http://www.kenand666.tk/) (nothing about the pack though) In-Game Name: Terrorist Missions v0.2 Directory Name: Terrorist (BigDaddyK changed this to KonradsenTerrorist when he installed, you can if you like too) Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_dust2_cz, ds_italy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_torn_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_airstrip_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_stadium_cz and as_tundra Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/terrorist.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 0.2, released on 05/06/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v0.0 - Changed the original pack to a T pack v0.1 - Minor bugs fixed - Added a new overview.tga v0.2 - New story line - New map order - Eddit bug fixed (mispelled name, should be Eddie) - Minor bugs fixedInstallation: Unzip all of this to your czero directory - apart from the Terrorist folder, which you should put in your czero\\MissionPacks directory (like it says in the readme) Description: This is what the Havok\' pack should have been like. The new missions mean you don\'t get \'rescue the hostage\' missions, but \'plant the bomb\' missions instead - much better than Havok\'s pack. This is the first pack to use a map that are not the 18 in Turtle Rock\'s campaign - as_tundra Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The National Insecurity Mission Pack Y E ni-v-0-1.zip Author: D-Link Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: National Insecurity Tour of Duty Directory Name: NationalInsecurityMissionPack Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_dust2_cz, ds_italy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_torn_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_airstrip_cz, cs_downed_cz and de_piranesi_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/NationalInsecurityMissionPack.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second version, updated 05/04/04. Installation: Put everything in your NationalInsecurityMissionPack folder, then put that in your MissionPacks folder Description: Basically a CT pack with new missions, but the same maps as in the Turtle Rock campaign. Bugs/Glitches: - The website link has not been changed - The pack description refers to the maps in their old order, not their new one Name: -=[Sj]=-\'s Original CS Mission Pack Y E originalcs-v-0-3.zip, originalcs-v-0-2-v-0-3.zip Author: -=[Sj]=- Ice Killer Website: http://www.clansj.com/ (http://www.clansj.com/) In-Game Name: ORIGINAL CS MISSION PACK V03 Directory Name: OriginalCS Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust, de_dust2, cs_office, de_prodigy, de_italy, de_inferno, cs_militia, cs_havana, de_cbble, de_aztec, de_torn, de_airstrip, de_train, de_vertigo, de_survivor, de_nuke, cs_seige and cs_747 Download Link:You can get the full install here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/MissionPackv03.zip), or you can get the v0.2-v0.3 patch here (http://www.clansj.com/downloads/quickfixv03.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 0.3, released 05/21/04 and last revised 05/22/04. The goals were changed and improved between the three releases, and a custom bot skin was added between the second and third releases. Installation: Inside this zip is an exe - just point it towards your Condition Zero directory when installing and it does the work for you [] Description: Instead of the CZ maps, this pack uses 18 of the original CS maps, hence the pack\'s name. It is also the first pack to use custom bot models. This is well worth getting. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description)' WHERE post_id = 920781 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: The Worst Case Scenario Mission Pack Y E wcs-v-1-0.zip Author: Blue Dog Anchorite Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: WORST CASE SCENARIO Directory Name: WorstCaseScenario Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_downed_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_nuke, cs_siege, de_cbble_cz, de_piranesi_cz, cs_estate, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, cs_backalley, de_vertigo, cs_assualt, de_train, de_fastline_cz, de_office_cz, cs_747 and as_oilrig Download Link: Welcome to Geocitiesville [] You need two files for this - this one (http://www.*********.com/tolgeros/WorstCaseScenario.zip) and this one (http://www..*********.com/tolgeros/WCSwidemaps.zip). You need to copy the 2 links, paste them into your browser and replace the stars with geocities... Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 05/05/04. Installation: Like downloading this pack, installing it is not as easy as it should be. Place the vga files, the db file and thumbnail.tga (all from WorstCaseScenario.zip) into czero\\MissionPacks\\WorstCaseScenario\\ Put the other files in WorstCaseScenario.zip into czero\\gfx\\thumbnails\\maps\\ Finally, put all the files in WCSwidemaps.zip into czero\\gfx\\thumbnails\\maps_wide\\ Description: This pack uses a mixture of the original CS maps and the new CZ maps. It is not a bad pack. Bugs/Glitches: - Installation is difficult (two parts when there could be one, geocities) - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Shadow Operations Mission Pack Y E shadowops-v-1-0.zip Author: D-Link Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: Shadow Operations Directory Name: ShadowOps Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_drugbust, de_train, cs_nightstrike, cs_747, as_oilrig, cs_estate, cs_assualt, de_iraqi, cs_siege, cs_backalley, de_vertigo, de_nuked, de_suntower, de_mill, as_palace, de_ruins, de_scud and de_museum Download Link: You can get it here (ftp://public:content@65.39.204.184/COURTESY/GAME_RELATED/CZERO/MISSION_PACKS/D_MONKEY/shadowops.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version of this pack, released on 06/05/04. Installation: Extract it all to your czero directory - except for the ShadowOps folder, which should be moved into your MissionPacks folder - and the botpacklist.db file, which needs to then be put into the ShadowOps folder. Description: This was D-Link\'s second pack and the first mission pack to feature wholly custom CS maps, but as a result is much much bigger than the ones which came before it. It is still worth getting though. Bugs/Glitches: - The website link has not been changed - Some of the maps included in the download are just renamed versions of CS maps - so don\'t need to be included at all Name: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg]\'s Mission Pack N Author: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg] Website: http://www.mkg-clan.tk/ (http://www.mkg-clan.tk/) In-Game Name: -MKG-[Kidd-Egg] maps mission pack Directory Name: Kidd-Eggmissions Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_militia_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_office_cz, cs_mortal, cs_rats5, de_dock, de_rats6 and de_schoolke Download Link: You can get it here (http://home.filternet.nl/~j.van.baalen/files/KEmissions.zip). Release Info/Changelog: Released on 05/08/04, this is the first and only version. Installation: Everything is already in the right directory, so unzip it straight. Description: This pack uses a mixture of 5 custom CS missions and the CZ missions. A good pack. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Operation Black Sun Mission Pack Y E blacksun-v-1-4.zip Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/) In-Game Name: Black Sun Directory Name: BlackSun Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust2_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_tides_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_cbble_cz, cs_militia_cz, cs_italy_cz and as_oilrig Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun/downloads/blacksun1-4.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the fifth release, released on 05/20/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Simplified install - Some unneeded files removed - Added botprofile.db v1.2 - Added custom names for teammates - Updated bot weapon preferences v1.3 - Completely custom bot file created for CTs and Ts - bot settings updated - NOTE: This version is a beta version - easy, normal, hard and expert modes are all the same for now v1.4 - Renamed from \'Black Sun 2\' to \'Black Sun\' - Readded different missions for different difficulty settings (should now be more challenging) - Changed the number of missions needed to win back to default (3)Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory Description: This pack doesn\'t contain any custom maps, but it is very balanced and well worth getting. The Version 2.0 is in the works at the moment. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The S.I.J. Clan\'s Terrorist Mission Pack Y E sij-v-1-3.zip Author: The S.I.J. (Japanese) Clan Website: http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/ (http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/) (it\'s in Japanese) In-Game Name: T\'s Mission Directory Name: sij_t_mission Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www3.tok2.com/home2/sij/tool/sij_t_mission.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 1.3, released on 05/09/04. Version 1.0 was the initital conversion to terrorists, 1.1 changed the goals slightly, 1.2 changed/removed missions requiring the use of CT-only weapons and 1.3 removed missions involving hostage rescue. Installation: Just put it straight into your Condition Zero directory [] Description: While this doesn\'t have any new maps, some missions have changed. The map order is the same though. It is similair to the Terrorist Mission Pack, in fact. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name and description) - The website link is invalid' WHERE post_id = 920842 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: Tony-Strike: Condition Hawk - Blue Version Y (but N for patch) Author: Rip3001 Website: There used to be one, but it appears to no longer exist... In-Game Name: Tony-Strike: Condition Hawk - Blue Version Directory Name: Tony-Strike Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_vegas, aim_map_usp, cs_old_office, cs_mansion, cs_rio, de_dust2_cz, de_nuke, cs_pacman, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, awp_city, de_rotterdam, cs_downed_cz, aim_dust2003, de_skud_2k1, de_morningstar_csc, fy_snow and de_vertigo Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.kormagraphics.com/tonystrike_missionpack.zip). Also, you need to get the 1.2 patch here (http://www.angelfire.com/hero/ripstuff/tsbv_patch1-2.zip) (for the patch, you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third release, released on 06/16/04. . A Red Version was coming soon, as was another secret Tony-Strike project... but who knows what\'s happened to them now! Installation: Just put it in your e-mail directory. Description: This pack features 12 non-standard maps and five new skins, making it the biggest yet. It is also the hardest yet, by far. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) - Some users have reported the game crashing on cs_rio and other levels. This is due to incomplete nav files for the bots. If you experience this bug, carry out the following steps: 1. Load the map up in either TOD or multiplayer with bots and then open your console. 2. Type bot_stop 1 then bot_nav_edit 1 then bot_nav_analize If, having done the above, the map still crashes, report it here in this thread. Thanks to Rip3001 for the fix [] Name: The Crimson Ice Mission Pack Y E crimsonice-v-1-2.zip Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/) In-Game Name: Crimson Ice Directory Name: CrimsonIce Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust2_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_dust_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_tides_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_cbble_cz, cs_militia_cz, cs_italy_cz and de_vostok_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/crimsonice/downloads/crimsonice1-2.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third release, released on 06/04/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Changed so that you get teammates earlier (3rd map instead of 4th) v1.2 - Removed as_oilrig - Added de_vostok and de_sienna - Increased reaction time for all bots (makes everything slightly easier)Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory Description: Was the first to make use of Sienna and Vostok, and features new missions as well. A fairly solid CT pack, designed to be the opposite of Black Sun. This one\'s very difficult... Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The Terrorist Missions Mission Pack Y E terrorists-v-0-1.zip Author: Napos Website: There used to be one, but it no longer exists... In-Game Name: Terrorist Missions Directory Name: MissionsTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, cs_office_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_tides_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_pirannesi_cz, de_fastline_cz and de_torn_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/naposterrorist-v1.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second release, released on 05/31/04. Installation: Just extract it to your email directory. Description: Much like the other Terrorist Mission pack, only IMO slightly worse. The author has removed the goals which are impssible for terrorists, but not added new ones (e.g. Plant the bomb...). A very small pack. Bugs/Glitches: - The pack name used is already taken by another pack! - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Counter-Strike: Evolutions Mission Pack Y E cse-v-1-3.zip Author: Crotch Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: CS Evolutions 1.3: Counter-Terrorist and CS Evolutions 1.3 - Terrorist Directory Name: CS_Evolutions_1-3_Counter-Terrorist and CS_Evolutions_1-3-Terrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Both Map List/Order: cs_assualt_beta1, de_dust_beta4, cs_mansion_beta1, de_inferno_old, cs_desert_beta1, de_vegas_beta7, cs_office_beta7, de_nuke_beta5, cs_747_beta6, de_train_beta5, cs_siege_beta7-1, de_prodigy_beta5, cs_estate_beta7, de_cbble_beta7, cs_militia_beta3, de_aztec_beta7, de_aztec_1-3 and de_jeepathon2k Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.endlessrayne.com/~crotch/CS_Evolutions_1-3_full.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the fourth release, released on 08/04/2004. Here is the changelog:quote: v1.0: - Replaced Intro music to CZ with music from Deleted Scenes - Replaced CZ background with CS: Evolutions Background - Added Easy, Normal, Hard, Expert difficulty settings - Added thumbnail.tga - Added Old CS Maps, plus navigation files v1.1 - Fixed minor glitches - Utilized BigDaddyK\'s T-Balancing botprofile - Replaced de_aztec_1-6 with de_jeepathon2k to the tour of duty (<<you got your wish Cliffe []) v1.1a - Fixed BigDaddyK\'s "3 problems" including the crash glitches [] v1.2 (never acyually publically released) - Replaced de_inferno_old with de_inferno_old (older verision without the carpet hallway) - Fixed minor glitches in the overview.vdf files - Bots no longer allowed to use shield - Bots use radio instead of mic - Custom background and music is now optional - Added CS 1.6 player models as custom bot models - Added old skin .tga files for bots - Updated Map Challenges - Added custom models/sounds from the CS betas (Optional - for a version listing, see the txt file that comes with the pack) v1.3 - Fixed bots being able to use shield - Added bunnyhoppingInstallation: Extract the \'Required\' section your Condition Zero directory. The \'Optional\' section contains replacement weapon models/sounds and background/background music. Description: This is a very big pack, with a lot of custom maps. It has various versions of the same maps (e.g. aztec from 7 beta and aztec from 1.3). I recommend you get it, if only to see how the maps have changed over time. The replacement weapon models/sounds add even more authenticity. It is also the first pack to have both a Terrorist and a Counter-Terrorist section. This is one of the better supported packs - there is a planned patchsoon. Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack directory name) - Gramatical errors (pack name) - Gramatical errors (pack description) - Known bug: After playing this mission pack ,bunnyhopping will still be activated when switching to another mission pack/creating a server. Simply restart CZ or type anx_bunnyjump 0 in console.' WHERE post_id = 920851 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: The Operation X: Code Omega Mission Pack Y E oxco-v-0-3.zip, oxco-v-0-0-v-0-3.zip Author: -=[Sj]=-Ice Killer Website: http://www.clansj.com/ (http://www.clansj.com/) In-Game Name: OPERATION X: CODE OMEGA v1 Directory Name: OperationX-CODE-OMEGA Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: cs_shogun_final, de_avalley, de_priory, de_aztec2 (unofficial verson), cs_pine, cs_tibet, cs_pipeline, de_indust, de_legato, de_cstle, cs_ciudad, de_tartarico, de_karnak, de_luxor, de_citadel, de_vine, de_plaka and de_celtic Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.liveice.com/download/OXCO.zip). There are also now three small patches - you only need the third one from here (http://www.liveice.com/download/fixv3.zip), which fixes some bugs and also lowers the difficulty settings. Release Info/Changelog: This is the fourth release, released on 06/20/2004. Here is a changelog:quote:v0.0 - Release v0.1 - Lowered the bots\' start from 6 to 4 - Lowered the bots\' agression - Fixed misspelling on the Overview.vdf file - Tweaked the bot profile a bit v0.2 - Fixed an issue with a bot not buying a \'Galil\' or \'IDF\' on the first level on Easy v0.3 - Fixed bots not buying the MAC 10 - Added as_tundra.wad, which was missing from the installer beforeInstallation: Inside the zips are installers. Just point them towards your Condition Zero directory [] Description: This is a very big pack - it weighs in at a hefty 324MB unzipped! It contains custom maps and is the first to feature fully custom skins - every bot has a unique skin! Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Black Sun 2: Reign Of Terror Mission Pack Y E blacksun2-v-1-2.zip, blacksun2-v-1-0-v-1-2.zip Author: SteelV Website: http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/ (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/) In-Game Name: Black Sun 2: Reign of Terror (CT) and Black Sun 2: Reign of Terror (T) Directory Name: BlackSun2 and BlackSun2CT Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Both Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_prodigy_cz, de_builder_yard, de_canal_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_inferno_cz, de_italy_cz, de_fastline_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_torn_cz, de_tides_cz, de_vostok_cz, cs_creetor_cz and de_plaka Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/blacksun2_v1-1.zip), and then put the 1.2 patch on top here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/blacksun2_v1-1-1-2patch.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the third version, released on 06/19/2004. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Removed some unnecessary .tga files (pointed out by BigDaddyK) - Fixed the directory of the team-selection screen thumbnails (they will now display the new models) v1.2 - Fixes an error on de_canal_cz map that disallowed it to run.Installation: Just extract it to your czero directory. You can view the readme online here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun2/readme_v1-2.html). Description: This is one of the best and most solid packs out there. You can now only select ten bots, meaning that you get to know the bots better. The pack uses a selection of standard and well-picked custom maps, meaning it\'s great fun to play. The pack is also regularly patched, which is good. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The Counter-Strike: Condition Zero (REMIX) Mission Pack Y E czremix-v-1-1.zip, czremix-v-1-0-v-1-1.zip Author: peterchen620 Website: http://peterchen620.proboards15.com/index.cgi (http://peterchen620.proboards15.com/index.cgi) In-Game Name: Counter-strike: Conditon Zero (REMIX) Directory Name: czremix Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust_cz, de_dust2_cz, de_corruption_cz, de_vostok_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_inferno_cz, cs_office_cz, de_tides_cz, de_stadium_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_sienna_cz, de_cbble_cz, de_truth_cz, cs_downed_cz, de_airstrip_cz, de_aztec_cz, de_fastline_cz and cs_torn_cz. Download Link: You can get it here (http://peterchen620.orcon.net.nz/czmissionpack/czremix_1.0.zip), with the 1.1 patch here (http://peterchen620.orcon.net.nz/czmissionpack/czremix_1.0-1.1.zip). You must go \'Save target as...\' to get them, otherwise it comes up as being corrupt or invalid (that is what I found anyway). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second version, released on 07/18/2004. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation - Removed cs_militia_cz, cs_havana_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_chateau_cz - Added de_truth_cz, de_corruption_cz, de_vostok_cz, de_sienna_cz - Decreased the reaction time and increased the skill of the enemy bots on Expert Mode. - Increased the reaction time and decreased the skill of the enemy bots on Easy Mode. - Deleted and re-added newer tasks - Added New CZ Model GFX (Thanks to SteelV []) v1.1 - Removed all Spetsnaz Models (In the Bot Selection) - Removed all Militia Models for Terriosts - Improved tasks to be alot more LESS fustrating and easier to complete - Fixed an issue with de_corruption_cz, preventing it from running - Changed Normal.vdf to change the required number of kills on one goal from 45 to 25 - Fixed the EddiT typo - Removed Weasel as there were too many terrorist bots (9 to 8)Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero directory. Description: This pack has a geniunly simple idea. Since release, several new maps have come out officially on top of the original 18. All peterchen620 has done (apart from changing objectives, difficulties etc) is swapped the old for the new. Not only does this mean that some of these maps are in a pack for the first time and that all the maps are of high quality, but it also means that the installer is incredibly small, while the pack is still very different from the offical one. This makes the name very appropriate, as the pack seems like a continuation of the offical one. Taking a leaf out of Tony-Strike\'s book, this pack is very hard though, so beware... Bugs/Glitches: - Gramatical errors (pack name) - Gramatical errors (pack description) Name: The Extended Duty Mission Pack Y E extendedduty-v-1-1.zip Author: BigDaddyK Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: Condition Zero : Extended Duty Directory Name: ExtendedDuty Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List (the order is different on each difficulty): de_stadium_cz, cs_italy_cz, de_airstrip, de_inferno_cz, cs_militia_cz, de_storm, de_truth_cz, de_chateau_cz, de_train, de_fastline_cz, cs_assualt, de_dust_cz, de_vostok_cz, cs_seige, de_cbble_cz, de_piranesi_cz, de_prodiy_cz, de_nuke, de_corruption_cz, cs_backalley, cs_italy_cz, de_survivor, cs_havana_cz, de_torn_cz, de_sienna_cz, cs_office_cz, de_vertigo, de_aztec_cz, cs_downed_cz and (deep breath) de_tides_cz Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/ExtendedDuty-1-1.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the second version, released on 08/03/2004. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v 1.1 - Adjusted Hard and Expert levels for lack of Mac-10, and the availabiltity of the Kreig 552 availabilityInstallation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero directory. Description: If we had a best-size-to-quality competition, this pack would win - it is a tiny pack! It is the first pack at three things. It is the first pack to use more than 6 tours - it has 10! This means it has 30 official CS/CZ maps - almost all of them - in use. It is also the first pack to take advantage of the recent increase in the number of goals per map from 4 to 8 - meaning many missions have 8 goals! And finally, it is the first pack to have a different map order for each difficulty, providing for a more varied play experience each time through. The bots are rock solid - after all, this pack comes from the master of pack knowledge, BigDaddyK. If you want a small pack which is still amazing to play, then look no further [] Bugs/Glitches: None' WHERE post_id = 920860 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: The Skrivan Mission Pack Y E skrivan-v-1-0.zip Author: chessclubreject Website: There isn\'t one In-Game Name: Skrivan Mission Pack Directory Name: Skrivan_Mission-Pack Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Counter-Terrorist Map List/Order: de_dust2_cz, de_italy_cz, he_dodgeball_cz, de_wallmart, cs_office_cz, fy_iceworld2k, de_inferno_cz, cs_assault, as_iraq, de_aztec_cz, cs_estate, aim_ak-colt, de_nuke, cs_747, awp_monopoly, de_train, cs_deagle5 and playground_x Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/Skrivan Mission Pack v1-0.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is the first version, released on 08/24/2004. Installation: Just extract the contents of Skrivan Mission Pack v1-0 to your czero directory (apart from Skrivan Mission Pack v1-0\\special thanks, which I personally put into Skrivan Mission Pack v1-0\\MissionPacks\\Skrivan_Mission-Pack\\. Description: Nowadays, every Mission Pack has to have a gimmick to make it stand out from the other mission packs. Offten that means the packs end up at around 200 MB, but this one is only 9 MB. So what is this pack\'s gimmick? It\'s a good one - in a word, variety. Each tour has one DE map, one CS map and one other map. This makes for some refreshing play, when compared to the endless DEs and occasional CSes that most packs are made up of. One minute you\'re defusing bombs, then you\'re saving hostages, and then you\'re playing he_dodgeball_cz! There are 6 tours, and on top of that there are 50 allied bots (a new record high) to choose from, 10 at each skill level - which means you have more choice in who goes in your team (you could have a team of AWPers, for example!). This pack isn\'t exactly easy, either. So, in summary: Tough pack, lots of variety, medium download size. Good work [] Bugs/Glitches: None That\'s 19 mission packs so far [] (including the official one) Below are any tools designed specifically to aid the creation of mission packs: Name: The Terrorist Balancing Guide Y E tbalance-v-1-1.zip Author: BigDaddyK Website: There isn\'t one Directory Name: It doesn\'t have one, but I put it in BalancedTerrorist Terrorist or Counter-Terrorist?: Terrrorist Download Link: You can get it here (http://www.sandwiregames.com/missionpacks/t-balance.zip). Release Info/Changelog: This is version 1.1, relesed on 05/07/04. Here is the changelog:quote:v1.0 - Creation v1.1 - Readme created - CareerBotProfile.DB was editted to smooth over T teammate imbalances - The T \'Characters\' list was amended (the Eddie/Eddit name mispelling bug again)Installation: Everything is in place for you to unzip it to MissionPacks\\Nameofyourchoicehere Description: This is not a pack, and cannot be played. It\'s actually some better balanced terrorist bots, created for any other pack-creator to use if they wish. BigDaddyK sugests you put the files here into another pack\'s directory, and see how it affects gameplay. Bugs/Glitches: None Name: The RND Mission Pack Creator Author: Ross and Andromeda Website: http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/ (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/) Release Info/Changelog: This is the first and only version, released on 05/16/04. Download Link: You can get the installer here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/setup.exe) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). You computer needs to be able to read Delphi in order to use it, however, so if it doesn\'t work immediately, get this (http://www.infojet.cz/download/files/qtintf.exe) and extract it to your C:\\WINDOWS\\system\\ folder [] Installation: Install the application to your Condition Zero directory. You can also get some sample thumbnails (the pictures which appear by the map names when selecting a map to play) for some maps. Get some awp_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/AWP_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") , some as_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/AS_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") , some cs_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/CS_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As...") and some de_ thumbnails here (http://planeta.terra.com.br/lazer/csmusic/downloads/DE_Library.zip) (you must right-click and go "Save Target As..."). Put these dlls in your czero directory. Then, when you run the application, you can go to \'Library Images\', select the directory as your Condition Zero directory, and extract each of the thumbnails to the correct place, ready for your map pack. Description: Personally I wouldn\'t bother with this. Some of the thumbnails are handy to have, but due to the poor english of the creators this is in fact harder to use than czmissiondoc.rtf (the text file Cliffe made on how to create map packs). Get it for the thumbnails, but don\'t use it for the actual coding... Bugs/Glitches: - Grammatical errors make this almost unusable - Could be more straightforward to use - Is not actually needed ([]) That\'s two pack creators [] Also, here are any Deleted Scenes maps currently availlable: Name: Swamps Of Zambia Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_swamp (cz_swamp1, cz_swamp2 and cz_swamp3) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, released on 05/01/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_swamp.zip). You can also get the source for it if you want, here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_swamp_ent_src.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_swamp1 in the console. Description: An excellent map, made by one of Ritual\'s mappers, so it is very profesionally done - indistinguishable from the official maps. The map sees you first trying to stop terrorists blowing up a railway line, and then you must rescue hostgaes they have captured. My only complaint is that to get to it you have to use the console, and it isn\'t on the World Map - but there is nothing the author can do about this. Bugs/Glitches: - Some terrorists are sometimes inivisble at one point near the end of the mission Name: Bloody Rubble Author: abalone Website: http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/ (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/) Map List/Order: rubble (rubble, rubble1, rubble2, rubble3, rubble4 and rubble5) Release Info/Changelog: This is the second release, released on 05/19/04. Download Link: You can get it here (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/rubble.zip). Installation: Put the maps folder in your czeror folder, then put the graphs folder in your czeror\\maps folder. This is where it ends for people who bought CZ in a shop - but if you bought it over Steam, you must then also download this (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/steamwads.zip) and extract it to your czeror directory. Description: This is not as professionally done as Swamp - there are no custom sound files, or event sequences. The map feels like it has less atmosphere as well. It is also harder to install for people who bought CZ over Steam. Furthermore, it is much harder to play - in places almost insanely hard. I got to this one bit where I found myself with 10 hp, no bullets and facing 2 guys with LAWs. Despite the difficulty, however, it was fun to play through, and well worth getting. Bugs/Glitches: - Harder to install for people who bought CZ over Steam (see above) - At one point I got onto a roof I shouldn\'t have, and could see over the edge of the map Name: Terrorist Retaliation Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_retaliation (cz_retaliation2 and cz_retaliation) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, and it was released on 07/12/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_retaliation.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_retaliation in the console. Description: Again from Kiltron, this map is the first to be played from the Terrorist perspective, breaking new grounds. Set in Scotland, you play a member or the Real IRA trying to rescue a botched mission, whilst fighting the SAS. Like Swamp, this mission features a strong atmosphere, and is as professionally done as the official maps. Well worth a play [] Bugs/Glitches: - Sometimes, the hostages call you \'commander\'. This seems a bit inappropriate. - There is one room inside where it rains. This may be intentional ceiling dripping, but does not seem like it to me. - Sometimes the enemies forget they are Counter-Terrorists now and think they are Terrorists, so start shooting each other. Kiltron knows about this, but does not know how to fix it. - At some points you must press a button to move a crate, which will move back after a certain period of time. On the second of these occasions, pressing the button again does not re-move the crate. Also, it is possible to get stuck on top of this crate.' WHERE post_id = 920875 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Name: Runaway Trains Author: Kiltron Website: http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/ (http://www.planetquake.com/meanarena/) Map List/Order: cz_trainrun (cz_trainrun2 and cz_trianrun) Release Info/Changelog: There is only one release, and it was released on 07/30/04. Download Link: You can get it off Fileplanet here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/cz_trainrun.zip). Installation: Just extract it to your Condition Zero Deleted Scenes directory. To start it, type map changelevel cz_trainrun in the console. Description: Kiltron\'s third release, this map reminds me of a bit in Poke646 and a Sven Co-op custom map - you\'re on two parallel moving trains, and you must move down them both, informing your collegues of hostage locations, defusing warheads (:P) and eventually stopping the trains. This was a pretty tough map - I blew all my health and ammo at the start, and more wasn\'t very readily forecoming. At one point you must take down a helicopter, and I felt that some people might not have enough ammo to do that at that stage of the level, which I thought was harsh. The time limit of 15 minutes isn\'t too tight, but you do have to be aware of it - time limits haven\'t been used much before, and here it adds a feeling of panic whilst playing the map. The foggy atmosphere fitted perfectly, and despite being under 15 minutes (:P) I feel that this is one of the better maps by far. Bugs/Glitches: None That\'s four DS maps [] Coming Soon: - chessclubreject\'s Training Pack - Crimson Ice 2 - Operation: Lone Wolf (peterchen) - It Ain\'t Easy Bein A T/CT, by 1nev1table - The Loner Mission Pack (peterchen) - CS Evolutions 1.4 (Final) - Mooshi\'s rats mission pack (not coming soon, but is coming still :P) - v0.4 of the Original CS Mission Pack (might not be happening now - PMed -Sj-Ice Killer 08/16 - waiting for response) - Tony-Strike: Red Version (might not be happening now - PMed -Rip3001 08/16 - waiting for response) - New secret Tony-Strike project (might not be happening now - PMed Rip3001 08/16 - waiting for response) - Pancak3\'s aim mission pack (might not be happening now - PMed Pancak3 08/16 - waiting for response) - willover\'s mission pack (might not be happening now - PMed willover 08/16 - waiting for response) - DS map: Death From Above, made by Kiltron - you can get a video of it here (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?/planetquake/meanarena/dfa_sneakpeak01.zip) - DS map: Urban Ruins, by abalone - you can see the website here (http://blake.prohosting.com/brubble/urban.htm) - DS map: Frost Mission, by Snake18 - CZ DS .fgd, as created by Kiltron :P Bugs Caused By Valve: The following bugs in packs are not the fault of the pack creators, but due to flaws in CZ: - If you have too many mission packs to fit on the list, some go off the bottom of the screen - and there is no scroll bar - When you complete a Terrorist mission pack, it says \'Goodjob, Counter-Terrorist\' - A terrorist goal which can be set is to kill a CT who is escorting hostages. When this is done, the goal is not awarded - CTs can be set \'plant the bomb\' and Ts can be set \'rescue the hostages\' - I think that if these impossible tasks are set, they should not show up in-game. Ditto for setting these on the wrong type of map. - The weapon thumbnails in the team selection menu are the old weapons - You cannot have more than 8 goals on a mission - this causes the mission to crash upon completion. 8 is plenty though, so I\'m happy, but this is still worth noting here [] - You cannot have more than 71 bots in your team - the extra ones do not show. 71 is plenty though, so I\'m happy, but this is still worth noting here [] - Bots cannot press buttons or drive vehicles - Many of the maps could be called by better names (e.g. \'Tundra\', not \'as_tundra\') in the map selection screen. Valve CAN fix this, by adding extra coding options where this can be varied - Following on from the above bug, de_sienna_cz is displayed instead of Sienna. The same error occurs for Corruption/de_corruption_cz. - When names do not fit onto the map/bot selection menu, they could be squashed or put on two lines - You cannot have first names and surnames - if you do, there must be an underscore between the names. This should be a space - When a map is loading, its\' name often does not fit in to the top of the description box you can see - it is partly concealed behind the thumb-nail. The name should be centered between the left side of the box and the thumbnail, not the two sides of the box - Pistol images are missing from czero/gfx/career/weapons/ in the GCF - Spetsnaz and Militia are not properly supported in mission packs like the other bots - Bots do not connect immediately in the first round while playing, meaning that only half the bots could be involved. This is probably due to "Improved bot behavior when all 32 player slots are filled" and "Improved bot_auto_vacate behavior" in a recent update, but these changes should not apply in TOD play. - There are various other mini-glitches with the official pack (see the listing for it at the top) - Request: Being able to force a player to play maps in a set order, not in tours of three - Request: Being able to give a description of the map along with the goals in the map selection screen - Various corrections/modification requests by BigDaddyK (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=88092&perpage=15&pagenumber=32) - \'Tour Of Duty 10\' is not called \'Tour Of Duty 10\' in-game, it\'s called \'Tour Of Duty :\'. i don\'t know what \'Tour Of Duty 11\' is called, as no-one has created a pack with that many tours yet! - Deleted Scenes: To get to custom DS maps you have to use the console - they aren\'t on the World Map. This would be tricky to fix, but maybe there could be some way a custom mission creator could define co-ordinates to have their map put onto automatically when the world map is loaded - Deleted Scenes: Sometimes the health things on the wall won\'t give you the second health bit, right after you\'ve used the first one - Deleted Scenes: Cannot access a gun to use the flashlight when there is no ammo left in the gun and the player has switched to another two weapons since last using it - Deleted Scenes: You cannot pull out a knife/grenade and STILL have the shield out, a la CZ itself. The shield is put away when you do this' WHERE post_id = 920881 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'To-Do List/Recent Updates: Here\'s what\'s needs to be done atm (in rough order of priority): - ACTUALLY UPDATE THIS THREAD! (sorry, all) - Sort out new zips for the packs whose links are not working (marked with an "N" by their names) - Add all files to FileFront (need to talk to them in order to arrange a more organised system!) - Add Matt\'s Tour Of Duty (new pack I only found the other day!) - Add the Terrorist Campaign Mission Pack (ditto this one! you think people\'d tell me!) - Add Tassadarmaster\'s Terrorist Mission Pack - Add Urban Ruins (DS map) - Chase up some of the mission packs on the coming soon list, to see if they are still coming soon, and if so how soon (PMed everyone 08/16/04 - Mooshi replyed 08/22/04 (pack still in development), D-Monkey replied 09/28/04 (pack cancelled)) Tasks done (so you can see what\'s been updated since your last visit easily!): - Add the CS BANANA Mission Pack Creator Tools - they\'re linked on the CS BANANA page [] (done 10/27/04) - Upload the pack details to CS BANANA (done 10/27/04) - 1.4 of CS Evolutions coming soon... (done 08/07/04) - Added Runaway Trains (done 08/12/04) - Created Mark 3 of this list (done 08/12/04) - Added CS Evolutions 1.3 (done 08/13/04) - Added Extended Duty 1.1 (done 08/13/04) - Re-download all the packs (I deleted my maps folder by accident!) (done 08/13/04) - I found that one pack\'s mirror is now down - Terrorist Missions - if anyone could provide a mirror, it would be apreciated - Update the known bugs list - thanks BigDaddyK (done 08/14/04) - Crotch released a slightly updated pack today with no background in the wrong place - I\'ve updated the pack info to reflect this (done 08/20/04) - Updated links for 4 of the packs - all packs have working mirrors again as far as I know (done 08/24/04) - Moved the Terroist Balancing Guide to \'Pack Creation Tools\', where it more realistically should be (done 08/24/04) - chessclubreject\'s Training Mission Pack is cancelled - removed from Coming Soon list (done 08/25/04) - Moved this post up above the placeholder posts, where it should be, and given it the proper orange tags [] (done 08/25/04) - Added the following to the Bugs List (thanks, chessclubreject!) - "You cannot have more than 72 bots in your team - the extra ones do not show. 72 is plenty though, so I\'m happy, but this is still worth noting here []" (done 08/25/04) - Number decreased from 72 to 71, due to glaring error by chessclubreject :P (done 08/26/04) - Started uploading the pack details to CS BANANA (done 09/05/04) - FINALLY added chessclubreject\'s Skrivan Mission Pack - sorry about that (done 09/25/04) - Removed mirrors of old versions of packs that were listed "just for reference purposes" as I do not plan to support the links to them... (done 10/09/04) - Re-download and rezipped all the packs in more appropriate forms - took me all day! (done 10/09/04)' WHERE post_id = 920885 AND is_historical = 1;
