UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Ok so. I turn on net graph 1, And from what I see, When these spikes and lagouts happen my FPS will stay at 100,99 my IN : and OUT : will still be fluxuating like it does in regulare play but the little line graph things the very buttom one will start going super fast as little red dots the line above it will connect to my green first line and turn into a thick red line and it will go from a lagout to saying flush_entity packet loss to connection warning problume and it happends when it wants to there its just random... I did adaware se , sb S&D and found nothign i ran nortan 2004 nothing i changed internet ip\'s nothing my cable still works fine when im lagged as u can c it in net_graph 1. SO steam since 5/19/04 update this sh*t has been going on and it really need to be fixxed ... And for another thing "[10:39pm] <- SteamBot: Your message has been recorded and assigned request ID#68516. A helper should contact you shortly. The oldest unhandled request has been waiting for 13 hours and 46 minutes. Everything you tell me until you are helped (or you leave #Steam) will be recorded." 13 hours 46 min since the last unheld request was helped is fu*king rediculess.............................' WHERE post_id = 951487 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here are some commands that may help: rate 2500 Variable Maximum amount of bytes that can be received from server in a second. Setting this value too low will cause choke and setting it too high will cause choke(if your connection cannot handle it). It is said the max value of this setting is 20000. Even 32 player CS servers in big battles hardly ever send out more than 12000 bytes a second. Suggested values: 2000 - 3000 for 56k 10000 - 20000 cable/DSL cl_rate 9999 Variable Maximum amount of bytes that can be sent to a server in a second. This command isn\'t really worth changing, you barely ever send out more than 7K of data a second. The default value of 9K is just fine, well, unless you have 56k it isn\'t. cl_cmdbackup 2 Variable Amount of extra commands to be send with normal packets. Setting this value to a high value such as 500 will increase your latency by 15 or so. This command doesn\'t make you send out more packets, it just makes the packets bigger. cl_timeout 300 Variable Max is 3500 Inactivity time before a client is disconnected. Does not affect alt-tabbed timing out any longer. cl_lc 1 Boolean Lag compensation On/Off. Unless you are on LAN, you probably don\'t want to disable this. hpk_maxsize 0 Variable Sets the max size, of custom.hpk file, in megabytes. Default setting of zero has no limit. If your CS joins server slowly or map loading takes a long time change this to .5 or so. If file size is exceeded it is deleted and recreated. Edit: BTW run net graph 3 not 1 or 2.' WHERE post_id = 953702 AND is_historical = 1;
