UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'The Ultimate CS:S Review [35 Screenshots!]', post_text = '(this is a long read, but its highly informative for the people who want the most information out of this game. i\'ve extracted most of the questions you guys have left so hopefully i\'ll answer everything. if you have anything else in mind, ask, and you shall receive...) oh yes, and i got c4 explosions and flashlight screenshots below. I Managed to get to play CS: Source today and as a veteran player im appalled at the mistakes that many people have about this game. From the review\'s ive read, alot of them are wrong and many even jump to conclusions! I\'ve taken screenshots of the lesser known details of CSS and came up with my own review. Here it is with screenshots. [These screenshots were taken without Anti Aliasing to show the raw-ness of CSS. with AA this game looks amazing. These screenshots are also saved at the highest possible quality rate, so you might have some trouble loading them if you\'re on a slow connection. Wait up abit, their worth it [] Dont worry none of them are above 1mb.] First of i wanted to test whether this game was any different from the 1.6/cz we all come to know and love. Opened up CSS, and i must say even the smallest of details was nice. the menu faded in and the menu\'s were the ones we were used to in steam but had a visual upgrade to them, as you\'ll see in the next few screenshots. http://img63.exs.cx/img63/9475/CSS01.jpg (http://img63.exs.cx/img63/9475/CSS01.jpg) http://img22.exs.cx/img22/1315/CSS02.jpg (http://img22.exs.cx/img22/1315/CSS02.jpg) http://img22.exs.cx/img22/383/CSS03.jpg (http://img22.exs.cx/img22/383/CSS03.jpg) Also one thing many reviews and screenshots did not note is the visual options. there are many to choose from and on the computer i used, i had a 9600XT, and i could easily enable all of them without lag. I used fraps and tested the fps, and to my amazement, i got 70-80 fps in everything that i do. maybe it was cause i didnt enable AA, but thats for later []. take note that i also hosted a server (non DS) and it was that smooth. good job. http://img22.exs.cx/img22/2466/JPG04.jpg (http://img22.exs.cx/img22/2466/JPG04.jpg) http://img22.exs.cx/img22/9162/JPG05.jpg (http://img22.exs.cx/img22/9162/JPG05.jpg) ah.. dust 2. first thing i notice when my level loads is that a bottle rolls across the floor. THERE IS WIND! nice stuff. adds to the atmosphere. i must say the textures look better than i thought they would be. the trees swaying in the background, and you can see dust particles moving through the air just like some people have said. and the game feels alot smoother too. i then played around and got a few weapons and stuff and experimented with them. one little thing i noticed was that the awp reverted to its old style and that it was much smoother to use and aim. the zooming effect is also extremely well done. the crosshair has been changed too. http://img49.exs.cx/img49/1239/JPG11.jpg (http://img49.exs.cx/img49/1239/JPG11.jpg) http://img49.exs.cx/img49/3783/JPG12.jpg (http://img49.exs.cx/img49/3783/JPG12.jpg) http://img49.exs.cx/img49/6304/JPG13.jpg (http://img49.exs.cx/img49/6304/JPG13.jpg) http://img46.exs.cx/img46/3862/JPG14.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/3862/JPG14.jpg) http://img46.exs.cx/img46/6712/JPG15.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/6712/JPG15.jpg) http://img46.exs.cx/img46/4526/JPG16.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/4526/JPG16.jpg) now, time to play with the grenade! http://img46.exs.cx/img46/968/JPG19.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/968/JPG19.jpg) as you can see, the grenade effect is pretty cool on the new source engine. (the smoke comes out later, i didnt manage to get a screen capture of that, but this will do.) i tend to lag the first few times i threw the grenade, probably due to texture swapping on the card. after awhile it was smooth sailing. http://img46.exs.cx/img46/5748/JPG20.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/5748/JPG20.jpg) http://img46.exs.cx/img46/2397/JPG21.jpg (http://img46.exs.cx/img46/2397/JPG21.jpg) one thing alot of people are complaining about is the flashbang. yes, it does flash you when you turn your back to it, but it works exactly like the 1.6 counterpart, your flash ends almost the second it flashes you, and goes away like it never happened. the further you are from it, the less it\'ll affect you. also, it feels as if when you continue to run after you are flashed, or you\'re moving when you\'re flashed, the effect ends lesser. overall its not really that irritating as people put it out to be. http://img14.exs.cx/img14/209/JPG23.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/209/JPG23.jpg) http://img14.exs.cx/img14/9738/JPG24.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/9738/JPG24.jpg) http://img14.exs.cx/img14/8030/JPG25.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/8030/JPG25.jpg) http://img14.exs.cx/img14/2538/JPG26.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/2538/JPG26.jpg) http://img14.exs.cx/img14/9738/JPG27.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/9738/JPG27.jpg) ah.. the smoke grenade. i walked straight into the smoke, and the effect is as you see it there. it works best when you see it moving in action. it works great, and the new lighting techniques are wonderful. see for yourself. also. it seems that if you are directly in the middle of the smoke, you can see nothing but grey []. The best thing is, it doesnt lag! well, not when i was playing. it seems that smoke is calculated a little differently and works better. next i\'ll play with the decals. the knife now has an awesome decal, and sprays look great. http://img14.exs.cx/img14/8785/JPG30.jpg (http://img14.exs.cx/img14/8785/JPG30.jpg) http://img27.exs.cx/img27/894/JPG39.jpg (http://img27.exs.cx/img27/894/JPG39.jpg) here a shot where you can see the dust effect a little. specs of dust fly past you as you continue to walk. http://img29.exs.cx/img29/8692/JPG40.jpg (http://img29.exs.cx/img29/8692/JPG40.jpg) why, no one managed to screencap a c4 blast? i did. http://img29.exs.cx/img29/647/JPG41.jpg (http://img29.exs.cx/img29/647/JPG41.jpg) http://img29.exs.cx/img29/7559/JPG42.jpg (http://img29.exs.cx/img29/7559/JPG42.jpg) http://img29.exs.cx/img29/2271/JPG44.jpg (http://img29.exs.cx/img29/2271/JPG44.jpg) The Long awaited Flashlight Screenshots! http://img33.exs.cx/img33/5043/flashlight1.jpg (http://img33.exs.cx/img33/5043/flashlight1.jpg) http://img33.exs.cx/img33/45/flashlight2.jpg (http://img33.exs.cx/img33/45/flashlight2.jpg) http://img33.exs.cx/img33/295/flashlight3.jpg (http://img33.exs.cx/img33/295/flashlight3.jpg) As you can see, the new flashlight is spiffy. the new nightvision looks great too. it does its job, and is less irritating than the old one. however it will be very difficult to see in the light now, much worse than before. http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5066/JPG50.jpg (http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5066/JPG50.jpg) http://img13.exs.cx/img13/1959/JPG51.jpg (http://img13.exs.cx/img13/1959/JPG51.jpg) http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5660/JPG52.jpg (http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5660/JPG52.jpg) more random pics. and notice in the 1st pic, that fence looks really realistic. http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5808/JPG54.jpg (http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5808/JPG54.jpg) http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5733/JPG55.jpg (http://img13.exs.cx/img13/5733/JPG55.jpg) overall i felt they did a complete job. With more updates coming along and even more maps, this game is sure to be fun for a long time to come. finally, shooting feels exactly the same. so is jumping. whoever said you stopped in your tracks now is a loser. it has no difference. sound wise, the newly recorded sounds take some getting used to, but overall they feel more powerful. Different materials have different sound effects too. Shooting the floor tiles in the tunnel will get you a ...well.. breaking tiles [] and your aiming doesnt go to zero when you get hit...silly. Multiplayer wise, the boosting issue is a server side issue, the one i played on had no boosting on, but it didnt affect my gameplay much. Lag doesnt seem to be an issue, it feels the same as 1.6. The new dust map does bring some new tactics into play, you can now walk in some places before where you couldnt. anymore questions or regards? i\'ll try to answer them for you. sorry i cant take videos, the cpu speed is horrible. oh and feel free to spread the screenshots if you must. besides its only a few more days before we get to play it. com specs: 2.66ghz p4 processor with no HT 512mb SDRAM 128MB ATI Radeon 9600XT -edit- oh yes, i played it at my friends lan. he had about 50+ computers hooked up on lan and they had a 20 on 20, and it was abit laggy, but still playable. however dust was abit too crowded for 20 on 20. UPDATE Here\'s a screenie with my framerate on it. Anti Aliasing was turned on at 4x, and that was my average framerate. http://img69.exs.cx/img69/2259/screenie27.jpg (http://img69.exs.cx/img69/2259/screenie27.jpg) SECOND UPDATE UPDATE! http://img56.exs.cx/img56/5537/cssource01.jpg (http://img56.exs.cx/img56/5537/cssource01.jpg) This is the new added passageway in dust, connecting the top of the bridge to the CT\'s snipers nest. makes for more fun situations! http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5636/cssource02.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5636/cssource02.jpg) http://img55.exs.cx/img55/4958/cssource03.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/4958/cssource03.jpg) Items like glass bottles break when you hit them [] hey. even weaved baskets can be cut up. http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5401/cssource06.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5401/cssource06.jpg) hey, you like big explosions? http://img55.exs.cx/img55/796/cssource09.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/796/cssource09.jpg) http://img55.exs.cx/img55/9307/cssource10.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/9307/cssource10.jpg) How about flying Barrels? http://img55.exs.cx/img55/9879/cssource14.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/9879/cssource14.jpg) http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5797/cssource16.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/5797/cssource16.jpg) And this is what happens when you shoot the floor... http://img55.exs.cx/img55/6951/cssource24.jpg (http://img55.exs.cx/img55/6951/cssource24.jpg) How much damage does a HE do? well you have your answer. http://img16.exs.cx/img16/7639/cssource20.jpg (http://img16.exs.cx/img16/7639/cssource20.jpg) http://img16.exs.cx/img16/6370/cssource21.jpg (http://img16.exs.cx/img16/6370/cssource21.jpg)' WHERE post_id = 930690 AND is_historical = 1;
