UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = '#1 Priority: FIX THE NETCODE', post_text = 'Sorry for the capitals... But after about 15 hours playing the Beta, the main thing that is killing the "CS Feel" is the netcode more than any in-game tweaks or "realism" additions. I was on a sub-30 ping server and was about three (game) feet from an enemy, aimed directly at his head and he didn\'t die. This is after emptying half a magazine of an MP5 on him as well. And before all the 12-year olds invade this thread with pointless, "You just suxors, dude!", or "Learn to aim, F*got Biatch!" posts... The problem was experienced by every other person on the 14 player server -- Meaning, this wasn\'t some uber 20 vs. 20 game where pings were spiking all over the place. In addition, I had these cvars set in my config as follows: cl_smooth 0 cl_smoothtime 0.1 cl_interp 0.1 cl_predict 1 cl_lagcompensation 0 The in-game movement is indeed smooth... But again, actual shots registering was a common occurance and the main reason people started dropping from the game because they felt it was "no fun" to just "spray and pray" in the hopes that the server (finally) registered their shots. I know that Source is not the HL-1 engine and that Server Admins really need to upgrade a lot of their hardware to run it... But I can tell you, this is the root cause for half of the complaints and comments about this game on this forum that go like: 1) "My uber X800XT PE/6800 Ultra gets sh*tty frames per second. WTF? Source Suxxors!" and... 2) "Quit ruining CS you Valve Nubs! It\'s too random and has no skillz!" Truly. The hit detection (and object collision) needs to be of a much better quality when the final game ships, or you will have more flaming and upset CS players that actually don\'t know WHY they are saying the things they are (or will). Don\'t make the mistake UBISoft did with the Raven Shield netcode -- which is actually about at the same, subpar level as the CSS Beta -- And just leave it like this because there are much better games with better netcode that register hits and misses as they should be.' WHERE post_id = 1007528 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'well said... experienced similar stuff in the past few days - netcode defiantly needs working on.' WHERE post_id = 1007535 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'That isn\'t necissarily due to the net code. Usually mistakes like that are due to the users computer. Eg- you shoot the guy just as , as he is getting lag it just doesn\'t seem as obvious like in 1.6 when models looked liek they were having siezers.' WHERE post_id = 1007538 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Nicely said. The hit detection is... cringing at times.' WHERE post_id = 1007541 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No it is not because of the users computer. I\'m getting 100fps no choke or loss and pinging under thirty on servers. I\'ve lost count of how many times I\'ve ran up behind someone with autoshotty, plugged them in the back/head with all 7 shots, and had only one or no shots register. When you flank someone and have 7 easy pointblank shotgun shots the result shouldn\'t be that you have to switch to your pistol to finish them off. The netcode/hitdetection is way off at times. And yes it has a lot of that same crap feeling you get from raven shield where what the server decides hits hardly ever matches up with what you see. This has to be fixed or it will kill the FEEL of CS. If physics objects have to be reduced to get the netcode back to at least 1.6 quality then they should do that.' WHERE post_id = 1049814 AND is_historical = 1;
