UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'i got no problems with the netcode, but let me tell you what i saw the other night. I was spectating a guy on the other team and i watched his pitiful aim, first off to the left and then to the right and then finally on him. The only problem was that the other guy had enough time to turn around and shoot him in a few shots. Well, instantly the guy I am spectating begins by saying \'omfg\', so I chirped up before he could go further and said, \'you missed him, so be quiet". Well dude begins losing it on me and I tell him I was spectating him. So he continued to tell me off etc. Now what I ask is, how many of you are the same when you go on about emptying a mp5. If I have noticed anything it was rare and at times even I will (to myself) fly off the hook when I am playing. Let\'s face it, it\'s a new game, it has bugs but the hit prediction is not as bad as everyone has made it out to be. I have put in about 75 hours if not more into this game and though there are some things that need improving, I have had zero problems with netcode(packetloss is server) and the hitboxes have been fine. Anyhow a lot of what the original poster has said is great, but for the tweaking, I\'ve done nothing on my CS:S and it runs perfectly fine and smooth as CS 1.6. Could be because of some of my XP tweaks.. I don\'t know. I\'m looking forward to some CS:S Update news.' WHERE post_id = 1050794 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by mediaxs IF the choice was between having barrels and trash to kick and shoot around or having the SOLID netcode/hit detection of 1.5 or 1.6, then I\'m sorry to say the barrels and trash HAVE TO GO. The gameplay would be much better without the objects and have solid hit detection than it is now with iffy fudgy lazy hit detection and some trash, tires, and barrels to kick/shoot around. hey, we need that new buggy stuff to make css a new better game, just let them fix it..if you dont want those trash and barrels, you HAVE TO GO back to cs 1.6' WHERE post_id = 1050832 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'How to convert you old 1.6 buyscript', post_text = 'This post was made to explain to players of Counter-strike source how to convert their old buy script from CS 1.6. Its painfully easy realy, what you have to do it edit old script and add "buy" infront of the weapon your are buying. Here is a example: quote:The Old 1.6 way alias buyteamheavy "sg552;primammo" quote:How to do it in CS S alias buyteamheavy "buy aug;buy sg552;buy primammo" Here is a list of all the commands the buy command supports: quote: usage: buy <item> primammo secammo vest vesthelm defuser nvgs flashbang hegrenade smokegrenade galil ak47 scout sg552 awp g3sg1 famas m4a1 aug sg550 glock usp p228 deagle elite fiveseven m3 xm1014 mac10 tmp mp5navy ump45 p90 m249 How to install your newly made buy script First off find your steam folder, then got to: Valve Steam\\SteamApps\\Your@MailAddy.com\\counter-strike source beta\\cstrike\\cfg place your buyscript in this folder ( or the one you can download from the bottom off the post). Then edit your config.cfg and add quote:exec buyscript.cfg ( Notice that you dont have to add exec cfg/buyscript.cfg, it assumes your running a config inside the cfg folder) Download example buyscript (http://eks.wtfux.com/buyscript.cfg) ( Hosted by: www.clanhq.com (http://www.clanhq.com) ) EDIT: Also note that the source engine will not allow you to load as big "scripts" as HL1 did. You will get a error message " Cbuf_AddText: buffer overflow", this means in my xp that the file you executed is to big. Just cut you script into several files (HL1 allowed me to exec files around 15kb but source only allows about 7kb)' WHERE post_id = 1007846 AND is_historical = 1;
