UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'you should check your console to see hwat error message yuou get. then you should use the search feature on the forum to see if anyoen else has the same problem. Heres the post in response to these problems (IF its the one you have): /forums/show...threadid=101151 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=101151) mostl likely, its your firmware. this happened to a lot of poeple abouyt a month back, and they said that you should downgrade your firmware. I didnt want to do that, so I took the alternative. It says it in the post, but Ill tell you. You go to Play Games on Steam. You right click the game(s) you want to do this with. Then you click Create Desktop Shortcut. On the desktop shortcut, right click it and go to Properties. In the directory, add a space at the end and type this in: +clientport 26007 Then you hsould be able to play A-OK, is your problem. First you should check your console to see the error message/' WHERE post_id = 1049305 AND is_historical = 1;
