UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: What I Suggested To Valve "LINUX"!!!', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Kschreck *snip*...The denial of service is a Windows only attack. Hmm you don\'t know too much about DOS attacks do you ? The very term applies to a level that is OS independant quote:Linux can not and will not ever be attacked. *snip*... LOLage, do they tell you this at the propaganda meetings... Seriously try reading some of the professional (and perhaps more objective than the sources you have read so far if any) sites on hacking. http://project.honeynet.org/ (http://project.honeynet.org/) Some time ago I read about a test they did (I cannot find the article anymore) They put up a RedHat Linux box, straight out of the box, default settings all the way through. They gave it an interesting DNS name, and waited. Actually they only waited I think 2 or 3 hours then the system was port scanned, attacked AND compromised. Would you like to repeat that statement I quoted ? quote:The files on a Linux computer are owned by the user. Which means even you can not acces them unless you give yourself permission. *snip*... Apart from WINtendo systems (for an explanation of that search the forum I explained it before) NTFS is equally secured. Did you however hear of a root kit? a type of tool that let\'s you have administrative permissions on a compromised computer, It\'s called a root kit because of it\'s origins in the unix world, this includes the BSD and SVR4 branch alike which would include linux. quote:The hacker can not get the password because it goes through around 8 levels of encryptions. I *snip*... again with a root kit you can just change the users password, but why would you with root permissions you can access them anyhow. (even with a million levels of encryption) quote:the Linux computer can have Internet.*snip*... Right, but this is the very thing that would make it prone for hacking attacks.... quote:It would deffinetly guarenteed them that they will not be attacked. If you really believe this, you are one of those people making their computer even more prone to attacks, cuz blindly trusting your security based upon which OS you are using is just plain stupid and NO guarantee no matter which OS you use... I\'m really growing tired of people having religious discussions about Operating Systems. This is NOT a rant against Linux, Unix, LUNIX, Microsoft Windows, Apple MAC OS, IBM OS/2 or any other Operating System, it\'s a plain objective analysis of the post you wrote... And before anyone asks about LUNIX: I included it because someone misspelled linux in another thread, probably not knowing that is a UNIX/Linux version for C64 http://hld.c64.org/poldi/lunix/lunix.html (http://hld.c64.org/poldi/lunix/lunix.html)\n\n__________________ *Help! the paranoids are stalkling me!*' WHERE post_id = 149214 AND is_historical = 1;
