UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'It\'s a brilliant idea, but it won\'t stop Warez. Someone will crack it just like they always do. Whether they crack the executable and remove the necesseity for Steam, write some kind of "no Internet" crack, or simply design some sort of local Steam server emulator with a hacked client... it\'ll just fuel the cracker community and then Valve will have to start all over. But I don\'t know what I\'m talking about really. I don\'t have any knowledge on the subject beyond supposition. I guess we\'ll see, this COULD be the end of warez, or it might just delay the warez until a few weeks after release, which will fuel sales on it\'s own. Doom 3 and Sims 2 were both available illegally on the internet before they even hit store shelves... but they\'ve both sold extremely well anyway. Whatever, I think it\'s a great idea, and I don\'t care about it because I have an internet connection, I have Steam, and i am going to buy Half Life 2. Steam is free, the internet is cheaper than it\'s ever been (Bellsouth is offering DSL for $9.95 a month) and the only people who lose are the dumb little kids who go to Wal-Mart and convince their illiterate parents buy games without even considering the limitations of their ancient PC.' WHERE post_id = 1247741 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I agree with you on that one. I also have steam, cable connection(balls fast), and a locked copy of HL2 on my PC. I think it will definitely cut down on the amount of people using a cracked copy of the game. Developers are smart but so are h4x0rz and there is no way to stop them, they will eventually find a way to crack anything. I kinda liked the battle between h4x0rz and cd protection myself, CD protection would be knocked down and then they would just develop a different one, I think they are up to Safedisc 3.3 or some crap now. LOL.' WHERE post_id = 1247771 AND is_historical = 1;
