UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '^ That\'s (30 fps) a myth. If we couldn\'t tell the difference between 30 fps and 100 fps very few people would complain about having crappy fps. A good monitor will refresh @ 100 hz. I\'m also positive that I can tell the difference between 50, 60, 70, 80, 90 and 100 fps. Anything below 100 is not perfectly smooth for me because of the high refresh rate -- particularly when my view is changing (such as turning the mouse and turning around ingame). Otherwise, it looks fairly smooth with 60 fps and a static camera. FPS games are very different to watching TV or playing strategy games etc. Also, TV / Cinema has motion blur to fool our brain, computer games do not. *edit - http://www.100fps.com/how_many_fram..._humans_see.htm (http://www.100fps.com/how_many_frames_can_humans_see.htm) []' WHERE post_id = 1264513 AND is_historical = 1;
