UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'As I understand it, cards are restricted to one purchase per game. This is to prevent fraud. There is, of course, the slight possibility that a situation such as your\'s will arrive (as it apparently has), but it is acceptably nominal. The obvious work-around is to use someone else\'s credit card.' WHERE post_id = 1269742 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Well i understand to limit it becuse of fraud, but why limit it to one? Also the wording they use to tell you this makes you think that you can use it more than once before that message should come up. It says "This transaction was not prossessed becuse the Cedit Card below has been used too many time in Steam." It should say, Has already been used in steam, within <time frame> (as i am sure you would eventualy be able to use it agian)' WHERE post_id = 1269765 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Let me see if I have this correct', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Lunchtimemama As I understand it, cards are restricted to one purchase per game. This is to prevent fraud. There is, of course, the slight possibility that a situation such as your\'s will arrive (as it apparently has), but it is acceptably nominal. The obvious work-around is to use someone else\'s credit card. 1. Steam requires a CC to buy a game via Steam. 2. VALVe will not accept cash, a check, or a money order for Steam purchases. 3. Only one purchase per card per game is allowed. Assuming all of the above is correct, I\'d say this poster has a VERY legit complaint. I personally would be royally pi$$ed off if this happened to me- enough so that I would refuse to spend my own money on the game (i.e., beg for it as a gift if I want it badly enough). My bank issued my card to *me*. Who are YOU people to tell me how often I can use it? I think I may have to give a call to the CC vendors your system supports and see if they know about this. After all, they make a percentage of every sale here, too, just by virtue of their cards being used. I wonder what Mastercard or Visa would have to say to a vendor that only allows a customer to use the cards they issued once per customer (I already know the answer to that, I just want YOU to think about it for a bit). I bet they\'d have some reservations about renewing their various service contracts with VALVe. If I stressed it enough, I bet they would even make a call or two to the Interested Parties and have a little chat. "...use someone else\'s credit card." Beg pardon? Are you *asking* this guy to commit CC fraud, or are you merely asking him to trade on connections with friends or relatiives to get VALVe\'s software? Both really, really suck as a business plan, VALVe people. You should know this. I think is a VERY dumb thing to do, for a number of reasons. How would you feel if a grocer did this? A power company? "I\'m sorry, sir, but you are not allowed to use your card to pay the surcharges on your bill, because you already used the card to pay the bill itself. No, sorry, we don\'t take cash, checks, or money orders. I guess you\'re just SOL..." Would *you* do business with a company like that? Had I known about this policy when I got my ATI card (one with a voucher) I likely would have bought the lower-priced non-HL2 Nvidia card instead, and just waited to get the game off the shelf when it came out. To protect against fraud? Have you never heard the phrase, "never try to bull$hit a bull$hitter"? With all the fraud protections on accounts these days, I very, very strongly doubt this is the real reason. It may be the reason you were given, but I really doubt it\'s the real reason... it\'s just a ridiculous explanation. Even Enron made better excuses than that! Come on, VALVe, you can do better than this. And yes, I would consider this one a Steam "dealbreaker" if I didn\'t already have a voucher. Until you drop this policy, VALVe, I think I\'ll err on the side of caution for my friends and tell them to just get it off the shelf and not bother with the Steam-download thing. I want to protect *them* against fraud, too. See? That door swings both ways!' WHERE post_id = 1270541 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'It came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database?' WHERE post_id = 1270625 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Sitro It came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database? I doubt that would matter much to the card issuers if they don\'t already know about this policy. If you *really* don\'t like it, that\'s the way to go. They would be ones who are actually in a position to force a change in VALVe\'s policy regarding this.' WHERE post_id = 1270653 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Sitro It came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database? We store what is called a "one-way hash" of the number. It can never be used to find out the original number, but we can hash an incoming number and compare the result to the list of hashes in the database. There is an incredibly small possibility (eg, it\'ll never happen) that two card numbers result in the same hash value. Incidentally, passwords work the same way. Your Steam password never leaves your computer. A one-way-hash is calculated of it, and that is what is actually sent to our servers and stored in / compared to the database. It\'s a very common technique - Windows domain passwords are the same.' WHERE post_id = 1270676 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'As far as the original topic goes - we\'re looking into some things that may allow us to loosen the restriction. For now though, we have enough fraud w/ stolen credit cards that we really need the restriction. There are some places in the world right now where such fraud is very common, and every time it happens it costs us money (more than just the purchase price). If it happens too much, it can jeopardize our relationship with the bank. It\'s really lame, in other words. Even something as simple as raising the limit to two purchases per package per card, would not be good: it would basically double the fraud rate. Believe me, it\'s no fun rejecting people\'s attempts to give us money! []' WHERE post_id = 1270696 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I trust you in this fact but for example in germany aren\'t many CCs in use. So my father agreed to by the games for my friends with his own card. Is there a way to reactivate the card?' WHERE post_id = 1271185 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Maddin I trust you in this fact but for example in germany aren\'t many CCs in use. So my father agreed to by the games for my friends with his own card. Is there a way to reactivate the card? Create a Support request using the link at the top of the page. You have to view one FAQ before submitting a request, fyi. Then click "ask a question".' WHERE post_id = 1271191 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'CS:Source - Walling needs to return [and other aspects]', post_text = 'I belive that dealing moderate damage to an enemy through a wall and knowing certain spam spots to get an edge on the map was something unique to counter-strike. The ability to \'wall\' someone was nicely implemented into the game. It adds a different aspect to the game, especially in competative lan tournaments. Getting walled is part of the game. It was part of the game to shoot at someone while they were running behind a wall. That is Counter-Strike. I dont think that an excuse like, "Oh, it was removed to help protect against cheating" is a good excuse, because that is what VAC is there for. Valve should be working on VAC to the point that where players could have a high trust in it that other players wouldnt be cheating. Source has completely removed traditional walling and made shooting thru doors and thin walls nearly useless. I think we need to bring back part of Counter-Strike. [edit] I was going to add this to a different post in the future, but I decided to do it now after seeing the first reply. Some other things that valve needs to think about to increase gameplay. I\'ve always belived that gameplay should come before beauty and realism. When spraying or at farther ranges it is nearly impossible to see where your bullets are landing, so you cannot efficiently control your spray. These should be visible. It is nearly impossible to tell when you\'ve hit someone in the head. In traditional CS if they werent equipped with a helmet you could see a trail of blood exit the enemies head. In Source it looks more like if a small can of spray paint was heated and it happened to burst. In traditional CS there was always a loud and rewarding sound to a headshot, the \'dink\'. If this game wants to replace Counter-Strike in league play and online play, I think it needs to live up to it\'s ancestors gameplay value.' WHERE post_id = 1274970 AND is_historical = 1;
