UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'I believe I found a solution', post_text = 'Follow these steps to get a fresh CS:S dedicated Linux server if you have problems downloading srcds_run: # is the linux command prompt and I make comments in () 1. Make sure you have no previous .blob files # find / -name "*.blob" /root/.steam/ClientRegistry.blob (I ran steam as root before so this file is in root\'s home directory) /usr/steam/srcds_l/InstallRecord.blob 2. If you find any, rm them # rm -rf /root/.steam/ClientRegistry.blob # rm -rf /usr/steam/srcds_l/InstallRecord.blob 3. If you ran steam before, let\'s start fresh. Delete the /usr/steam directory # rm -rf /usr/steam 4. Then remake it and a srcds_l subdirectory and go there # mkdir /usr/steam # mkdir /usr/steam/srcds_l # cd /usr/steam/srcds_l 5. Now download the steam linux client from here # wget http://acm.cs.umn.edu/~cleric/steam.tar.gz (http://acm.cs.umn.edu/~cleric/steam.tar.gz) 6. Uncompress it # tar zxvf steam.tar.gz 7. Make sure it\'s executable # chmod +x steam 8. I also made sure that root owned the file # chown root:root steam 9. If you have not made a DEDICATED steam account to run this dedicated server you should do that now. # ./steam -command create -username <uname> -email <real email address> -password <passwd> (If you have created this account anytime before, go to the next step) 10. Now run the command to install CS:S and al the necessary files with it including srcds_run # ./steam -command update -game "counter-strike source" -dir . -username <uname> -password <passwd> -remember_password (make sure to use a uname and passwd that is NOT the one you used to purchase HL2 or the one you use to run your steam client to play. Use the uname and passwd you created just to run the dedicated server) (also make sure that there are no hlds* files in this directory. If you started fresh, you should have any) 11. The download will take some time so go eat something or take a nap or go play CS:S on your client box in the meantime. (If everything is working you\'ll see: Checking/Installing \'Counter-Strike Source Shared Content\' version 13 ... Checking/Installing \'Linux Source HLDS\' version 11 ... The above line means you will get the srcds_run file) 12. Once everthing is downloaded you\'ll get "HLDS installation up to date" 13. Now you should be able to run the server # ./srcds_run +ip <your host ip> +maxplayers 16 +map cs_office +log on -autoupdate &' WHERE post_id = 1296861 AND is_historical = 1;
