UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: Slightly', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Opo I personally use all five of these commands, I\'m not to sure about how much they affect FPS, but I haven\'t noticed any difference. The only ones that may hurt your FPS is the mp_decals and r_lod commands. Do you really notice a big difference in image quality or do you have view side by side screenshots to really see it?' WHERE post_id = 1298534 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Uhhh', post_text = 'The commands change just what my descriptions say. The mp_decals on max makes the game look better because you won\'t be playing and then suddenly see a bunch of bullet holes just dissappear off the wall. The cl_ragdoll_collide is nice because you don\'t see anymore ragdolls clipping through each other. The cl_c4dynamiclight looks good because you can see the ticking light on the C4 bounce off walls and objects around where it is planted. The r_lod command is really nice because, well if you go on de_dust or de_dust2 you know those weird seed baskets things, if you\'re far away from them, you\'ll notice they have a huge black mark at the bottom of them its like a tear in the basket then when you get closer it suddenly disappears into nowhere. This command set to r_lod "-5" prevents such things from happening. The r_decal_cullsize command is nice because it allows you to see decals from any distance. So when you get close to them they don\'t suddenly appear out of nowhere, you can see them from no matter how far away your are if you set this command to 0. The commands in the list so far don\'t affect image quality, they make effects and various things in the game look better. But who knows there might be some commands that improve image quality, just haven\'t found them yet []' WHERE post_id = 1298572 AND is_historical = 1;
