UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'The AWP Delay: Revisited (Valve, please take note)', post_text = 'Upon listening to many different sides of the issue, I believe I have come to a better solution to the delay that was added onto the AWP to protect against the "quickswitch exploit." Basically, KillerKoala is right in the sense that while the game has realism factors, it also has other factors that detract from the realism, therefore making the gameplay much more enjoyable. I couldn\'t agree with that view more. While the game has many factors attached to realism, there are other factors that are added to the game playability that make Counter-Strike one of the best FPS games on the market, even after 5 years. Basically what I\'m going to try and do, is explain KillerKoala\'s opinion, Professional player\'s opinions, as well as the opinions of some of the other players I have talked to. Then I will give my solution to the AWP. While I know that many have tried to argue against the change, and many have argued for the change, this is my arguement; and I feel that this option would best represent the ENTIRE community. From what I understand, KillerKoala has said that if you "quickswitched" that you would do the following: 1) Scope. 2) Shoot. 3) Switch from the AWP to your pistol. 4) Switch from the pistol to your AWP. You would then be able to shoot your AWP within a matter of miliseconds. All of this without seeing the pistol animation, the rebolt animation, and the AWP animation, which would mean that you skipped through the animations to be able to shoot the AWP faster. So basically, a delay was added to compensate for the animations being skipped after completing a quickswitch. Now, talking to a few professional players, I have come to understand that the game has been slowed down in the competitive scene due to the change. Many players feel as though Valve has been making the game slower over the years, mainly starting with the release of 1.4. I recently had the opportunity to play 1.3 and I am going to admit right now that the game has indeed become much slower gameplay-wise over the years. Of course, that\'s not nessicarily a bad thing on it\'s own. However, the changes that have been made that have made the game slower could have been gone about differently, which would make the game more fun. This arguement is about the AWP, so I\'ll continue. Overall what I think the community needs, is to have some sort of balancing. While I agree with this statement: "You can\'t be pro at your own game, you can only be pro at a game that everyone plays." made by a fellow player, it\'s getting harder with each update to maintain a good league system. As a competitive player, I would like to offer my input, because I love this game to death, and I feel as though I am being treated like a pawn. I have heard one of the creators of Counter-Strike call the competitive community a "vocal minority," and I completely disagree. I view myself as a paying customer, and as a paying customer, I fully believe that I deserve an equal voice. My solution is as follows. Create a serverside option that allows the creater of the server to decide how the weapon should work. You already have an option that allows for silent-running, so I see no problem with adding an option that gives a sense of balance to the community. Basically the option would work like this. [ ] AWP Behavior Having the box checked would make it so the AWP would have a delay on it. Having the box unchecked would make it so the AWP would have no delay. This would cater to the competitive players, as well as the players who feel as though quickswitching is an exploit. Contrary to KillerKoala\'s belief, the ability to quickswitch was never the reason why many of the top competitive players got so many kills. The facts are that almost every single player who KillerKoala talks about still quickswitch (even though the delay is there) and they still the same amount of kills. The problem with the "exploit" being "fixed" is that it has slowed down the pace of competitive Counter-Strike by a large margin. I\'m not asking for a professional mod, I\'m just asking for an option. This is a very big issue to a lot of players, and while it might not seem that big to the likes of KillerKoala and people who agree with him, it is big to us. I would also like to point out, that beyond being a "vocal minority." We are you\'re biggest supporters, and we are the reason you\'re game was ever sucsessful. If you disagree with that, please take note... Professional Counter-Strike has been featured on ABC, NBC, CNN, and more. We have multiple leagues and tournaments sponsered by many of the biggest names in the buisness. Intel, Hitachi, etc. Teams are sponsered by Nvidia, ATi, Intel, AMD, etc. We have stuck with Valve through thick and thin, and WE are the "vocal minority" that kept this game alive and well. I\'d like to know how many of the players in public servers have stuck with this game through the beta versions. I\'d like to know how many of these players even play the game for more than a couple months. I\'d like to know how many of these players need to complain before you (Valve) decides to make the game slower, easier, and less fun. Above all, I\'d like to know how many of these useless updates it will take for you to realize that you\'re ruining the game. Worry about VAC, not non-existant exploits.' WHERE post_id = 1317848 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'i agree.' WHERE post_id = 1317913 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Oh god, not another thread. Just lock this. You can\'t do options for exploits. It\'s a sniper weapon, not a sidearm. If you used it to do quickshots, that\'s not what a sniper weapon is used for. I know you think it looks cool, but it\'s unrealistic in every manner. A sniper shoots from a concealed place from a large distance. It isn\'t meant for close quarters. That\'s just its disadvantage and you\'ll have to deal with it.' WHERE post_id = 1317996 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I have to say that was a very well written article, and I totally agree with the author.' WHERE post_id = 1318002 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Yes, it is unrealistic koala... This isn\'t America\'s Army, or Firearms, when you get shot in the face or leg you aren\'t hindered in any way but health and armor, oooh let\'s make it one headshot = death by glock. Helmets seem to cover our faces too let\'s get rid of that, and hey while we\'re at it let\'s kill gooseman and make him spin inside his grave. I agree with Aeon' WHERE post_id = 1318093 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'CS obviously isn\'t about realism because in 1.6 Valve made headshots from the M4 non-lethal in one hit. Cool, huh? Edit: what he said ^' WHERE post_id = 1318095 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Koala. There is really no point in having a sniper weapon in Counter-Strike then is there? If you honestly take the time to look at the game for a good 10 minutes you\'ll realize that this isn\'t DoD. You can\'t sit in a window a mile away from somone so that they can\'t see you. This game is almost close range even at far range. Don\'t lock this. If you\'re going to lock this, lock every single post that has been made in the suggestion forums. This is my belief, and it is my opinion. My opinion counts, wether you would like it to count or not is irrelivant. Do NOT talk to me about realism Koala. You wouldn\'t know realism if it hit you in the face. You wan\'t to talk about realism? I\'ve talked it before, and I\'ll talk it again. M4A1: Switch between this weapon and a pistol after starting to put a silencer on and you won\'t see an animation. But then when you switch back to it, the silencer will be there. Realistic? I think not. M492: Running around with a fully automatic machine gun while shooting? Try it. I dare you to not shoot you\'re self in the foot, or drop it. Oh yeah, and I believe that a machine gun shoots faster than an MP5. Scout: Running faster with a sniper than a knife??? Blasphemy! Realistic? Again, no. You keep trying to pull the "realistic" card on me man, let me tell you, it will never work. Ever. Oh yeah, try and run around with an AWP all over the place. Go ahead and shoot it while running. Prepare to break your arm. Koala. I grow very tired of you\'re "realistic" excuses. They aren\'t realistic at all, it was, and still is a bad thing, and it needs to be balanced. Yes I DO believe that an option to keep the ability to quickswitch is a viable option, and yes I DO believe that you are wrong. Also, I\'m assuming these weapons are strapped to the player somehow, so actually, grabbing you\'re AWP and putting you\'re eye to the scope wouldn\'t take as long as you think. Take that from somone who knows a little bit about that. It\'s like you said, added "unrealism" for added gameplay. If the AWP had a strap on it, it wouldn\'t even take 1.5 seconds to get ready, especially in CS. Taking out you\'re M4 would take more time to be completely honest.' WHERE post_id = 1318101 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks guys, appreciate the input.' WHERE post_id = 1318128 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'mal1ce. Please just do me a favor and edit that from you\'re post. I want this post to be read by Valve and that doesn\'t help at all. Thanks.' WHERE post_id = 1318143 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Shut up Killer :\\ I agree aeon' WHERE post_id = 1318147 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'See, your problem is you don\'t see realism and gameplay together so you fail to comprehend anything if it\'s not 100% real or 100% gameplay. CS is a combination of both so it doesn\'t kill gameplay while trying to keep the realism factor.' WHERE post_id = 1318151 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'while your at it make the no-scope accurate p.s. bit hacks' WHERE post_id = 1318152 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Killer Koala See, your problem is you don\'t see realism and gameplay together so you fail to comprehend anything if it\'s not 100% real or 100% gameplay. CS is a combination of both so it doesn\'t kill gameplay while trying to keep the realism factor. You have become better at Evasion! (200) the best path would probably be a "pro" or "league" mode, which has been mentioned a lot. But then, I don\'t expect them to do it, because it is a lot of work for something they won\'t get paid for :/ And a balance between realism and gameplay is good, but the awp delay is unrealistic, "unfun", and unnecessary' WHERE post_id = 1318175 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'koala\'s a nerd' WHERE post_id = 1318189 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No Koala. YOU don\'t get it. You can have realism and gameplay at the same time. You however are intent on ruining the gameplay for those of us who don\'t agree with you\'re opinion. Look, Say I\'m a counter-terrorist. I have an AWP. I\'m not pulling the AWP out of my pocket right? I have it strapped on. With the following in mind: You can switch from pistol to knife to primary weapon to knife to pistol in less than a second please take a second to understand that the above is an example of "gameplay." Now go ahead an take what I said about the AWP being strapped on. Since there is no delay on weapon drawing, why is there a delay on the AWP? We can draw every other weapon in the game and shoot each one just as fast as the other ones. Well... Every weapon EXCEPT the AWP. Now why is that? The weapon is strapped on, shouldn\'t be too hard (given the fact that there is no draw delay) to put my eye to the scope, aim and shoot if I have the skill. Right? I got you. Now please try to prove me wrong.' WHERE post_id = 1318191 AND is_historical = 1;
