UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No one can steal your STEAMID, its a myth (unless ofcourse they steal your account). The pirated version must be bound to an account which has its own STEAMID, its not randomly generated. Some people will get the "SteamID in use" error in certain servers because they are cracked servers, just ignore those servers as they usually suck anyway.' WHERE post_id = 1443273 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'its your own fault if someone gets ahold of your password whether it be from you telling them or a key logger or some other way.' WHERE post_id = 1443300 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'In the near future you will be able to make a CD Backup of your games. KeyGens as a rule don\'t work and we have never had an instance of a KeyGen\'d CD-Key getting registered on a Steam account. Most often people lose accounts because they don\'t use strong passwords. Having your Account name and password the same is one of the most common ways to get your account stolen by another user...so don\'t do it. Also keep in mind that you shouldn\'t share your login information / e-mail account password / or *ANY* other account information with anyone...including (especially) your brother / sister / kids / mates / buddies / pals / pets / etc. If you use Steam at a cafe or friends\' house make sure you log out completely.' WHERE post_id = 1443444 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by DougV In the near future you will be able to make a CD Backup of your games.Is this feature being added directly into Steam to back up the files? quote:KeyGens as a rule don\'t work and we have never had an instance of a KeyGen\'d CD-Key getting registered on a Steam account. Unfortunately, there have been a few occasions where I used to play (when the old WON system was in place) and it said my key was already in use. Now if that person had my key (which they must have got from a keygen) - there is nothing stopping them registering that key with that account on Steam [exception being that I got registered first] - The same could be said for HL2 keys. How can you be sure that a year down the line someone who buys HL2 legit in the shop cant get online because someone keygenned the key thats been in a sealed box for a year?' WHERE post_id = 1443599 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Spooky Is this feature being added directly into Steam to back up the files? >Yes Unfortunately, there have been a few occasions where I used to play (when the old WON system was in place) and it said my key was already in use. Now if that person had my key (which they must have got from a keygen) - there is nothing stopping them registering that key with that account on Steam [exception being that I got registered first] - The same could be said for HL2 keys. How can you be sure that a year down the line someone who buys HL2 legit in the shop cant get online because someone keygenned the key thats been in a sealed box for a year? > We have not had that happen in Steam with someone using a KeyGen. More likely someone has opened the box in the store and taken a picture of the CD-Key and used that to register in Steam. As a rule, whoever has the physical CD-Key from a retail box is the owner of the key. We will disable any account containing a duplicate key. You can\'t imagine the stories that people come up with. Also, never purchase an account from someone on EBay or IRC...chances are they have obtained the account through less than honest means and there is a great liklihood that account will be disabled and you will be out your purchase price.' WHERE post_id = 1443670 AND is_historical = 1;
