UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'BAD ERROR! NEED TO FIX IT! Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit', post_text = '"Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit" I get that error when I try to start Half-Life 2 under "My Games" in steam. I bought the game for over 30 hours ago and I\'ve tried to fix this problem ever since (well I slept a little too). I\'ve tried all tips and tricks, workarounds etc etc. Someone says it\'s my DVD-drive. I doubt, then it\'s 20 more DVD-drives out there wrong. Because that\'s the amount of people I have spoken to who also encountered this problem. Imagin all other people with this problem world wide -- I can\'t even think about it. This is really really bad. And for you who wonders: Yes, I have installed Steam, Half-Life 2, entered my CD-key, authenticated with Steam, downloaded all updates etc etc. Steam even said to me this morning that everything was okey and I was ready to play the game. But ACK, NO. I still get "Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit". Why the HECK must Steam use my CD when I\'ve installed the game and even get a green light from Steam servers? This is really bad. And to extra clear. I\'ve updated my list firmware (hardware) and software for my DVD-drive/burner (which is a Plextor one I bought yesterday, JUST (I repeate, JUST) to install, play and ENJOY Half-Life 2. Any fixes for this? Will fixes be released? If it is, when? As I wrote, I\'m not the only one with this problem. When I buy a game, I would AT LEAST expect to play it whenever I want. And finally, just to say my opinion. Valve, you\'ve sunk deep in my thoughts about you as game developers. You don\'t have my respect anymore, I\'m sorry.... Thanks, All help appreciated. Cheers to all other people having problem, I feel your anger. UnclePunk' WHERE post_id = 1533571 AND is_historical = 1;
