UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'good golly i want hl3 right now!' WHERE post_id = 1543157 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'This thread is too good to drown really. I hope the GMan isnt merely a middle-man for some big organisation, I prefer to think of him as some kind of higher-being, and the ending to HL2 would seem to bear that theory out. As would the marvels that Dr Breen was describing to Dr Vance in his office at the citadel.' WHERE post_id = 1543221 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I like the G-Man is Gordon theory, but for some reason it just doesn\'t entirely jive with me. Here are my reasons: 1. First of all, we have never heard anyone in the games refer to the G-Man as the G-Man. That name was just tacked onto the Model if you wanted to use it in Half-Life Multiplayer and it has just stuck ever since. We technically don\'t really know what to call him, unless there is some VALVe interview somewhere I am missing. In my opinion, that makes the G-Man = Gordon freeMAN link really flimsy. 2. Part of the reason that VALVe never has Gordon speak is because that way, we become Gordon Freeman. He does not know anything that we do not know. Our confusion in the game is the exact same as his. If the G-Man turns out to be Gordon from the future, wouldn\'t that detract from this ideal? 3. In response to Gordon having the teleportation technology...well....he doesn\'t really. He has been teleported several times, yes, but never through his own devices. Always it was some outside thing that did the teleporting. In the first game, he used pre-established portals and was sent through to Xen by the Science Team. And in Half Life 2, it was Dr. Kleiner\'s teleporter that bounced Gordon around. 4. The G-Man makes too good of an antangonist. If VALVe made him into a future version of Gordon, there could never be a plot where Gordon tried to escape his forced service. 5. And besides, if the G-Man was Gordon from the future, the entire series would be a paradox. If you assume that the G-Man is from the future and is coming back in time to set Gordon on the right path, well then who went back in time to set the G-Man on that path back when he was in Gordon\'s shoes? If you assume that the G-Man is changing his own past, couldn\'t he end up erasing his existence of causing some kind of time-space paradox? It just gets too confusing to try to work out, in my opinion. Anyone else\'s thoughts?' WHERE post_id = 1546092 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Okay, I don\'t have time to respond to all of that, but that part about Ravenholm and the Priest tending his flock--- Go read the bible if you want to understand that [] It has nothing to do with eating, its indicating that these zombies were once humans he knew that were in his congregation. He mentions later while killing them that he is letting them rest-freeing their souls. There are many references, in this part and throughout.' WHERE post_id = 1546200 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I think that the combine once enslaved the beings of xen, i read in a article in a website (cant remember which one) that the cuffs around the vortigaunts wrists might have been used to control them, and that nihlanth or whatever also had those around his wrists. so i think that the combine are from a diffrent dimention and they want complete control. One thing that supports this theory is that when you are talking to one of the vortigaunts he says "keep fighting, for freedom" or something so i belive that they were once enslaved by the combine as well. edit: Or perhaps the combine are just humans that are being used to control the human race kinda like they did with the xen, and breen was just a pawn of these yet unseen beings like nihlanth was.' WHERE post_id = 1546294 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Just a slight idea on the g-man = freeman thing, I was reading everyone else\'s posts, and noticed everyone saying gordon doesnt speak, which is true. BUT, if you listen to G-man talk, he has sort of a speed up, slow down, stutter kind of speech. perhaps that is why gordon never spoke, because he had that problem, seein as how g-man would then = freeman, just a possibility.' WHERE post_id = 1546433 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Awesome thread guys... I\'m sure (or hope, rather) that Valve will release an expansion that tells more of the story. As I was reading this, me and my roommate have just been playing HL2 for the past few days nonstop. He was looking at the thing on Dr. Vance\'s wall that says "Earth surrenders to Combine after 7 hour war" and he says "You should be able to play the 7 hour war" And then I said "As... Adrian Shepard." He says "Holy ©©©©..." Valve, we\'re on to something, baby.' WHERE post_id = 1546467 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Playing as Shepard during the 7 hour war would be pretty intense. Think about it this way: If you do assume that the Combine really were in control of Xen, then in order to partake in the 7 Hour War, Shepard would have to fight his way out of Xen, through the Combine, and back to Earth, ending up right in the middle of this huge war. Now that would be cool. EDIT: Although on second thought, this does kind of sound a bit like Halo... I think Shepard makes the most sense to play as in an expansion back, from a story-telling point of view. With him, they can essentially do anything they wish to, since he has no true ties to the Half-Life 2 plotline yet. With everyone else, that becomes a problem. Playing as Alyx has been mentioned, but you would have to connect that around times when she wasn\'t standing at Gordon\'s side. Playing as Barney would be interesting, but as others have said, he isn\'t incredibly tied into the plot aside from just a grunt\'s point of view. And playing as the G-Man himself...I don\'t know, seeing the G-Man running around with a gun just doesn\'t work for me. It would ruin the all powerful illusion of him we have at this point. Another thing to consider though, is that there are others from Black Mesa we haven\'t heard much about. What happened to Dr. Rosenberg, who we helped escape in Blue Shift? Or, if you want to get really fussy, what about the two female scientists you played as in Co-Op Playstation 2 Half-Life? I haven\'t played it myself, but I assume they escaped as well....' WHERE post_id = 1546539 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'i am stoopid', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Ash Dizzle Awesome thread guys... I\'m sure (or hope, rather) that Valve will release an expansion that tells more of the story. As I was reading this, me and my roommate have just been playing HL2 for the past few days nonstop. He was looking at the thing on Dr. Vance\'s wall that says "Earth surrenders to Combine after 7 hour war" and he says "You should be able to play the 7 hour war" And then I said "As... Adrian Shepard." He says "Holy ©©©©..." Valve, we\'re on to something, baby. awww man, I feel like an idiot because I can\'t remember names... but who the hell is Adrian Shepard?' WHERE post_id = 1546605 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'He\'s the marine character you play in Opposing Force.' WHERE post_id = 1546662 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Half-Life 2/Steam', post_text = 'Well, I bought Half-Life 2 a few days ago. Day after I bought it, I sent this email to Valve Software. Frankly, I would urge anyone else having "issues" with Half-Life 2 to do the same and really kick it home into the minds of those at Valve that either don\'t know, or do not care about this. Half-Life 2\'s distribution method in no way resembles anything that might be considered acceptable. Valve Software\'s contact email is: contact@valvesoftware.com (mailto:contact@valvesoftware.com) -------- Hello, I\'ve purchased Half-Life 2 today, and have played it some(albet while being required to be online while doing so). Seems to be a fairly decent game, though I\'ve not gotten particularly far in it. You guy\'s have recaptured the immersive feel of the original Half-Life with the gameplay. Good job. However, this isn\'t why I\'m contacting you. Steam is. In a word? Awful. I\'ve just now received my "receipt" from Steam regarding my CD Key. This is six hours after I actually installed the game. (Which took two hours itself, as well as several issues with the installation software.) I\'m not going to rant or tirade like many of those expressing their dissatisfaction with this arrangement--in a more abrasive manner--on the SteamPowered forums. I suppose my feelings on how you\'ve handled Half-Life 2 are best summed up like so: If you wanted your customers and fans never to come back, all you had to do was ask. Much easier than spending a few years developing Steam and HL2, I would think. I wish you well on your future business, but will never again purchase any software you\'ve bundled with Steam. PC Games should not be more complex or painstaking to install and configure than operating systems. Regards, Jason Hutton -------- Also posted here: http://www.livejournal.com/users/xbahamut/ (http://www.livejournal.com/users/xbahamut/)' WHERE post_id = 1541924 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'ive used both steam gold pack and retail version both installed and played with no problems what so ever. what took 2 hours to install it took me maybe 10 minutes or so' WHERE post_id = 1541979 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Excellent letter. FOr my own part, I ranted and screamed and swore at them 8 times or so that day as well as leaving two voice mails for Gabe. It didn\'t help with the game or steam or anything, but I felt a whole lot better. I was patient up until Tuesday, at that point, I felt I had been raped or otherwise violated after believing them for over a year. I\'m probably naive but I actually believed the 9/30/2003 date and even bought the game on 9/1/2003. I don\'t even know what steam is yet. All the cultists sound like its the same as the sun rising in the east, but I paid for H-L2, not steam and I don\'t really care what it is. With Zone Alarm, I found I can play w/o letting steam report to these evil barnyards, so that\'s kind of good. And I\'ve been taking my residual anger out in the forums and on the kool-aid drinkers who insist steam is perfect. LOL! It cracks me up that people can be so deluded. But then, I believed in 9/30/2003 so I guess I shouldn\'t really laugh at the poor brain dead zombies as I was one once myself.' WHERE post_id = 1542252 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Nobody has ever said Steam is perfect to my recollection. I just feel people are overreacting. I\'ve never had any real issues with Steam that didn\'t resolve on their own with patience. This clues me in that all those that are complaining are mostly impatient.' WHERE post_id = 1542667 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Retail users CD / DVD check solution', post_text = 'Sticky would be nice! I posted this in another thread. I did this for my retail install of Condition Zero (which also required the CD to run) and when I have some spare time I\'ll do it for HL2 and CS:Source. Once you have registered your CD-KEY with Valve through steam, If you can be bothered to download all the HL2 and CS:source content you can play without the DVD. Just create a new steam install in a different location, open that install of steam and download the content through steam. HL2 and CS:source will appear is the "My Games" list and you can install them from there. Same way ATI vouchers had a CD Key your CD Key is registered to your Steam account and it\'s that key that allows you to download the content that you have purchased. This should install it the same way as everyone who purchased it through steam meaning you won\'t have to use the DVD to play it. Vivendi are responsable for making sure the DVD\'s etc are not copied and distributed easily, you can\'t blame them for that considering the Piracy these days. It\'s a lot of pissing about but it works. I\'d like to see Valve fix this for us retail users but it\'s unlikely as it will probably breach their contract with Vivendi or something and cause more problems. This may be our only solution STICKY STICKY STICKY there are a few threads about this subject already!' WHERE post_id = 1549110 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'So basicly you just re-download all of the half-life 2 content?' WHERE post_id = 1549147 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'not exactly. You need to install a seperate version of steam, either on another partition or just a different folder...eg. c:\\MySteam\\Steam Anything as long as it\'s not your default Steam install. Right click and exit your existing steam install before you do this though. Then log into the new steam install with your existing account details by double clicking the steam.exe file and then download the content through steam. This version of steam will not detect your games installed on your previous install of steam BUT once logged in it will recognise your account and allow you to install HL2 and CS:Source. Please rate this thread if you think it\'s helpful I know it\'s harsh having to download all the content even though you\'ve got the disk but it\'s the only way I know of.' WHERE post_id = 1549217 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'yeah.. lets spend an extra $40 or so on a dvd that you hardly even use... just get the silver pack through steam... its cheaper and u get more than the "collectors" edition.' WHERE post_id = 1549219 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by unleashed yeah.. lets spend an extra $40 or so on a dvd that you hardly even use... just get the silver pack through steam... its cheaper and u get more than the "collectors" edition. that\'s not really what this thread is about but I only paid �26.99 for my DVD. I\'m just trying to help people like me who are pissed off with having to disk swap whenever they play CS:Source or HL2' WHERE post_id = 1549233 AND is_historical = 1;
