UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'So you are saying I got an DVD just to ignore it and download the game instead, which was the very reason I bought the DVD (lowly ADSL would take a week to download HL2)? Brilliant solution... I think Valve need to add the option to: STEAM ONLINE - NO CD REQUIRED STEAM OFFLINE - CD REQUIRED Simple as that. No warez issues, since I assume steam will catch on if you use an illegal account.' WHERE post_id = 1549291 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:No warez issues, since I assume steam will catch on if you use an illegal account. The problem is that in theory you could buy the DVD, register the game, return the DVD, then not only do you have a \'free\' copy, but whoever buys the DVD after you will find their CD key is already registered...' WHERE post_id = 1549304 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'redownloading now. thx for info.' WHERE post_id = 1549339 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'thanks mate! okay laymans terms, do this: 1. Exit Steam 2. Install a new installation of Steam (just steam nothing else) to a different folder or partition. Eg. C:\\My Steam\\Steam or d:\\Program Files\\Steam if you have a D drive with plenty of space. Whatever as long as it\'s not the same place as your existing Steam install. 3. Log into the new Steam install with your existing steam account. 4. Goto play games and in the "My games" section you\'ll see that HL2 and CS:Source are not highlighted or \'lit up\'. 5. Steam recognises what games you are entitled to by the account you have with Valve, therefore it knows what your allowed to download. It\'s no different to those that had ATI voucher CD keys, were entitled to the software in the same way they are. 6. Double click it/ right click choose properties - whatever it will then let you install them through steam which will download all the files you need. This way you won\'t have to portion of the retail install that tells the game to check you DVD is inserted. 7. Play the game and never complain again! Hope this helps people who like me are fed up with swapping disks, I don\'t like no-cd cracks. Apart from being illegal you never know what malicious code is in them.' WHERE post_id = 1549410 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by MarkG The problem is that in theory you could buy the DVD, register the game, return the DVD, then not only do you have a \'free\' copy, but whoever buys the DVD after you will find their CD key is already registered... So? How many people would do that? Do shops even accept an opened game for return? It is really such an issue that they needed to piss off all their retail customers? Besides, you don\'t need a CD for the original Half-Life, meaning you could do the same with it, but that didn\'t bother Valve?' WHERE post_id = 1549412 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by merka So you are saying I got an DVD just to ignore it and download the game instead, which was the very reason I bought the DVD (lowly ADSL would take a week to download HL2)? Brilliant solution... I think Valve need to add the option to: STEAM ONLINE - NO CD REQUIRED STEAM OFFLINE - CD REQUIRED Simple as that. No warez issues, since I assume steam will catch on if you use an illegal account. I agree with you 100% but at the moment this is the only way and I doubt that will change because Vivendi will probably be a bit annoyed with Valve if they just disable their anti piracy measures. I\'m just trying to help the people that really want a solution.' WHERE post_id = 1549460 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Does this actually work?', post_text = 'Has anyone got this to work? I hope it works (I\'m in the same boat) but I\'m a bit dubious, for this reason: if you have the CD-key version on your Steam account, you may get the retail (.i.e. containing "source shared securom.gcf") version when you download it from Steam, since Steam knows you\'ve purchased the retail version, as opposed the online only product-key version. So you\'ll still need your original CD/DVD to run the game once you\'ve downloaded it. I\'m trying this suggestion now. Only 200 minutes until I find out if it works.' WHERE post_id = 1549470 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Sorry, but IT WILL NOT WORK. Steam knows by your CD-Key that you have the retail version and will re-download the "source shared securom.gcf" file with the protection too and use it when starting the game... EDIT: ahhh, amphion beat me to it by a minute...' WHERE post_id = 1549481 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Besides, you don\'t need a CD for the original Half-Life, meaning you could do the same with it, but that didn\'t bother Valve? But you only have half the problem with an offline game: people can pirate it by installing it and returning the CD, but you don\'t get irate customers finding they can\'t play a game they just bought because the CD key has been stolen and registered. Also, I suspect that it\'s more an issue for publishers than for Valve. Valve would probably prefer that everyone bought from Steam in the first place [].' WHERE post_id = 1549483 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Steam Client Update Released November 19, 2004 A small number of Half-Life 2 customers have been experiencing problems while playing the game, and we have traced these issues to corrupt Steam cache files. We\'ve released a Steam update (/index.php?area=news&id=351) to help resolve these issues. If you have been experiencing problems such as crashing during gameplay or startup of Half-Life 2, please restart Steam and then click on one of the links below. Steam will then automatically verify your cache files. The verification process will take roughly five minutes to complete. To validate Half-Life 2 click here (steam://validate/220) To Validate Counter-Strike: Source click here (steam://validate/240) To Validate Half-Life 1: Source click here (steam://validate/280) We\'re also investigating a solution for the sound skipping problems a small number of users are running into. We\'ll have a solution for this as soon as possible. return to news page' WHERE post_id = 1555897 AND is_historical = 1;
