UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Is there a definite fix the update problem?', post_text = 'Ok, Ive been scouring all the posts looking for away to get steam(half life, counterstrike etc ) working again. Some post say to reinstall but the next will say that doesnt even work. Does anyone know what we are really supposed to do to remedy this problem. Steams news page was anything but specific about what to do.' WHERE post_id = 181025 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I hear ya I can\'t get it to work either after last update. I tried reinstalling the whole thing again after the 700 mb download yet notta still stuck. I feel as If I\'m back at the very first day I installed steam non-beta. Seems like even though I got the steam installer with all games that it is trying to update all games from scratch.' WHERE post_id = 181125 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'fixed', post_text = 'Okay I got it working again. Here is what i tried and here is what worked. I first tried to repair the installaion with the uninstall wizard, no luck, then i figured f it. I uninstalled steam by itself, and then reinstalled the 723mb file. Ran steam, it updated itself in minutes. First try didnt work, but then after a reboot all is well. Side note: I think this method will only work based upon the settings you chose when you installed steam in the first place. I have noticed that i can no longer play half life (or locate its executable for that matter ) I tried the same method above on another computer on my network and it didnt work. But on that computer the half life exacutable is still visible and he can still play 1.5. I think its all hinged on your first install of steam and the option of leaving the file system intact or caching it ( i think those were the options ) but i cant remember what i chose. Hope this is of some help to anyone. http://www.clanlebowski.com (http://www.clanlebowski.com)' WHERE post_id = 181156 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Hl2 crash ---FIX---', post_text = 'hello, i like many of you had hl2 crashing to desktop when i tried to load it, but when i was looking for a solution i came across something at another forum, and here it is. Originally Posted by fireflaie Hi all Here is the translation of a solution to have the game working !! Part 1 : -------------- Go in the directory : E:\\Valve\\Steam\\SteamApps\\STEAM _ACCOUNT_NAME\\half-life 2 there is a directory named "bin" that contains many .dll etc Part 2 : -------------- Enter the "bin" directory and copy all the files (ctrl+A, ctrl+C) go back at E:\\Valve\\Steam\\SteamApps\\STEAM _ACCOUNT_NAME\\half-life 2 then paste the files here (Ctrl+V) Part 3 : -------------- Select all the files and directorys (EXCEPT THE "BIN" DIRECTORY) in E:\\Valve\\Steam\\SteamApps\\STEAM _ACCOUNT_NAME\\half-life 2 Copy it !!! Part 4 : -------------- No Go back in the "bin" directory then Paste the files and dir you\'ve just copy if windows tell you that there is files that have the same name so just overwrite it, as you want that\'s not seams to be a problem if you don\'t Part 5 : -------------- Quit Steam => Reload Steam, right click : Games, right click on Half-Life 2 and Launch the game Enjoy if that works , sorry if that don\'t This worked perfectly for me, and i hope it does for you guys too !' WHERE post_id = 1570007 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'you are my hero. the steam fix didnt work but this sure did.' WHERE post_id = 1570726 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Thanks for the advice, was able to help a friend out.' WHERE post_id = 1570760 AND is_historical = 1;
