UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Yet another temporary "stutterbug" fix until patch release...', post_text = 'System: Athlon XP2400 Radeon 9700 pro NForce2 chipset 1G Dual channel DDR Seagate 160 7200 IDE SBLive SP2 I\'ve tried all the cvars - none of them make a difference for me. I\'ve tried all the Catalyst drivers, public and beta. The best performing one thus far (30-60fps minus the stutter, w/2X AA, Tri-lenear AF, no V-Sync) has been the Omega drivers: http://www.omegadrivers.net/ (http://www.omegadrivers.net/) Everything\'s defragged. But nothing has been able to rid me of the "stutterbug" yet... ...except for one very ODD thing: ***Reducing the process priority of hl2.exe from "normal" to "low" in the Windows task manager.*** ...don\'t ...ask ...me ...why. It just works for me. And at least one other forum visiter who has tried it. On a "playability" scale of 1-10, where before doing this would be about 5, changing this setting makes it around 9. The unbearable stuttering is now reduced to an occasional mere hiccup. I can wait no longer for a patch to enjoy this amazing game, so this will have to do for now. I am posting this for those of you desperate for a fix, willing to try something new. I hope it helps at least a few of you. [] If you are unfamiliar with how to do this, here is a walkthrough (it\'s quite easy, I promise): -With HL2 loaded at the menu screen, hit the keys "ctrl+alt+delete". This will minimize the game and bring up the Windows task manager. -In the task manager, select the "Processes" tab, locate "hl2.exe" in the list of processes below, right-click, and select "Set Priority > Low". -Close the task manager and bring HL2 back to the front. It will take about 30-40 seconds for the game to regain control. -That\'s it! Hopefully, this helps you as much as it does me. If not, doublecheck that you have absolutely NOTHING else running in the background, as the game is now temporarily set to be the least important task running on the computer and everything ELSE gets first dibbs on CPU cycles. Once again, I don\'t know why this works (you\'d think it would be the other way around), but (for me) it does. -------------------------------------------------- Well, I have some even more odd news to report. I just tried out some of the trainstation level first with, then without the priority tweak using my NForce Soundstorm instead of the Live and got some amusing results: With the tweak - the same typical hiccups, but some of the dialog is out of sync - ex; Dr Kleiner\'s first line on the video screen was absent at first, only to begin playback at the same time as his second line. No major stutters. Without the tweak (normal priority) - a few more hiccups, no major stutters yet (my Live card st-st-st-stutters like crazy at this setting), but dialog WILDLY out of sync. None of the Dr\'s lines played back until the 3rd line, and then all at once - also, the soldier harassing the civilian lines were delayed and piled on top of one another. So I guess if you guys are having some bad dialog sync/playback issues, this tweak might help you there as well. [] --------------------------------------------- Good luck, and hopefully Valve will have this all sorted out soon enough! []' WHERE post_id = 1738223 AND is_historical = 1;
