UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I don\'t think there is such a thing as entirely random (when dealing with computers, anyway). Everything is pseudo random, or uses some kind of value to generate the result (such as the exact time in hours, minutes, seconds and milli/microseconds). I\'m not 100% sure on this, feel free to correct me if anyone knows better.' WHERE post_id = 275493 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'You\'re right - however, a pseudo-random number seeded from the microseconds value of the PC clock is close enough to true random-ness to make no difference in practical terms. What the OP was getting at is that almost all software validates CD keys using a simple mathematical algorithm of some sort. For example, Microsoft Publisher 97 used the laughably simply system of xxxx-yyyy-zzzz, where xxxx must be divisible by 7, zzzz must be divisible by 9, and yyyy can be any value. Reversing this process is how keygens work. If Steam issued totally random keys, and after payment gave you X days to enter your key and register it with an account, then keygenning would be nigh-on impossible because of the sheer quantity of 13 digit numbers out there.' WHERE post_id = 275944 AND is_historical = 1;
