UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I located the problem with the lag and solved it at least for now. The update to the server VGUI2.DLL module is the culprit. The good news is you can replace it with the old one and the problem will go away and there isn\'t any compatibility problems, AND you don\'t lose anything except the problem from what I can tell. If you don\'t have a backup of the old VGUI2.DLL then you can grab a copy from here: http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip) Just put it in place of the one in your HLServer directory. The lag is caused by the fact that the server FPS with the updated VGUI2.DLL module seems to be unbelievably low, I was getting 16fps, and any ping booster just gives you totally weird results (certainly not a boost). Try the fix and let me know how it works. Edit: You can also try and run in console mode for the server which bypasses the VGUI2.DLL, do this by adding " -console" to your launch properties. Important update: The 09Feb2004 Update appears to have fixed the VGUI2.DLL problem for both stand-alone and for client HLDS (yea!).\n\n__________________ Would you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?' WHERE post_id = 319516 AND is_historical = 1;
