UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'HIGH Priority Batch File for HLDS', post_text = 'Here is a somewhat generic batch file to start your Stand-Alone HLDS Server at HIGH priority. http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/Steam_HLDS.bat (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/Steam_HLDS.bat) You can put this on your desktop for easy clicking. Inside it looks like this: c: cd c:\\HLServer start /high c:\\HLServer\\hlds.exe -port 27015 +maxplayers 9 -noipx -condebug -secure If you don\'t have your hlserver installed on the C: drive edit the file and change it to your install disk (edit 3 places there). The other thing you will want to change is the maxplayers (9 here). For internet this depends on what your uplink connection can handle. If you don\'t know, then go to www.dslreports.com (http://www.dslreports.com) and run the free speedtest. You will see two numbers, download and upload (or uplink). Download is how fast you can get data to the server. Upload/uplink is how fast the server can send data out to players. Basically for internet connections (bits/second): 128K uplink = 4 players 256k uplink = 7 players 320k uplink = 9 players 512k uplink = 14 players 768k uplink = 21 players 1024k uplink = 28 player 1140k uplink = 32 players (max number) Of course your particular line may or may not be stable enough to support the number I have listed there. Local players on LAN are not included in this count. The rule of thumb is 35.6Kbits per player. Certain maps and MODs may take more uplink bandwidth too. This maxplayers setting also assumes you are running the following server rate limits (in the server.cfg file): sv_minrate 3500 // no limit on maxrate for LAN only use 7500 for regular server // this controls how fast maps can be downloaded by clients //sv_maxrate 0 sv_maxrate 7500 // this is the minimum playable updaterate, leave this at 13 sv_minupdaterate 13 // 60 for updaterate is LAN ONLY use 13 for internet // 20 is default but will cut the maxplayers you can handle in 1/2 // sv_maxupdaterate 60 sv_maxupdaterate 13' WHERE post_id = 321442 AND is_historical = 1;
