UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Ive just been informed that Steam now uses GUILAG technology to make things fairer to all users by slowign down the users that had an advantage of low ping and good framerate, it also gives you that classic feel of an early 90\'s box struggling to cope with the game. The new code is embedded in the updated VGUI2.DLL, server operators that do not wish to use the GUILAG technology can use an older copy of VGUI2.DLL if they have one, as this is proven to fix your issues. GUILAG was written in 5 minutes by a valve employee, who must have been smart, becasue they snuck it in there so quietly, some might mistake it as a bug, but we all know that that is impossible as each STEAM update is obvioulsy tested thoroughly before being released. GUILAG will slow your server to around 10-20 fps, this will prevent overloading your server CPU, which casues wear on the internal circutry and shortens CPU life! This has the effect of raising overall player ping level, which helps your internet connection, as less player data is transmitted which gives you more bandwidth for downloading more steam updates! Amazing stuff. VALVe so far have not responded to the gratitude of the community, possibly because they are too modest to accpet any [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] licking... or possibly because they are too busy trying to trace and shutdown all the leaked CZ servers, and setting up more bundling deals for HL2 (need to print out more IOUs to put in graphics card boxes).... ... or maybe they just assume youre making a bug report, and we all know how big _that_ list is =). *** UPDATE I have just been informed that I havent done valve justice, not only did they add GUILAG technology to the server, but the client also, however the client does not have the option of replacing the VGUI2.DLL to disable GUILAG, as STEAM enforces the file for the client.' WHERE post_id = 321806 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'YAY FIXED', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by qUiCkSiLvEr I located the problem with the lag and solved it at least for now. The update to the server VGUI2.DLL module is the culprit. The good news is you can replace it with the old one and the problem will go away and there isn\'t any compatibility problems, AND you don\'t lose anything except the problem from what I can tell. If you don\'t have a backup of the old VGUI2.DLL then you can grab a copy from here: http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip) Just put it in place of the one in your HLServer directory. The lag is caused by the fact that the server FPS with the updated VGUI2.DLL module seems to be unbelievably low, I was getting 16fps, and any ping booster just gives you totally weird results (certainly not a boost). Try the fix and let me know how it works. THANKS A LOT MAN !!!!!!' WHERE post_id = 321810 AND is_historical = 1;
