UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Here is an important Note! I have had several people trying to apply the VGUI2.DLL fix to the HLDS that is part of the Steam Client. Unfortunately the Client HLDS will not allow the older VGUI2.DLL to work. Here is a summary of all (WIN) server types and if they can be fixed or not: ***************************************** There are actually three types of servers in Half-life. Listen Server: ========== This is where you start a server from the game itself and play at the same time ... there is only a minimal control panel. This requires the Steam Client to always be running. All the stock game content is contained in a single cache file. This version does not require the VGU2.DLL fix [] Client HLDS Server: ============== This is the option in the Steam Games Menu. This server is a full server and you have to connect to it from lan or from internet. This requires Steam Client to always be running. This has the full control panel. All the stock game content is contained in a single cache file. This version will not allow the old VGUI2.DLL fix [] Stand-Alone HLDS_1120 Server ====================== This is a totally independent install from Steam. It does not require Steam client to be running. This server is a full server and you have to connect to it from lan or from internet. There are no cache files, all the maps and things are unpacked. This version will allow the VGUI2.DLL fix to work []' WHERE post_id = 321471 AND is_historical = 1;
