UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Installation of custom maps and add/remove programs list', post_text = 'I play custom maps in DoD quite a bit. I generally download these maps seperately and adjust the auto installer install directory accordingly to get the files in the right place. Recently, however, I was going through my add/remove programs list and found 2 listings. One for each of the maps I had most recently installed. I don\'t really see this as unusual until I notice that no other maps are listed AND there size is 1,528.00MB each! Then I look at Steam and it is rated at over 3,000MB. Could someone theorize on what is going on here? Is it just DoD and Counter-Strike installs with incorrect names? Is it something else. These programs listings are WAY too big to be the maps I installed (obviously). EDIT: I would also like to add that this has been reported by at least 1 other person who has virtually the same issue. That said, check your program listings and see what it says. Does it look the same?' WHERE post_id = 414016 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'well, some self-installers create uninstallers. So, when you feel like uninstalling some maps, you could easily just run the uninstaller and it\'d delete those specific maps. Now, the file-size. The file size that shows on the add/remove program thingie gets its number from the FOLDER in which the program (or file) is installed. The map itself is probably only about 5 megs big. But your maps folder is most likely 1,528 MBs. (1.5 gigs, roughly). That is why both maps show the same size, because they (and their uninstallers) are located in the same directory. Also, you\'ll notice weird file-sizes on other programs. Some games will only show sizes like "327 kbs" or "4,300 kbs" when in reality the game takes up 2-3 gigs of space. That\'s caused of the same reason. The uninstaller is probably placed in a seperate folder within the game\'s folder, so it doesn\'t read the rest of the material, thus creating a small size (whatever\'s in the folder it\'s in) ... get the drift? Steam is, in fact, over 3 gigs big. That\'s just the way steam is, lol... So, those two maps are not sucking up all your space... just your custom maps and steam in general are! =b' WHERE post_id = 414095 AND is_historical = 1;
