UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Possible fix for microphone input changing (livedrive problem)', post_text = 'I\'ve had the problem which I think is described here: /forums/show...;threadid=13208 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=13208) /forums/show...;threadid=43849 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=43849) /forums/show...;threadid=24977 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=24977) /forums/show...;threadid=57348 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=57348) /forums/show...;threadid=53560 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=53560) /forums/show...;threadid=11287 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=11287) where steam games switch my recording line (in my case, line-in) to microphone every time they are loaded/change maps. With a bit of poking around the windows mixer APIs, I made a tiny tool that should help people suffering from this problem, removing the need to alt-tab to switch your settings back. It is located here: http://fa.glassfish.net/mixerfixer.zip (http://fa.glassfish.net/mixerfixer.zip) Basically what it does is reset the recording input device to a value you specify at a time interval (say every 30 seconds or so, but you can tell it to do it faster/slower). Note that I do not have an SB Live or any such other card. I have a Santa Cruz Turtle Beach. So if this does not work for you (and you are sure you are setting it correctly), please copy the full output of the program and e-mail it to me. It works for me just fine though. It was also a very quick utility to program, and looking at the dates on those threads, I\'m surprised Valve hasn\'t fixed such a glaring issue after all these months. It really just takes a few lines of code once you have the mixer device open... I thought steam was supposed to encourage these kind of quick fixes?' WHERE post_id = 524693 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'it works! nice one []' WHERE post_id = 524751 AND is_historical = 1;
