UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Always love a GUI but this program gets the job done perfectly and is as lightweight as a workaround can possibly be. Great work! I tried it with my Audigy 2 and it worked just fine. I have a theory on why Valve has left this behavior in Steam unfixed. Do any of you remember when voice communication was first added to HL in that one update? Remember what option they gave you if you didn\'t have a headset? Buy a Plantronics headset! More specifically... a USB headset like the DSP-500 (they even make/made? one branded for CS). Well guess who actually owns that headset and never has problems in Steam? Me. The mixer for this headset is very basic as it only has a playback and a recording volume control in the mixer. When I plug it in, it takes over as the default sound card and when I go into Steam, it is set as the default mic. That is just one theory that, to me, seems to make sense. I could be totally off here. It could be that Valve just decided that everyone plugs their mic into the mic jack and anyone who is different doesn\'t matter...' WHERE post_id = 526718 AND is_historical = 1;
