UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'but i don get what our connection has to do wit dis... "bad prase in client command" can tat mean tat the client is doing something wrong to make this happen?' WHERE post_id = 566231 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Bad Parse means that a packet of information that your client sent to the server got messed up. Routers handle all packets from the client going out to the world and then handle all packets coming back in. If anything is wrong with the router\'s programming then it may improperly handle the data which can lead to this problem. Players that can connect to insecure servers but not secure servers almost always have out-of-date router firmware. The other source of this problem is if you have spyware on your computer like marketscore or ISPs like freeserve and some AOL connections where all your data is sent to one of their routers and the data gets messed up there. In that case, the solution is to remove the spyware: What to Do About SpyWare & Virus Problems FAQ (/forums/showthread.php?threadid=76462) remove yourself from the "transparent proxy" service that the ISP has your connection on (some UK ISPs are doing this) or get a new ISP. There are a few other things that might cause this but these ones I\'ve listed are the most common.' WHERE post_id = 566373 AND is_historical = 1;
