UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'DONT INTRDUCE THINGS THAT DONT WORK FOR ANYONE SO what if we didn\'t pay for the friends network, STOP sticking up for VALVE your not gona become a mod or something. They MADE us download FRIENDS so it\'s SHOULD work bottom line.' WHERE post_id = 806364 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Both sides make strong points. But I go with stanley. If your going to put it in there, make it work. Or take the PoS out.' WHERE post_id = 806491 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Why dont you give them time to take it out? Are they not working on enough already? Do you think they have an army of a million workers ready to fix your every personal problem? Stanley M. -- Valve did not make you download anything. Friends came inside of STEAM which you downloaded, by yourself. And Stanely, you post "dont introduce things [Friends] that dont work for anyone" right after someone that posts that Friends is working for them. Tell me how that makes sense? CG1 -- You say the same things I said in other posts, and these people are acting the same towards you as others towards me where I posted. It\'s pretty draining to try to explain to people they\'re expectations are to high. I think its futile to try to stop their ulcers from forming. However its nice to see someone that is defending common sense. Even though we seem like we\'re sucking up to Valve for it.' WHERE post_id = 806638 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'I can see valve are busy anyone can see that..but if your going to include something make it work or get rid. On the other hand having a friends network there doesnt harm the user in anyway.. its a nice bonus especially when it works' WHERE post_id = 807711 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'No, but the whole point of steam was to eliminate hassles like having to use 3rd party apps like messengers and the likes, and yet people pretty much have to, plus these lag and performance issues don\'t give me tons of confidence in the system. You\'ll notice the fanbois have pretty much given up on defending steam besides saying "shut up whiney n00b," or "oh god, heres another one." But honestly, what is the point of steam now? It was touted as an all in one, sever browser, updater, launcher, buddy list/IMing. Updating seems to be a joke, with valve updating at some of the worst possible times, not seeming to consult with clans and league organizers. The afformentioned friends list seems to be a failure at the moment, and having a performance issues with hardware that there is really no excuse to have them (and then the fanbois saying "well you just don\'t know anything about computers," or something similar). So really? Why is steam so great?' WHERE post_id = 807735 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '"oh god heres another one","shut up you whiney n00b"' WHERE post_id = 807747 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by Stanley M DONT INTRDUCE THINGS THAT DONT WORK FOR ANYONE SO what if we didn\'t pay for the friends network, STOP sticking up for VALVE your not gona become a mod or something. They MADE us download FRIENDS so it\'s SHOULD work bottom line. Yes, they made you download friends. It\'s part of steam. Try reading the valve subscriber agreement. and yes, I was sticking up for valve for this reason, because we DIDN\'T pay for a friends network. We paid for a video game. Running steam isn\'t cheap you know. And you should think about what you type because what you said there makes you look like a right idiot. quote:Originaly posted by undeniable Why dont you give them time to take it out? Are they not working on enough already? Do you think they have an army of a million workers ready to fix your every personal problem? Stanley M. -- Valve did not make you download anything. Friends came inside of STEAM which you downloaded, by yourself. And Stanely, you post "dont introduce things [Friends] that dont work for anyone" right after someone that posts that Friends is working for them. Tell me how that makes sense? CG1 -- You say the same things I said in other posts, and these people are acting the same towards you as others towards me where I posted. It\'s pretty draining to try to explain to people they\'re expectations are to high. I think its futile to try to stop their ulcers from forming. However its nice to see someone that is defending common sense. Even though we seem like we\'re sucking up to Valve for it. Both good points yes but there are alot of kids around whining things aren\'t working, when they don\'t even contribute to them. Nobody pays for steam friends network apart from Valve. They are a business and are suppost to be making money, not losing. tbh the sensible people here are getting damn fed up of people complaining constantly about steam, friends, etc when they don\'t know how hard it is to impliment and maintain a network like Steam. Steam is one of a kind, no other company has done anything like it. Of couse there are going to be problems fs. quote:Originaly posted by Dauvin No, but the whole point of steam was to eliminate hassles like having to use 3rd party apps like messengers and the likes, and yet people pretty much have to, plus these lag and performance issues don\'t give me tons of confidence in the system. You\'ll notice the fanbois have pretty much given up on defending steam besides saying "shut up whiney n00b," or "oh god, heres another one." But honestly, what is the point of steam now? It was touted as an all in one, sever browser, updater, launcher, buddy list/IMing. Updating seems to be a joke, with valve updating at some of the worst possible times, not seeming to consult with clans and league organizers. The afformentioned friends list seems to be a failure at the moment, and having a performance issues with hardware that there is really no excuse to have them (and then the fanbois saying "well you just don\'t know anything about computers," or something similar). So really? Why is steam so great? As I just said - Steam is one of a kind, nobody has ever made an automated content system like this on such a massive scale. It can\'t be perfect first time. I mean, look at Windows 95. **** loads of bugs, but that was one of a kind at it\'s time, and now we\'re on XP/2003 things are improving. Give steam time. About performance issues, over 90% of people complaining about performance and lag with steam is because of their own computer. Alot of people seem to be forgetting the point that technology moves forward. It doesn\'t stand still and it most certainly doesn\'t go backwards (apart from with Windows ME but I won\'t go into that). If people use old computers, they are going to get poor performance. Steam does not need changing to improve performance, users computers do. Have you seen the half life 2 hardware survey page? There are people with 16 MHz computers using steam, which is absolutely crap and yet I bet they all complain. You mentioned about "shut up whiney noob, etc". Well the only reason people here say that is because there are far to many ungreatful spoilt brats around constantly whining about steam when 9 times out of 10 it\'s their own fault. Steam was made for the majority, not the minority. Now your mentioning valve updating at worse times? m8 shut up. How the hell can valve know when it\'s a good time to update or not for people? "Oh hey, dauvin doesn\'t want steam updated now lets wait a whole month to release this important bug fix and piss loads of people off just to suit him". And about consulting with clans and leages, now your really losing it tbh, what the hell? It\'s not up to valve to inform every clan and league orginiser about an update or whatever happens, why should have change their busy enough schedule just to suit the minority, it\'s not as if we pay much towards steam. and yes we all seem to know by now that friends has failed but you are missing the point that we paid for a video game, not a friends network, or board games. We pay so little for a half life cd key that grants us so many games. Why is steam so great? Well, ok steam has some bugs, it\'s not perfect but why dont you try implimenting such an automated network yourself? Can you do that? Didn\'t think so. Almost as stupid as when a whole croud boo at someones football shot, when most of them can\'t even kick the ball. ________ Ok that\'s the end of this long post [] Thanks for reading.' WHERE post_id = 807817 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Continuous Game Crashes - Memory Errors', post_text = 'Howdy all, I\'ve been hopping from server to server trying to see wether or not it\'s just been me that has been seeing consistant crashes of CS, but I\'ve talked to many people and this is not the case. Everyone seems to be getting a certain memory error: "The Instruction at "0x0f3a5969" referenced memory at "0x0f635808". The memory coule not be "read". Click on OK to terminate the program." Anywho, I\'ve noticed that it only happens when there is a kill or a hit from the Auto Sniper Rifles, the Scout, and the AWP (we all know which weapons)... If there is a way to fix this cool, I would try the Linksys Firmware crap if I felt like it, but I\'m in a bad mood already, and I don\'t believe that I should have to change the settings of my router in order to be compatible with the new CS update... Why not rollback to the last update? I thought it had been working beautifully ever since the Friends list had been updated. I don\'t want servers to ban the weapons because of the update. I like my scout... [] Well anywho, that\'s all I got... By the way, I like this guy: "steam gave us the update with the error steam will give us the error fix i will not change a thing in my pc steam is ****ed up fix it or lose a lot of customers" Maybe a tad harsh but... I think we all just want to play some CS.' WHERE post_id = 812531 AND is_historical = 1;
