UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Newbie Questions', post_text = 'Hello Mr Taylor Sir, I am a new member and so have a few questions..... 1: I have got steam but haven\'t installed any games yet so I haven\'t put my ATI key in anywhere yet. Does this mean that I just update my steam to the new steam when it\'s out and enter my key in the appropriate box? 2: Is there anyway to backup the games such as half life 2 or to backup saved games at all? 3: Do you have to be logged into steam all the time to play HL2 or can I play it offline? 4: Any idea roughly how long it will take to download HL2 and CS Source over a 512K ADSL broadband connection? 5: Any idea\'s yet as to the release dates of HL2 and CS Source Beta on steam?' WHERE post_id = 870895 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = '1. You can wait until HL2 comes out and enter it then, or you can enter it now - click Browse Games, then click Register a Product I Already Own. It will accept the ATI key -- and though it looks like nothing has changed, unless you see an error message, the key is on your account and HL2 will show up in My Games when it\'s released. 2. sure - you can backup the entire SteamApps directory if you want. Or, you can just backup the config files and save games (in the SAVE folders), and/or the Steam cache files (.gcf - where most of the data lives). 3. You will be able to play HL2 offline. However, to do this, you first have to Login to Steam "online" -- to go Offline, Steam requires that the last time you ran it you were logged in, so that it can be sure that you own the games you are trying to play. So, if you use Steam "online", the game is at 100% loaded, and you choose "Exit" and NOT "Exit and Logout", you should then be able to launch Steam when not connected, and play. 4, 5: sorry, don\'t have an answer for either of these yet.' WHERE post_id = 871894 AND is_historical = 1;
