UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Pretty sure this is marketing ploy...', post_text = 'Pretty sure this is marketing ploy...I\'m going to try and prove that this is. I took a pic of all currently playing players of CZ. Roughly 10,000. That tells us about atleast 10,000 people play CZ. Now if that number doubles triples then that would prove that the delay was a scheme thought up by some guy in the marketing department. With this scheme you could get more people buying CZ to play CS:S,because they know they have more time. Haveing 20,000 or 30,000 people testing beta is a lot better for the company, because these people are potential buyers. Having 15,000 players buying CS:S at the end of the beta phase is better than 5,000 dont you think so? Also, there is or may also be another reason.Having more people testing the beta will get more people finding bugs faster(if thats the case). Now why dont they just give it to, and let the CS community test it...I\'m sure they\'ll find all the bugs in a matter of minutes/hours/days whatever. The point is they wouldnt be making any money from the CS owners. That is why! Lets do some math say 1 copy of CZ is $30, and $10,000 people buy the game, how much do you get?$300,000. Now lets delay the beta...and wait till we get another $10,0000 people from the CS community to buy CZ.Dont you get more money?Now this would make up for poor sales and maybe some other things. Now you have 20,000 people testing the beta,I garuntee atleast half those people would buy CS:S or HL2. See this is a simple strat used by Valve to make some money. Although I dont like this strat, I think its a good Idea...but aleast give an indepth explanation for delaying a game. Thats all I have to say,and I\'m sure a few would be agreeing with me on this. -Cole3000' WHERE post_id = 874008 AND is_historical = 1;
