UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by domomike dude get off the forums you\'re lagging them!!! good example.' WHERE post_id = 892385 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by WrG|IceMouse Well if their ping is so high(800) that they aren\'t able to play, they are only increasing the load on the server and taking up a spot... I agree that if it\'s less than 250~300, then they should still be allowed on yeah, i understand that there\'s other reasons to boot them; i was just wondering why the idea exists that one player can completely lag everyone to the point of unplayability. it seemed pretty strange to me. if everyone is pinging >400, then the issue is likely with the server, not some player on it. but i wanted to make sure there wasn\'t something in the server code itself that i wasn\'t aware of that would actually give credence to the idea.' WHERE post_id = 892485 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'nah, nobody is going to lag a server. the server should have net settings capped properly to limit bandwidth overusage, other than that no lagger will lag a server. i think ppl set that autokick on b/c laggers are damn hard to hit and they get lots of random kills thx to lag compensation.' WHERE post_id = 892754 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by w00ters nah, nobody is going to lag a server. the server should have net settings capped properly to limit bandwidth overusage, other than that no lagger will lag a server. i think ppl set that autokick on b/c laggers are damn hard to hit and they get lots of random kills thx to lag compensation. You kinda contradicted yourself there. With lag compensation enabled, this does tend to create a sensation of the server lagging when ping ranges varry so much, but more shots seems to register (low ping vs high ping). Without lag compensation, the low pinger tends to either walk through a high-pinger, half the bullets dont seem to register, or they look like they are teleporting instead of running . Either way it does effect the game, just gotta decide how ya want your server to play.' WHERE post_id = 892817 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'trust me, if evry1 is pinging at 40-50 and some geezer comes on with 300 ping he will lag the WHOLE server out.' WHERE post_id = 892883 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by SoNofSaTaN trust me, if evry1 is pinging at 40-50 and some geezer comes on with 300 ping he will lag the WHOLE server out. That\'s simply not true, and not how the Half-Life client/server architecture works. The main reason people with higher pings are kicked from servers is because they tend to lag so badly that they appear to "warp" through the level and are much harder to hit.' WHERE post_id = 892911 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Players with lower pings actually lag the server out... Their broadband demands higher download/upload rates and puts a strain on the server (ever wonder why servers have their clients limited to a "rate" of 9999. Higher rate means better pings for clients but more strain on the server. LPB\'s are hogging all the bandwidth and blaming it on dial-up users who actually use the least bandwidth from the server...' WHERE post_id = 892920 AND is_historical = 1;
