UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'Great idea. What better way to keep pubbers and competitors happy at the same time? There isnt really that much to change but it makes a big difference. With a new game, everyone has to buy it including the competitors and thats becoming a larger and larger portion of the community. Besides, what could get you more customers than ones who play console games (a lot more people than the number of cs players) and other pc games than hearing about a CPL tournament for $200,000. I myself played other games before i played cs and didnt even play competitively until soon after 1.6\'s release. It\'s not that big of a step to go from casual pubber to cal-o/im teams and if valve wants the game to spread by word of mouth theyre gonna have to please more than youre typical pubber.' WHERE post_id = 922014 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'In my opinion, having a \'pro-mode\' (or mod) created for CS:Source would make the most number of people the happiest, and is virtually a win-win situation. I do not understand how ANYBODY can even attempt to argue at this topic, there are virtually no valid points in my opinion. A \'pro-mode\' keeps server companies in business, sponsors interested in the game, a large (continously growing and will only remain to get larger mind you) fanbase, and the competitive players what they have always wanted; the best version of CS ever. If Valve actually took the time and the initiative to listen to us (by us I am referring to the competitive CS community) then I can gurantee more money will be both coming to their games, and coming out (more investments into teams, tournaments, LAN events, etc.). Where is there a problem with this suggestion? The \'average\' gamer (the non-competitive stream player) has his own CS:Source, that he can enjoy and play casually; and the competitive gamer has his (or her) version, customized to provide the best competitive gaming environment EVER in Counter-Strike. Am I missing something ... where is the problem here? Wait, there is none. The only issue is if Valve is willing to put a little extra work into the release of their latest title, CS:Source, for an outcome which will produce a much more positive gaming experience, and in turn will produce much higher sales. I hope that VALVE realizes the potiential of a creation of a \'pro-mode\' of CS can have, and just how beneficial it will be to their company. If and when the time comes, I hope Valve contacts members of the competitive community and works with us (rather than against us) to produce the BEST version of CS ever created.' WHERE post_id = 922021 AND is_historical = 1;
