UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'That\'s the spirit =) The only problem I have with CS right now is that it\'s not very spectator friendly. Valve isn\'t my type of company to be honest. They just don\'t know how to appeal to all of the players. Let me tell you, there are ways to appeal to public players and competitive players alike. Blizzard is a stunning example of this. They have tuned StarCraft to it\'s fullest potential over it\'s 5 years of existance. The public players have their fun, I\'ve seen people play public games all day and have no complaints whatsoever. If you have ever seen a professional game of StarCraft, it\'s pure art. The things these people can do is amazing, and the same goes with Counter-Strike. The competitive players make this game worth playing. Blizzard has sponsered tournaments for the competitive scene, they have even done a COMPLETE update BASED on the competitive needs. Valve can do the same thing but they don\'t for some reason. I\'m not really sure what the reason is, but they could be so much more than they are right now. The competitive scenes of video games is where their attention should be. Whoever said "You can\'t be pro at you\'re own game, you can only be pro at the game everyone plays." I completely agree. But why lower the standards of skill in the game that everyone plays? Why can\'t we increase the skill gap again without any of the exploits and problem areas. It\'s entirely possible, and it wouldn\'t be too hard if Valve actually did it. Basing a game off of the competition makes game thrive. Believe me when I say that. StarCraft, WarCraft III, and Unreal Tournament are all perfect examples of this. If you did a simple study, I guarantee you that more people have heard of WarCraft III, and would be more willing to buy it over Counter-Strike any day of the week. I was forunate enough to be given a sponsership while playing StarCraft. I was able to travel and meet the people at Blizzard. All I can say is, Blizzard will be the #1 company in my eyes until Valve takes a step forward in the right direction and starts listening to the fanbase that will get them somewhere. Also, go ahead and tell me that they are a great company. Great companies don\'t get sued by the publishers. Great companies don\'t have to delay their games every year. Great companies don\'t release an unfinished product to the consumer for $60. Nor does a great company release a minor update for $40. Go ahead and argue you\'re points with me, but I have played every game Valve has made, and every game Blizzard has made. Blizzard is the better company. Believe that.' WHERE post_id = 1309376 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by krokko I\'ve played with the best cs players in Sweden. Unless you have too, no you don\'t know what you\'re talking about. The aiming skill is not comparable. It\'s just a different universe. They\'re just as good as the best pub-allstars in terms of aim. On that note I don\'t think i\'ve ever come across a player that is better than me in terms of aim. (have found many players equal to me) Those guys are getting old, and the older you get, the slower your reaction time becomes. What those teams do shine at is working at as a team, and when the skill gap is so small in the cal-i area, your teams strats are all that really matter. Edit- please don\'t take this as ignorance, because im not trying to be.' WHERE post_id = 1309387 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_text = 'KonkreteAngel : "cal-i player are so overhyped when it comes to pub demos. They\'re just as good as pub-allstars in terms of aim." That is without a doubt the quote of the year. Worse than coL.1 saying 3D are washups then losing to them 13-1.' WHERE post_id = 1309388 AND is_historical = 1;
