UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'It\'s called ENTRAPMENT and it\'s ILLEGAL!', post_text = 'I do not condone warez, nor stealing, nor any illegal activities. My steam account has not been disabled for any reason whatsoever (however it may be if the steam flower-power-junkiess read this post and see that not everyone just goosesteps along with them []). HOWEVER: In America, entrapment is illegal. A police officer cannot give a person illegal drugs or stolen property and then attempt to punish them for posessing it. I cannot speak for other countries, but that is the way it is here. While I may not agree with those that would have attempted to use a pirated CD key to play HL2, I also do not agree with the illegal way the issue is being handled. If a person attempted to use a pirated key, and then actually PURCHASED the exact same game after that, how is it fair to ban their account? Also, if you are going to ban accounts, you should do it on a case by case basis because the circumstances surrounding each case may be different. I suggest that all of those in America who have had their accounts banned should find each other through these forums, get together, and get a nice class action lawsuit going. It is very hard to take on a large company individually, but together, you may have a chance. Again, these proceedings may be legal in other countries, so if you are not in America, then you should check with a lawyer in your country. I DO NOT CONDONE the reasons for your account being banned, but TWO WRONGS DON\'T MAKE A RIGHT. ENTRAPMENT IS ILLEGAL, and I would love to see American justice work for Americans. In closing, flame all you want because I have said my piece and have no reason to return to this thread (and I don\'t care what flamers have to say anyway).' WHERE post_id = 1607597 AND is_historical = 1;
UPDATE phpbb_posts SET post_subject = 'Re: It\'s called ENTRAPMENT and it\'s ILLEGAL!', post_text = 'quote:Originally posted by mystakill I do not condone warez, nor stealing, nor any illegal activities. My steam account has not been disabled for any reason whatsoever (however it may be if the steam flower-power-junkiess read this post and see that not everyone just goosesteps along with them []). HOWEVER: In America, entrapment is illegal. A police officer cannot give a person illegal drugs or stolen property and then attempt to punish them for posessing it. I cannot speak for other countries, but that is the way it is here. While I may not agree with those that would have attempted to use a pirated CD key to play HL2, I also do not agree with the illegal way the issue is being handled. If a person attempted to use a pirated key, and then actually PURCHASED the exact same game after that, how is it fair to ban their account? Also, if you are going to ban accounts, you should do it on a case by case basis because the circumstances surrounding each case may be different. I suggest that all of those in America who have had their accounts banned should find each other through these forums, get together, and get a nice class action lawsuit going. It is very hard to take on a large company individually, but together, you may have a chance. Again, these proceedings may be legal in other countries, so if you are not in America, then you should check with a lawyer in your country. I DO NOT CONDONE the reasons for your account being banned, but TWO WRONGS DON\'T MAKE A RIGHT. ENTRAPMENT IS ILLEGAL, and I would love to see American justice work for Americans. In closing, flame all you want because I have said my piece and have no reason to return to this thread (and I don\'t care what flamers have to say anyway). psst...here\'s a tip. Valve is a game company...not a law enforcement agency, \'entrapment\' doesnt apply to them.' WHERE post_id = 1607608 AND is_historical = 1;
